window.ZGCLAB_DETAILS["news-0"]=[{"id":"news-2117","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"众议员亚当斯就国土安全部向夏洛特部署边境巡逻队和ICE发表声明","title_en":"Rep. Adams on DHS’s Deployment of Border Patrol & ICE to Charlotte","summary_cn":"2025年11月13日，北卡罗来纳州第12选区众议员阿尔玛·亚当斯就美国国土安全部计划向夏洛特部署边境巡逻队和移民与海关执法局人员发表声明。她表示极度担忧，称夏洛特的移民社区是这座城市的骄傲，不会坐视选民受到恐吓或骚扰，并批评边境巡逻队和ICE在芝加哥、洛杉矶等地过度使用武力、对和平抗议者使用催泪瓦斯，认为这些做法不应出现在夏洛特和梅克伦堡县。她表示正与地方、州和联邦领导人及移民活动人士保持联系。","summary_en":"On November 13, 2025, Congresswoman Alma S. Adams (NC-12) released a statement on the U.S. Department of Homeland Security's plans to deploy U.S. Border Patrol and ICE agents to Charlotte. She expressed extreme concern, saying Charlotte's immigrant community is a proud part of the city and that she will not stand by while constituents are intimidated or harassed. She criticized Border Patrol and ICE tactics in Chicago and Los Angeles, including excessive force and tear-gassing peaceful protesters, saying such tactics have no place in Charlotte or Mecklenburg County. She remains in contact with local, state, and federal leaders and immigration activists.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-24T20:49:53.305509+00:00","url":"http://adams.house.gov/media-center/press-releases/rep-adams-dhss-deployment-border-patrol-ice-charlotte","content":"Image\nHome\nMedia Center\nPress Releases\nRep. Adams on DHS’s Deployment of Border Patrol & ICE to Charlotte\nImage November 13, 2025 Press ReleaseCHARLOTTE, NC—Today, Congresswoman Alma S. Adams, Ph.D. (NC-12) released a statement on the U.S. Department of Homeland Security’s (DHS) plans to deploy U.S. Border Patrol and ICE agents to Charlotte.“I am extremely concerned about the deployment of U.S. Border Patrol and ICE agents to Charlotte,” said Congresswoman Adams. “Charlotte’s immigrant community is a proud part of the Queen City, and I will not stand by and watch my constituents be intimidated or harassed. Everyone deserves to be treated with dignity and what we have seen border patrol and ICE agents do in places like Chicago and Los Angeles—using excessive force in their operations and tear gassing peaceful protestors—threatens the wellbeing of the communities they enter. Those tactics and values have no place in the City of Charlotte or Mecklenburg County.”Rep. Adams remains in contact with local, state, and federal leaders, as well as immigration activists in the 12th District, to ensure fair and appropriate treatment of her constituents and the proud immigrant community that calls Charlotte home.\nNC12","content_cn":"图片\n首页\n媒体中心\n新闻稿\n亚当斯议员谈国土安全部向夏洛特部署边境巡逻队和移民及海关执法局人员\n图片 2025年11月13日 新闻稿\n北卡罗来纳州夏洛特——今天，国会议员阿尔玛·S·亚当斯博士（北卡罗来纳州第12选区）就美国国土安全部（DHS）计划向夏洛特部署美国边境巡逻队和移民及海关执法局人员发表声明。\n亚当斯议员说：“我对向夏洛特部署美国边境巡逻队和移民及海关执法局人员深感担忧。夏洛特的移民社区是女王城引以为傲的一部分，我不会袖手旁观，看着我的选民受到恐吓或骚扰。每个人都应受到有尊严的对待，而我们看到边境巡逻队和移民及海关执法局人员在芝加哥和洛杉矶等地采取过度武力开展行动，并向和平抗议者发射催泪瓦斯——这些做法威胁到他们进入的社区的福祉。这些策略和价值观在夏洛特市或梅克伦堡县都没有立足之地。”\n亚当斯议员仍与地方、州和联邦领导人以及第12选区的移民活动人士保持联系，以确保她的选民以及把夏洛特称为家园的自豪移民社区得到公平、适当的对待。\nNC12","publish_source":"adams.house.gov","publish_time":"2025-11-13T15:44:23-05:00"}},{"id":"news-1826","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"众议员亚当斯提出针对国土安全部长克里斯蒂·诺姆的弹劾条款","title_en":"Rep. Adams Introduces Impeachment Articles Against DHS Sec. Kristi Noem","summary_cn":"2026年1月15日，众议员阿尔玛·亚当斯与众议院70名民主党人共同提出针对国土安全部长克里斯蒂·诺姆的弹劾条款，指控其妨碍国会、违背公众信任和谋取私利。亚当斯称，诺姆任内DHS、CBP和ICE系统性侵犯美国人权利，夏洛特行动导致美国公民被袭击和非法逮捕，且其扣留国会拨付的FEMA资金，延误了北卡罗来纳州飓风海伦的数十亿美元灾后重建。","summary_en":"On January 15, 2026, Congresswoman Alma Adams joined 70 House Democrats in introducing articles of impeachment against DHS Secretary Kristi Noem for obstruction of Congress, violation of public trust, and self-dealing. Adams said that under Noem, DHS, CBP and ICE have systematically violated Americans' rights, that the Charlotte operation led to U.S. citizens being assaulted and unlawfully arrested, and that Noem's withholding of congressionally appropriated FEMA funds delayed billions in Hurricane Helene recovery for North Carolina.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-18T15:43:59.020098+00:00","url":"http://adams.house.gov/media-center/press-releases/rep-adams-introduces-impeachment-articles-against-dhs-sec-kristi-noem","content":"Image\nHome\nMedia Center\nPress Releases\nRep. Adams Introduces Impeachment Articles Against DHS Sec. Kristi Noem\nImage January 15, 2026 Press ReleaseWASHINGTON, DC—Today, Congresswoman Alma S. Adams, Ph.D. (D-NC-12) joined 70 House Democrats in introducing Articles of Impeachment against Department of Homeland Security (DHS) Secretary Kristi Noem for obstruction of Congress, violation of public trust, and self-dealing. North Carolina has been directly impacted by Sec. Noem’s abuse of power. The Customs and Border Patrol (CBP) operation in Charlotte late last year terrorized the community, leading to U.S. citizens being assaulted and arrested. Sec. Noem’s unconstitutional withholding of Congressionally appropriated FEMA funds has resulted in the delay of billions of dollars of Hurricane Helene recovery to North Carolina, severely impacting recovery efforts in Western North Carolina.“Under Secretary Noem’s tenure, DHS, CBP, and ICE have systemically violated the rights of Americans and the U.S. Constitution,” said Congresswoman Adams. “Border Patrol’s operation in Charlotte saw American citizens assaulted and unlawfully arrested for practicing their Constitutional rights, while their refusal to coordinate with local law enforcement threatened the safety of every person in Charlotte-Mecklenburg. At the same time, Sec. Noem’s willful withholding of Congressionally appropriated FEMA funds has impeded North Carolina’s ability to recover from the worst natural disaster in state history. I do not take Articles of Impeachment lightly but it is clear that Sec. Noem has violated federal law and her oath of office, and, for the safety of our country, she must be removed from office.”\nIssues:National Security\nNC12","content_cn":"图片\n首页\n媒体中心\n新闻稿\n亚当斯众议员提出针对国土安全部部长克里斯蒂·诺姆的弹劾条款\n图片 2026年1月15日 新闻稿\n华盛顿特区——今天，国会女议员阿尔玛·S·亚当斯博士（北卡罗来纳州第12选区民主党人）与70名众议院民主党人共同提出针对国土安全部（DHS）部长克里斯蒂·诺姆的弹劾条款，指控其妨碍国会、违背公众信任以及谋取私利。北卡罗来纳州直接受到诺姆部长滥用权力的影响。去年年底，海关与边境保护局（CBP）在夏洛特的行动令社区陷入恐慌，导致美国公民遭到殴打和逮捕。诺姆部长违宪扣留国会拨款的联邦紧急事务管理局（FEMA）资金，导致数十亿美元的海伦飓风灾后重建资金延迟拨付给北卡罗来纳州，严重影响了北卡罗来纳州西部的重建工作。“在诺姆部长的任期内，国土安全部、海关与边境保护局和移民及海关执法局（ICE）系统性地侵犯了美国人的权利和美国宪法，”亚当斯众议员表示。“边境巡逻队在夏洛特的行动中，美国公民因行使宪法权利而遭到殴打和非法逮捕，而他们拒绝与地方执法部门协调，威胁到夏洛特-梅克伦堡每一位居民的安全。与此同时，诺姆部长故意扣留国会拨款的FEMA资金，阻碍了北卡罗来纳州从该州历史上最严重的自然灾害中恢复的能力。我并非轻率地提出弹劾条款，但很明显，诺姆部长违反了联邦法律和她的就职誓言，为了我们国家的安全，她必须被免职。”\n议题：国家安全\n北卡罗来纳州第12选区","publish_source":"adams.house.gov","publish_time":"2026-01-15T13:30:51-05:00"}},{"id":"news-3248","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"阿莫迪重返众议院拨款委员会国土安全小组委员会主席职位","title_en":"Amodei Returns as House Appropriations Homeland Security Chairman","summary_cn":"2025年1月17日，众议员马克·阿莫迪就再次被任命为美国众议院拨款委员会国土安全小组委员会主席发表声明。他表示荣幸重返该职位，感谢拨款委员会主席汤姆·科尔信任，并称将致力于应对边境危机，期待与国土安全部长克里斯蒂·诺姆、边境事务负责人汤姆·霍曼及地方、州和联邦伙伴合作，提供所需资源。科尔称赞阿莫迪经验丰富、领导有力。阿莫迪还将任职于金融服务与一般政府小组委员会及内政、环境及相关机构小组委员会。","summary_en":"On January 17, 2025, Congressman Mark Amodei issued a statement after being appointed to return as Chairman of the Homeland Security Subcommittee on the U.S. House Committee on Appropriations. He said it was an honor to return and thanked Chairman Tom Cole for entrusting him with leading the subcommittee in addressing the border crisis. He looked forward to working with Homeland Security Secretary Kristi Noem, Border Czar Tom Homan, and other partners to provide needed resources. Cole praised Amodei's experience and leadership. Amodei will also serve on the Financial Services and General Government Subcommittee and the Interior, Environment, and Related Agencies Subcommittee.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-24T22:15:01.516255+00:00","url":"http://amodei.house.gov/news-releases/amodei-returns-house-appropriations-homeland-security-chairman","content":"Home\nNews Releases\nAmodei Returns as House Appropriations Homeland Security Chairman\nImage\nJanuary 17, 2025 Press Release\nWashington, D.C. — Congressman Mark Amodei issued the following statement after being appointed to return as the Chairman of the Homeland Security Subcommittee on the U.S. House Committee on Appropriations:“It’s an honor to return as Chairman of the House Appropriations Homeland Security Subcommittee,” said Rep. Mark Amodei. “I want to thank Chairman Tom Cole for entrusting me with the responsibility of leading this subcommittee as we work to find a path forward in addressing the ongoing border crisis.“Under the Biden Administration, every community has felt the consequences of the unchecked surge in illegal immigration. I look forward to working alongside Secretary of Homeland Security Kristi Noem, Border Czar Tom Homan, and other key local, state, and federal partners to provide the resources needed to swiftly and effectively fulfill the promises made by the incoming administration.“We remain committed to securing our borders, restoring order to our immigration system, and eliminating the violence and drug trafficking that have infiltrated and devastated our communities. This subcommittee holds significant power to improve the lives of all Americans, and we will not rest until confidence in our nation's safety and security is fully restored.”“Congressman Amodei brings over a decade’s worth of experience on the House Appropriations Committee and has consistently demonstrated strong leadership grounded in common-sense, conservative values,” said Appropriations Committee Chairman Tom Cole. “Last year, I appointed him Chairman of the Homeland Security Subcommittee, where he successfully passed the FY25 Homeland Security bill out of committee and on the House floor. With significant focus on the next 100 days, I am confident in his ability to deliver for the American people, who have made it clear we must act now to secure our borders and restore national security.”In addition to serving as Chairman of the Homeland Security Subcommittee, Congressman Mark Amodei will also serve as a member on the Financial Services and General Government Subcommittee and the Interior, Environment, and Related Agencies Subcommittee.Learn more about the Homeland Security Subcommittee here.","content_cn":"首页\n新闻稿\n阿莫迪回任众议院拨款委员会国土安全小组委员会主席\n图片\n2025年1月17日 新闻稿\n华盛顿特区——众议员马克·阿莫迪在获任回归担任美国众议院拨款委员会国土安全小组委员会主席后发表了以下声明：\n“能够回任众议院拨款委员会国土安全小组委员会主席，我深感荣幸，”马克·阿莫迪议员说。“我要感谢主席汤姆·科尔对我的信任，让我负责领导这个小组委员会，努力寻找解决持续边境危机的前进道路。\n“在拜登政府执政期间，每个社区都感受到了不受控制的非法移民激增所带来的后果。我期待与国土安全部长克里斯蒂·诺姆、边境事务主管汤姆·霍曼以及其他关键的地方、州和联邦合作伙伴携手，为迅速有效地履行新政府的承诺提供所需资源。\n“我们仍致力于守卫边境、恢复移民体系秩序，并消除已渗透社区、给社区造成破坏的暴力和毒品贩运。这个小组委员会拥有改善所有美国人生活的重要权力，在我国安全与保障的信心完全恢复之前，我们不会停歇。”\n“阿莫迪议员在众议院拨款委员会拥有十多年的经验，并始终展现出以常识为基础、植根于保守价值观的强大领导力，”拨款委员会主席汤姆·科尔说。“去年，我任命他担任国土安全小组委员会主席，在那里他成功推动2025财年国土安全法案通过委员会审议，并提交众议院全院审议。鉴于未来100天将重点推进相关工作，我相信他有能力为美国人民带来成果；美国人民已经明确表示，我们必须立即采取行动，守卫边境并恢复国家安全。”\n除担任国土安全小组委员会主席外，马克·阿莫迪议员还将担任金融服务和一般政府小组委员会以及内政、环境及相关机构小组委员会成员。\n在此了解更多关于国土安全小组委员会的信息。","publish_source":"amodei.house.gov","publish_time":"2025-01-17T11:22:59-05:00"}},{"id":"news-1758","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"阿莫代伊主席的2026财年国土安全拨款法案在众议院通过","title_en":"Chairman Amodei’s FY26 Homeland Security Bill Passes the House","summary_cn":"2026年1月22日，众议院通过H.R. 7147《2026年国土安全部拨款法案》，连同H.R. 7148完成本财年政府拨款工作。国土安全拨款小组委员会主席马克·阿莫代伊表示，该法案加强空中、陆地、海上及新兴网络领域防护，支持2026年世界杯等大型活动安保，维持2.2万名边境巡逻人员经费，扩大海岸警卫队在印太的存在以应对中国，并为CISA关键岗位提供人员经费。","summary_en":"On January 22, 2026, the House passed H.R. 7147, the Department of Homeland Security Appropriations Act, 2026, completing fiscal year government funding along with H.R. 7148. Homeland Security Subcommittee Chairman Mark Amodei said the bill strengthens protections across air, land, maritime and emerging cyber domains, supports security for events like the 2026 FIFA World Cup, sustains funding for 22,000 Border Patrol agents, expands the Coast Guard's Indo-Pacific footprint to counter China, and enables staffing of critical CISA positions.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-18T15:41:18.847286+00:00","url":"http://amodei.house.gov/news-releases/chairman-amodeis-fy26-homeland-security-bill-passes-house","content":"Home\nNews Releases\nChairman Amodei’s FY26 Homeland Security Bill Passes the House\nImage\nJanuary 22, 2026 Press Release\nWashington, D.C. – Today, the House of Representatives passed H.R. 7147, the Department of Homeland Security Appropriations Act, 2026. With the passage of this bill, along with H.R. 7148, the Consolidated Appropriations Act, 2026, the House completed its work on government funding for the fiscal year. Homeland Security Subcommittee Chairman Mark Amodei issued the following statement after its passage in the House of Representatives:“When we look back to a year ago and the disaster at the border the Trump Administration inherited, it’s clear the voices of the American people were taken seriously when they went to the ballot box with the hope of more secure borders, streets free of drugs and violent criminals, and the peace of mind that comes with safer communities,” said Chairman Mark Amodei. “This funding addresses every aspect of our national security where the United States could be vulnerable. It strengthens protections across air, land, maritime, and emerging cyber domains, while supporting innovation, training, and modern technologies needed to stay ahead of bad actors and adversaries.“It’s also fiscally responsible, saving taxpayer dollars by cutting programs and offices that pursue missions unrelated to security of the homeland and refocusing resources on initiatives that truly keep Americans safe.“The road to restoring regular order was not an easy one, but Chairman Cole’s leadership and commitment to the process brought us to this point. I want to thank my colleagues on the committee and the subcommittee staff for their partnership and hard work in getting this across the finish line.”Key Takeaways:Enhances resources to detect and counter the spread of deadly drugs, like fentanyl, that poison our communities. Supports security preparation and planning for the 2026 FIFA World Cup, America250, the 2028 Summer Olympics and Paralympics, and other National Special Security Events. Funds the 2026 pay raise and avoids a Coast Guard recruiting pause.Sustains funding for 22,000 Border Patrol agents. Counters China by increasing the Coast Guard’s Indo-Pacific footprint. Bolsters custody operations to detain and deport all criminal and removable aliens. Improves baggage screening equipment at airports.Invests in unmanned systems to improve maritime domain awareness.Enables the staffing of critical positions at the Cybersecurity and Infrastructure Security Agency (CISA) to counter the threat from China. Eliminates handouts to non-governmental organizations that facilitated the Biden border crisis.\nIssues:\nBills I've Sponsored/Co-Sponsored","content_cn":"首页\n新闻稿\n阿莫迪主席的2026财年国土安全拨款法案在众议院获得通过\n图片\n2026年1月22日 新闻稿\n华盛顿特区——今天，众议院通过了H.R. 7147号法案，即《2026年国土安全部拨款法案》。随着该法案以及H.R. 7148号法案《2026年综合拨款法案》的通过，众议院完成了本财年政府拨款工作。国土安全小组委员会主席马克·阿莫迪在众议院通过该法案后发表以下声明：“当我们回顾一年前特朗普政府接手边境灾难时的情形，可以清楚地看到，美国人民在投票箱前表达的希望——更安全的边境、没有毒品和暴力罪犯的街道、以及更安全社区带来的安心——得到了认真对待，”马克·阿莫迪主席表示。“这项拨款涉及我们国家安全的方方面面，涵盖美国可能面临脆弱性的所有领域。它加强了空中、陆地、海上以及新兴网络领域的防护，同时支持保持领先于不法分子和对手所需的创新、培训和现代技术。“这项法案在财政上也是负责任的，通过削减那些从事与国土安全无关任务的项目和办公室来节省纳税人的钱，并将资源重新聚焦于真正保障美国人安全的举措上。“恢复常规秩序的道路并不容易，但科尔主席的领导和对这一进程的承诺使我们走到了今天。我要感谢委员会的同仁和小组委员会工作人员的合作与辛勤工作，使这项法案最终得以完成。”\n要点：\n加强资源以侦查和打击芬太尼等毒害我们社区的致命毒品的扩散。\n支持2026年国际足联世界杯、美国250周年、2028年夏季奥运会和残奥会以及其他国家特别安全活动的安保筹备和规划。\n为2026年加薪提供资金，并避免海岸警卫队招募暂停。\n维持22,000名边境巡逻人员的经费。\n通过扩大海岸警卫队在印太地区的存在来对抗中国。\n加强拘留行动，以拘留和驱逐所有犯罪外国人和可驱逐外国人。\n改善机场行李安检设备。\n投资无人系统以提高海域态势感知能力。\n使网络安全和基础设施安全局（CISA）能够配备关键职位人员，以应对来自中国的威胁。\n取消对协助拜登边境危机的非政府组织的资助。\n议题：\n我发起/共同发起的法案","publish_source":"amodei.house.gov","publish_time":"2026-01-22T17:52:36-05:00"}},{"id":"news-1615","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"阿莫代伊主席就国土安全监督听证会发表声明","title_en":"Chairman Amodei’s Statement on Homeland Security Oversight Hearing","summary_cn":"2026年2月12日，国土安全拨款小组委员会主席马克·阿莫代伊就前一日关于DHS停摆潜在影响的监督听证会发表声明。他称民主党人要求削弱内部移民执法，否则将关闭整个国土安全部，此举将危及海岸警卫队搜救、FEMA应急准备与灾后恢复、网络安全与通信等核心国家安全职能，并提及在汤姆·霍曼领导下明尼苏达州紧张局势已通过地方官员接触得以缓和。","summary_en":"On February 12, 2026, Homeland Security Appropriations Subcommittee Chairman Mark Amodei issued a statement after the previous day's oversight hearing on the potential impacts of a DHS shutdown. He said Democrats are demanding that Congress weaken interior immigration enforcement or risk shutting down the entire department, which would put at risk core national security functions including Coast Guard search-and-rescue, FEMA preparedness and disaster recovery, and cybersecurity and communications, and noted that tensions in Minnesota were deescalated under Tom Homan's leadership.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-18T15:32:17.972810+00:00","url":"http://amodei.house.gov/news-releases/chairman-amodeis-statement-homeland-security-oversight-hearing","content":"Home\nNews Releases\nChairman Amodei’s Statement on Homeland Security Oversight Hearing\nImage\nFebruary 12, 2026 Press Release\nWashington, D.C. – Homeland Security Appropriations Subcommittee Chairman Mark Amodei released the following statement following yesterday’s oversight hearing on the potential impacts of a DHS shutdown:“Under the leadership of Chuck Schumer, progressive Democrats are now demanding that Congress weaken interior immigration enforcement or risk shutting down the entire Department of Homeland Security,” said Chairman Mark Amodei.“If you think that’s acceptable because you oppose ICE or Border Patrol operations, it’s worth remembering that DHS funds far more than immigration enforcement. Threatening to shut it down puts core national security functions at risk.“The Coast Guard, which carries out critical maritime search-and-rescue missions, would be sidelined. FEMA’s emergency preparedness and disaster recovery efforts would be delayed and disrupted, even as states across the country are still dealing with historic winter weather. At a time of heightened global tensions, DHS cybersecurity and communications capabilities would shift from proactive to reactive defense. During the last shutdown, Americans saw firsthand what happens when TSA operations are disrupted: longer wait times, widespread flight cancellations, and unnecessary chaos. Some lawmakers are apparently willing to see that happen again. “None of these consequences have anything to do with immigration enforcement.“While I’ve previously said ICE needs to refocus on its core mission, that pivot is already underway. Under Tom Homan’s leadership, tensions in Minnesota were successfully deescalated through engagement with local officials, leading to the conclusion of surge operations in the state and the deployment of body cameras for personnel remaining on the ground.“It’s also important to note that ICE still has resources funded in the One Big Beautiful Bill if the third shutdown in less than 100 days takes place. At the same time, a continuing resolution does little to resolve the issue, as it keeps funding at FY25 levels, which are actually higher than what’s proposed for FY26.“Policy disagreements are not the responsibility of the appropriations process; rather, they should be taken up with the authorizing committees. I urge my colleagues on the other side of the aisle to reflect on the lessons of the longest government shutdown in history, which proved it accomplishes nothing.”Watch the full hearing here. Read Chairman Amodei’s full remarks here.","content_cn":"首页\n新闻稿\n阿莫迪主席关于国土安全监督听证会的声明\n图片\n2026年2月12日 新闻稿\n华盛顿特区——国土安全拨款小组委员会主席马克·阿莫迪在昨日就国土安全部停摆潜在影响举行的监督听证会后发表以下声明：“在查克·舒默的领导下，进步派民主党人现在要求国会削弱内部移民执法，否则就要冒着让整个国土安全部停摆的风险，”主席马克·阿莫迪表示。“如果你因为反对移民和海关执法局或边境巡逻队的行动而认为这是可以接受的，那么值得记住的是，国土安全部资助的远不止移民执法。威胁让其停摆会使核心国家安全职能面临风险。“负责执行关键海上搜救任务的海岸警卫队将被搁置。联邦紧急事务管理局的应急准备和灾后恢复工作将被延误和中断，而全国各州仍在应对历史性的冬季天气。在全球紧张局势加剧之际，国土安全部的网络安全和通信能力将从主动防御转向被动防御。在上一次停摆期间，美国人亲眼目睹了运输安全管理局运作中断时会发生什么：更长的等待时间、大范围的航班取消以及不必要的混乱。一些议员显然愿意看到这种情况再次发生。“这些后果都与移民执法毫无关系。“虽然我之前说过移民和海关执法局需要重新聚焦其核心使命，但这一转变已经在进行中。在汤姆·霍曼的领导下，通过与地方官员接触，明尼苏达州的紧张局势成功降级，导致该州的增援行动结束，并为留在当地的人员部署了随身摄像头。“同样重要的是要注意，如果不到100天内发生第三次停摆，移民和海关执法局在《一项大而美的法案》中仍有资金保障。与此同时，持续决议对解决问题几乎没有帮助，因为它将资金维持在2025财年水平，而这实际上高于2026财年的拟议水平。“政策分歧不是拨款程序的责任；相反，它们应该提交给授权委员会处理。我敦促对岸的同事们反思历史上最长政府停摆的教训，那次停摆证明它一事无成。”在此观看完整听证会。在此阅读阿莫迪主席的完整讲话。","publish_source":"amodei.house.gov","publish_time":"2026-02-12T12:35:21-05:00"}},{"id":"news-753","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"众议院拨款委员会通过阿莫迪主导的2027财年国土安全拨款法案","title_en":"ICYMI: Against the Odds, Amodei Guides Homeland Security Bill Through Committee","summary_cn":"2026年6月12日，众议院拨款委员会以34票对27票通过国土安全小组委员会主席阿莫迪提出的2027财年国土安全拨款法案。法案为国土安全部提供649亿美元可自由支配拨款，重点加强边境安全、移民执法、打击芬太尼、保护儿童免受剥削、灾害应对，并为2028年奥运会安保做准备，同时禁止资助DEI项目。","summary_en":"On June 12, 2026, the House Appropriations Committee approved the FY27 Homeland Security Appropriations Bill led by Subcommittee Chairman Amodei by a vote of 34 to 27. The bill provides $64.9 billion in discretionary funding for DHS, focusing on border security, immigration enforcement, countering fentanyl, protecting children from exploitation, disaster response, and security for the 2028 Olympics, while prohibiting DEI funding.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-18T14:18:17.885069+00:00","url":"http://amodei.house.gov/news-releases/icymi-against-odds-amodei-guides-homeland-security-bill-through-committee","content":"Home\nNews Releases\nICYMI: Against the Odds, Amodei Guides Homeland Security Bill Through Committee\nImage\nJune 12, 2026 Press Release\nWashington, D.C. – This week, the House Appropriations Committee approved Subcommittee Chairman Amodei’s FY27 Homeland Security Appropriations Bill, delivering a hard-fought victory during one of the most pivotal and politically contentious periods in the Department’s history. Rep. Mark Amodei has served on the House Appropriations Committee since the 114th Congress in 2015. After chairing the Legislative Branch Subcommittee during the 118th Congress, he assumed leadership of the Homeland Security Subcommittee in the 119th Congress. Taking the gavel amid the Biden Administration’s border crisis, Amodei has worked to strengthen border security and ensure the Department has the resources needed to support the current administration’s enforcement and homeland security priorities.“First, I’d like to thank each member of this subcommittee for working together to deliver a bill that embodies responsible legislating,” said Homeland Security Subcommittee Chairman Mark Amodei. “We all know the importance of this agency and the work it does every day to secure our homeland. While it has been no easy feat to chair a subcommittee in such a polarized environment, this bill was drafted with a deliberate focus on building upon investments that have strengthened our capabilities while ensuring resources are directed where they are needed most. “At its core, this bill maintains our strong posture on immigration enforcement, expands the use of technology to detect and stop deadly drugs from entering our communities, provides resources to investigate and protect victims of exploitation and human trafficking, streamlines preparedness and security efforts for upcoming and major national events, modernizes maritime operations, strengthens disaster response efforts, and helps deter ongoing aggression generated by nation-state adversaries. “It has been an absolute honor to serve as a cardinal on the Appropriations Committee. I am proud of what we have accomplished over the years, especially our diligence to restore regular order and bring fiscal sanity back to the appropriations process under Chairman Cole’s leadership. While you can never say mission accomplished in this business, I feel incredibly grateful to be concluding my service with a strong proposal such as this and a deep appreciation for the colleagues and staff who make the work possible.” Quote of the week: “Though I walk through the valley of the shadow of death, I will fear no evil.”  Fiscal Year 2027 Homeland Security Appropriations ActThe Homeland Security Appropriations Act provides a total discretionary allocation of $64.9 billion for the Department of Homeland Security (DHS), of which $2.9 billion is provided for defense activities. The bill also includes $6.2 billion in discretionary appropriations that are offset by fee collections and $28.39 billion as an allocation adjustment for major disaster response and recovery activities.The legislation includes the resources required to protect the homeland and keep American communities safe, secure, and resilient. The bill provides the necessary personnel, training, and technology to secure our air, land, and maritime borders and the nation’s critical infrastructure against nation-state adversaries.The measure was approved by the Committee with a vote of 34 to 27.  Key TakeawaysChampions public safety and homeland preparedness by: Upholding the America First vision by realigning DHS priorities around its fundamental mission: defending the nation against the threat posed by terrorists, criminals, and foreign adversaries to ensure the safety and security of every American.Enhancing resources to detect and counter the spread of deadly drugs, like fentanyl, that poison our communities.Partnering with state and local law enforcement to enhance immigration enforcement and homeland defense capabilities.Protecting vulnerable children by strengthening investigations of exploitation, human trafficking, and forced labor.Bolstering disaster preparedness, response, and recovery efforts for U.S. communities through increased grant funding for firefighters and first responders.Supporting security preparation and planning for the 2028 Summer Olympics and Paralympics, and other National Special Security Events.Supports the Trump Administration and mandate of the American people by: Enhancing the operational execution of Public Law 119-21, which prioritizes security and safety through long-term border security and immigration investments.Funding the military pay raise for Coast Guard servicemembers.Prohibiting funding for Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion (DEI) efforts.Ensuring no funding to non-governmental organizations that facilitated the Biden border crisis.Codifying the Trump Administration’s reductions to bloated federal bureaucracy.Bolsters U.S. national security and border protections by: Providing $3.8 billion for ICE custody operations to strengthen the Trump Administration’s efforts to detain and deport all criminal and removable aliens.Providing $439 million to sustain 22,000 Border Patrol agents.Providing $226 million to improve baggage screening equipment at airports.Providing $135 million to counter China by increasing the Coast Guard’s Indo-Pacific footprint.Providing $97 million for unmanned systems to improve maritime domain awareness.Safeguards American taxpayer dollars and preserves core functions by: Reallocating $100 million from previous appropriations to sustain the Cybersecurity and Infrastructure Security Agency’s (CISA) core mission functions.A summary of the bill is available here.\nIssues:\nBills I've Sponsored/Co-Sponsored","content_cn":"首页\n新闻稿\n【重要消息回顾】逆势而上，阿莫迪推动国土安全拨款法案通过委员会审议\n图片\n2026年6月12日 新闻稿\n华盛顿特区——本周，众议院拨款委员会批准了小组委员会主席阿莫迪提出的2027财年国土安全拨款法案，在该部门历史上最关键、政治争议最激烈的时期之一取得了一场来之不易的胜利。马克·阿莫迪众议员自2015年第114届国会起一直任职于众议院拨款委员会。在第118届国会担任立法分支小组委员会主席后，他在第119届国会接掌国土安全小组委员会的领导权。在拜登政府边境危机期间接过主席槌，阿莫迪一直致力于加强边境安全，并确保该部门拥有支持现任政府执法和国土安全优先事项所需的资源。“首先，我要感谢本小组委员会的每一位成员共同努力，提交了一份体现负责任立法的法案，”国土安全小组委员会主席马克·阿莫迪表示。“我们都清楚这个机构的重要性，以及它每天为保卫我们的国土所做的工作。在如此两极分化的环境中担任小组委员会主席绝非易事，但这份法案在起草时有意聚焦于在已加强我们能力的投资基础上再接再厉，同时确保资源投向最需要的地方。“从根本上说，这份法案维持了我们在移民执法方面的强硬姿态，扩大了利用技术侦查和阻止致命毒品进入我们社区的范围，为调查和保护剥削及人口贩运受害者提供了资源，简化了即将举行和重大全国性活动的筹备与安保工作，实现了海上行动的现代化，加强了灾难应对工作，并有助于遏制民族国家对手持续不断的侵略行为。“能够担任拨款委员会的‘核心成员’（cardinal），我深感荣幸。我为我们多年来取得的成就感到自豪，尤其是我们在科尔主席领导下为恢复常规秩序、让拨款程序回归财政理性所做的努力。在这个行当里，你永远不能说‘任务完成’，但能在结束我的任期时提出这样一份强有力的提案，并对使这项工作得以实现的同事和工作人员深怀感激，我感到无比感恩。”本周金句：“我虽然行过死荫的幽谷，也不怕遭害。”2027财年国土安全拨款法案国土安全拨款法案为国土安全部（DHS）提供了总额649亿美元的可自由裁量拨款，其中29亿美元用于国防活动。该法案还包括62亿美元由收费收入抵消的可自由裁量拨款，以及283.9亿美元用于重大灾难应对和恢复活动的拨款调整。该立法包含保护国土、保障美国社区安全、稳固和具有韧性所需的资源。法案提供了必要的人员、培训和技术，以保卫我们的空中、陆地和海上边界以及国家关键基础设施，抵御民族国家对手。该法案以34票对27票获得委员会批准。主要内容要点捍卫公共安全和国土准备工作，具体包括：坚持“美国优先”愿景，围绕国土安全部的根本使命重新调整其优先事项：保卫国家免受恐怖分子、犯罪分子和外国对手构成的威胁，确保每一位美国人的安全与保障。加强资源以侦查和打击芬太尼等毒害我们社区的致命毒品扩散。与州和地方执法部门合作，加强移民执法和国土防御能力。通过加强针对剥削、人口贩运和强迫劳动的调查来保护弱势儿童。通过增加对消防员和急救人员的拨款，加强美国社区的灾难准备、应对和恢复工作。支持2028年夏季奥运会和残奥会以及其他国家特别安全活动的安保筹备和规划。支持特朗普政府和美国人民的授权，具体包括：加强第119-21号公法的执行，该法通过长期边境安全和移民投资优先保障安全与安保。为海岸警卫队军人的军饷上调提供资金。禁止为多元化、公平和包容（DEI）工作提供资金。确保不向协助拜登边境危机的非政府组织提供任何资金。将特朗普政府对臃肿联邦官僚机构的削减编入法律。加强美国国家安全和边境保护，具体包括：为移民和海关执法局（ICE）拘留行动提供38亿美元，以加强特朗普政府拘留和驱逐所有犯罪及可驱逐外国人的努力。提供4.39亿美元以维持22,000名边境巡逻人员。提供2.26亿美元用于改善机场行李安检设备。提供1.35亿美元用于通过扩大海岸警卫队在印太地区的存在来对抗中国。提供9,700万美元用于无人系统，以提升海上态势感知能力。守护美国纳税人资金并保留核心职能，具体包括：从先前拨款中重新调配1亿美元，以维持网络安全和基础设施安全局（CISA）的核心使命职能。法案摘要可在此处查阅。\n议题：\n我发起/共同发起的法案","publish_source":"amodei.house.gov","publish_time":"2026-06-12T13:10:55-04:00"}},{"id":"news-814","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"阿莫迪、科尔出席2027财年国土安全小组委员会审议","title_en":"Amodei, Cole at FY27 Homeland Security Subcommittee Markup","summary_cn":"2026年6月5日，众议院拨款委员会国土安全小组委员会审议2027财年法案并获通过。小组委员会主席阿莫迪表示，法案全额资助2.2万名边境巡逻人员，维持4.15万张拘留床位，为DHS执法人员提供4000万美元随身摄像头资金，并为海岸警卫队增加印太地区存在以应对中国。","summary_en":"On June 5, 2026, the House Appropriations Homeland Security Subcommittee met to consider its FY27 bill, which was approved. Subcommittee Chairman Amodei said the bill fully funds 22,000 Border Patrol agents, maintains 41,500 detention beds, provides $40 million for body-worn cameras for DHS law enforcement, and increases the Coast Guard's Indo-Pacific footprint to counter China.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-18T14:22:16.235908+00:00","url":"http://appropriations.house.gov/news/press-releases/amodei-cole-fy27-homeland-security-subcommittee-markup","content":"Home\nNews\nPress Releases\nAmodei, Cole at FY27 Homeland Security Subcommittee Markup\nJune 5, 2026 Press Release\nWashington, D.C. – Today, the House Appropriations Homeland Security Subcommittee met to consider its Fiscal Year 2027 bill. The measure was approved by the Subcommittee.\nImage\nHomeland Security Subcommittee Chairman Mark Amodei (R-NV), in prepared remarks, said, \"In terms of the details in this bill, it takes into account the substantial one-time investment of nearly $191 billion in the first reconciliation package and does not duplicate those funding decisions, but instead focuses on base requirements such as: fully funding 22,000 Border Patrol Agents, maintaining 41,500 detention beds – so that ICE can fulfill the Administration’s priority of detaining and deporting all criminal and removable aliens, and providing $40 million for body-worn cameras for DHS law enforcement personnel – double last year’s level. We build on investments in Fiscal Year 2026 by providing the Coast Guard increases of: $135 million to counter China by increasing the Coast Guard’s Indo-Pacific footprint, $48 million for overdue facility maintenance, and $45 million for maintenance shortfalls... In short, this bill ensures that we fund the core mission of the Department – protecting the Homeland.\"Full remarks, as prepared for delivery, are available here.\nImage\nChairman Tom Cole (R-OK) said, \"The power of the purse carries with it an obligation to govern – and this Fiscal Year 2027 bill reflects that responsibility. This legislation funds every core mission of DHS. It strengthens border security, supports immigration enforcement, and combats fentanyl and other illicit drugs. It reinforces the Trump Administration's efforts that have helped restore operational control of the border – while ensuring the personnel, technology, and resources are in place to sustain that success. This includes funding to sustain 22,000 Border Patrol Agents and support for needed ICE detention beds, and it doubles the resources for body-worn cameras for DHS personnel we provided last year. Additionally, the bill enhances America's posture in the Indo-Pacific by providing increased resources for Coast Guard operations to counter China and other adversaries.  Investments in maritime domain awareness, unmanned systems, technology modernization, and an expanded Coast Guard presence in the region help safeguard critical waterways, support allies and partners, and advance U.S. national security interests. The measure also bolsters our cyber defenses by refocusing resources on protecting federal networks and critical infrastructure from increasingly sophisticated threats posed by nation-state adversaries and criminals.\" Full remarks, as prepared for delivery, are available here.\nImage\nA summary of the bill is available here.Bill text is available here. ###","content_cn":"首页\n新闻\n新闻稿\n阿莫迪、科尔在2027财年国土安全小组委员会审定会上\n2026年6月5日 新闻稿\n华盛顿特区——今天，众议院拨款委员会国土安全小组委员会召开会议，审议其2027财年法案。该法案获得小组委员会批准。\n图片\n国土安全小组委员会主席马克·阿莫迪（内华达州共和党人）在准备好的发言中表示：“就这份法案的细节而言，它考虑到了第一个和解方案中近1,910亿美元的大规模一次性投资，并未重复这些拨款决定，而是聚焦于基本需求，例如：为22,000名边境巡逻人员提供全额资金，维持41,500张拘留床位——以便ICE能够履行本届政府拘留和驱逐所有犯罪及可驱逐外国人的优先事项，并为国土安全部执法人员的随身摄像头提供4,000万美元——是去年水平的两倍。我们在2026财年投资的基础上再接再厉，为海岸警卫队增加了：1.35亿美元用于通过扩大海岸警卫队在印太地区的存在来对抗中国，4,800万美元用于逾期设施维护，以及4,500万美元用于维护缺口……简而言之，这份法案确保我们为该部门的核心使命——保护国土——提供资金。”准备好的完整发言稿可在此处查阅。\n图片\n主席汤姆·科尔（俄克拉何马州共和党人）表示：“钱袋权伴随着治理的责任——这份2027财年法案体现了这一责任。这项立法为国土安全部的每一项核心使命提供资金。它加强了边境安全，支持移民执法，并打击芬太尼和其他非法毒品。它强化了特朗普政府的努力，这些努力帮助恢复了边境的行动控制——同时确保人员、技术和资源到位以维持这一成果。这包括维持22,000名边境巡逻人员的资金，支持所需的ICE拘留床位，并将我们去年为国土安全部人员提供的随身摄像头资源翻倍。此外，该法案通过为海岸警卫队行动提供更多资源以对抗中国和其他对手，增强了美国在印太地区的态势。对海上态势感知、无人系统、技术现代化以及扩大海岸警卫队在该地区存在的投资，有助于保护关键水道、支持盟友和伙伴，并推进美国国家安全利益。该法案还通过将资源重新聚焦于保护联邦网络和关键基础设施免受民族国家对手和犯罪分子日益复杂的威胁，加强了我们的网络防御。”准备好的完整发言稿可在此处查阅。\n图片\n法案摘要可在此处查阅。法案文本可在此处查阅。###","publish_source":"appropriations.house.gov","publish_time":"2026-06-05T10:41:40-04:00"}},{"id":"news-771","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"委员会通过2027财年国土安全拨款法案","title_en":"Committee Approves FY27 Homeland Security Appropriations Act","summary_cn":"2026年6月11日，众议院拨款委员会以34票对27票通过2027财年国土安全拨款法案。法案为国土安全部提供649亿美元，加强边境安全、移民执法、网络安全和灾害应对，并为海岸警卫队增加印太地区资源以应对中国。委员会还否决了多项民主党修正案。","summary_en":"On June 11, 2026, the House Appropriations Committee approved the FY27 Homeland Security Appropriations Act by a vote of 34 to 27. The bill provides $64.9 billion for DHS, strengthening border security, immigration enforcement, cybersecurity, and disaster response, and increases Coast Guard resources in the Indo-Pacific to counter China. The committee also rejected several Democratic amendments.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-18T14:19:05.806480+00:00","url":"http://appropriations.house.gov/news/press-releases/committee-approves-fy27-homeland-security-appropriations-act","content":"Home\nNews\nPress Releases\nCommittee Approves FY27 Homeland Security Appropriations Act\nJune 11, 2026 Press Release\nWashington, D.C. – Today, the House Appropriations Committee met to consider the Fiscal Year 2027 Homeland Security Appropriations Act. The measure was approved by the Committee with a vote of 34 to 27.\nImage\nHomeland Security Subcommittee Chairman Mark Amodei (R-NV) said, \"First, I’d like to thank each member of this subcommittee for working together to deliver a bill that embodies responsible legislating. We all know the importance of this agency and the work it does every day to secure our homeland. While it has been no easy feat to chair a subcommittee in such a polarized environment, this bill was drafted with a deliberate focus on building upon investments that have strengthened our capabilities while ensuring resources are directed where they are needed most. \"At its core, this bill maintains our strong posture on immigration enforcement, expands the use of technology to detect and stop deadly drugs from entering our communities, provides resources to investigate and protect victims of exploitation and human trafficking, streamlines preparedness and security efforts for upcoming and major national events, modernizes maritime operations, strengthens disaster response efforts, and helps deter ongoing aggression generated by nation-state adversaries. \"It has been an absolute honor to serve as a cardinal on the Appropriations Committee. I am proud of what we have accomplished over the years, especially our diligence to restore regular order and bring fiscal sanity back to the appropriations process under Chairman Cole’s leadership. While you can never say mission accomplished in this business, I feel incredibly grateful to be concluding my service with a strong proposal such as this and a deep appreciation for the colleagues and staff who make the work possible.\"\nImage\nChairman Tom Cole (R-OK) said, \"Securing the homeland and protecting the American people is among the federal government's most fundamental responsibilities. The just-reported FY27 Homeland Security bill provides the personnel, technology, and resources necessary to secure our borders, enforce our laws, combat illicit drug trafficking, strengthen cybersecurity defenses, and bolster disaster preparedness and recovery efforts. This legislation takes a comprehensive approach to the threats facing our nation. It builds on the Trump Administration's success in restoring operational control of the border, supports the frontline personnel who carry out critical homeland security missions every day, strengthens Coast Guard capabilities, and enhances our ability to confront challenges whether they emerge at our borders, in cyberspace, on our shores, or in communities across the country. From transnational criminal organizations and cyberattacks to natural disasters and emerging security threats, this bill ensures America is prepared. I commend Chairman Amodei for his leadership in developing this measure and guiding it through the appropriations process. As the final appropriations bill he will lead in Congress, it reflects the steady judgment, practical leadership, and commitment to mission that have defined his service. The result is a stronger, more capable homeland security enterprise prepared to meet the challenges of today and tomorrow.\" Subcommittee Chairman Amodei's opening remarks are available here.Chairman Cole's opening remarks are available here.\nImage\nFiscal Year 2027 Homeland Security Appropriations ActThe Homeland Security Appropriations Act provides a total discretionary allocation of $64.9 billion for the Department of Homeland Security (DHS), of which $2.9 billion is provided for defense activities. The bill also includes $6.2 billion in discretionary appropriations that are offset by fee collections and $28.39 billion as an allocation adjustment for major disaster response and recovery activities.The legislation includes the resources required to protect the homeland and keep American communities safe, secure, and resilient. The bill provides the necessary personnel, training, and technology to secure our air, land, and maritime borders and the nation’s critical infrastructure against nation-state adversaries.Key TakeawaysChampions public safety and homeland preparedness by: Upholding the America First vision by realigning DHS priorities around its fundamental mission: defending the nation against the threat posed by terrorists, criminals, and foreign adversaries to ensure the safety and security of every American.Enhancing resources to detect and counter the spread of deadly drugs, like fentanyl, that poison our communities.Partnering with state and local law enforcement to enhance immigration enforcement and homeland defense capabilities.Protecting vulnerable children by strengthening investigations of exploitation, human trafficking, and forced labor.Bolstering disaster preparedness, response, and recovery efforts for U.S. communities through increased grant funding for firefighters and first responders.Supporting security preparation and planning for the 2028 Summer Olympics and Paralympics, and other National Special Security Events.Supports the Trump Administration and mandate of the American people by: Enhancing the operational execution of Public Law 119-21, which prioritizes security and safety through long-term border security and immigration investments.Funding the military pay raise for Coast Guard servicemembers.Prohibiting funding for Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion (DEI) efforts.Ensuring no funding to non-governmental organizations that facilitated the Biden border crisis.Codifying the Trump Administration’s reductions to bloated federal bureaucracy.Bolsters U.S. national security and border protections by: Providing $3.8 billion for ICE custody operations to strengthen the Trump Administration’s efforts to detain and deport all criminal and removable aliens.Providing $439 million to sustain 22,000 Border Patrol agents.Providing $226 million to improve baggage screening equipment at airports.Providing $135 million to counter China by increasing the Coast Guard’s Indo-Pacific footprint.Providing $97 million for unmanned systems to improve maritime domain awareness.Safeguards American taxpayer dollars and preserves core functions by: Reallocating $100 million from previous appropriations to sustain the Cybersecurity and Infrastructure Security Agency’s (CISA) core mission functions.A summary of the bill is available here.During the markup, Committee Republicans also stood with the America First agenda and rejected Democrat amendments that would have:  Attempted to over-resource an office beyond operational need.Weakened physical border security infrastructure.Restricted CBP and ICE authorities.Obstructed reforms to modernize grant rules.Sought to impose limitations on homeland security funding Democrats previously opposed.Hindered law enforcement's ability to arrest or detain criminals.Enabled Democrats to rescind funding they never supported and reallocate it to their priorities.Promoted mass migration in the United States. Restricted DHS’s ability to protect communities using common law-enforcement tools.Mandated a partisan-focused report unrelated to DHS’s core mission.Expanded bureaucracy and regulations to address nonexistent problems.Made it harder to enforce America’s federal immigration laws.Weakened screening and vetting resources for inbound travelers and cargo transactions.Pushed pro-union policies on government workers.Undermined efforts to maintain adequate detention capacity through unnecessary location restrictions.Increased taxpayer spending without offsets.Adopted Amendments Amodei (Manager’s Amendment) – Makes technical, bipartisan changes to the bill and report. The amendment was adopted by voice vote.Clyde #1 – Protects free speech by blocking funding for government efforts to monitor or influence lawful speech. The amendment was adopted by voice vote.Frankel #1 – Prohibits funding provided in the amendment for third-country removals without court approval; the amendment has no impact on any federal funding provided to ICE. The amendment was adopted by voice vote.Escobar #5 – Requires findings of an ongoing investigation to be submitted to the committee. The amendment was adopted by voice vote.Escobar #6 – Allows for the recouperation of certain charges at an ICE facility. The amendment was adopted by voice vote.Bill text, before adoption of amendments, is available here.Bill report, before adoption of amendments, is available here.A table of included Community Project Funding requests is available here.  ###","content_cn":"首页\n新闻\n新闻稿\n委员会批准FY27国土安全拨款法案\n2026年6月11日 新闻稿\n华盛顿特区——今天，众议院拨款委员会召开会议，审议2027财年国土安全拨款法案。该法案以34票对27票获得委员会批准。\n图片\n国土安全小组委员会主席马克·阿莫迪（内华达州共和党人）表示：“首先，我要感谢本小组委员会的每一位成员共同努力，提交了一份体现负责任立法的法案。我们都清楚这个机构的重要性，以及它每天为保卫我们的国土所做的工作。虽然在如此两极分化的环境中担任小组委员会主席绝非易事，但这份法案在起草时特意着眼于在已加强我们能力的投资基础上再接再厉，同时确保资源被投向最需要的地方。“从根本上说，这份法案维持了我们在移民执法方面的强硬姿态，扩大了利用技术来侦查和阻止致命毒品进入我们社区的工作，提供了调查和保护剥削与人口贩运受害者的资源，简化了即将到来的重大全国性活动的筹备和安保工作，实现了海上行动的现代化，加强了灾难应对工作，并有助于遏制民族国家对手持续制造的侵略行为。“能够担任拨款委员会的一名小组委员会主席，我深感荣幸。我为多年来我们取得的成就感到自豪，尤其是我们在科尔主席领导下为恢复常规秩序、让拨款程序回归财政理性所付出的勤勉努力。虽然在这个行当里你永远不能说‘任务完成’，但我无比感激能以这样一份强有力的提案结束我的任期，也深深感谢让这项工作得以实现的同事和工作人员。”\n图片\n主席汤姆·科尔（俄克拉何马州共和党人）表示：“保卫国土、保护美国人民是联邦政府最基本的职责之一。刚刚报告的FY27国土安全法案提供了必要的人员、技术和资源，以保卫我们的边境、执行我们的法律、打击非法毒品贩运、加强网络安全防御，并增强灾难准备和恢复工作。这项立法对我们国家面临的威胁采取了全面的应对方式。它建立在特朗普政府成功恢复边境行动控制的基础上，支持每天执行关键国土安全任务的一线人员，加强海岸警卫队的能力，并提升我们应对挑战的能力——无论这些挑战出现在我们的边境、网络空间、我们的海岸，还是全国各地的社区。从跨国犯罪组织和网络攻击，到自然灾害和新出现的安全威胁，这份法案确保美国做好准备。我赞扬阿莫迪主席在制定这项法案并引导其通过拨款程序方面展现的领导力。作为他将在国会领导的最后一份拨款法案，它体现了一贯的稳健判断、务实领导和对使命的承诺，这些正是他任职期间的写照。其结果是打造一个更强大、更有能力的国土安全体系，准备好迎接今天和明天的挑战。”阿莫迪小组委员会主席的开场发言可在此处查阅。科尔主席的开场发言可在此处查阅。\n图片\n2027财年国土安全拨款法案国土安全拨款法案为国土安全部（DHS）提供了总计649亿美元的可自由支配拨款，其中29亿美元用于国防活动。该法案还包括62亿美元由收费收入抵消的可自由支配拨款，以及283.9亿美元用于重大灾难应对和恢复活动的拨款调整。该立法包含保护国土、保障美国社区安全、稳固和具有韧性所需的资源。该法案提供了必要的人员、培训和技术，以保卫我们的空中、陆地和海上边境以及国家关键基础设施，抵御民族国家对手。要点通过以下方式捍卫公共安全和国土准备工作：坚持“美国优先”愿景，围绕国土安全部的根本使命重新调整其优先事项：保卫国家免受恐怖分子、罪犯和外国对手构成的威胁，以确保每一位美国人的安全与保障。加强资源以侦查和打击芬太尼等毒害我们社区的致命毒品的扩散。与州和地方执法部门合作，加强移民执法和国土防御能力。通过加强对剥削、人口贩运和强迫劳动的调查来保护弱势儿童。通过增加对消防员和急救人员的拨款，加强美国社区的灾难准备、应对和恢复工作。支持2028年夏季奥运会和残奥会以及其他国家特别安全活动的安保筹备和规划。通过以下方式支持特朗普政府和美国人民的授权：加强第119-21号公法的执行，该法通过长期边境安全和移民投资来优先保障安全与安保。为海岸警卫队军人的军饷加薪提供资金。禁止为多样性、公平和包容（DEI）工作提供资金。确保不向协助拜登边境危机的非政府组织提供任何资金。将特朗普政府对臃肿联邦官僚机构的削减编入法律。通过以下方式加强美国国家安全和边境保护：提供38亿美元用于移民和海关执法局（ICE）的拘留行动，以加强特朗普政府拘留和驱逐所有犯罪和可驱逐外国人的努力。提供4.39亿美元\n[正文过长，翻译截断；对象库保留全文]","publish_source":"appropriations.house.gov","publish_time":"2026-06-11T00:37:45-04:00"}},{"id":"news-1472","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"民主党导致国土安全部停摆，在关键时刻削弱国土安全","title_en":"Democrat DHS Shutdown Undermines Homeland Security at Critical Moment","summary_cn":"美国众议院拨款委员会新闻稿称，民主党导致国土安全部停摆近三周，限制其保护美国人的能力。文中提及奥斯汀枪击案、伊朗相关威胁、未审查移民及恐怖观察名单人员等问题，并引用主席汤姆·科尔批评民主党将政治置于安全之上，呼吁通过两党拨款协议恢复国土安全部全面运作。","summary_en":"A House Appropriations press release says Democrats' shutdown of the Department of Homeland Security, nearly three weeks old, limits the department's ability to protect Americans. It cites the Austin shooting, Iran-related threats, unvetted immigrants and terror watch-list cases, and quotes Chairman Tom Cole urging passage of the bipartisan funding deal to fully fund DHS.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-24T20:34:16.824649+00:00","url":"http://appropriations.house.gov/news/press-releases/democrat-dhs-shutdown-undermines-homeland-security-critical-moment","content":"Home\nNews\nPress Releases\nDemocrat DHS Shutdown Undermines Homeland Security at Critical Moment\nMarch 4, 2026 Press Release\nWashington, D.C. – Nearly three weeks into the Democrats’ shutdown of the Department of Homeland Security, the American people are facing an evolving threat environment. Democrats must agree to the bipartisan, bicameral funding agreement they helped negotiate in January.Senate Democrats irresponsibly shut down DHS, knowingly limiting the capabilities of the department responsible for protecting Americans from dangerous individuals.The attack in Austin, TX, over the weekend underscores the need for our homeland security teams to be fully funded and functioning. In what is being investigated as a potential lone-wolf terror attack, a Senegalese immigrant – seemingly motivated by support for the murderous regime in Iran – opened fire on a bar in Austin, killing multiple Americans.\nImage\nFollowing President Trump’s successful strike on Iran, terrorist allies already inside our borders are likely seeking openings to retaliate. Democrats’ refusal to fully fund DHS is reckless, increasing the danger to every American.The threat environment is not theoretical. Millions of unvetted, illegal immigrants released under the Biden Administration remain in our communities, along with an estimated 2 million known “gotaways.” Nearly 400 individuals on the terror watch list were caught trying to enter our country illegally during the Biden Administration – and those are just the ones we know about. Violent gangs like MS-13 and Tren de Aragua, as well as Taliban terrorists released from Afghan prisons, are present inside the United States. Chairman Tom Cole (R-OK) said, “Once again, Democrats have chosen political games over the safety of the American people – and, as usual, their timing could not be worse. President Trump is delivering peace through strength abroad, but Democrats are undermining our defenses at home. This puts every American at risk. And for what? Shutdowns never work. It’s never a good idea to hold government funding hostage – for any reason. The first duty of government is to protect its citizens. My colleagues will have the opportunity this week to put senseless partisanship aside and do the responsible thing by funding DHS and ensuring safety for the American people. I hope they make the right choice.”\nImage\nThe safety of the American people is non-negotiable. At a time of rising global tensions, evolving terror threats, and severe weather at home, preparedness delayed is security denied.Democrats will have another opportunity this week to do the right thing, end the shutdown, and fully fund DHS with the bipartisan deal they already agreed to. It’s time to stop putting politics ahead of protection.The vote is simple: defend the homeland or deliberately defund it.\nImage\nBackground:Democrats previously agreed to a bipartisan, bicameral bill to fund DHS through the end of FY26, but turned their backs on that deal at the last minute, forcing a shutdown of DHS. They continue to hold critical security funding hostage over radical partisan demands that impede immigration enforcement. While CBP and ICE continue operations through supplemental funding provided in the OBBBA, critical agencies protecting Americans are operating at limited capacity: CISA: Iran is known for its targeting and hacking of U.S. critical infrastructure, such as water facilities. At a moment of heightened risk, CISA is operating at limited capacity. Democrats’ vote to defund CISA weakens our nation’s cyber defense agency and sets back emergency communications, risk assessments, and our ability to defend hospitals, energy grids, and more against attacks.Coast Guard: The Coast Guard, whose maritime search and rescue, port security, drug interdiction patrols, and other critical missions risk disruption. Further, Coastguardsmen and women – some of whom are in the direct line of fire in Bahrain due to the recent hostilities in Iran – deserve to know they have full resources and support behind them.Secret Service: Iran’s regime and its intelligence networks have a documented history of directing assassination plots and violent operations against U.S. interests – including a foiled plan to kill President Trump ahead of the 2024 election. Now is not the time to limit the agency charged with protecting our leaders and securing major national events. The Democrats’ shutdown is impacting security preparations that are already underway for America 250 celebrations, the FIFA World Cup, the 2028 LA Olympics, and more national events.TSA: Nobody wants another 9/11. TSA personnel stand on the frontlines of aviation security every day – keeping airports safe, secure, and moving. Yet, the same Democrat politicians voting against funding for these critical personnel rely on them to screen their flights back to Washington. Forcing TSA officers to work without pay erodes morale, strains staffing, increases the likelihood of long security lines and travel delays, and ultimately weakens the security posture millions of Americans depend on.FEMA: FEMA has substantially drawn down the Disaster Relief Fund in recent weeks. With operations already scaled back to bare-minimum, life-saving functions, further depletion of these critical resources jeopardizes preparedness, response, and recovery efforts just as additional and intense winter storms are on the horizon. Additionally, FEMA has halted almost all critical trainings for emergency managers across our communities, which undermines the nation’s ability to respond to disasters – whether natural or man-made.Homeland Security Investigations (HSI): This shutdown is hindering HSI, the department’s premier federal law enforcement agency, from carrying out its mission of investigating wide-ranging illicit activity such as drugs and weapons smuggling or cyber and financial crime. HSI leads the federal government in combating child exploitation and human trafficking.Air Traffic Controllers: Democrats are denying air traffic controllers a pay raise, which is included in this bill.H.R. 7744, the Homeland Security Appropriations Act, 2026 Bill SummaryCommunity Project Funding ###","content_cn":"主页\n新闻\n新闻稿\n民主党关闭国土安全部，在关键时刻削弱国土安全\n2026年3月4日 新闻稿\n华盛顿特区——民主党关闭国土安全部（DHS）已近三周之际，美国民众正面临不断变化的威胁环境。民主党必须同意他们在一月份参与谈判达成的两党、两院拨款协议。参议院民主党人不负责任地关闭DHS，明知这会限制该部门保护美国民众免受危险人员侵害的能力。\n周末发生在得克萨斯州奥斯汀市的袭击凸显了我们的国土安全团队获得充分资金并正常运转的必要性。这起事件正作为潜在的“独狼”恐怖袭击接受调查：一名塞内加尔移民似乎受到对伊朗杀人政权的支持所驱动，在奥斯汀一家酒吧开枪，导致多名美国人死亡。\n图片\n在特朗普总统成功打击伊朗之后，已经身处我国境内的恐怖分子盟友很可能正在寻找机会进行报复。民主党拒绝为DHS提供全部资金是不计后果的，增加了每一位美国人面临的危险。威胁环境并非理论上的。拜登政府时期获释的数百万未经审查的非法移民仍留在我们的社区中，此外还有估计200万名已知的“偷渡入境者”。拜登政府时期，近400名恐怖分子观察名单上的人员在试图非法进入我国时被捕——而这些只是我们知道的人。MS-13和特伦·德·阿拉瓜等暴力帮派，以及从阿富汗监狱获释的塔利班恐怖分子，都已进入美国境内。众议院拨款委员会主席汤姆·科尔（俄克拉何马州共和党）表示：“民主党再次把政治游戏置于美国人民的安全之上——而且像往常一样，他们选择的时机糟糕透顶。特朗普总统正在海外通过实力带来和平，但民主党正在削弱我们在国内的防御。这使每一位美国人都处于风险之中。而这是为了什么？关闭政府从来不起作用。以任何理由扣押政府资金都不是好主意。政府的首要职责是保护公民。本周，我的同事们将有机会把毫无意义的党派之争放在一边，通过为DHS提供资金并确保美国人民的安全来做负责任的事。我希望他们作出正确选择。”\n图片\n美国人民的安全不容谈判。在全球紧张局势加剧、恐怖威胁不断演变、国内恶劣天气频发之际，延误准备就意味着安全无保障。民主党本周还将有机会做正确的事，结束关闭，并通过他们已经同意的两党协议为DHS提供全部资金。是时候停止把政治置于保护之上了。投票很简单：保卫国土，还是蓄意削弱国土安全。\n图片\n背景：民主党此前同意一项两党、两院法案，为DHS提供资金至2026财年结束，但他们在最后一刻背弃了该协议，迫使DHS关闭。他们继续因阻碍移民执法的激进党派要求而扣押关键安全资金。尽管海关与边境保护局（CBP）和移民及海关执法局（ICE）继续通过《一项大而美丽的法案》（OBBBA）提供的补充资金开展行动，但保护美国民众的关键机构正以有限能力运作：网络安全与基础设施安全局（CISA）：伊朗被知晓曾针对并攻击美国关键基础设施，例如供水设施。在风险升高之际，CISA正以有限能力运作\n能力。民主党人投票取消对CISA的拨款，削弱了我国的网络防御机构，并使应急通信、风险评估以及我们保护医院、能源电网等免受攻击的能力倒退。\n\n海岸警卫队：海岸警卫队承担海上搜救、港口安保、缉毒巡逻及其他关键任务，这些任务面临中断风险。此外，海岸警卫队男女官兵——其中一些人因伊朗近期的敌对行动而身处巴林的直接火线——理应知道，他们身后有充足的资源和支持。\n\n特勤局：伊朗政权及其情报网络有策划暗杀阴谋和针对美国利益实施暴力行动的有据可查的历史——包括一项在2024年大选前刺杀特朗普总统但被挫败的计划。现在不是限制负责保护我国领导人和保障重大国家活动安全的机构的时候。民主党的政府停摆正在影响美国建国250周年庆祝活动、国际足联世界杯、2028年洛杉矶奥运会以及更多国家活动已经开展的安保准备工作。\n\n运输安全管理局（TSA）：没有人希望再发生一次9·11事件。TSA人员每天都站在航空安全的最前线——确保机场安全、可靠并顺畅运行。然而，那些投票反对为这些关键人员提供资金的民主党政客，却依赖他们为自己飞回华盛顿的航班进行安检。迫使TSA官员无薪工作会削弱士气、加剧人员配置压力，增加安检长队和旅行延误的可能性，并最终削弱数百万美国人所依赖的安全态势。\n\n联邦紧急事务管理局（FEMA）：近几周，FEMA大幅动用了灾害救济基金。在行动已经缩减至最低限度的救命职能之际，这些关键资源进一步减少，将危及准备、响应和恢复工作，而更多、更强烈的冬季风暴正即将来临。此外，FEMA已暂停社区应急管理人员几乎所有关键培训，这削弱了国家应对灾害的能力——无论是自然灾害还是人为灾害。\n\n国土安全调查局（HSI）：这次政府停摆阻碍了HSI——该部门首要的联邦执法机构——履行调查广泛非法活动的使命，例如毒品和武器走私、网络犯罪及金融犯罪。HSI在打击儿童剥削和人口贩运方面引领联邦政府。\n\n空中交通管制员：民主党人拒绝给空中交通管制员加薪，而本法案中已包含这项加薪。\n\nH.R. 7744，《2026年国土安全拨款法案》\n法案摘要\n社区项目拨款\n###","publish_source":"appropriations.house.gov","publish_time":"2026-03-04T12:10:26-05:00"}},{"id":"news-1620","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"面对现实：民主党人在国土安全部停摆前无视事实","title_en":"Facing Reality: Democrats Ignore the Facts Heading into a DHS Shutdown","summary_cn":"2026年2月11日，众议院国土安全拨款小组委员会就DHS潜在停摆影响举行听证会。主席阿莫代伊称，即便停摆，移民与遣返行动、边境墙建设及和解法案资助项目仍将继续，但海岸警卫队、TSA、网络安全与反恐、FEMA、执法培训等将受冲击。多位共和党议员指责参议院民主党领导层制造停摆，并强调DHS下辖22个机构、26万名雇员，停摆将危及公共安全。","summary_en":"On February 11, 2026, the House Homeland Security Appropriations Subcommittee held a hearing on the impacts of a potential DHS shutdown. Chairman Amodei said that even under a shutdown, immigration and removal operations, wall construction and reconciliation-funded programs would continue, while the Coast Guard, TSA, cybersecurity and counterterrorism, FEMA and law enforcement training would suffer. Several Republican members blamed Senate Democratic leadership for manufacturing the shutdown and stressed that DHS spans 22 agencies and 260,000 employees, warning of public safety risks.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-18T15:32:26.250613+00:00","url":"http://appropriations.house.gov/news/press-releases/facing-reality-democrats-ignore-facts-heading-dhs-shutdown","content":"Home\nNews\nPress Releases\nFacing Reality: Democrats Ignore the Facts Heading into a DHS Shutdown\nFebruary 11, 2026 Press Release\nWashington, D.C. – Today, the Homeland Security Subcommittee held a hearing on the impacts of a potential shutdown of the Department of Homeland Security (DHS). As it stands, funding is set to run out for DHS by the end of the week, and Democrats seem prepared to shut the government down, even though the bipartisan FY26 Homeland Security Appropriations Act already passed the House several weeks ago. A shutdown of DHS would not have the impact on immigration operations that Democrats hope it would – there is plenty of funding from last year's Big, Beautiful Bill specifically meant for immigration enforcement and construction of a border wall. However, many other agencies and programs under DHS will suffer should the government shut down, including: the Coast Guard, TSA, cybersecurity and counter-terrorism efforts, FEMA, law enforcement training, and more. Panelists from the Department of Homeland Security include: Admiral Thomas Allan, Vice Commandant, U.S. Coast GuardDr. Madhu Gottumukkala, Acting Director, Cybersecurity and Infrastructure Security AgencyHa Nguyen McNeil, Acting Administrator, Transportation Security AdministrationMatthew Quinn, Deputy Director, United States Secret ServiceGregg Phillips, Associate Administrator, Office of Response and Recovery, Federal Emergency Management Agency\nImage\nHomeland Security Subcommittee Chairman Mark Amodei (R-NV) highlighted in his opening statement the ineffectiveness of a shutdown to address the issues Democrats are concerned with, saying, \"If we shut down the Department over ICE and CBP enforcement actions in Minneapolis and my colleagues’ list of extreme policy demands, here is what will happen: immigration and removal operations will continue; wall construction will continue; and anything funded by reconciliation will continue. The good work the Department does outside of immigration enforcement will come to a screeching halt, and that’s what today’s hearing is all about.\"Read Chairman Amodei's full remarks here.\nImage\nChairman Tom Cole (R-OK) joined the hearing to address Democrats' abrupt abandonment of bipartisan negotiations, even after the bill passed the House with bipartisan votes. Chairman Cole said, \"I find [their] position difficult to reconcile with the facts. Neither a shutdown nor a continuing resolution enhances oversight – but our bipartisan, bicameral FY26 bill did. That final, full-year legislation was negotiated in good faith across chambers and parties. It included funding for body-worn cameras and de-escalation training, invested in FEMA and cybersecurity efforts, and upheld the missions of the Coast Guard and TSA. Our Homeland Security measure is not a single-issue bill. Treating it as such ignores the full scope of impacts before us – and abandons responsible governance. Further, these actions will not achieve the objectives Democrats claim to seek.\" Read Chairman Cole's full remarks here.\nImage\nRep. John Rutherford (R-FL) said, \"If there is a shutdown, it is a Senate Democrat leadership shutdown being manufactured. If your men and women are furloughed, if your men and women are forced to work without pay, it's because of the Senate leadership. No doubt about it. And today's meeting is about public safety that you all provide to this country day in and day out, and in the near future. Think about the responsibility that you all are going to have around all of the NSC events coming up with the FIFA World Cup, with all the America 250 events, and we're giving you fits and stops of funding.\"\nImage\nRep. Dan Newhouse (R-WA) said, \"Hearing what's truly at stake, members of Congress and members of the public need to have the information that you're going to be giving us... The things that we anticipate happening in the Senate ignore what is about to happen. And I, for one, 100% agree with you coming here to this hearing so that we know the impacts of the things that are truly being ignored.\"\nImage\nRep. Ashley Hinson (R-IA) said, \"I find it curious how some of my colleagues gloss over the fact that taxpayers were on the hook for billions and billions of dollars in soft-sided facilities to deal with a raging border crisis, which we have now reversed course on over the last four years and we are fixing the problems that were created by the previous administration... From the Coast Guard to TSA to CISA, these officers are showing up at work to do this job while going unpaid for weeks on end. I'm sure there's incredible unease and uncertainty amongst your staff as we head into Friday, and for that, I am sorry. We are trying to fix this problem here today.\"\nImage\nRep. Michael Guest (R-MS) said, \"As I sit here today, and I've listened to these witnesses and members of our side be lectured over the upcoming shutdown, a shutdown that we are trying to prevent, a shutdown that is driven by the Democrats in the Senate as they separated out DHS funding and then forced us to vote on a bill that only allowed funding to continue for two weeks, knowing that it was very likely we would end up right here in a government shutdown. You see, DHS funds more than just ICE. DHS pays the salary of 260,000 men and women over 22 different agencies... The men and women [at DHS] are just now digging out of the longest shutdown in government history that the Democrats forced us through in the Senate as they tried to attach unrelated legislation to a CR to keep the government funded.\"\nImage\nRep. Tony Gonzales (R-TX) said, \"We have major events happening. If there is a lapse in funding, if any votes against [funding DHS], it isn't a matter of just plain politics, which you often see up here. It's a matter of life and death. It's a matter of these drone attacks, they're happening all over the world. This isn't a 'what if', this isn't a video game, this isn't off in the near future. This is now... We're counting on FEMA, Department of War, and Department of Homeland Security to get that done.\"\nImage\nRep. Juan Ciscomani (R-AZ) said, \"Make no mistake, it's not hard to understand when we have continually, in the previous shutdown and obviously in the efforts with this one, voted to keep the government open and funded, and others are voting no on that. It's not more complicated than that... I want to say that I believe strongly that shutting down the government and agencies and departments over policy disagreements is completely inappropriate and reckless. I've never supported a shutdown, and if Congress does not pass DHS funding measures, the result will be critical services to the public, as we've heard, including disaster response, law enforcement, cybersecurity, and emergency preparedness, being delayed or suspended with increased risk across the department.\"\nImage\nBottom line: shutdowns don't work.And yet, Democrats are set to shut the government down for the third time in recent months. This isn't responsibility, and it's not what the American people elected them to do. Shutdowns have very real, negative impacts on real people. As appropriators heard in today's hearing, multiple agencies critical to the safety and security of American communities are in the crosshairs over Democrat complaints that have already been addressed in bipartisan, bicameral legislation. Democrats did not take the topic of this hearing seriously, and wasted their time on the dais today rehashing already-negotiated compromises and berating the only agencies within DHS that will remain funded in the event of a shutdown – and therefore were not on the panel. It's crystal clear who is governing and who is fueling chaos and obstruction.  ###","content_cn":"首页\n新闻\n新闻稿\n面对现实：民主党人在国土安全部停摆临近之际无视事实\n2026年2月11日 新闻稿\n华盛顿特区——今天，国土安全小组委员会就国土安全部（DHS）可能停摆的影响举行了听证会。目前的情况是，国土安全部的资金将在本周末耗尽，而民主党人似乎准备让政府停摆，尽管两党支持的FY26国土安全拨款法案已在数周前通过了众议院。国土安全部停摆不会像民主党人希望的那样对移民行动产生影响——去年的《大而美法案》中有大量资金专门用于移民执法和边境墙建设。然而，如果政府停摆，国土安全部下属的许多其他机构和项目将受到影响，包括：海岸警卫队、运输安全管理局（TSA）、网络安全和反恐工作、联邦应急管理署（FEMA）、执法培训等。来自国土安全部的听证嘉宾包括：托马斯·艾伦海军上将，美国海岸警卫队副司令马杜·戈图穆卡拉博士，网络安全和基础设施安全局代理局长阮·麦克尼尔，运输安全管理局代理局长马修·奎因，美国特勤局副局长格雷格·菲利普斯，联邦应急管理署响应与恢复办公室副主任\n图片\n国土安全小组委员会主席马克·阿莫迪（内华达州共和党人）在开场陈述中强调，停摆无法有效解决民主党人所关注的问题，他说：“如果我们因为ICE和CBP在明尼阿波利斯的执法行动以及我的同事们列出的极端政策要求而让该部门停摆，将会发生以下情况：移民和驱逐行动将继续；边境墙建设将继续；任何由和解法案资助的项目都将继续。该部门在移民执法之外所做的良好工作将戛然而止，而这正是今天听证会的主题。”在此处阅读阿莫迪主席的完整发言。\n图片\n主席汤姆·科尔（俄克拉何马州共和党人）参加了听证会，就民主党人在法案以两党票数通过众议院后突然放弃两党谈判一事发表意见。科尔主席说：“我发现[他们的]立场难以与事实相符。无论是停摆还是持续决议都无法加强监督——但我们两党、两院的FY26法案做到了。那份最终的全年立法是跨议院、跨党派真诚谈判达成的。它包括为随身摄像头和缓和冲突培训提供资金，投资于FEMA和网络安全工作，并维护了海岸警卫队和TSA的使命。我们的国土安全法案不是一份单一议题法案。将其视为单一议题法案，无视了我们面前影响的全部范围——并放弃了负责任的治理。此外，这些行动不会实现民主党人声称追求的目标。”在此处阅读科尔主席的完整发言。\n图片\n众议员约翰·拉瑟福德（佛罗里达州共和党人）表示：“如果发生停摆，那是参议院民主党领导层制造出来的停摆。如果你们的男女员工被迫休假，如果你们的男女员工被迫无薪工作，那都是因为参议院领导层。毫无疑问。今天的会议关乎你们日复一日、在不久的将来为这个国家提供的公共安全。想想你们即将在FIFA世界杯和所有‘美国250’活动等所有国家特别安全活动中承担的责任，而我们却给你们制造资金中断和停顿。”\n图片\n众议员丹·纽豪斯（华盛顿州共和党人）表示：“听到真正利害攸关的事情，国会议员和公众需要获得你们将要提供给我们的信息……我们预计参议院将发生的事情无视了即将发生的事。而我个人百分之百同意你们来到这个听证会，让我们了解那些真正被忽视的事情的影响。”\n图片\n众议员阿什利·欣森（艾奥瓦州共和党人）表示：“我觉得奇怪的是，我的一些同事轻描淡写地略过了一个事实：纳税人曾为应对汹涌的边境危机而花费数十亿美元建造软体设施，而我们在过去四年里已经扭转了这一方向，正在修复上届政府造成的问题……从海岸警卫队到TSA再到CISA，这些官员们出现在工作岗位上履行职责，却连续数周拿不到工资。我相信随着周五的临近，你们的员工中有着极大的不安和不确定性，对此我感到抱歉。我们今天在这里正试图解决这个问题。”\n图片\n众议员迈克尔·格斯特（密西西比州共和党人）表示：“今天我坐在这里，听着这些证人和我们这边的成员就即将到来的停摆被说教，一个我们正试图阻止的停摆，一个由参议院民主党人驱动的停摆——他们先把国土安全部的资金单独拆出来，然后迫使我们投票通过一项只允许资金继续两周的法案，明知我们很可能最终走到政府停摆这一步。你看，国土安全部资助的不仅仅是ICE。国土安全部为22个不同机构的26万名男女员工支付工资……[国土安全部的]男女员工们刚刚才从政府历史上最长的停摆中缓过来，那是民主党人在参议院迫使我们经历的，当时他们试图将不相关的立法附加到持续决议上以维持政府运转。”\n图片\n众议员托尼·冈萨雷斯（得克萨斯州共和党人）表示：“我们有重大活动正在举行。如果资金中断，如果任何人投票反对[为国土安全部提供资金]，这不仅仅是你们在这里经常看到的普通政治问题。这是生死攸关的问题。这是这些无人机袭击的问题，它们正在世界各地发生。这不是‘如果’，这不是电子游戏，这不是在不久的将来。这就是现在……我们依赖FEMA、国土安全\n[正文过长，翻译截断；对象库保留全文]","publish_source":"appropriations.house.gov","publish_time":"2026-02-11T15:30:04-05:00"}},{"id":"news-1455","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"众议院通过H.R. 7744，结束民主党停摆并全额资助国土安全","title_en":"House Passes H.R. 7744 to End Democrat Shutdown and Fully Fund Homeland Security","summary_cn":"美国众议院以221票对209票通过H.R. 7744《2026年国土安全部拨款法案》，第二次推动全额资助国土安全部并保护边境。拨款委员会主席汤姆·科尔批评民主党持续停摆，导致网络安全、应急培训、联邦应急管理局拨款、运输安全管理局薪资和海岸警卫队任务受影响，呼吁参议院民主党人停止将国土安全资金作为政治筹码。","summary_en":"The House passed H.R. 7744, the Department of Homeland Security Appropriations Act, 2026, by 221 to 209, advancing full-year DHS funding for a second time. Chairman Tom Cole criticized Democrats for prolonging the shutdown, citing impacts on cybersecurity, first-responder training, FEMA grants, TSA pay and Coast Guard missions, and urged Senate Democrats to stop treating homeland security funding as a political bargaining chip.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-24T20:34:10.483222+00:00","url":"http://appropriations.house.gov/news/press-releases/house-passes-hr-7744-end-democrat-shutdown-and-fully-fund-homeland-security","content":"Home\nNews\nPress Releases\nHouse Passes H.R. 7744 to End Democrat Shutdown and Fully Fund Homeland Security\nMarch 5, 2026 Press Release\nWashington, D.C. – Today, the House of Representatives passed H.R. 7744, the Department of Homeland Security Appropriations Act, 2026, with a vote of 221 to 209. This is the second time legislation to fully fund DHS and protect the nation’s border has advanced through the House, once again demonstrating bipartisan support for protecting the nation and ending the Senate Democrat-instigated shutdown.\nImage\nChairman Tom Cole (R-OK) said, “The Constitution places the safety and security of the American people at the center of the federal government’s responsibilities. It is a duty I don’t take lightly. Amidst rising global tensions and natural disaster possibilities, jeopardizing security operations and emergency preparedness is the last thing anyone should be doing. Yet, Democrats have kept the Department of Homeland Security shuttered for weeks – and again voted to keep it that way. “They are actively choosing to deny resources to the very people responsible for protecting the American homeland. Cybersecurity operations are at limited capacity, as adversaries like Iran, Russia, and China seek to exploit infrastructure vulnerabilities. Training for first responders has been canceled. FEMA grants – utilized by state and local entities to ensure safety and combat terrorism – can’t be accessed. TSA officers are being forced to work through the shutdown while missing paychecks. Coast Guard men and women – including those in harm’s way in Bahrain – are completing missions without full resources behind them. Even security preparations to keep attendees safe at the America 250 celebrations, the FIFA World Cup, the LA 2028 Olympics, and more face disruption. These impacts are not political or hyperbole – they are the direct cost of Democrats’ decision to play politics with the safeguards of this country.” “My priority is serving and protecting the American people, which is why I voted again today to pass bipartisan, bicameral, full-year DHS funding. No selective resourcing – full operational funding for the Department of Homeland Security and the personnel who stand watch over this nation every day. Despite bipartisan majorities in both chambers, Senate Democrats continue to hold this funding hostage. Shielding the homeland should never be treated as a political bargaining chip.” ###","content_cn":"首页\n新闻\n新闻稿\n众议院通过H.R. 7744法案，结束民主党政府停摆并全面资助国土安全部\n2026年3月5日 新闻稿\n华盛顿特区——今天，众议院以221票对209票通过了H.R. 7744号法案，即《2026年国土安全部拨款法案》。这是为国土安全部提供全额资金并保护国家边境的立法第二次在众议院取得进展，再次彰显了保护国家、结束由参议院民主党人煽动的政府停摆所获得的两党支持。\n图片\n主席汤姆·科尔（俄克拉何马州共和党）表示：“宪法将美国人民的安全与保障置于联邦政府职责的核心位置。这是我绝不轻视的责任。在全球紧张局势加剧、自然灾害可能发生之际，危及安全行动和应急准备是任何人都不应做的最后一件事。然而，民主党人让国土安全部关闭了数周——并再次投票维持这种状态。他们正在主动选择拒绝向那些负责保护美国国土的人提供资源。网络安全行动目前只能以有限能力开展，而伊朗、俄罗斯和中国等对手正试图利用基础设施漏洞。急救人员培训已被取消。联邦紧急事务管理局（FEMA）拨款——州和地方实体利用这些拨款来确保安全并打击恐怖主义——无法获得。运输安全管理局（TSA）官员被迫在停摆期间继续工作，却拿不到工资。海岸警卫队官兵——包括那些在巴林身处险境的人员——在没有充分资源支持的情况下完成任务。甚至旨在确保参加者在‘美国250周年庆典’、国际足联世界杯、2028年洛杉矶奥运会等活动中安全的安保准备工作也面临中断。这些影响不是政治作秀，也不是夸大其词——而是民主党人决定拿这个国家的安全保障进行政治操作所付出的直接代价。”“我的首要任务是服务并保护美国人民，这就是为什么我今天再次投票支持通过两党、两院共同支持的全年国土安全部拨款。不是选择性提供资源——而是为国土安全部及其每天守护这个国家的人员提供全面运营资金。尽管两院都有两党多数支持，参议院民主党人仍继续扣押这笔资金作为人质。保护国土绝不应被当作政治讨价还价的筹码。”\n###","publish_source":"appropriations.house.gov","publish_time":"2026-03-05T16:58:23-05:00"}},{"id":"news-1777","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"阿莫代伊关于H.R. 7147《2026年国土安全部拨款法案》的发言","title_en":"Amodei Remarks on H.R. 7147, the Department of Homeland Security Appropriations Act, 2026","summary_cn":"2026年1月22日，国土安全拨款小组委员会主席马克·阿莫代伊在众议院发言支持H.R. 7147。他称该法案取消上届政府用于软体处理帐篷的17亿美元支出、削减6.5亿美元被指助长边境危机的NGO拨款，并取消移民拘留监察员办公室。法案为ICE增加拘留床位至4.45万张，为TSA提供3亿美元安检设备，为海岸警卫队提供超1.15亿美元以应对中国并扩大印太存在，同时为CISA提供应对中俄的资源。","summary_en":"On January 22, 2026, Homeland Security Appropriations Subcommittee Chairman Mark Amodei spoke on the House floor in support of H.R. 7147. He said the bill eliminates $1.7 billion in soft-sided processing tent spending, cuts $650 million in NGO grants said to have exacerbated the border crisis, and eliminates the Office of Immigration Detention Ombudsman. It raises ICE detention beds to 44,500, provides $300 million for TSA screening equipment, over $115 million for the Coast Guard to counter China and expand its Indo-Pacific footprint, and resources for CISA against China and Russia.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-18T15:41:15.941703+00:00","url":"http://appropriations.house.gov/news/remarks/amodei-remarks-hr-7147-department-homeland-security-appropriations-act-2026","content":"Home\nNews\nRemarks\nAmodei Remarks on H.R. 7147, the Department of Homeland Security Appropriations Act, 2026\nJanuary 22, 2026\nRemarks\n&amp;nbsp; Thank you, Mr. Speaker.I rise today in strong support of the homeland security bill under consideration. As the Chairman of the Homeland Security Subcommittee, I'd like to thank the Full Committee chair, Mr. Cole, for his leadership in helping to return us to regular order and producing a series of bills that will fully fund the government by the January 30th deadline.I would also like to thank my good friend, the Subcommittee Ranking Member, Mr. Cuellar.  Negotiations on a bill like this are never easy, but he was and continues to be a great partner. And finally, I'd like to take the time to thank the Committee staff on both sides of the aisle, who worked tirelessly over the past month to negotiate the product before us. From the majority side: Paul Anstine, Anna Lanier Fischer, Fern Gibbons, Alessandra Ramirez, Ashley Truluck, and Nkosi Thomas. And from the minority: Shannon McCully, Jamie Wise, and Jim Ellsworth. Thank you all for your dedication and effort. Last year, we had a year-long Continuing Resolutions, but Continuing Resolutions should only be used when there is no other option. They lock us into outdated spending levels, and in last year's case, they continued funding priorities set under the Biden Administration. And, as a reminder, the Biden Administration was uninterested in securing the border or enforcing immigration law in any real, meaningful way. Thankfully, the Trump Administration's actions from day one has reversed the crisis left in the wake of Biden Administration. This Administration's strong border security policies have transformed a border in crisis, with record-breaking illegal border crossings that overwhelmed our agents and officers, into the most secure border since the Border Patrol began keeping records.The fiscal year 2026 Homeland Security bill under consideration today furthers this Administration's goals of undoing the damage caused by the Biden border crisis. It funds the President's priorities, codifies DOGE reductions and efficiencies, and operationalizes border security and immigration enforcement investments from the One Big Beautiful Bill Act. For example, this bill eliminates spending on soft-sided, processing tents used under the previous Administration – saving the American taxpayer $1.7 billion. We don't need to spend that money because our border is now secure.This bill eliminates $650 million in grants that were a handout to NGOs and other nonprofits that only exacerbated the border crisis by providing services to aliens once they were released into the interior of the country. This funding essentially incentivized aliens to enter into the country illegally, because they knew that the NGOs would provide them everything they would need once processed and released after encounter, such as transportation and housing services, all at the expense of our taxpayers. And we eliminate funding for the Office of Immigration Detention Ombudsman, which was an office led and staffed by people who fundamentally opposed ICE's mission to detain and remove dangerous criminal aliens from our communities. Speaking of, I want to reassure my colleagues that this bill does not hamper, in any way, shape, or form, ICE's ability to continue its mission of enforcing immigration law, detaining criminal aliens, and removing those who no longer have a legal basis to remain in this country. In ICE, we maintained an increase of $485 million included in last year's CR for detention, enforcement, and removal operations. In fact, we provide additional funding for detention to increase our base bed level by 3,000 to 44,500, offset by savings found elsewhere in the agency. This is on top of the nearly $75 billion appropriated to ICE in the One Big Beautiful Bill – $45 billion of which is for detention capacity alone. That's $9 billion a year through fiscal year 2029 just for ICE beds. For context, ICE's entire appropriation in this bill is $10 billion.ICE will have more than $25 billion this year to execute every single aspect of the President's immigration enforcement agenda. In addition, this bill ensures that the other component within ICE-Homeland Security Investigations-has the tools and resources needed to protect the most vulnerable throughout our communities by strengthening human trafficking and forced labor investigations, and countering the deadly influx of fentanyl and other drugs we saw come across the border under the previous Administration. In TSA, we provide $300 million to make sure the latest in screening equipment is deployed to airports to make the screening process easier and our flights more secure.For the Coast Guard, we fully fund the military pay raise, provide over $115 million for the Coast Guard to counter China and expand its footprint in the Indo-Pacific, and include investments in cutting-edge technology and unmanned systems. The bill fully funds all Secret Service personnel hired with supplemental funds following the assassination attempt of President Trump in Butler, PA. We also provide the necessary resources to ensure the Secret Service can prepare for and defend upcoming National Special Security Events, such as the 2026 FIFA World Cup and America250.Our bill supports first responders in our communities with increases to grant funding that will enable firefighters and others to respond capably when a tragedy occurs. And as attacks on houses of worship have increased over the last few years, we are providing $300 million to support security enhancements to churches and synagogues threatened with violence. Finally, we ensure that CISA, the civilian agency charged with protecting critical infrastructure like power and water, have the resources required to prevent attacks from nation-state adversaries like China and Russia.Simply put-this bill ensures that the men and women of the Department of Homeland Security, who work tirelessly to keep America safe, have the resources and tools they need to protect this great nation. I ask my colleagues to support this bill, and I yield back the balance of my time.","content_cn":"首页\n新闻\n讲话\n阿莫代伊关于H.R. 7147《2026年国土安全部拨款法案》的讲话\n2026年1月22日\n讲话\n谢谢您，议长先生。我今天起立，强烈支持正在审议的这项国土安全法案。作为国土安全小组委员会主席，我要感谢全体委员会主席科尔先生，感谢他的领导，帮助我们恢复常规秩序，并推动一系列法案在1月30日截止日期前为政府提供全额资金。我还要感谢我的好朋友、小组委员会资深成员奎利亚尔先生。像这样的法案谈判从来都不容易，但他过去是、现在仍然是一位出色的合作伙伴。最后，我要花时间感谢两党的委员会工作人员，他们在过去一个月里不知疲倦地工作，谈判出摆在我们面前的这份成果。多数党方面：保罗·安斯汀、安娜·拉尼尔·费舍尔、弗恩·吉本斯、亚历山德拉·拉米雷斯、阿什利·特鲁拉克和恩科西·托马斯。少数党方面：香农·麦卡利、杰米·怀斯和吉姆·埃尔斯沃思。感谢你们所有人的奉献和努力。去年，我们有一项长达一年的持续决议，但持续决议只应在没有其他选择时使用。它们把我们锁定在过时的支出水平上，而且在去年的情况下，它们继续为拜登政府设定的优先事项提供资金。并且，提醒一下，拜登政府对以任何真正、有意义的方式保障边境安全或执行移民法都不感兴趣。值得庆幸的是，特朗普政府从第一天起的行动扭转了拜登政府留下的危机。本届政府强有力的边境安全政策已将边境从危机状态——创纪录的非法越境压垮了我们的探员和官员——转变为边境巡逻队有记录以来最安全的边境。今天审议的2026财年国土安全法案进一步推进了本届政府消除拜登边境危机所造成损害的目标。它为总统的优先事项提供资金，将DOGE的削减和效率举措编入法律，并落实《一项大而美的法案》中的边境安全和移民执法投资。例如，该法案取消了上届政府使用的软边处理帐篷的支出——为美国纳税人节省了17亿美元。我们不需要花这笔钱，因为我们的边境现在安全了。该法案取消了6.5亿美元的拨款，这些拨款是对非政府组织和其他非营利机构的施舍，这些机构在外国人被释放到美国内陆后为其提供服务，只会加剧边境危机。这笔资金实质上激励了外国人非法进入美国，因为他们知道，一旦在遭遇后被处理和释放，非政府组织会为他们提供所需的一切，例如交通和住房服务，而这一切都由我们的纳税人承担。我们还取消了移民拘留监察长办公室的资金，该办公室由从根本上反对ICE拘留和驱逐危险犯罪外国人使命的人领导和任职。说到这一点，我想向我的同事们保证，该法案在任何方面、任何形式都不会妨碍ICE继续执行其使命，即执行移民法、拘留犯罪外国人和驱逐那些不再有合法依据留在我国的人。在ICE方面，我们维持了去年持续决议中用于拘留、执法和驱逐行动的4.85亿美元增长。事实上，我们为拘留提供了额外资金，将基本床位水平增加3000张至44500张，由该机构其他地方的节省来抵消。这还不包括《一项大而美的法案》中拨给ICE的近750亿美元——其中450亿美元仅用于拘留容量。这意味着到2029财年，仅ICE床位每年就有90亿美元。作为参照，ICE在该法案中的全部拨款为100亿美元。ICE今年将拥有超过250亿美元，用于执行总统移民执法议程的每一个方面。此外，该法案确保ICE内的另一个组成部分——国土安全调查局——拥有所需的工具和资源，通过加强人口贩运和强迫劳动调查，以及打击上届政府时期我们看到的芬太尼和其他毒品致命流入，来保护我们社区中最脆弱的群体。在TSA方面，我们提供3亿美元，确保最新筛查设备部署到机场，使筛查过程更容易，我们的航班更安全。对于海岸警卫队，我们全额资助军人加薪，为海岸警卫队提供超过1.15亿美元以对抗中国并扩大其在印太地区的存在，并包括对尖端技术和无人系统的投资。该法案为在宾夕法尼亚州巴特勒市特朗普总统遇刺未遂事件后通过补充资金聘用的所有特勤局人员提供全额资金。我们还提供必要资源，确保特勤局能够为即将到来的国家特别安全活动做好准备并加以保卫，例如2026年国际足联世界杯和America250。我们的法案通过增加拨款支持我们社区的一线应急人员，使消防员和其他人员能够在悲剧发生时有能力应对。随着过去几年对礼拜场所的袭击增加，我们提供3亿美元，支持受到暴力威胁的教堂和犹太教堂的安全增强。最后，我们确保CISA——负责保护电力和水等关键基础设施的民事机构——拥有防止中国和俄罗斯等民族国家对手袭击所需的资源。简而言之——该法案确保国土安全部的男女工作人员\n[正文过长，翻译截断；对象库保留全文]","publish_source":"appropriations.house.gov","publish_time":"2026-01-22T01:45:11-05:00"}},{"id":"news-1768","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"科尔就H.R. 7147《2026年国土安全部拨款法案》发表院会讲话","title_en":"Cole Floor Remarks on H.R. 7147, The Department of Homeland Security Appropriations Act, 2026","summary_cn":"众议院拨款委员会主席科尔在院会发言支持H.R. 7147《2026年国土安全部拨款法案》，称这是本财年最后一项拨款措施。法案为边境巡逻与执法、拘留与遣返、侦测非法活动的先进技术以及海岸警卫队提供资金，并加强打击芬太尼等毒品、调查人口贩运和强迫劳动，同时强化灾害准备与应对。科尔赞扬小组委员会主席阿莫迪与资深成员奎利亚尔跨党派合作，呼吁支持该法案。","summary_en":"House Appropriations Chairman Cole spoke on the floor in support of H.R. 7147, the Department of Homeland Security Appropriations Act for fiscal year 2026, calling it the final measure of the FY26 agenda. The bill funds Border Patrol and enforcement agents, detention and deportation, cutting-edge technology to detect illicit activity, and Coast Guard investments, while boosting efforts against fentanyl and other deadly drugs and expanding investigations into human trafficking and forced labor. It also strengthens disaster preparedness and response. Cole praised Subcommittee Chairman Amodei and Ranking Member Cuellar for bipartisan work and urged support.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-18T15:41:14.350521+00:00","url":"http://appropriations.house.gov/news/remarks/cole-floor-remarks-hr-7147-department-homeland-security-appropriations-act-2026","content":"Home\nNews\nRemarks\nCole Floor Remarks on H.R. 7147, The Department of Homeland Security Appropriations Act, 2026\nJanuary 22, 2026\nRemarks\n&amp;nbsp;Mr. Speaker, I yield myself such time as I may consume.I rise in support of H.R. 7147, the Department of Homeland Security Appropriations Act. This bill marks the final measure in our FY26 agenda. Our work here is about one of our most important duties: keeping the American people and our homeland safe. This legislation delivers just that and upholds the America first agenda through supporting: Border patrol and enforcement agents;Detention and deportation efforts;Cutting-edge technology to detect illicit activity; andCoast guard investments to counter Communist China's aggression in the maritime sphere. We enhance resources to combat fentanyl and other deadly drugs while safeguarding children through expanded investigations into human trafficking and forced labor.From our borders and ports to aviation and cyberspace, this legislation delivers the personnel, training, and technology needed to reinforce our defenses and confront those who wish us harm. It also prioritizes strong and resilient communities by bolstering disaster preparedness, response, and recovery efforts. Subcommittee Chairman Mark Amodei prioritized safety at every level. Even in the face of political challenge, he and Ranking Member Henry Cuellar worked together to produce a serious, responsible bill.H.R. 7147 is focused on outcomes – not partisan rhetoric. It equips frontline personnel, strengthens enforcement, and provides the certainty DHS needs to carry out its mission effectively. I thank our members and staff for their work, and I urge support for this bipartisan legislation. With that, I reserve the balance of my time.","content_cn":"首页\n新闻\n讲话\n科尔关于H.R. 7147《2026年国土安全部拨款法案》的院会讲话\n2026年1月22日\n讲话\n议长先生，我让出我可能使用的时间。我起立支持H.R. 7147，即《国土安全部拨款法案》。该法案是我们26财年议程的最后一项措施。我们在这里的工作关乎我们最重要的职责之一：保护美国人民和我们的国土安全。这项立法正是为此，并通过支持以下方面来维护美国优先议程：边境巡逻和执法探员；拘留和驱逐行动；检测非法活动的尖端技术；以及海岸警卫队投资，以对抗共产主义中国在海上的侵略。我们加强资源以打击芬太尼和其他致命毒品，同时通过扩大对人口贩运和强迫劳动的调查来保护儿童。从我们的边境和港口到航空和网络空间，这项立法提供了加强防御和对抗那些希望伤害我们的人所需的人员、培训和技术。它还通过加强灾难准备、响应和恢复工作，优先考虑强大而有韧性的社区。小组委员会主席马克·阿莫代伊将安全置于各个层面的优先位置。即使面对政治挑战，他和资深成员亨利·奎利亚尔也共同努力，制定出一项严肃、负责任的法案。H.R. 7147注重结果——而非党派言论。它为一线人员提供装备，加强执法，并为国土安全部有效执行其使命提供所需的确定性。我感谢我们的成员和工作人员所做的工作，并敦促支持这项两党立法。至此，我保留我的剩余时间。","publish_source":"appropriations.house.gov","publish_time":"2026-01-22T13:28:02-05:00"}},{"id":"news-1301","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"机场陷入瘫痪之际，巴雷特第三次投票为国土安全部拨款并支付TSA人员薪资","title_en":"As Airports Grind to a Halt, Barrett Votes for Third Time to Fund Homeland Security and Pay TSA Agents","summary_cn":"2026年3月26日，众议员汤姆·巴雷特（密歇根州第七选区）支持以218比206通过《保卫国土薪酬法案》（H.R. 8029），第三次为国土安全部提供全额拨款。文章称国土安全部已停摆41天，TSA、海岸警卫队、联邦应急管理局及特勤局等任务受影响，部分机场安检等待时间超过六小时，针对TSA人员的袭击增加500%。巴雷特呼吁参议院采取行动。","summary_en":"On March 26, 2026, Congressman Tom Barrett (MI-07) helped pass the Pay Our Homeland Defenders Act (H.R. 8029) by a 218-206 vote, fully funding the Department of Homeland Security for the third time this year. The release states DHS has been shut down for 41 days, jeopardizing TSA, Coast Guard, FEMA, Secret Service and counterterrorism missions, with airport security waits exceeding six hours and assaults on TSA officers up 500%. Barrett urged the Senate to act.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-24T20:30:22.421090+00:00","url":"http://barrett.house.gov/media/press-releases/airports-grind-halt-barrett-votes-third-time-fund-homeland-security-and-pay","content":"Home\nMedia\nPress Releases\nAs Airports Grind to a Halt, Barrett Votes for Third Time to Fund Homeland Security and Pay TSA Agents\nMarch 26, 2026 Press Release\nWashington, D.C. — As the longest airport security lines in history grind airports to a halt, Congressman Tom Barrett (MI-07) today helped pass legislation to fully fund the Department of Homeland Security (DHS) for the third time this year. The Pay Our Homeland Defenders Act (H.R. 8029) was approved by a 218-206 vote, with all but four Democrats voting to keep DHS shut down.“Airports across the United States are a complete mess with people spending hours on end waiting to get through security because TSA agents simply can’t afford to keep coming to work without getting paid,” said Barrett. “This nightmare is only going to get worse as thousands of Americans get ready to travel for spring break and Easter unless we fund the Department of Homeland Security and pay TSA. I just voted to do that for the third time, and it’s time we demand the Senate to do the same.”DHS has been shut down for 41 days, jeopardizing the missions of the TSA, Coast Guard, FEMA, Secret Service, and various other counterterrorism and security agencies. Since then, security wait times at some airports have reached more than six hours long. In testimony before Congress this week, acting TSA Administrator Ha Nguyen McNeill highlighted that assaults against TSA officers have increased 500% since the shutdown began on February 14.The Pay Our Homeland Defenders Act is identical to the bipartisan DHS funding bills that passed the House in January and earlier this month with Barrett’s support. The funding plan was negotiated this winter by Republicans and Democrats in the House, Senate, and White House, but Democrats then proceeded to block the legislation in the Senate, where the bill requires several Democrat votes to pass.\nMedia\nPress Releases\nMedia","content_cn":"首页\n媒体\n新闻稿\n随着机场陷入停摆，巴雷特第三次投票为国土安全部提供资金并向TSA特工发薪\n2026年3月26日 新闻稿\n华盛顿特区——随着史上最长的机场安检队伍使机场陷入停摆，国会议员汤姆·巴雷特（密歇根州第07选区）今日协助通过一项法案，今年第三次为国土安全部（DHS）提供全额资金。《支付我们的国土捍卫者法案》（H.R. 8029）以218票对206票获得通过，除四名民主党人外，其余民主党人均投票支持让DHS继续停摆。\n\n“美国各地机场一片混乱，人们花费数小时等待通过安检，因为TSA特工在没有薪水的情况下根本负担不起继续上班，”巴雷特说。“随着数千名美国人准备在春假和复活节期间出行，除非我们为国土安全部提供资金并向TSA发薪，这场噩梦只会愈演愈烈。我刚刚第三次投票支持这样做，现在我们应当要求参议院也这么做。”\n\nDHS已停摆41天，危及TSA、海岸警卫队、联邦紧急事务管理局（FEMA）、特勤局及各类其他反恐和安全机构的任务。自那以后，部分机场的安检等待时间已超过六小时。在本周向国会作证时，代理TSA局长Ha Nguyen McNeill强调，自2月14日停摆开始以来，针对TSA官员的袭击事件增加了500%。\n\n《支付我们的国土捍卫者法案》与今年1月及本月早些时候在巴雷特支持下获众议院通过的两项两党DHS拨款法案完全相同。该拨款计划于今年冬天由众议院、参议院和白宫的共和党人与民主党人协商达成，但民主党人随后在参议院阻止了该法案；该法案在参议院需要数名民主党人的支持票才能通过。\n\n媒体\n新闻稿\n媒体","publish_source":"barrett.house.gov","publish_time":"2026-03-26T17:18:15-04:00"}},{"id":"news-1453","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"巴雷特再次投票为国土安全部拨款，称民主党玩弄政治危及国家安全","title_en":"Barrett Votes Again to Fund DHS While Democrats Play Politics and Jeopardize National Security","summary_cn":"2026年3月5日，众议员汤姆·巴雷特与众议院以221比209通过H.R. 7744，第二次为国土安全部提供全额拨款。巴雷特批评民主党在伊朗冲突背景下拒绝拨款，称海岸警卫队、反恐部门和TSA人员无薪履职。文章称众议院民主党领导层要求本党议员投反对票，法案在参议院受阻，国土安全部已停摆近三周。","summary_en":"On March 5, 2026, Congressman Tom Barrett and the U.S. House passed H.R. 7744 by 221-209, fully funding the Department of Homeland Security for the second time this year. Barrett criticized Democrats for refusing funding amid conflict with Iran, noting Coast Guard, counterterrorism and TSA personnel working without pay. The release says House Democratic leadership urged a no vote, the bill stalled in the Senate, and DHS has been shut down for nearly three weeks.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-24T20:34:06.860082+00:00","url":"http://barrett.house.gov/media/press-releases/barrett-votes-again-fund-dhs-while-democrats-play-politics-and-jeopardize","content":"Home\nMedia\nPress Releases\nBarrett Votes Again to Fund DHS While Democrats Play Politics and Jeopardize National Security\nMarch 5, 2026 Press Release\nWashington, D.C. — Today, Congressman Tom Barrett and the U.S. House of Representatives passed legislation to fully fund the Department of Homeland Security (DHS) for the second time this year. The bill (H.R. 7744) was approved by a 221-209 vote with all but four Democrats voting to keep DHS shut down despite the increased risk to public safety and national security resulting from the conflict in Iran.“Democrats are outright refusing to fund the Department of Homeland Security at a time when Iran is actively seeking to do us harm and undermine our national security,” said Barrett. “Now is not the time to play political games with the agency tasked with protecting our homeland — from the Coast Guard to counterterrorism units and airport TSA — all of which are risking their lives to keep Americans safe without a paycheck. I will stand with our troops and vote for this funding package as many times as it takes for the other side of the aisle to join us.”Ahead of today’s vote, House Democratic leadership strongly urged their members to vote “no” on H.R. 7744, which is identical to the bipartisan DHS funding bill that passed the House in January with Barrett’s support. Meanwhile, members of the U.S. Coast Guard stationed in Bahrain — who are risking their lives without a paycheck — have fallen under attack from Iran.Despite increased tensions and this legislation passing the House twice, progress has since stalled in the Senate where the bill requires several Democrats’ support to pass. As a result, DHS has been shut down for nearly three weeks, jeopardizing the missions of the U.S. Coast Guard, TSA, FEMA, and various other counterterrorism units.\nMedia\nPress Releases\nMedia","content_cn":"主页\n媒体\n新闻稿\nBarrett再次投票为国土安全部提供资金，而民主党人玩弄政治并危及国家安全\n2026年3月5日 新闻稿\n华盛顿特区——今天，国会议员Tom Barrett和美国众议院第二次通过立法，为国土安全部（DHS）提供全年足额资金。该法案（H.R. 7744）以221比209票获通过；在伊朗冲突导致公共安全和国家安全面临更大风险之际，除四名民主党人外，所有民主党人都投票支持继续让DHS停摆。\n“民主党人公然拒绝在伊朗正积极寻求伤害我们、破坏我们国家安全之际，为国土安全部提供资金，”Barrett说。“现在不是对负责保护我们国土的机构玩弄政治游戏的时候——从海岸警卫队、反恐部队到机场运输安全管理局（TSA），这些机构的人员都在没有薪水的情况下冒着生命危险保护美国人的安全。我将与我们的军人站在一起，并会为这项拨款方案投票，直到对方党派加入我们为止，无论需要多少次。”\n在今天投票之前，众议院民主党领导层强烈敦促其成员对H.R. 7744投“反对”票；该法案与1月份在Barrett支持下于众议院通过的两党国土安全部拨款法案完全相同。与此同时，驻扎在巴林、在没有薪水的情况下冒着生命危险的美国海岸警卫队成员遭到伊朗袭击。\n尽管紧张局势加剧，且该法案已两次在众议院通过，但进展此后在参议院陷入停滞；该法案需要数名民主党人的支持才能通过。因此，DHS已停摆近三周，使美国海岸警卫队、TSA、联邦紧急事务管理局（FEMA）以及其他各类反恐部队的任务面临风险。\n媒体\n新闻稿\n媒体","publish_source":"barrett.house.gov","publish_time":"2026-03-05T17:07:23-05:00"}},{"id":"news-1297","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"众议员贝吉奇投票恢复国土安全部拨款并支持国土安全人员","title_en":"Congressman Begich Votes to Restore DHS Funding and Support Homeland Security Personnel","summary_cn":"2026年3月26日，众议员尼克·贝吉奇（阿拉斯加州共和党）投票支持H.R. 8029《保卫国土薪酬法案》，恢复国土安全部全额拨款。法案提供644亿美元可自由支配资金，用于国防活动、灾害应对、边境安全、移民执法及芬太尼打击，并补发停摆期间一线人员薪资，同时加强海岸警卫队在印太地区的存在并为其加薪。文章称参议院民主党人拒绝推进该法案。","summary_en":"On March 26, 2026, Congressman Nick Begich (R-AK) voted for H.R. 8029, the Pay Our Homeland Defenders Act, restoring full funding for the Department of Homeland Security. The bill provides $64.4 billion in discretionary funding for defense activities, disaster response, border security, immigration enforcement and fentanyl interdiction, plus retroactive pay for frontline personnel. It also boosts Coast Guard presence in the Indo-Pacific and raises servicemember pay. Senate Democrats have refused to advance it.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-24T20:30:14.665869+00:00","url":"http://begich.house.gov/media/press-releases/congressman-begich-votes-restore-dhs-funding-and-support-homeland-security","content":"Home\nMedia\nPress Releases\nCongressman Begich Votes to Restore DHS Funding and Support Homeland Security Personnel\nMarch 26, 2026 Press Release\nWASHINGTON, D.C. – March 26, 2026 – Today, Congressman Nick Begich (R-AK) voted in favor of H.R. 8029, the Pay Our Homeland Defenders Act, legislation to restore full funding for the Department of Homeland Security (DHS) and ensure that critical national security personnel.“Americans depend on the men and women of DHS to keep our nation safe,” said Congressman Begich. “Congress must prioritize the safety and security of the American people, and this legislation restores critical funding and ensures DHS can carry out its mission without disruption.”BACKGROUND:H.R. 8029 provides $64.4 billion in discretionary funding to support DHS operations and protect the homeland. The legislation includes funding for defense activities, disaster response, and key security priorities, while also ensuring retroactive pay for frontline personnel impacted by the funding lapse.The bill strengthens border security by supporting staffing and detention capacity for immigration enforcement and prioritizing the removal of criminal and removable aliens. It also enhances efforts to combat the flow of deadly drugs like fentanyl into American communities.H.R. 8029 invests in national security by increasing the Coast Guard’s presence in the Indo-Pacific region and providing a pay raise for Coast Guard servicemembers. The House has repeatedly passed legislation to fund DHS, but Senate Democrats have refused to come to the table and advance these measures, prolonging uncertainty for frontline personnel and risking national security operations.Following House passage, H.R. 8029 now moves to the Senate.###\nMedia\nPress Releases\nIn the News\nOp-Eds\nBack to top button","content_cn":"首页\n媒体\n新闻稿\n贝吉奇众议员投票支持恢复国土安全部资金并支持国土安全人员\n2026年3月26日 新闻稿\n华盛顿哥伦比亚特区——2026年3月26日——今天，尼克·贝吉奇众议员（共和党，阿拉斯加州）投票赞成H.R. 8029《支付国土防卫人员薪酬法案》，该法案旨在恢复对国土安全部（DHS）的全额拨款，并确保关键国家安全人员获得保障。“美国人依靠国土安全部的男女工作人员维护国家安全，”贝吉奇众议员说。“国会必须把美国人民的安全与保障置于优先地位，这项立法恢复关键资金，并确保国土安全部能够不受干扰地履行其使命。”\n背景：\nH.R. 8029提供644亿美元的自由裁量资金，用于支持国土安全部运作并保护国土。该立法包括国防活动、灾害应对和关键安全优先事项的资金，同时确保受资金中断影响的一线人员获得追溯薪酬。\n\n该法案通过支持移民执法人员配备和拘留能力，以及优先遣返犯罪外国人和可遣返外国人，来加强边境安全。它还加强了打击芬太尼等致命毒品流入美国社区的工作。\n\nH.R. 8029通过增加海岸警卫队在印太地区的部署并为海岸警卫队军人加薪，对国家安全进行投资。众议院已多次通过为国土安全部提供资金的立法，但参议院民主党人拒绝参与谈判并推进这些措施，延长了一线人员面临的不确定性，并危及国家安全行动。\n\n在众议院通过后，H.R. 8029现已提交参议院。\n###\n媒体\n新闻稿\n新闻报道\n评论文章\n返回顶部按钮","publish_source":"begich.house.gov","publish_time":"2026-03-26T20:21:51-04:00"}},{"id":"news-1764","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"众议员加西亚将投票反对国土安全部拨款法案","title_en":"Congressman García to Vote Against DHS Funding Bill","summary_cn":"伊利诺伊州民主党众议员赫苏斯·“丘伊”·加西亚发表声明，表示将投票反对2026财年国土安全部拨款法案。他批评该法案扩大移民和海关执法局（ICE）的资金且未施加实质改革，称在ICE和海关与边境保护局已获1700亿美元后继续增加拨款是纵容其“恐吓社区”。他援引本周ICE在明尼苏达州以五岁儿童利亚姆·拉莫斯为诱饵抓捕其父亲并拘留两人的事件，称不会支持这种纳税人资助的暴力。","summary_en":"Rep. Jesús “Chuy” García (IL-04) issued a statement announcing he will vote against the fiscal year 2026 Department of Homeland Security funding bill. He criticized the legislation for expanding ICE’s funding without serious reforms, saying that giving billions more to ICE and CBP after the $170 billion they received is a green light to continue terrorizing communities. He cited this week’s case in Minnesota where ICE allegedly used five-year-old Liam Ramos as bait to capture his father, then detained both and sent them to Texas, and said he will not sanction taxpayer-funded violence.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-18T15:41:13.489233+00:00","url":"http://chuygarcia.house.gov/media/press-releases/congressman-garcia-to-vote-against-dhs-funding-bill","content":"Image\nHome\nMedia\nPress Releases\nCongressman García to Vote Against DHS Funding BillJanuary 22, 2026 Press ReleaseWASHINGTON, D.C. — Congressman Jesús “Chuy” García (IL-04) issued the following statement on the bill to fund the Department of Homeland Security (DHS) in fiscal year 2026:“This legislation betrays our communities and funds more violence and terror by DHS. Far from cutting funding for ICE, the bill expands its slush fund and imposes no serious reforms to end its rampage through our cities. Giving billions more to ICE and CBP, after the $170 billion they received in the Big Ugly Bill and without any meaningful action to rein them in, is a green light to continue terrorizing communities around the country. Just this week, ICE used Liam Ramos, a five year-old in Minnesota, as bait to capture his father, then detained both of them and sent them to Texas. I will vote NO because I will not sanction this taxpayer-funded violence against my constituents or anyone else.“DHS’s brutal assault on Chicago, Minneapolis, Los Angeles, and other cities is not new. This rogue and lawless agency has consistently trampled on our rights since it was founded less than 25 years ago. Instead of giving billions more to violent thugs who kidnap and murder people with impunity, Congress should be dismantling DHS and rebuilding the immigration enforcement system from the ground up.”# # #\nIssues:Judiciary Issues/Oversight","content_cn":"图片\n首页\n媒体\n新闻稿\n加西亚众议员将投票反对国土安全部拨款法案2026年1月22日 新闻稿华盛顿特区——众议员赫苏斯·“丘伊”·加西亚（伊利诺伊州第4选区）就2026财年国土安全部（DHS）拨款法案发表以下声明：“这项立法背叛了我们的社区，为国土安全部更多的暴力和恐怖行为提供资金。该法案远未削减移民和海关执法局（ICE）的经费，反而扩大了其秘密资金，并且没有实施任何严肃改革来终止其在我们的城市中横冲直撞。在ICE和海关与边境保护局（CBP）已从《大而丑法案》中获得1700亿美元之后，再给它们数十亿美元，却不采取任何有意义的行动加以约束，就是为继续恐吓全国各地的社区开绿灯。就在本周，ICE利用明尼苏达州五岁的利亚姆·拉莫斯作为诱饵来抓捕他的父亲，随后将两人都拘留并送往德克萨斯州。我将投反对票，因为我不会批准这种由纳税人出资、针对我的选民或任何其他人的暴力行为。“国土安全部对芝加哥、明尼阿波利斯、洛杉矶和其他城市的残暴攻击并非新鲜事。这个流氓且无法无天的机构自不到25年前成立以来，一直践踏我们的权利。国会不应再给那些肆无忌惮地绑架和谋杀他人的暴力暴徒数十亿美元，而应解散国土安全部，并从零开始重建移民执法体系。”# # #\n议题：司法议题/监督","publish_source":"chuygarcia.house.gov","publish_time":"2026-01-22T15:55:56-05:00"}},{"id":"news-2383","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"伊利诺伊州代表团议员就布罗德维尤处理中心条件要求国土安全部和ICE作出答复","title_en":"Illinois Delegation Members Demand Answers from DHS and ICE on Conditions at the Broadview Processing Center","summary_cn":"伊利诺伊州国会代表团民主党议员加西亚、拉米雷斯、杰克逊和戴维斯致信国土安全部部长诺姆及ICE代理局长莱昂斯，要求说明布罗德维尤ICE处理中心的羁押条件、容量和基本服务。此前议员试图进行监督访问但被拒绝，并收到关于被拘留者缺乏床位、食物、淋浴和卫生用品等恶劣条件的报告。信中要求DHS和ICE回答设施容量、在押人数、医疗护理及律师和家属联系程序等问题。","summary_en":"Democratic members of the Illinois Congressional Delegation—García, Ramirez, Jackson and Davis—sent a letter to DHS Secretary Kristi Noem and ICE Acting Director Todd Lyons demanding answers on conditions, capacity and basic services at the Broadview ICE Processing Center. After being denied an oversight visit, they cited reports of detainees lacking beds, food, showers and hygiene products, and asked about capacity, custody numbers, medical care and access to lawyers and family.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-24T21:09:47.466839+00:00","url":"http://chuygarcia.house.gov/media/press-releases/illinois-delegation-members-demand-answers-from-dhs-and-ice-on-conditions-at-the-broadview-processing-center","content":"Image\nHome\nMedia\nPress Releases\nIllinois Delegation Members Demand Answers from DHS and ICE on Conditions at the Broadview Processing CenterSeptember 18, 2025 Press ReleaseWASHINGTON, D.C. —  As the Trump administration continues to flout federal law, Democratic members of the Illinois Congressional Delegation Jesús “Chuy” García (IL-04), Delia Ramirez (IL-03), Jonathan Jackson (IL-01), and Danny Davis (IL-04) sent a letter to Department of Homeland Security (DHS) Secretary Kristi Noem and Immigration and Customs Enforcement (ICE) Acting Director Todd Lyons demanding answers on the conditions, capacity, and basic services for immigrants held at the Broadview ICE Processing Center in Illinois. On June 18, after receiving reports of abuses and misuse of a processing center to detain people in inhumane conditions, the Members tried to conduct an oversight visit but were unlawfully denied access, even after documenting their identity. Members of Congress have the right to conduct oversight and enter any facility operated by or for DHS used to detain or house immigrants without previous notice. Since then, they continue to receive reports about community members detained in the facility in deplorable conditions that violate their human and legal rights as well as state laws that prohibit existence of detention centersIn the letter, the Members state “we sought access to the Broadview facility because of credible reports that the facility was being used to unlawfully detain immigrants, including our constituents. The reports suggested that people are being detained for prolonged periods of time without access to basic necessities and legal counsel. One person detained there detailed how she was one of approximately 30 women who were held in a room with no beds, no blankets and very little food. She and her fellow detainees had to sleep on the floor and had no access to showers or any hygiene products.”The Members demand that DHS and ICE respond to questions including the facility’s total holding capacity, how many people they actually have in custody, how the center will be utilized in connection to Operation Midway Blitz, what medical care is provided at the facility, and what process exists for people to communicate with their lawyers and family members.  “We take our responsibility to uphold the Constitution and laws of the United States seriously, even if you do not. We continue to be deeply concerned about the conditions at the Broadview facility, and we will not be deterred by your refusal to comply with the law.”A copy of the full letter can be found here.  # # #\nIssues:ImmigrationJudiciary Issues/Oversight","content_cn":"图片\n首页\n媒体\n新闻稿\n伊利诺伊州代表团成员要求国土安全部和移民与海关执法局就布罗德维尤处理中心的状况作出答复\n2025年9月18日 新闻稿\n华盛顿特区——随着特朗普政府持续藐视联邦法律，伊利诺伊州国会代表团的民主党成员赫苏斯·“丘伊”·加西亚（IL-04）、德莉娅·拉米雷斯（IL-03）、乔纳森·杰克逊（IL-01）和丹尼·戴维斯（IL-04）致信国土安全部（DHS）部长克里斯蒂·诺姆和移民与海关执法局（ICE）代理局长托德·莱昂斯，要求就被关押在伊利诺伊州布罗德维尤ICE处理中心的移民所处条件、收容能力和基本服务作出答复。\n6月18日，在收到有关虐待行为以及将一处处理中心用于以不人道条件拘押人员的报告后，这些议员试图进行监督访问，但即使在出示身份证明后仍被非法拒绝进入。国会议员有权进行监督，并且无需事先通知即可进入由国土安全部运营、或为国土安全部运营、用于拘押或安置移民的任何设施。此后，他们持续收到报告称，社区成员被拘押在该设施中，处于恶劣条件之下，其人权和合法权利以及禁止设立拘押中心的州法律均遭到违反。\n议员们在信中表示：“我们寻求进入布罗德维尤设施，是因为有可信报告称，该设施被用于非法拘押移民，其中包括我们的选民。报告显示，人们被长期拘押，无法获得基本生活必需品和法律顾问服务。一名被拘押者详细说明，她是大约30名被关押在一间没有床、没有毯子且食物极少的房间里的女性之一。她和其他被拘押者不得不睡在地板上，也无法使用淋浴设施或获得任何卫生用品。”\n议员们要求国土安全部和移民与海关执法局答复的问题包括：该设施的总收容能力、实际拘押人数、该中心将如何配合“中途闪电行动”使用、该设施提供何种医疗护理，以及人员可通过何种程序与律师和家人沟通。\n“我们认真履行维护美国宪法和法律的责任，即使你们并不如此。我们仍然对布罗德维尤设施的状况深感担忧，也不会因你们拒绝遵守法律而退缩。”\n完整信件副本可在此处查阅。\n# # #\n议题：移民\n司法议题/监督","publish_source":"chuygarcia.house.gov","publish_time":"2025-09-18T12:10:46-04:00"}},{"id":"news-1471","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"众议员科恩就“遣返最恶劣罪犯”说法质询国土安全部长诺姆","title_en":"Congressman Cohen Questions DHS Secretary Noem about her Claim to be Deporting “the Worst of the Worst”","summary_cn":"田纳西州民主党众议员史蒂夫·科恩在监督听证会上质询国土安全部长克里斯蒂·诺姆，指出其多次称ICE正在遣返“最恶劣的罪犯”，但统计显示多数被拦截和试图遣返者并未犯罪。科恩还询问诺姆为何未回复他过去一年发出的八封信，并质询有关ICE特工培训包含违法“秘密指令”的指控，以及其部门是否雇用了1月6日事件相关人员。科恩此前曾呼吁诺姆辞职或被弹劾。","summary_en":"Rep. Steve Cohen (TN-9), a senior Judiciary Committee member, questioned Homeland Security Secretary Kristi Noem at an oversight hearing about her repeated claim that ICE is deporting “the worst of the worst,” noting statistics show most people stopped and targeted for deportation have committed no crimes. Cohen also asked why Noem has not responded to eight letters he sent over the past year, and raised allegations that ICE agent training includes secretive orders to violate the law, as well as whether any January 6 participants have been hired by her department. Cohen has previously called for Noem to resign or face impeachment.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-18T15:26:33.391706+00:00","url":"http://cohen.house.gov/media-center/press-releases/congressman-cohen-questions-dhs-secretary-noem-about-her-claim-be","content":"Home\nMedia\nPress Releases\nCongressman Cohen Questions DHS Secretary Noem about her Claim to be Deporting “the Worst of the Worst”\nImage\nMarch 4, 2026 Press Release\nAlso seeks information on ICE agent training, hiring of January 6 defendants\nWASHINGTON – Congressman Steve Cohen (TN-9), a senior member of the Judiciary Committee, today questioned Department of Homeland Security Secretary Kristi Noem at an oversight hearing. Congressman Cohen asked Secretary Noem about her lack of response to repeated letters he has written to her over the past year and about claims that Immigration and Customs Enforcement (ICE) agents are deporting the “worst of the worst.”In his exchange with the Secretary, Congressman Cohen said in part:“This gives me the opportunity to show you the eight letters I’ve sent you in the last year…and gives me the opportunity to ask you the questions and try to get answers. One of the things you’re most famous for is quote ‘we’re going after the worst of the worst’ – the murderers, pedophiles, the rapists, et cetera. In my letters, I said I agree with you: People who are in this country illegally or not citizens and commit those crimes should be deported. The facts show that most of the people you stopped and tried to deport have not committed those crimes. In fact, they’ve committed no crimes at all…“Why do you continue to talk about the ‘worst of the worst’ when all the statistics show you’re not stopping the worst of the worst?...“Go after the worst of the worst and, if you did, people wouldn’t find your department the worst department in the United States of America.”Congressman Cohen also asked Secretary Noem about recent allegations that ICE agent training includes “secretive orders” that they violate the law. He also asked whether any of the January 6 insurrectionists have been hired by her department.See the entire exchange here.Congressman Cohen has previously called for Secretary Noem to resign, be fired, or face impeachment proceedings. # # #\nIssues:\n9th District\nHomeland Security\nJudiciary\nMemphis\nShelby County\nTennessee","content_cn":"首页\n媒体\n新闻稿\n国会议员科恩就诺姆部长声称驱逐“最恶劣中的最恶劣者”一事向其质询\n图片\n2026年3月4日 新闻稿\n还寻求有关ICE探员培训、聘用1月6日被告人的信息\n华盛顿——国会众议员史蒂夫·科恩（田纳西州第九选区），司法委员会资深成员，今天在监督听证会上质询了国土安全部部长克里斯蒂·诺姆。科恩议员就诺姆部长对他过去一年中多次致函却未予回应一事，以及有关移民和海关执法局（ICE）探员正在驱逐“最恶劣中的最恶劣者”的说法，向诺姆部长提出质询。在与部长的交锋中，科恩议员部分表示：“这让我有机会向你展示我过去一年寄给你的八封信……也让我有机会向你提出问题并试图得到答案。你最出名的一点就是那句‘我们要追查最恶劣中的最恶劣者’——杀人犯、恋童癖者、强奸犯等等。在我的信中，我说我同意你的看法：那些非法居留在这个国家或不是公民并犯下这些罪行的人应该被驱逐出境。事实表明，你们拦截并试图驱逐的大多数人并没有犯下这些罪行。事实上，他们根本没有犯任何罪……“为什么在所有统计数据都表明你们并没有在拦截最恶劣中的最恶劣者时，你还在继续谈论‘最恶劣中的最恶劣者’？……“去追查最恶劣中的最恶劣者吧，如果你们真这么做了，人们就不会认为你的部门是美利坚合众国最糟糕的部门了。”科恩议员还就近期有关ICE探员培训包含让他们违法的“秘密指令”的指控质询了诺姆部长。他还询问她的部门是否聘用了任何1月6日叛乱分子。在此观看完整交锋。科恩议员此前曾呼吁诺姆部长辞职、被解职或面临弹劾程序。# # #\n议题：\n第九选区\n国土安全\n司法\n孟菲斯\n谢尔比县\n田纳西州","publish_source":"cohen.house.gov","publish_time":"2026-03-04T13:10:18-05:00"}},{"id":"news-1457","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"国土安全部长诺姆在与科恩议员交锋后被解职","title_en":"DHS Secretary Noem Fired after Exchange with Congressman Cohen on Wednesday","summary_cn":"众议员史蒂夫·科恩（田纳西州第9选区）对特朗普政府解雇国土安全部部长克里斯蒂·诺姆表示欢迎。此前一天诺姆出席司法委员会监督听证会，科恩质疑其“遣返最恶劣者”的说法，并再次呼吁其辞职、被解职或弹劾。科恩在声明中批评ICE失控、诺姆领导失败，并提及孟菲斯一个阿富汗四口之家被逮捕拘留，称继任者马林应吸取教训。","summary_en":"Rep. Steve Cohen (TN-9) welcomed the Trump administration's firing of DHS Secretary Kristi Noem a day after she appeared before the Judiciary Committee oversight hearing, where he challenged her deportation claims and again called for her removal or impeachment. In his statement, Cohen criticized ICE as out of control and Noem's tenure as failed, citing the detention of an Afghan family of four in Memphis and urging successor Markwayne Mullin to learn from her tenure.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-24T20:33:58.531063+00:00","url":"http://cohen.house.gov/media-center/press-releases/dhs-secretary-noem-fired-after-exchange-congressman-cohen-wednesday","content":"Home\nMedia\nPress Releases\nDHS Secretary Noem Fired after Exchange with Congressman Cohen on Wednesday\nImage\nMarch 5, 2026 Press Release\nAt Judiciary Committee markup on forcing states to enforce immigration law earlier today, he had called again for Secretary Noem’s impeachment\nWASHINGTON – Congressman Steve Cohen (TN-9), a senior member of the Judiciary Committee, welcomed the Trump administration’s decision to fire Department of Homeland Security Secretary Kristi Noem a day after she appeared before the Judiciary Committee at an oversight hearing.  In yesterday’s hearing, Congressman Cohen challenged Secretary Noem on her claim that she was deporting “the worst of the worst.” In remarks at this morning’s markup, Congressman Cohen followed up on his line of questioning, explaining why local law enforcement agencies decline to cooperate with an “out of control” Immigration and Customs Enforcement (ICE) agency. The legislation being considered would force state and local governments to enforce federal immigration law. He again called for Noem’s firing, impeachment or resignation.In response to the announced firing of Noem, Congressman Cohen made the following statement:“Even Donald Trump saw the need to end this 14-month horror show. Noem was in over her head and remained unaccountable until the end. The department has serious work ahead in any attempt to restore its credibility. After killing Americans and destroying the lives of millions of immigrants and their families, Noem’s removal could not come soon enough.  ICE is out of control and reports that her department obstructed its own Trump-appointed inspector general’s efforts to root out wrongdoing underscored Secretary Noem’s lawlessness, cruelty and corruption. She may leave office, but she will not be able to escape the accountability from Congress and the American people. Noem’s successor, Senator Markwayne Mullin, should absorb the many lessons to be learned from her failed tenure.” In his remarks at today’s markup, Congressman Cohen said in part:“There are reasons why cities don’t want to cooperate with ICE. ICE has become recognized as the worst agency in this government. They have no respect for citizens. They do not act like law enforcement. Law enforcement acts with regard to people and to serve them. They wear badges. They have their names on their uniforms. They don’t have masks on. They don’t just come up and break your window and pull you out. And they don’t shoot you in the face or shoot you in the back ten times when you’ve done nothing wrong, certainly nothing violent. They did nothing wrong – Ms. Good and Mr. Pretti – nothing that a law enforcement officer would kill them for because they can only use deadly force under certain circumstances“ICE has gotten totally out of control and this committee needs to do something about it…It’s not really law enforcement; it’s a paramilitary group…We have a paramilitary group operating in our streets in America, taking peoples’ rights away and killing them without oversight, and absolutely it’s Ms. Noem’s fault.“She needs to be impeached if she doesn’t resign…She’s a discredit to this government and to her president.”In his remarks, Congressman Cohen discussed the human toll of these policies, including the arrest and detention of an Afghan family of four in Memphis.See Congressman Cohen’s entire remarks here.# # #\nIssues:\n9th District\nChildren and Families\nGovernment Reform\nHomeland Security\nJudiciary\nMemphis\nShelby County\nTennessee","content_cn":"首页\n媒体\n新闻稿\n国土安全部部长诺姆在周三与科恩众议员交锋后被解职\n图片\n2026年3月5日 新闻稿\n在今天早些时候司法委员会就强制各州执行移民法进行审议时，他再次呼吁弹劾诺姆部长\n\n华盛顿——司法委员会资深成员史蒂夫·科恩众议员（田纳西州第9选区）欢迎特朗普政府决定解职国土安全部部长克里斯蒂·诺姆；此前一天，她曾在一次监督听证会上出席司法委员会。在昨日的听证会上，科恩众议员质疑诺姆部长关于她正在驱逐“最坏中的最坏者”的说法。在今天上午的审议发言中，科恩众议员继续追问，解释了为何地方执法机构拒绝与“失控的”移民与海关执法局（ICE）合作。正在审议的立法将强制州和地方政府执行联邦移民法。他再次呼吁解职、弹劾或要求诺姆辞职。\n\n针对已宣布解职诺姆一事，科恩众议员发表如下声明：\n\n“就连唐纳德·特朗普也看到了结束这场持续14个月的恐怖闹剧的必要性。诺姆能力不及所任，且直到最后仍不承担责任。该部门在任何恢复其公信力的尝试中，都有严肃的工作要做。在造成美国人死亡、摧毁数百万移民及其家人生活之后，诺姆被免职来得再快也不为过。ICE 已经失控，而有报道称她的部门阻挠了由特朗普任命的本部门监察长清除不当行为的努力，这凸显了诺姆部长的无法无天、残酷和腐败。她或许会离开职位，但无法逃避国会和美国人民的问责。诺姆的继任者，参议员马克韦恩·马林，应当吸取她失败任期中能够汲取的诸多教训。”\n\n在今天的审议发言中，科恩众议员部分表示：\n\n“城市不愿与 ICE 合作是有原因的。ICE 已被视为本届政府最糟糕的机构。他们不尊重公民。他们不像执法部门那样行事。执法部门要顾及并服务民众。他们佩戴徽章。他们的制服上有姓名。他们不戴面罩。他们不会只是走上来砸破你的车窗，把你拖出来。他们也不会在你没有做错任何事、当然也没有做任何暴力之事时，朝你的脸开枪，或朝你的背部开十枪。他们没有做错任何事——古德女士和普雷蒂先生——没有任何一件会让执法人员杀死他们的事，因为执法人员只能在特定情形下使用致命武力。\n\n“ICE 已完全失控，本委员会需要对此采取行动……这并不是真正的执法；它是一个准军事组织……我们有一个准军事组织在美国街头活动，剥夺人们的权利、在没有监督的情况下杀害他们，而这绝对是诺姆女士的错。\n\n“如果她不辞职，她就应该被弹劾……她令本政府和她的总统蒙羞。”\n\n在发言中，科恩众议员谈到了这些政策造成的人道代价，其中包括在孟菲斯逮捕并拘留一个四口阿富汗家庭一事。\n\n请在此处查看科恩众议员的完整发言。\n# # #\n议题：\n第9选区\n儿童与家庭\n政府改革\n国土安全\n司法\n孟菲斯\n谢尔比县\n田纳西州","publish_source":"cohen.house.gov","publish_time":"2026-03-05T15:53:03-05:00"}},{"id":"news-1454","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"科尔就众议院投票结束民主党政府停摆并全额资助国土安全部发表声明","title_en":"Cole Statement on House Vote to End Democrat Shutdown and Fully Fund Homeland Security","summary_cn":"2026年3月5日，众议员汤姆·科尔（俄克拉荷马州第4选区）提出的H.R. 7744法案在众议院通过，该法案旨在为美国国土安全部提供全额资金并保护边境。科尔发表声明称，民主党人已使国土安全部停摆数周，导致网络安全行动能力受限、急救人员培训取消、FEMA拨款无法使用、TSA人员无薪工作、海岸警卫队资源不足，并影响美国250周年庆典、世界杯和洛杉矶奥运会等活动的安保准备。他强调保护国土安全不应成为政治筹码。","summary_en":"On March 5, 2026, Congressman Tom Cole's (OK-04) legislation H.R. 7744, which fully funds the Department of Homeland Security and protects the border, passed the House. Cole stated that Democrats have kept DHS shuttered for weeks, leaving cybersecurity operations at limited capacity, canceling first responder training, blocking FEMA grants, forcing TSA officers to work without pay, and under-resourcing the Coast Guard. He noted disruptions to security preparations for America 250, the FIFA World Cup, and LA2028 Olympics, stressing that homeland security should never be a political bargaining chip.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-24T20:33:59.250035+00:00","url":"http://cole.house.gov/media/press-releases/cole-statement-house-vote-end-democrat-shutdown-and-fully-fund-homeland","content":"Cole Statement on House Vote to End Democrat Shutdown and Fully Fund Homeland SecurityMarch 5, 2026 Press ReleaseFOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE | CONTACT: Olivia Porcaro 202-225-6165Washington, D.C. – Today, Congressman Tom Cole’s (OK-04) legislation, H.R. 7744, which is second time legislation to fully fund the Department of Homeland Security (DHS) and protect the nation’s border, passed the House of Representatives. After the legislation passed, Congressman Cole released the following statement:“The Constitution places the safety and security of the American people at the center of the federal government’s responsibilities. It is a duty I don’t take lightly,” said Congressman Cole. “Amidst rising global tensions and natural disaster possibilities, jeopardizing security operations and emergency preparedness is the last thing anyone should be doing. Yet, Democrats have kept the Department of Homeland Security shuttered for weeks – and again voted to keep it that way.”“They are actively choosing to deny resources to the very people responsible for protecting the American homeland. Cybersecurity operations are at limited capacity, as adversaries like Iran, Russia, and China seek to exploit infrastructure vulnerabilities. Training for first responders has been canceled. FEMA grants – utilized by state and local entities to ensure safety and combat terrorism – can’t be accessed. TSA officers are being forced to work through the shutdown while missing paychecks. Coast Guard men and women, including those in harm’s way in Bahrain, are completing missions without full resources behind them. Even security preparations to keep attendees safe at the America 250 celebrations, the FIFA World Cup, the LA2028 Olympics, and more face disruptions. These impacts are not political or hyperbole. They are the direct cost of Democrats’ decision to play politics with the safeguards of this country,” said Congressman Cole.“My priority is serving and protecting Oklahomans and all Americans, which is why I voted again today to pass full-year DHS funding. No selective resourcing – full operational funding for the Department of Homeland Security and the personnel who stand watch over this nation every day. Despite bipartisan majorities in both chambers, a small minority of Democrats continue to hold this funding hostage. However, let me be clear: shielding the homeland should never be treated as a political bargaining chip,” said Congressman Cole.\nIssues:Immigration","content_cn":"科尔就众议院投票结束民主党停摆并为国土安全部提供全额资金发表声明\n2026年3月5日 新闻稿\n立即发布 | 联系人：Olivia Porcaro 202-225-6165\n华盛顿特区——今日，众议员汤姆·科尔（Tom Cole，俄克拉何马州第04选区）的法案H.R. 7744获得众议院通过；这是第二次就为国土安全部（DHS）提供全额资金并保护国家边境进行立法。法案通过后，科尔众议员发表如下声明：\n“宪法将美国人民的安全与保障置于联邦政府职责的核心。我绝不轻视这一责任，”科尔众议员表示。“在全球紧张局势加剧以及可能发生自然灾害之际，危及安全行动和应急准备，是任何人最不该做的事情。然而，民主党人已让国土安全部停摆数周——并再次投票决定维持这种局面。”\n“他们正在主动选择拒绝向那些负责保护美国本土的人提供资源。随着伊朗、俄罗斯和中国等对手试图利用基础设施漏洞，网络安全行动的能力受到限制。急救人员培训已被取消。各州和地方实体用于确保安全及打击恐怖主义的FEMA拨款无法获取。运输安全管理局（TSA）官员在停摆期间被迫继续工作，却领不到薪水。海岸警卫队男女官兵，包括在巴林身处危险地区的人员，正在缺乏完整资源支持的情况下执行任务。就连保障美国250周年庆祝活动、国际足联世界杯、LA2028奥运会等活动参与者安全的安保准备也面临中断。这些影响并非政治说辞，也非夸大其词。它们是民主党人决定拿国家安全保障玩政治的直接代价，”科尔众议员表示。\n“我的首要任务是服务并保护俄克拉何马州民众和所有美国人，因此我今天再次投票通过国土安全部的全年拨款。不是选择性提供资源——而是为国土安全部及每日守卫这个国家的人员提供全额运营资金。尽管两院均有跨党派多数支持，少数民主党人仍继续将这笔资金扣作人质。不过，请允许我说清楚：保护本土绝不应被视作政治谈判的筹码，”科尔众议员表示。\n\n议题：移民","publish_source":"cole.house.gov","publish_time":"2026-03-05T17:05:56-05:00"}},{"id":"news-1762","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"科尔投票支持国防、劳工卫生与公众服务教育、交通住房与城市发展及国土安全拨款法案","title_en":"Cole Votes in Favor of Defense; Labor, Health and Human Services, Education; Transportation, Housing, and Urban Development; and Homeland Security Appropriations Packages","summary_cn":"2026年1月22日，众议员汤姆·科尔（俄克拉荷马州第4选区）投票支持H.R. 7149《2026年综合拨款法案》和H.R. 7147《2026年国土安全部拨款法案》。科尔表示，国土安全拨款法案为加强边境安全及保护美国本土免受恐怖分子、毒贩、罪犯等威胁提供了必要投资。法案包括维持22,000名边境巡逻人员、38亿美元拘留行动资金、4.2亿美元用于网络安全和基础设施安全局（CISA）应对中国威胁等条款。众议院已完成全部十二项2026财年拨款法案的通过。","summary_en":"On January 22, 2026, Congressman Tom Cole (OK-04) voted for H.R. 7149, the Consolidated Appropriations Act of 2026, and H.R. 7147, the Department of Homeland Security Appropriations Act of 2026. Cole said the DHS funding bill provides investments in border security and protects the homeland from terrorists, narco-traffickers, and criminals. Key provisions include $513 million for 22,000 Border Patrol agents, $3.8 billion for custody operations, and $420 million for CISA to counter China. The House completed all twelve FY2026 funding bills.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-24T20:42:17.515215+00:00","url":"http://cole.house.gov/media/press-releases/cole-votes-favor-defense-labor-health-and-human-services-education","content":"Cole Votes in Favor of Defense; Labor, Health and Human Services, Education; Transportation, Housing, and Urban Development; and Homeland Security Appropriations PackagesJanuary 22, 2026 Press ReleaseFOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE | CONTACT: Olivia Porcaro 202-225-6165Washington, D.C. – Today, Congressman Tom Cole (OK-04) voted in favor of H.R. 7149, the Consolidated Appropriations Act of 2026, which includes funding for Defense; Labor, Health, and Human Services, Education; and Transportation, Housing, and Urban Development, and H.R. 7147, the Department of Homeland Security Appropriations Act of 2026. After voting in favor of the bills, Congressman Cole released the following statement:“Over the past 250 years in America, we have created the greatest volunteer military in the world, made significant medical advances through biomedical research, improved transportation through the Interstate Highway System, and transformed security preparedness across all domains. Today, in passing these full-year funding measures, we recognized that legacy and our obligation to carry it forward,” said Congressman Cole.“These bills champion American military power, support lifesaving biomedical research and resilient medical supply chains, and back the growth of America’s transportation sector. Additionally, the Homeland Security funding bill provides for much-needed investments into enhanced border security, as well as other measures essential to protecting the American homeland from terrorists, narco-traffickers, criminals, and other bad actors who wish us harm,” said Congressman Cole.“Today, the House of Representatives finished the job, as we have now officially passed all twelve funding bills for the Fiscal Year 2026. Subcommittee Chairmen Calvert, Aderholt, Womack, and Amodei have worked hard to get this legislation across the finish line, and I look forward to seeing it placed on President Trump’s desk,” said Congressman Cole.  Key Provisions in the Defense; Labor, Health, and Human Services, Education; Transportation, Housing, and Urban Development; and Homeland Security Appropriations Acts of 2026DefenseChampions American military superiority enhancing investments in 5th and 6th generation aircraft.Boosts production of munitions critical to winning conflicts with pacing adversaries like China.Provides $13.3 billion for Special Operations Forces operations, equipment, and capabilities development.Provides a 3.8% pay raise for all servicemembers.Provides a 1% civilian employee pay increase.Combats international actors who facilitate drug manufacturing and trafficking into our country.Ensures no funding for diversity, equity, and inclusion (DEI) programs, Critical Race Theory, or abortion-related travel at the Pentagon.Labor, Health, and Human Services, EducationProtects the right to life by maintaining the Hyde Amendment, which prohibits taxpayer funding for abortion on demand.Maintains the Dickey Amendment, which ensures that federal funds cannot be used to advocate or promote restrictions to Second Amendment rights.Rescinds the Biden Administration’s massive expansion of the IRS.Champions President Trump and Secretary Kennedy’s Make America Healthy Again (MAHA) agenda.Increases funding to train workers and educate students in rural America.Provides $48.7 billion to ensure America remains the pioneer in biomedical research.Prioritizes increased funding for the Social Security Administration to enhance frontline customer service provided directly for America’s seniors.Transportation, Housing, and Urban DevelopmentIncreases funding for the Federal Aviation Administration (FAA) by $1.588 billion, which will keep our skies safe and help build a world-class air traffic control system.Provides the FAA with resources to hire 2,500 new air traffic controllers.Invests in highway and airport infrastructure.Codifies DOGE recommendations to reduce the federal bureaucracy at Transportation, Housing, and Urban Development agencies by 29%.Reinforces citizenship requirements for housing assistance.Prohibits the Department of Transportation from enforcing COVID-19 mask mandates on public transportation conveyances and transportation hubs.Maintains “Buy American” provisions.Homeland SecurityRealigns the Department of Homeland Security’s priorities around its fundamental mission: defending the nation against the threat imposed by terrorists, criminals, and foreign adversaries to ensure the safety and security of every American.Enhances resources to detect and counter the spread of deadly drugs.Partners with state and local law enforcement to enhance immigration enforcement and homeland defense capabilities.Bolsters disaster preparedness, response, and recovery efforts for U.S. communities through increased grant funding for firefighters and first responders.Includes a military pay raise for Coast Guard servicemembers.Provides $513 million to sustain 22,000 Border Patrol agents, $3.8 billion for custody operations to strengthen this Administration’s efforts to detain and deport all criminal and removable aliens, and $420 million to hire critical positions at the Cybersecurity and Infrastructure Security Agency (CISA) to counter the threat from China.Ends programs that incentivize illegal immigration. Oklahoma Priorities/ Congressman Cole Secured in the Defense; Labor, Health, and Human Services, Education; Transportation, Housing, and Urban Development; and Homeland Security Appropriations Acts of 2026Defense$715 million for Paladin Integrate Management to support ammunition operations and testing at Fort Sill.$740 million for programs that support operations, soldier health, and counter-UAS advancements at Fort Sill.Includes language to safeguard and prevent the closure of the Fort Sill National Historic Landmark and Museum.$1.1 billion for research, development, test, and evaluation of the E-7 Wedgetail to help accelerate this replacement for the aging E-3 AWACS platform at Tinker Air Force Base.Includes language to protect and bolster the E-7 Wedgetail aircraft program and prohibits funds to pause, cancel, or terminate the program.$1.17 billion for programs that support operations at Tinker Air Force Base including advancements in additive manufacturing and 3D printing capabilities.$17 million for the Indian Incentive Program to support Native American economic development initiatives.$1.043 billion for TACAMO Modernization to support the Navy’s strategic command missions at Tinker Air Force Base.Over $180 million for programs and industry support located within the Fires Innovation Science and Technology Accelerator (FISTA) in Lawton, Oklahoma. This includes support for advancements in counter-UAS, AI implementation, and surveillance technology.Over $160 million for advancements in radar technology, MRADS, software innovations, and fuel capability enhancements in partnership or led by the University of Oklahoma.Over $256 million in cutting-edge technologies and innovations spearheaded by industries in Lawton, Ardmore, Chickasha, Duncan, and Oklahoma City.Labor, Health, and Human Services, Education3 to 13% in tribal set-asides for National Health Service Corps Loan Repayment Program, Tribal Epidemiology Centers, Child Care and Development Block Grant, and opioid response grants.$207.4 million for tribal behavioral grants for substance abuse prevention and mental health programs.$6 million for Tribal minority HIV/AIDS Prevention and Treatment program.Includes language supporting a National Rural Water Apprenticeship Program to promote workforce development and opportunities.$116.8 million for Native American Caregiver, Nutrition Support Services, and Native American training and employment programs.$67.8 million for Tribally Controlled Colleges, Universities, and Postsecondary Career and Technical Institutions.$602.9 million for universal flu vaccine research, pandemic influenza preparedness, and Infectious Disease Rapid Response Reserve Fund.$415 million increase for the National Institutes of Health (NIH).$100 million increase in Alzheimer’s disease research funding across the NIH.$75 million for Medical Student Education grants to improve primary care physician training in rural and underserved areas.$27 million for the Good Health and Wellness in Indian Country program to promote chronic disease prevention in Tribal communities.$735 million in Public Health Emergency Preparedness Cooperative Agreement Program, which aids public health departments to respond effectively to public health threats.$450.95 million for the Institutional Development Award Program (IDeA), which increases biomedical research capacity in States with the lowest levels of NIH funding.$63.5 million for Native American social and economic programs to improve the wellbeing of Native people and local economy.$9 million for the Improving Native American Cancer Outcomes Program to address higher cancer incidence and mortality among Native Americans.$12.4 million in funding for Head Start.$1.05 billion for Biomedical Advanced Research and Development Authority (BARDA).$850 million for Project Bioshield, a secure funding source for the purchase of critical medical countermeasures, such as vaccines, therapeutics, and diagnostics.$1 billion for the Strategic National Stockpile.$1.191 billion for TRIO.$388 million for GEAR UP.$13 million for Rural Community Facilities Technical Assistance Program.$4.045 billion for the Low Income Home Energy Assistance Program.Report language requiring CDC funds to State health departments be passed through to local health departments.$10 million for the ALS Registry.$2.1 million for Interstitial Cystitis research.$6 million for the Center for Indigenous Innovation and Health.$440 million for the Charter Schools Program.Report language promoting training and technical assistance to Community Health Centers.$14.365 million for national activities within the Office of Indian Education.$1.477 billion for Impact Aid Basic Support Payments, which provides support for federally impacted schools that don’t receive traditional funding through local taxes, such as schools serving a high percentage of military or Native American students.$38 million for Special Olympics.$185 million in state grants for employment and training services for veterans.$3 million for Strengthening State Indian Child Welfare Act Compliance.Transportation, Housing, and Urban Development$7 million for Haliburton Field Improvements at Duncan Municipal Airport.$15 million for Ada Regional Airport improvements.$17.1 million for the University of Oklahoma Westheimer Airport improvements.$3.96 million for the City of Lindsay’s New Electrical Substation.$4.34 million for the Walters Public Works Authority Substation Rebuild and Capacity Enhancement Project.$5 million for the City of Lawton’s Alternate Water Supply.$6.286 million for the Pauls Valley Lake Emergency Overflow Spillway project.$7 million for Goldsby Municipal Water improvements.$7.5 million for Ardmore Storm Water and Street improvements.$8.45 million for the Chickasaw Nation Water Quality and Hazardous Substance Testing Center.$11.5 million for the Fires Innovation Science and Technology Accelerator’s (FISTA) Science and Technology Convergence Institute.$12 million for the Newcastle Wastewater Treatment Facility.$4 million for the FAA to continue the work established in Fiscal Year 2024 at the Mike Monroney Aeronautical Center, in partnership with aviation manufacturers, to accelerate testing, certification, and the implementation of new radio altimeter capabilities consistent with the next generation of avionics standards.Includes language preventing funds to be used for the construction of a second Air Traffic Control Training Academy.$13.71 billion for FAA operations.$4 billion for FAA facilities and equipment.$1.236 billion for the Native American housing block grant program.$200 million for the Tribal transportation program.$1.8 million for the Indian housing guarantee fund program.$1 million for the Title VI Loan Program under the Native American Housing Assistance and Self-Determination Act of 1996 (NAHASDA).$10 million for the Tribal HUD-VASH program.$14 million for Unmanned Aircraft System (UAS) research that will support the FAA in their mission to integrate UAS into the National Airspace System, complimenting the work being done at the University of Oklahoma.$158 million for the Neighborhood Reinvestment Corporation.$57.5 million for housing counseling assistance at HUD.$1.031 billion for housing for the elderly.$529 million for housing opportunities for people with AIDS.$5 million to support the wide adoption of multiple technologies that provide the necessary GPS backup and complementary position, navigation, and timing.$3.3 billion for the community development block grant program at HUD.$10 million to test the utilization of high-powered microwave systems in the national airspace system to defend against unmanned aircraft systems (UAS) at the Mike Monroney Aeronautical Center.$7.426 million for consolidated rail infrastructure and safety improvements.$10 million to address lead and other residential environmental stressors in low-income communities in older housing stock.Homeland Security$48 million for the Next Generation Warning System Grant Program that funds public safety communications infrastructure.$11.4 million for the National Dam Safety grants to assist states in mitigating and repairing high risk dams.$494 million for the State Homeland Security Program, which funds the Oklahoma Counter Terrorism Intelligence Center (OCTIC).$14.25 million provided for the Tribal Homeland Security Grant Program.$5 million for Long-Endurance Unmanned Aircraft Systems within CBP, which are currently developed at Fort Sill.###\nIssues:Defense, National Security & Foreign AffairsEducationHealthcareImmigrationLifeSecond AmendmentTransportationTribal RelationsVeterans & Military Retirees","content_cn":"科尔投票支持国防；劳工、卫生与公众服务、教育；交通、住房与城市发展；以及国土安全拨款方案\n2026年1月22日 新闻稿\n立即发布 | 联系人：Olivia Porcaro 202-225-6165\n华盛顿特区——今天，众议员汤姆·科尔（俄克拉何马州第4选区）投票支持H.R. 7149《2026年综合拨款法案》，该法案包括国防；劳工、卫生与公众服务、教育；以及交通、住房与城市发展的拨款；以及H.R. 7147《2026年国土安全部拨款法案》。在投票支持这些法案后，科尔众议员发表了以下声明：\n“在美国过去250年里，我们建立了世界上最强大的志愿役军队，通过生物医学研究取得了重大的医疗进步，通过州际公路系统改善了交通，并在所有领域推动了安全准备工作的转型。今天，在通过这些全年拨款措施时，我们铭记了这一遗产，也认识到我们有义务将其传承下去，”科尔众议员说。\n“这些法案彰显美国军事实力，支持拯救生命的生物医学研究和富有韧性的医疗供应链，并支持美国交通部门的发展。此外，国土安全拨款法案还为加强边境安全提供了急需的投资，以及其他对于保护美国国土免受恐怖分子、毒品贩运者、罪犯和其他企图伤害我们的不法分子侵害所必需的措施，”科尔众议员说。\n“今天，众议院完成了这项工作，因为我们现在已经正式通过了2026财年的全部12项拨款法案。小组委员会主席卡尔弗特、阿德霍尔特、沃马克和阿莫代伊为推动这项立法最终完成付出了艰苦努力，我期待看到它被送交特朗普总统的办公桌，”科尔众议员说。\n\n2026年国防；劳工、卫生与公众服务、教育；交通、住房与城市发展；以及国土安全拨款法案的主要条款\n国防\n通过加强对第五代和第六代飞机的投资，捍卫美国的军事优势。\n提高对赢得与中国等步调竞争对手冲突至关重要的弹药产量。\n为特种作战部队的行动、装备和能力开发提供133亿美元。\n为所有军人加薪3.8%。\n为文职雇员加薪1%。\n打击促成毒品制造并将毒品贩运进入我国的国际行为者。\n确保五角大楼不为多元、公平与包容（DEI）项目、批判种族理论或与堕胎有关的出行提供资金。\n劳工、卫生与公众服务、教育\n通过维持《海德修正案》保护生命权，该修正案禁止纳税人资金用于按需堕胎。\n维持《迪基修正案》，确保联邦资金不得用于倡导或推动限制第二修正案权利的措施。\n撤销拜登政府对国税局的大规模扩张。\n支持特朗普总统和肯尼迪部长的“让美国再次健康”（MAHA）议程。\n增加资金，用于培训美国农村地区的工人和教育学生。\n提供487亿美元，确保美国继续成为生物医学研究的先驱。\n优先增加对社会保障管理局的资金，以改善直接为\n美国老年人。交通、住房和城市发展增加联邦航空管理局（FAA）15.88亿美元的资金，这将确保我们的空域安全，并帮助建设世界一流的空中交通管制系统。为FAA提供资源，聘用2500名新的空中交通管制员。投资公路和机场基础设施。将DOGE关于将交通、住房和城市发展机构联邦官僚机构削减29%的建议编入法典。强化住房援助的公民身份要求。禁止交通部在公共交通工具和交通枢纽执行新冠疫情口罩强制令。维持“购买美国货”条款。国土安全部围绕其根本使命重新调整国土安全部的优先事项：保护国家免受恐怖分子、犯罪分子和外国对手构成的威胁，确保每一位美国人的安全与保障。加强侦测和遏制致命毒品扩散的资源。与州和地方执法部门合作，增强移民执法和国土防御能力。通过增加对消防员和第一响应人员的拨款，强化美国社区的灾害准备、应对和恢复工作。包括为海岸警卫队军人的军事加薪。提供5.13亿美元以维持2.2万名边境巡逻人员，提供38亿美元用于羁押行动，以加强本届政府拘押并驱逐所有犯罪分子和可被遣返外国人的努力，并提供4.2亿美元在网络安全与基础设施安全局（CISA）聘用关键岗位人员，以应对来自中国的威胁。终止激励非法移民的项目。俄克拉何马州优先事项／科尔议员在2026年《国防拨款法》《劳工、卫生与公共服务、教育拨款法》《交通、住房与城市发展拨款法》和《国土安全拨款法》中争取到的项目国防部为帕拉丁综合管理公司提供7.15亿美元，用于支持锡尔堡的弹药业务和测试。为支持锡尔堡的行动、士兵健康和反无人机系统技术进步提供7.4亿美元。纳入相关措辞，以保障并防止关闭锡尔堡国家历史地标和博物馆。为E-7“楔尾”飞机的研究、开发、测试和评估提供11亿美元，以帮助加速该机型在廷克空军基地替代老旧E-3“望楼”预警机平台。纳入相关措辞，以保护并加强E-7“楔尾”飞机项目，并禁止使用资金暂停、取消或终止该项目。为支持廷克空军基地行动的项目提供11.7亿美元，包括增材制造和3D打印能力的提升。为印第安人激励计划提供1700万美元，以支持美国原住民经济发展倡议。为TACAMO现代化提供10.43亿美元，以支持海军在廷克空军基地的战略指挥任务。在俄克拉何马州劳顿的火力创新科学与技术加速器（FISTA）内的项目和产业支持超过1.8亿美元，其中包括支持反无人机系统、人工智能实施和监视技术的进步。为与俄克拉何马大学合作或由其牵头的雷达技术、MRADS、软件创新和燃料能力提升提供超过1.6亿美元。为由……牵头的尖端技术和创新提供超过2.56亿美元\n劳顿、阿德莫尔、奇克沙、邓肯和俄克拉何马城的产业。劳动、卫生与公共服务、教育：在国家卫生服务队贷款偿还计划、部落流行病学中心、儿童保育与发展整笔拨款以及阿片类药物应对拨款的部落专项资金中划拨3%至13%。为部落行为健康拨款提供2.074亿美元，用于药物滥用预防和心理健康项目。为部落少数族裔艾滋病毒/艾滋病预防与治疗项目提供600万美元。包括支持建立国家农村供水学徒计划的条款，以促进劳动力发展和就业机会。为美洲原住民照护者、营养支持服务以及美洲原住民培训和就业项目提供1.168亿美元。为部落控制的学院、大学以及高等教育职业和技术院校提供6780万美元。为通用流感疫苗研究、流感大流行准备工作和传染病快速响应储备基金提供6.029亿美元。为国立卫生研究院（NIH）增加4.15亿美元。为NIH的阿尔茨海默病研究经费增加1亿美元。为医学学生教育拨款提供7500万美元，以改善农村和服务不足地区的初级保健医生培训。为“印第安地区良好健康与保健”项目提供2700万美元，以促进部落社区慢性病预防。为公共卫生紧急准备合作协议项目提供7.35亿美元，该项目帮助公共卫生部门有效应对公共卫生威胁。为机构发展奖助计划（IDeA）提供4.5095亿美元，该计划提高NIH资助水平最低的州的生物医学研究能力。为美洲原住民社会和经济项目提供6350万美元，以改善原住民福祉和当地经济。为改善美洲原住民癌症结局项目提供900万美元，以应对美洲原住民较高的癌症发病率和死亡率。为启蒙计划提供1240万美元。为生物医学高级研究与开发管理局（BARDA）提供10.5亿美元。为生物盾牌项目提供8.5亿美元，该项目为购买疫苗、治疗药物和诊断工具等关键医疗对策提供安全资金来源。为国家战略储备提供10亿美元。为TRIO提供11.91亿美元。为GEAR UP提供3.88亿美元。为农村社区设施技术援助计划提供1300万美元。为低收入家庭能源援助计划提供40.45亿美元。报告性条款要求，提供给州卫生部门的疾病控制与预防中心资金必须转拨给地方卫生部门。为肌萎缩性侧索硬化症登记处提供1000万美元。为间质性膀胱炎研究提供210万美元。为原住民创新与健康中心提供600万美元。为特许学校计划提供4.4亿美元。报告性条款促进向社区卫生中心提供培训和技术援助。为印第安教育办公室的国家活动提供1436.5万美元。为影响援助基本支持付款提供14.77亿美元，该计划为受联邦影响但未通过地方税收获得传统资金的学校提供支持，例如军人或美洲原住民学生比例较高的学校。为特殊奥林匹克运动会提供3800万美元。为退伍军人就业和培训服务提供1.85亿美元州拨款。为加强各州遵守《印第安儿童福利法》提供300万美元。交通、住房与城市发展：为邓肯市政机场的哈利伯顿机场改进提供700万美元。\n机场。$15 million用于Ada Regional Airport改进。$17.1 million用于University of Oklahoma Westheimer Airport改进。$3.96 million用于City of Lindsay新建电力变电站。$4.34 million用于Walters Public Works Authority变电站重建和容量提升项目。$5 million用于City of Lawton备用供水。$6.286 million用于Pauls Valley Lake紧急溢洪道项目。$7 million用于Goldsby市政供水改进。$7.5 million用于Ardmore雨水和街道改进。$8.45 million用于Chickasaw Nation水质和危险物质检测中心。$11.5 million用于Fires Innovation Science and Technology Accelerator（FISTA）科学与技术融合研究所。$12 million用于Newcastle污水处理设施。$4 million用于FAA继续在Mike Monroney Aeronautical Center开展财政年度2024年确立的工作，与航空制造商合作，加快测试、认证以及实施符合下一代航空电子标准的新型无线电高度计能力。包括禁止将资金用于建设第二所空中交通管制培训学院的条款。$13.71 billion用于FAA运营。$4 billion用于FAA设施和设备。$1.236 billion用于美国原住民住房整笔拨款项目。$200 million用于部落交通项目。$1.8 million用于印第安人住房担保基金项目。$1 million用于1996年《美国原住民住房援助和自决法案》（NAHASDA）下的Title VI贷款项目。$10 million用于部落HUD-VASH项目。$14 million用于无人机系统（UAS）研究，以支持FAA将UAS整合进国家空域系统的使命，并补充University of Oklahoma正在开展的工作。$158 million用于Neighborhood Reinvestment Corporation。$57.5 million用于HUD住房咨询援助。$1.031 billion用于老年人住房。$529 million用于艾滋病患者住房机会。$5 million用于支持广泛采用多种技术，这些技术提供必要的GPS备份以及辅助定位、导航和授时。$3.3 billion用于HUD社区发展整笔拨款项目。$10 million用于在Mike Monroney Aeronautical Center测试在国家空域系统中利用高功率微波系统防御无人机系统（UAS）。$7.426 million用于综合铁路基础设施和安全改进。$10 million用于解决低收入社区老旧住房存量中的铅污染及其他住宅环境压力因素。\n国土安全\n$48 million用于下一代预警系统拨款项目，为公共安全通信基础设施提供资金。$11.4 million用于国家大坝安全拨款，帮助各州缓解和修复高风险大坝。$494 million用于州国土安全项目，该项目为Oklahoma Counter Terrorism Intelligence Center（OCTIC）提供资金。$14.25 million用于部落国土安全拨款项目。$5 million用于CBP内部的长续航无人机系统，这些系统目前在Fort Sill开发。\n###\n议题：国防、国家安全与外交事务\n教育\n医疗保健\n移民\n生活\n第二修正案\n交通\n部落关系\n退伍军人与军事退休人员","publish_source":"cole.house.gov","publish_time":"2026-01-22T16:55:51-05:00"}},{"id":"news-919","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"中央谷地议员敦促国土安全部及美国公民及移民服务局解决DACA处理严重延误问题","title_en":"Central Valley Members Urge DHS, USCIS to Address Extreme DACA Processing Delays","summary_cn":"2026年5月21日，众议员吉姆·科斯塔（加州第21选区）、亚当·格雷（加州第13选区）、大卫·瓦拉道（加州第22选区）和乔什·哈德（加州第9选区）致信美国国土安全部（DHS）部长马克韦恩·马林及美国公民及移民服务局（USCIS）局长约瑟夫·埃德洛，敦促其立即解决DACA续签申请处理的严重延误。议员们指出，许多案件已等待超过六个月，DACA受益人在中央谷地担任急救人员、教育工作者、公交司机和医疗专业人员，延误对家庭、雇主和当地经济造成严重影响。加州拥有全国超过27%的活跃DACA受益人。","summary_en":"On May 21, 2026, Representatives Jim Costa (CA-21), Adam Gray (CA-13), David Valadao (CA-22), and Josh Harder (CA-09) urged the U.S. Department of Homeland Security (DHS) and U.S. Citizenship and Immigration Services (USCIS) to address significant delays in DACA renewal processing. In a letter to DHS Secretary Markwayne Mullin and USCIS Director Joseph Edlow, they noted many cases pending over six months, affecting DACA recipients working as first responders, educators, bus drivers, and healthcare professionals in California's Central Valley. California is home to over 27 percent of active DACA recipients nationwide.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-24T20:17:31.069644+00:00","url":"http://costa.house.gov/media/press-releases/central-valley-members-urge-dhs-uscis-address-extreme-daca-processing-delays","content":"Image\nHome\nMedia\nPress Releases\nCentral Valley Members Urge DHS, USCIS to Address Extreme DACA Processing DelaysMay 21, 2026 Press ReleaseWASHINGTON — Representatives Jim Costa (CA-21), Adam Gray (CA-13), David Valadao (CA-22), and Josh Harder (CA-09) are urging the U.S. Department of Homeland Security (DHS) and U.S. Citizenship and Immigration Services (USCIS) to immediately address significant delays in processing Deferred Action for Childhood Arrivals (DACA) renewal requests affecting communities across California’s Central Valley.In a letter sent to DHS Secretary Markwayne Mullin and USCIS Director Joseph Edlow, the lawmakers raised concerns over growing processing backlogs that are leaving DACA recipients in limbo and creating serious consequences for families, employers, and local economies throughout the region.“DACA individuals follow strict rules to comply with the renewal program and are valued members in our respective congressional districts located throughout the Central Valley of California. These recipients are employed as first responders, educators, bus drivers, and healthcare professionals,” the members wrote. “Our collective offices have seen a tremendous increase in DACA cases; many that are still pending after six months. This is unacceptable and we are asking for a thorough review of the extreme delay in processing DACA renewal cases.”California is home to more than 27 percent of all active DACA recipients nationwide, many of whom live and work in the Central Valley.The lawmakers are calling on DHS and USCIS to conduct a thorough review of the delays and take immediate action to ensure DACA renewal requests are processed in a timely manner.To read the full letter, click HERE.\nIssues:Immigration","content_cn":"图片\n首页\n媒体\n新闻稿\n中央谷地议员敦促DHS、USCIS解决DACA处理严重延误问题\n2026年5月21日 新闻稿\n华盛顿——众议员Jim Costa（CA-21）、Adam Gray（CA-13）、David Valadao（CA-22）和Josh Harder（CA-09）正在敦促美国国土安全部（DHS）和美国公民及移民服务局（USCIS）立即解决延期遣返儿童入境者行动（DACA）续期申请处理严重延误的问题。这一问题正影响加利福尼亚州中央谷地各地的社区。\n在致DHS部长Markwayne Mullin和USCIS局长Joseph Edlow的信中，这些议员对不断增加的处理积压表示担忧；积压使DACA受益人陷入悬而未决的状态，并给该地区的家庭、雇主和地方经济造成严重后果。\n“DACA人员遵守严格规定，以符合续期计划的要求，并且是我们各自位于加利福尼亚州中央谷地的国会选区中受到重视的成员。这些受益人从事急救响应、教育、公交驾驶和医疗保健等工作，”议员们写道。“我们的联合办公室看到DACA案件数量大幅增加；其中许多案件在六个月后仍处于待处理状态。这是不可接受的，我们要求对DACA续期案件处理严重延误的问题进行彻底审查。”\n加利福尼亚州拥有全国所有活跃DACA受益人的逾27%，其中许多人在中央谷地生活和工作。\n这些议员呼吁DHS和USCIS对延误进行彻底审查，并立即采取行动，确保DACA续期申请得到及时处理。\n要阅读完整信件，请点击此处。\n\n议题：移民","publish_source":"costa.house.gov","publish_time":"2026-05-21T18:08:04-04:00"}},{"id":"news-1098","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"杰弗里斯领袖：今天就把两党参议院通过的国土安全法案提交众议院表决","title_en":"LEADER JEFFRIES: \"BRING THE BIPARTISAN SENATE-PASSED DHS BILL TO THE HOUSE FLOOR TODAY\"","summary_cn":"2026年4月27日，众议院民主党领袖杰弗里斯举行记者会，批评共和党人宁愿屈从特朗普的极端大规模驱逐议程，也不愿为国土安全部雇员提供资金。他指出参议院两党法案已在众议院搁置数周，该法案可全额资助特勤局、TSA、FEMA、海岸警卫队和网络安全人员，呼吁立即提交表决。","summary_en":"On April 27, 2026, House Democratic Leader Jeffries held a press availability, criticizing Republicans for bending to Trump's extreme mass deportation agenda rather than funding DHS employees. He noted a bipartisan Senate-passed bill has languished in the House for weeks, which would fully fund the Secret Service, TSA, FEMA, Coast Guard, and cybersecurity professionals, and called for an immediate vote.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-18T14:31:17.710721+00:00","url":"http://democraticleader.house.gov/media/press-releases/leader-jeffries-bring-bipartisan-senate-passed-dhs-bill-house-floor-today","content":"Home\nMedia\nPress Releases\nLEADER JEFFRIES: \"BRING THE BIPARTISAN SENATE-PASSED DHS BILL TO THE HOUSE FLOOR TODAY\"\nApril 27, 2026 Press Release\nToday, House Democratic Leader Hakeem Jeffries held a press availability, where he emphasized that Republican sycophants would rather bend the knee to Trump’s extreme mass deportation agenda than fund the programs that pay our Department of Homeland Security employees and keep Americans safe.\nImage\nLEADER JEFFRIES: Donald Trump and House Republicans have now shut down the Department of Homeland Security for more than 70 days because Donald Trump and Republicans want to continue to drive their extreme immigration agenda and violent mass deportation machine led by ICE down the throats of the American people. Several weeks ago, a bill was sent over from the United States Senate that was supported by every single Republican and every single Democrat in the Senate. It's a bipartisan bill that has been languishing in the House of Representatives. We can bring that bill to the Floor today, and it would fully fund the United State Secret Service. Why is Mike Johnson and House Republicans continuing to refuse to bring that bipartisan bill to the Floor that would fund TSA, it would fund the Secret Service, it would fund FEMA, it would fund the Coast Guard and it would fund the cybersecurity professionals at the Department of Homeland Security who are working hard to keep us safe? Instead, it's House Republicans that continue to play partisan political games. If they really do believe we need to act swiftly, there's a vehicle to do it. Bring the bipartisan Senate-passed bill to the House Floor today and it would fund the Department of Homeland Security in its entirety with the exception of ICE and the violent Republican mass deportation machine.Full availability can be watched here.\nPress Releases\nLEADER JEFFRIES: \"THE AMERICAN PEOPLE HAVE HAD ENOUGH OF DONALD TRUMP AND THE FAILED REPUBLICAN ECONOMY\"21 hours ago\nJOINT DEMOCRATIC LEADERSHIP STATEMENT ON H.R. 53341 day ago\nInstagram\nView this profile on Instagram\nHakeem Jeffries (@hakeemjeffries) • Instagram photos and videos","content_cn":"首页\n媒体\n新闻稿\n领袖杰弗里斯：“今天就把参议院两党通过的国土安全部法案提交众议院表决”\n2026年4月27日 新闻稿\n今天，众议院民主党领袖哈基姆·杰弗里斯举行了媒体见面会，他强调共和党的谄媚者宁愿向特朗普的极端大规模驱逐议程屈膝，也不愿为支付我们国土安全部员工薪资、保障美国人安全的项目提供资金。\n图片\n领袖杰弗里斯：唐纳德·特朗普和众议院共和党人现在已经让国土安全部停摆超过70天，因为唐纳德·特朗普和共和党人想继续把他们由ICE主导的极端移民议程和暴力大规模驱逐机器强加给美国人民。几周前，美国参议院送来了一项法案，该法案得到了参议院每一位共和党人和每一位民主党人的支持。这是一项两党法案，却一直在众议院搁置。我们今天就可以把这项法案提交到院会表决，它将为美国特勤局提供全额资金。为什么迈克·约翰逊和众议院共和党人继续拒绝将这项两党法案提交院会表决？该法案将为运输安全管理局（TSA）提供资金，为特勤局提供资金，为联邦紧急事务管理局（FEMA）提供资金，为海岸警卫队提供资金，还将为国土安全部那些努力保障我们网络安全的专业人员提供资金。相反，是众议院共和党人继续玩弄党派政治游戏。如果他们真的认为我们需要迅速行动，是有途径可以做到的。今天就把参议院两党通过的法案提交众议院院会表决，它将为国土安全部提供全部资金，但ICE和共和党那台暴力大规模驱逐机器除外。完整见面会可在此观看。\n新闻稿\n领袖杰弗里斯：“美国人民已经受够了唐纳德·特朗普和失败的共和党经济”21小时前\n民主党领导层关于H.R. 5334的联合声明1天前\nInstagram\n在Instagram上查看此个人资料\n哈基姆·杰弗里斯（@hakeemjeffries）• Instagram照片和视频","publish_source":"democraticleader.house.gov","publish_time":"2026-04-27T17:37:02-04:00"}},{"id":"news-1607","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"德劳罗就国土安全部资金中断发表声明","title_en":"DeLauro Statement on Homeland Security Funding Lapse","summary_cn":"众议院拨款委员会民主党首席成员德劳罗就国土安全部资金到期发表声明，指责共和党导致资金中断，使TSA人员无薪工作，并削减救灾资金，影响海岸警卫队、特勤局和网络安全人员。她称民主党要求对ICE和CBP实施改革，包括申请搜查令、禁止蒙面、禁止种族定性等，并提到她已提出H.R. 7481法案，为国土安全部除ICE、CBP和部长办公室外的部分提供资金。","summary_en":"House Appropriations Committee Ranking Member Rosa DeLauro issued a statement on the lapse in Department of Homeland Security funding, blaming Republicans for forcing TSA officers to work without pay and reducing disaster relief, Coast Guard, Secret Service and cybersecurity resources. She said Democrats demand reforms to ICE and CBP, including warrants, bans on masks and racial profiling, and noted she introduced H.R. 7481 to fund DHS except ICE, CBP and the Office of the Secretary.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-24T20:37:53.144034+00:00","url":"http://democrats-appropriations.house.gov/news/press-releases/delauro-statement-homeland-security-funding-lapse","content":"Image\nHome\nNews\nPress Releases\nDeLauro Statement on Homeland Security Funding LapseFebruary 13, 2026 Press ReleaseWASHINGTON – Today, House Appropriations Committee Ranking Member Rosa DeLauro (D-CT-03) released the following statement ahead of a lapse in funding for the Department of Homeland Security:\"At midnight, funding for the Department of Homeland Security lapses. Republicans are responsible for this lapse which will force Transportation Security Officers to work without pay, severely reduce disaster relief funding, and negatively impact Coast Guard, Secret Service, and cybersecurity personnel. Services will be scaled back and workers will be furloughed.“The Department of Homeland Security is shutting down tonight because Republicans refuse to implement popular reforms to Immigration and Customs Enforcement, and Customs and Border Protection – the agencies responsible for the deaths of Renee Good and Alex Pretti.“The reforms that Democrats are demanding are backed by strong majorities of Americans. Requiring agents to get a warrant from a judge before kicking in someone’s door, removing masks and presenting identification, stopping stakeouts of schools, hospitals, and houses of worship, prohibiting racial profiling, requiring the use of body cameras, establishing a legally binding use-of-force policy, allowing independent investigations into misconduct, ending roving patrols, and preventing U.S. citizens from being detained or deported are all favored by an overwhelming majority of the public.“I have introduced a bill (H.R. 7481) that would fund the Department of Homeland Security, except for Immigration and Customs Enforcement, Customs and Border Protection, and the Office of the Secretary, while negotiations continue over much-needed reforms to those agencies.“The law-abiding agencies under the Department of Homeland Security should not be held hostage because Republicans refuse to agree to popular reforms for lawless agencies.” Bill text for H.R. 7481 can be found here.###\nIssues:Homeland Security\nSubcommittees 119th CongressCommittee on Appropriations (119th Congress)Homeland Security (119th Congress)\nNews\nPress Releases\nStatements\nAppropriators in Print\nFact Sheets\nVideos","content_cn":"图片\n主页\n新闻\n新闻稿\n\nDeLauro就国土安全部资金暂停发表声明\n2026年2月13日 新闻稿\n\n华盛顿——今日，众议院拨款委员会首席少数党成员罗莎·德劳罗（Rosa DeLauro，康涅狄格州第3选区民主党人）在国土安全部即将出现资金暂停之际发表了以下声明：\n\n“午夜时分，国土安全部的资金将暂停。共和党人应为此次暂停负责，这将迫使运输安全官员无薪工作，严重削减灾害救援资金，并对海岸警卫队、特勤局和网络安全人员造成负面影响。相关服务将被缩减，工作人员将被迫休假。\n\n“国土安全部今晚将停止运作，因为共和党人拒绝对移民与海关执法局以及海关与边境保护局实施广受欢迎的改革——这两个机构对Renee Good和Alex Pretti的死亡负有责任。\n\n“民主党人要求的改革得到绝大多数美国人的支持。要求执法人员在破门进入他人住所前先从法官处取得搜查令；取消遮面并出示身份证明；停止在学校、医院和礼拜场所进行监视；禁止种族画像；要求使用执法记录仪；制定具有法律约束力的武力使用政策；允许对不当行为进行独立调查；结束流动巡逻；并防止美国公民被拘留或驱逐——这些措施都得到压倒性多数公众的支持。\n\n“我提出了一项法案（H.R. 7481），将在继续就这些机构亟需的改革进行谈判期间，为国土安全部提供资金，但不包括移民与海关执法局、海关与边境保护局以及部长办公室。\n\n“国土安全部下属的守法机构不应因为共和党人拒绝同意对无法无天的机构实施广受欢迎的改革而被扣为人质。”\n\nH.R. 7481的法案文本可在此处找到。\n\n###\n议题：国土安全\n\n小组委员会\n第119届国会\n拨款委员会（第119届国会）\n国土安全小组委员会（第119届国会）\n\n新闻\n新闻稿\n声明\n拨款委员印刷品\n事实说明书\n视频","publish_source":"democrats-appropriations.house.gov","publish_time":"2026-02-13T15:26:06-05:00"}},{"id":"news-1460","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"首席成员德劳罗就国土安全部长克丽丝蒂·诺姆被免职发表声明","title_en":"Ranking Member DeLauro Statement on Removal of Homeland Security Secretary Kristi Noem","summary_cn":"众议院拨款委员会民主党首席成员德劳罗就国土安全部长克丽丝蒂·诺姆被免职发表声明，称“谢天谢地”，并批评诺姆任内滥用职权，包括挪用海岸警卫队资金购买私人飞机、为前发言人亲属企业提供巨额合同用于自我宣传。她还指责该部未能管理关键拨款、削弱网络防御，并称其政策伤害了守法美国公民，表示诺姆的离开不会令人怀念。","summary_en":"House Appropriations Committee Ranking Member Rosa DeLauro issued a statement on the removal of Homeland Security Secretary Kristi Noem, saying \"good riddance\" and accusing Noem of abusing her office, including taking $170 million from the Coast Guard for private jets and directing over $200 million in contracts to her former spokesperson's family business for self-promotional ads. She also criticized the department's failure to administer grants, weakened cyber defenses and harm to law-abiding Americans.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-24T20:33:47.256615+00:00","url":"http://democrats-appropriations.house.gov/news/press-releases/ranking-member-delauro-statement-removal-homeland-security-secretary-kristi","content":"Image\nHome\nNews\nPress Releases\nRanking Member DeLauro Statement on Removal of Homeland Security Secretary Kristi NoemMarch 5, 2026 Press ReleaseWASHINGTON – Today, House Appropriations Committee Ranking Member Rosa DeLauro (CT-03) released the following statement regarding the removal of Homeland Security Secretary Kristi Noem:“Good riddance. This closes perhaps the most corrupt chapter in the short history of the Department of Homeland Security. At every turn, Secretary Noem exploited the status and influence of her office. From taking $170 million from the Coast Guard to buy private jets for her own use, to doling out over $200 million for cushy contracts to her former spokesperson’s family business for ad campaigns starring herself, she never missed an opportunity to manipulate the public trust for personal gain.“Under her stewardship, the Department failed to administer critical grant funding, gutted our nation’s cyber defenses, and terrorized and killed law-abiding American citizens. Future generations will look back on this period and wonder with horror how such cruelty was allowed at so great a scale for so long a time with so little accountability. I join American families, free speech advocates, and dog-lovers across the nation in breathing a sigh of relief that Kristi Noem is no longer in a position of power in this government. She will not be missed.”###\nIssues:Homeland Security\nSubcommittees 119th CongressCommittee on Appropriations (119th Congress)Homeland Security (119th Congress)\nNews\nPress Releases\nStatements\nAppropriators in Print\nFact Sheets\nVideos","content_cn":"图片\n主页\n新闻\n新闻稿\n德劳罗就解除国土安全部长克里斯蒂·诺姆职务发表声明\n2026年3月5日 新闻稿\n华盛顿——今天，众议院拨款委员会首席少数党委员罗莎·德劳罗（康涅狄格州第03选区）就解除国土安全部长克里斯蒂·诺姆职务发表以下声明：\n\n“谢天谢地。这或许结束了国土安全部短暂历史上最腐败的篇章。诺姆部长每一步都在利用其职务的地位和影响力。从挪用海岸警卫队1.7亿美元购买供自己使用的私人飞机，到拨出超过2亿美元，为她前发言人的家族企业提供由她本人主演的广告宣传活动的优厚合同，她从未错过操纵公众信任、谋取个人利益的机会。\n\n“在她的领导下，该部门未能管理关键拨款，削弱了我国的网络防御，并恐吓、杀害守法的美国公民。后代回顾这段时期时，必将惊恐地思考：如此残酷的行为为何能以如此巨大的规模、持续如此长的时间，却几乎没有问责。我与全美的美国家庭、言论自由倡导者和爱狗人士一道，对克里斯蒂·诺姆不再担任本届政府的权力职位而如释重负。没有人会想念她。”\n###\n议题：国土安全\n小组委员会 119届国会\n拨款委员会（第119届国会）\n国土安全（第119届国会）\n新闻\n新闻稿\n声明\n拨款委员会成员报道\n情况说明书\n视频","publish_source":"democrats-appropriations.house.gov","publish_time":"2026-03-05T14:52:18-05:00"}},{"id":"news-1238","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"共和党人最终将通过两党参议院法案为国土安全部提供资金","title_en":"Republicans Finally Will Pass Bipartisan Senate Bill to Fund Homeland Security","summary_cn":"众议院拨款委员会民主党新闻稿称，众议院共和党领导层改变立场，同意通过参议院一致通过的国土安全部拨款两党法案。声明指出，该协议与拨款委员会资深成员德劳罗在政府停摆前提出的法案高度相似，将全额资助运输安全管理局、联邦应急管理局、海岸警卫队、网络安全和特勤局，同时将移民执法资金另行处理。声明批评共和党此前拒绝协议导致停摆延长，使国土安全部员工错过薪水，并重申民主党将继续推动对移民和海关执法局的改革。","summary_en":"A House Appropriations Committee Democratic press release states that House Republican leadership reversed course and agreed to the bipartisan Homeland Security funding bill passed unanimously by the Senate. The statement says the agreement closely mirrors a bill introduced by Ranking Member DeLauro before the shutdown began, fully funding TSA, FEMA, the Coast Guard, cybersecurity and the Secret Service while setting immigration enforcement funding aside. It criticizes Republicans for previously rejecting the deal, prolonging the shutdown and causing Department of Homeland Security workers to miss paychecks, and reiterates Democrats' push for ICE reforms.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-24T20:28:49.242117+00:00","url":"http://democrats-appropriations.house.gov/news/press-releases/republicans-finally-will-pass-bipartisan-senate-bill-fund-homeland-security","content":"Image\nHome\nNews\nPress Releases\nRepublicans Finally Will Pass Bipartisan Senate Bill to Fund Homeland SecurityApril 1, 2026 Press ReleaseAgreement closely mirrors bill introduced by Ranking Member DeLauro before shutdown beganWASHINGTON – Today, House Republican leadership reversed course and agreed to the bipartisan Homeland Security funding bill passed unanimously by the Senate. House Republicans previously rejected the agreement that they will now seek to pass, needlessly adding weeks to the shutdown.“Many workers across the Department of Homeland Security have already missed multiple paychecks, and thanks to House Republican leadership’s pointless choice to extend this shutdown, they will likely miss another.“This agreement closely mirrors the bill I introduced over a month ago, before the shutdown even began, that would fully fund TSA, FEMA, the Coast Guard, cybersecurity and the Secret Service, while setting funding for immigration enforcement aside.“Democrats have been proposing this for weeks as a pathway to end the shutdown. I only wish Republicans had come to their senses sooner. Federal workers have suffered because of their failure to govern. The American people deserve better.“Democrats will keep fighting to reign in ICE, and will continue to oppose new funding unless it is accompanied by reforms that most Americans support.”###\nIssues:Homeland Security\nSubcommittees 119th CongressCommittee on Appropriations (119th Congress)Homeland Security (119th Congress)\nNews\nPress Releases\nStatements\nAppropriators in Print\nFact Sheets\nVideos","content_cn":"图片\n首页\n新闻\n新闻稿\n共和党人最终将通过两党参议院法案，为国土安全部门提供资金\n2026年4月1日 新闻稿\n该协议与德劳罗排名委员在停摆开始前提出的法案高度相似\n华盛顿——今天，众议院共和党领导层改变立场，同意参议院一致通过的两党国土安全拨款法案。众议院共和党人此前曾否决这项协议，而他们现在将寻求通过该协议，这毫无必要地延长了数周的政府停摆。\n“国土安全部的许多工作人员已经错过了多次薪资发放，感谢众议院共和党领导层延长停摆这一毫无意义的选择，他们很可能还会再错过一次。”\n“这项协议与我一个多月前、甚至在停摆开始前提出的法案高度相似。该法案将为运输安全管理局（TSA）、联邦紧急事务管理局（FEMA）、海岸警卫队、网络安全部门和特勤局提供全部资金，同时将移民执法资金暂置一旁。”\n“民主党数周来一直在提出这一方案，将其作为结束停摆的途径。我只是希望共和党人能早点恢复理智。联邦工作人员因他们治理失败而遭受损失。美国人民应该得到更好的待遇。”\n“民主党将继续努力约束移民与海关执法局（ICE），并继续反对新的资金，除非这些资金同时附带大多数美国人支持的改革。”\n###\n议题：国土安全\n小组委员会\n第119届国会\n拨款委员会（第119届国会）\n国土安全（第119届国会）\n新闻\n新闻稿\n声明\n拨款委员会成员发表文章\n事实说明书\n视频","publish_source":"democrats-appropriations.house.gov","publish_time":"2026-04-01T17:28:38-04:00"}},{"id":"news-2313","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"民主党议员谴责卡什·帕特尔因LGBTQ+骄傲旗解雇FBI探员“卑劣”","title_en":"Angry Democratic lawmakers slam ‘despicable’ Kash Patel for firing FBI agent over LGBTQ+ Pride flag","summary_cn":"据《倡导者》报道，FBI局长卡什·帕特尔在联邦政府停摆首日解雇一名新探员，理由是该探员此前在洛杉矶外勤办公室桌上摆放彩虹骄傲旗。报道称该探员曾获司法部长奖，解雇信援引特朗普的“第二条权力”绕过正当程序。参议院司法委员会民主党人、众议员马克·高野及参议员德宾等谴责此举是更广泛的清除LGBTQ+联邦雇员行动的一部分，并质疑其违反联邦工作场所规则。","summary_en":"According to The Advocate, FBI Director Kash Patel dismissed a new agent on the first day of the federal government shutdown after learning the trainee had displayed a rainbow Pride flag at a desk during a prior Los Angeles assignment. The report says the trainee had received the Attorney General’s Award, and the dismissal letter invoked Trump’s claimed Article II powers to bypass due process. Senate Judiciary Committee Democrats, Rep. Mark Takano, and Sen. Dick Durbin condemned the firing as part of a broader purge of LGBTQ+ federal employees and questioned its conflict with federal workplace rules.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-18T16:11:09.896692+00:00","url":"http://equality.house.gov/media-center/in-the-news/angry-democratic-lawmakers-slam-despicable-kash-patel-firing-fbi-agent","content":"Image\nMEDIA CENTER\nPress Releases\nCEC In The News\nHome\nMedia\nIn the News\nAngry Democratic lawmakers slam ‘despicable’ Kash Patel for firing FBI agent over LGBTQ+ Pride flag\nOctober 3, 2025 In The News\nBy Christopher WigginsThe Advocate\nOn the first day of the federal government shutdown, FBI Director Kash Patel dismissed a trainee agent after learning that the person had displayed a rainbow Pride flag at their desk during a prior assignment in Los Angeles during the Biden administration.The move, first reported by MSNBC’s Carol Leonnig, a multiple Pulitzer Prize-winning journalist with deep law enforcement sourcing, highlights what civil-rights advocates describe as a sweeping campaign by the Trump administration to purge LGBTQ+ employees and dismantle decades of inclusion efforts in federal service.In a letter dated October 1, Patel invoked President Donald Trump’s claimed Article II powers to fire career personnel without the traditional due process.Patel informed the trainee: “You are being summarily dismissed from your position as a New Agent Trainee at the FBI Academy in Quantico, Virginia, and removed from the federal service.” The letter, obtained by MSNBC and delivered on the first day of a nationwide government shutdown that had already created job uncertainty across the federal workforce, accused the employee of poor judgment.“After reviewing the facts and circumstances and considering your probationary status, I have determined that you exercised poor judgment with an inappropriate display of political signage in your work area during your previous assignment in the Los Angeles Field Office,” Patel wrote, without directly referencing the flag itself.The signage referenced in the letter, according to people familiar with the case, was a small Pride flag, MSNBC reports.The dismissal stunned many within the Bureau, particularly because the trainee was a decorated employee who had coordinated diversity programming in a field office and received awards for service, including the Attorney General’s Award in 2022.Out in National Security respondsLuke Schleusener, CEO of Out in National Security, condemned the decision, calling it “a clear act of bias and a warning to public servants and allies who believe they should be free to show support for LGBTQIA+ Americans at work.” He told The Advocate that “in a free society, government employees should never fear retaliation for such a simple act of solidarity and pride.”Schleusener added that the firing was not an isolated incident. Federal employees have already been targeted for Pride lanyards and flags, and contractors and staff working on LGBTQ+ issues have been dismissed across multiple agencies. He pointed to the Department of Veterans Affairs’ recent restrictions on Pride displays at its clinics as part of what he described as a “Second Lavender Scare … in which LGBTQIA+ public servants and their allies are singled out and silenced.”“History is clear: prejudice is not strength but weakness,” Schleusener said. “It does not make America safer or stronger. It corrodes trust and undermines the values of fairness and freedom that our national security depends on.”What federal law saysPatel’s justification also appears to conflict with federal workplace rules. In July 2023, the Office of Personnel Management issued guidance reminding agencies that employees may display personal religious or secular symbols at their desks, provided that these rules are applied neutrally and without favoritism. According to the memo, if an agency permits a Bible, rosary, or crucifix, it cannot simultaneously forbid a Pride flag or another identity-affirming symbol.“That same protection extends to secular expressions, such as flags representing LGBTQ+ identity, disability awareness, or ethnic heritage,” The Mindful Federal Employee blog reported.The Human Rights Campaign responded to the firing on social media, writing, If true, this is the latest example of Donald Trump, Kash Patel, and the entire administration weaponizing the federal government to silence speech and deny our LGBTQ+ community’s existence. Plus, it’s illegal.\"The group added, \"Federal employees do not lose basic 1st Amendment protections. If you can be targeted for your expression, no one is safe.\"Congressional Democrats weigh inDemocrats on the Senate Judiciary Committee, which has direct oversight of the FBI, sharply criticized Patel’s action. “LGBTQ+ should be able to serve their country openly and proudly,” Josh Sorbe, spokesperson for Senate Judiciary Committee Democrats, told The Advocate. “Rather than policing desk displays, Kash Patel should focus on keeping our nation safe. Senate Judiciary Democrats will continue to hold the Trump-Patel FBI accountable as this FBI Director tragically deprofessionalizes and weaponizes the world’s strongest law enforcement agency.”Gay California U.S. Rep. Mark Takano, Chair of the Congressional Equality Caucus, went further, charging that the firing fits into a broader purge. “Trump and his Administration have been obsessively trying to purge our community from the federal workforce since they took power. This firing is just their next attack,” Takano told The Advocate in a statement. He pointed to agencies rolling back nondiscrimination protections, disbanding LGBTQI+ employee resource groups, and censoring Pride celebrations. “It’s not just censorship, they’re also firing people for simply being LGBTQI+ or doing work that supports the LGBTQI+ community. These despicable acts are just another example of how commonplace anti-LGBTQI+ discrimination is in this Administration.”U.S. Senate Democratic Whip Dick Durbin of Illinois, the ranking member of the Senate Judiciary Committee, also condemned the firing.“President Trump is attacking free speech and trying to quash any expression that he feels threatened by. Director Patel just further confirmed he’s willing to do his bidding,” Durbin said in a statement provided to The Advocate. “If you’re an LGBTQ+ person who wants to help protect our country at the FBI, you should be able to do so openly and with pride. We’re all on the same team—America’s team.\"He added, “Director Patel’s tenure has left America less safe, less free, and less secure. I will continue to fight to keep our FBI strong and hold this Administration accountable.”Patel’s contentious tenureThe firing also comes just weeks after Patel faced more than four hours of bruising testimony before the Senate Judiciary Committee, where Democrats accused him of politicizing the Bureau and carrying out loyalty purges. Lawmakers pressed Patel about a string of high-profile controversies, including his confusing public statements after the assassination of conservative activist Charlie Kirk, his management of Jeffrey Epstein–related files, and the ouster of FBI officials tied to investigations involving Trump.In one exchange, Durbin, the committee’s top Democrat, called Patel “arguably the most partisan FBI director ever” and accused him of directing a purge of senior officials even before his confirmation. Sen. Cory Booker of New Jersey told Patel he was “not long for [his] job,” while California Sen. Adam Schiff, in a heated clash, branded Patel “an internet troll” after Patel called him “a political buffoon.”Despite the withering criticism, Patel insisted his personnel decisions were “based on merit and qualification.” But the firing of a trainee over a Pride flag raises new questions about whether those firings are rooted in bias rather than performance.A Broader campaignThe firing also comes after earlier restrictions on LGBTQ+ visibility inside the bureau. In May, The Advocate reported that FBI leadership barred any official Pride Month observances, instructing agents that there should be “no official FBI actions, events, or messaging regarding Pride Month.” An internal email from Assistant Director for Public Affairs Ben Williamson told employees they could only celebrate “in their personal capacity” and on their own time. That directive rolled back policies from the Biden era, when the bureau not only flew the Pride flag at its Washington, D.C., headquarters but also encouraged agents to participate in local Pride events as part of outreach to LGBTQ+ communities.This week’s dismissal did not occur in isolation. AL.com reports that Patel previously fired about 20 agents who had been photographed kneeling during racial-justice protests after the 2020 killing of George Floyd.The episode also coincides with Patel’s move, reported by The Washington Post, to sever the Bureau’s decades-long partnership with the Anti-Defamation League. That relationship, which had included mandatory hate-crimes and Holocaust-education workshops for new agents, was dismantled after Patel denounced the ADL as a “political front.”Echoes of the Lavender ScareThe last time federal agencies terminated LGBTQ+ people for their identity was during the Lavender Scare of the 1950s, when thousands of government employees lost their jobs simply for being suspected of homosexuality. That campaign of mass firings, which paralleled the Red Scare targeting suspected communists, devastated careers and forced many into secrecy.The trauma of that era was dramatized in Fellow Travelers, the Showtime series that followed two men caught in the intersection of politics, McCarthyism, and anti-gay witch hunts. The show illustrated not only the personal toll of those purges but also the corrosive impact on democracy when loyalty tests are tied to identity.For critics of Patel’s decision, the parallels are unmistakable.","content_cn":"图片\n媒体中心\n新闻稿\nCEC 新闻报道\n首页\n媒体\n新闻报道\n愤怒的民主党议员抨击卡什·帕特尔因 LGBTQ+ 骄傲旗解雇 FBI 探员是“卑劣”之举\n2025年10月3日 新闻报道\n作者：克里斯托弗·威金斯，《倡导者》\n在联邦政府停摆的第一天，FBI 局长卡什·帕特尔解雇了一名见习探员，原因是他得知此人在拜登政府时期被派往洛杉矶期间，曾在自己办公桌上摆放一面彩虹骄傲旗。\n此举最初由 MSNBC 的卡罗尔·莱昂尼格报道。莱昂尼格是一位多次获得普利策奖的记者，在执法部门拥有深厚的人脉。民权倡导者称，此举凸显了特朗普政府发起的一场大规模行动，旨在清除 LGBTQ+ 雇员，并瓦解联邦服务领域数十年来在包容性方面所做的努力。\n在一封日期为10月1日的信中，帕特尔援引特朗普总统所主张的《宪法第二条》权力，在没有传统正当程序的情况下解雇职业人员。\n帕特尔告知这名见习探员：“你被即刻解职，不再担任弗吉尼亚州匡蒂科 FBI 学院的见习新探员，并被从联邦服务系统中除名。”这封信由 MSNBC 获得，并在全国性政府停摆的第一天送达。此次停摆已在整个联邦劳动力中造成就业不确定性。信中指控该雇员判断力差。\n帕特尔写道：“在审查相关事实和情况，并考虑你的试用期身份后，我认定你在先前被派往洛杉矶外地办事处期间，在工作区域不当展示政治标语，属于判断力差。”他没有直接提及那面旗帜本身。\n据 MSNBC 报道，据熟悉此案的人士称，信中提到的标语是一面小型的骄傲旗。\n这一解雇决定在 FBI 内部令许多人震惊，尤其是因为这名见习探员是一名获得嘉奖的雇员，曾在一个外地办事处协调多元化项目，并因服务获得奖项，包括2022年的司法部长奖。\n“国家安全中的出柜者”组织回应\n“国家安全中的出柜者”组织首席执行官卢克·施莱泽纳谴责这一决定，称其为“明显的偏见行为，也是对公务员及其盟友的警告，他们相信自己应当可以在工作中自由表达对 LGBTQIA+ 美国人的支持。”他告诉《倡导者》：“在一个自由社会中，政府雇员绝不应因为这样一种简单的团结与骄傲之举而害怕遭到报复。”\n施莱泽纳还说，这次解雇并非孤立事件。联邦雇员已经因为骄傲挂绳和旗帜而成为目标，多个机构中从事 LGBTQ+ 议题工作的承包商和工作人员也已被解雇。他提到退伍军人事务部最近限制其诊所展示骄傲标志，并将其描述为“第二次薰衣草恐慌……在这场恐慌中，LGBTQIA+ 公务员及其盟友被单独挑出并噤声”的一部分。\n施莱泽纳说：“历史很清楚：偏见不是力量，而是软弱。它不会让美国更安全或更强大。它侵蚀信任，破坏我们的国家安全所依赖的公平与自由价值观。”\n联邦法律怎么说\n帕特尔的理由似乎也与联邦工作场所规则相冲突。2023年7月，人事管理办公室发布指导意见，提醒各机构，雇员可以在办公桌上展示个人宗教或世俗象征，前提是这些规则被中立适用且没有偏袒。根据该备忘录，如果某机构允许摆放《圣经》、念珠或十字架，就不能同时禁止骄傲旗或其他肯定身份的象征。\n“正念联邦雇员”博客报道称：“同样的保护也延伸到世俗表达，例如代表 LGBTQ+ 身份、残障意识或族裔传承的旗帜。”\n人权运动组织在社交媒体上回应这次解雇，写道：“如果属实，这是唐纳德·特朗普、卡什·帕特尔和整个政府将联邦政府武器化，以压制言论并否认我们 LGBTQ+ 群体存在的最新例子。而且，这还是非法的。”\n该组织补充说：“联邦雇员不会失去基本的《第一修正案》保护。如果一个人可以因为其表达而被针对，那就没有人是安全的。”\n国会民主党人发声\n对 FBI 拥有直接监督权的参议院司法委员会民主党人严厉批评帕特尔的行动。参议院司法委员会民主党发言人乔什·索尔贝告诉《倡导者》：“LGBTQ+ 群体应当能够公开而自豪地为国家服务。卡什·帕特尔不应管办公桌上的展示，而应专注于维护国家安全。随着这位 FBI 局长可悲地将世界上最强大的执法机构去专业化并武器化，参议院司法委员会民主党人将继续追究特朗普-帕特尔 FBI 的责任。”\n加州同性恋联邦众议员、国会平等核心小组主席马克·高野进一步指出，这次解雇属于更广泛的清洗行动。高野在给《倡导者》的声明中说：“特朗普及其政府自上台以来，一直执迷于试图将我们群体从联邦劳动力中清除。这次解雇只是他们的下一次攻击。”他指出，一些机构正在削减反歧视保护、解散 LGBTQI+ 雇员资源小组，并审查骄傲庆祝活动。“这不仅仅是审查，他们还仅仅因为某人是 LGBTQI+ 或从事支持 LGBTQI+ 群体的工作就解雇他们。这些卑劣行为只是反 LGBTQI+ 歧视在本届政府中多么普遍化的又一个例子。”\n伊利诺伊州美国参议院民主党党鞭、参议院司法委员会资深成员迪克·德宾也谴责这次解雇。\n德宾在提供给《倡导者》的一份声明中说：“特朗普总统正在攻击言论自由，并试图压制任何让他感到受威胁的表达。帕特尔局长刚刚进一步证实，他愿意听命行事。如果你是 LGBTQ\n[正文过长，翻译截断；对象库保留全文]","publish_source":"equality.house.gov","publish_time":"2025-10-03T14:15:03-04:00"}},{"id":"news-2547","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"《长岛新闻》：加巴里诺与布莱克曼主持“恐怖星期二”国土安全简报会","title_en":"Long Island Press: Garbarino, Blakeman conduct Homeland Security briefing on ‘Terror Tuesday’","summary_cn":"2025年8月5日，美国众议院国土安全委员会主席安德鲁·加巴里诺与纳索县县长布鲁斯·布莱克曼、警察局长帕特里克·赖德及前国土安全委员会主席彼得·金共同出席纳索县每周“恐怖星期二”简报会，讨论潜在安全威胁。加巴里诺强调跨机构合作的重要性，并承诺为纳索县争取联邦资源，表示将与国土安全部长克里斯蒂·诺姆密切合作。","summary_en":"On Aug. 5, 2025, U.S. House Homeland Security Committee Chairman Andrew Garbarino joined Nassau County Executive Bruce Blakeman, Police Commissioner Patrick Ryder, and former committee chair Peter King at Nassau's weekly 'Terror Tuesday' briefing to discuss potential safety threats. Garbarino stressed interagency cooperation and pledged to secure federal resources for Nassau County, saying he would work closely with Homeland Security Secretary Kristi Noem.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-24T21:23:14.903947+00:00","url":"http://garbarino.house.gov/media/in-the-news/long-island-press-garbarino-blakeman-conduct-homeland-security-briefing-terror","content":"Home\nMedia\nIn the News\nLong Island Press: Garbarino, Blakeman conduct Homeland Security briefing on ‘Terror Tuesday’\nAugust 5, 2025 In The News\nBy Larissa Fuentes\nClick here to read the full article.\nU.S. Rep. Andrew Garbarino, chairman of the U.S. House Committee on Homeland Security, joined Nassau County Executive Bruce Blakeman, Police Commissioner Patrick Ryder, and former Homeland Security Committee Chair Peter King on Tuesday, Aug. 5, to discuss Nassau’s various potential safety threats during the county’s weekly “Terror Tuesday” briefing.The visit came during Nassau’s regular weekly meeting between federal, state, and local law enforcement and Homeland Security agencies just a week after the tragic New York City shooting that left four people dead, including an NYPD officer.“Terror Tuesday” meetings serve as a forum to exchange intelligence, discuss threats and tactics, and strengthen interagency partnerships, Blakeman said during a news conference.“This is how we ensure a safer region,” he said.Garbarino, a Republican from Long Island who replaced former Homeland Security chairman Rep. Peter King in the House, emphasized the importance of interagency cooperation, something he said was lacking before 9/11.\"Having that open discussion and seeing agencies working together every Tuesday is exactly what we need,” Garbarino said. “This is why Nassau County is one of the safest counties in the country.”Garbarino also toured the county’s Intelligence Center, training facility, and its new Police Training Village in Garden City, a facility being shared with other domestic and international law enforcement agencies.“This is a fantastic site,” Garbarino said. “We should be bringing people in from all over the country to train here.”Commissioner Ryder noted the facility’s growing global reach. He announced he would travel to Israel on Sept. 7 to meet with the Israeli National Police and the Israel Defense Forces, who have expressed interest in using Nassau’s training village for their own drills.“The Israeli police have seen the village and want to train here,” said Ryder. “That opens the door for international communication.”Blakeman credited the county Legislature, including Public Safety Committee Chair Patrick Mullaney, for providing funding and support for counterterrorism efforts.King also attended the event and voiced his confidence in Garbarino’s leadership.“New York remains the No. 1 terrorist target,” King said. “We’re lucky to have Andrew Garbarino, he’s going to be our best friend in Washington.”Garbarino pledged to secure whatever federal resources Nassau County needs.“My focus as chairman is counterterrorism,” he said. “I’ll work very closely with the president and the secretary of Homeland Security, Kristi Noem, to make sure that New York is the greatest city in the world, and it’s also one of the most targeted, and we have to protect it.”Click here to read the full article.\nIssues:\nHomeland Security\nStanding With Law Enforcement","content_cn":"首页\n媒体\n新闻报道\n《长岛新闻报》：加巴里诺、布莱克曼在“恐怖星期二”举行国土安全简报会\n2025年8月5日 新闻报道\n作者：拉里萨·富恩特斯\n点击此处阅读全文。\n美国众议院国土安全委员会主席、联邦众议员安德鲁·加巴里诺于8月5日星期二与拿骚县行政长官布鲁斯·布莱克曼、警察局长帕特里克·莱德以及前国土安全委员会主席彼得·金共同讨论了该县每周“恐怖星期二”简报会期间拿骚县面临的各种潜在安全威胁。此次访问正值拿骚县联邦、州和地方执法机构及国土安全机构举行例行每周会议期间，距离纽约市发生造成4人死亡（其中包括一名纽约市警察局警员）的悲剧性枪击事件仅一周。\n布莱克曼在新闻发布会上表示，“恐怖星期二”会议为交流情报、讨论威胁与战术、加强机构间伙伴关系提供了平台。\n“这就是我们确保地区更加安全的方式，”他说。\n接替前国土安全委员会主席彼得·金众议员的长岛共和党人加巴里诺强调了机构间合作的重要性；他说，在9·11事件之前，这种合作有所欠缺。\n加巴里诺说：“进行这种公开讨论，并看到各机构每周二共同协作，正是我们所需要的。这就是为什么拿骚县是全国最安全的县之一。”\n加巴里诺还参观了该县的情报中心、培训设施及其位于花园城的新警察培训村；该设施正与其他美国国内和国际执法机构共享。\n加巴里诺说：“这是一个极好的场地。我们应该把来自全国各地的人带到这里培训。”\n莱德局长指出该设施日益扩大的全球影响力。他宣布将于9月7日前往以色列，与以色列国家警察和以色列国防军会面；后两者已表示有兴趣使用拿骚县的培训村进行自己的演练。\n莱德说：“以色列警方已经看过这个培训村，并希望在这里训练。这为国际交流打开了大门。”\n布莱克曼称赞县立法机构，包括公共安全委员会主席帕特里克·穆兰尼，为反恐工作提供资金和支持。\n金也出席了活动，并表达了他对加巴里诺领导力的信心。\n金说：“纽约仍然是头号恐怖主义目标。我们很幸运拥有安德鲁·加巴里诺；他将成为我们在华盛顿最好的朋友。”\n加巴里诺承诺将争取拿骚县所需的一切联邦资源。\n他说：“作为主席，我的重点是反恐。我将与总统及国土安全部长克里斯蒂·诺姆密切合作，确保纽约是世界上最伟大的城市，同时它也是最受瞄准的城市之一，我们必须保护它。”\n点击此处阅读全文。\n议题：\n国土安全\n支持执法部门","publish_source":"garbarino.house.gov","publish_time":"2025-08-05T18:40:14-04:00"}},{"id":"news-1113","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"霍耶在C-SPAN《停火》节目中讨论伊朗战争、国土安全部持续停摆及美国民众面临的生活成本危机","title_en":"Hoyer Discusses the War with Iran, Ongoing Department of Homeland Security Shutdown, Affordability Crisis Facing Americans on C-SPAN's Ceasefire","summary_cn":"2026年4月25日新闻稿：马里兰州民主党众议员斯坦尼·H·霍耶与达莎·伯恩斯及内华达州共和党众议员马克·阿莫迪在C-SPAN《停火》节目中进行两党对话，讨论伊朗战争、国土安全部（DHS）持续停摆以及美国民众面临的生活成本危机。霍耶批评总统未经国会授权发动战争，并指出DHS停摆的核心争议在于ICE和CBP的执法行为，民主党已投票资助海岸警卫队、FEMA等其余机构。","summary_en":"Press release dated April 25, 2026: Congressman Steny H. Hoyer (MD-05) joined Dasha Burns and Congressman Mark Amodei (NV-02) on C-SPAN's Ceasefire for a bipartisan discussion on the war with Iran, the ongoing Department of Homeland Security (DHS) shutdown, and the affordability crisis. Hoyer criticized the President for going to war without congressional authorization and said the DHS shutdown dispute centers on ICE and CBP conduct, noting Democrats voted to fund the Coast Guard, FEMA, and other agencies.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-24T20:23:59.531579+00:00","url":"http://hoyer.house.gov/media/press-releases/hoyer-discusses-war-iran-ongoing-department-homeland-security-shutdown","content":"REGIONAL LEADERSHIP COUNCIL\nHOW CAN STENY HELP?\nHome\nMedia\nPress Releases\nHoyer Discusses the War with Iran, Ongoing Department of Homeland Security Shutdown, Affordability Crisis Facing Americans on C-SPAN's Ceasefire\nApril 25, 2026 Press Release\nWASHINGTON, DC – Congressman Steny H. Hoyer (MD-05) joined Dasha Burns and Congressman Mark Amodei (NV-02) on C-SPAN's Ceasefire for a bipartisan conversation to discuss the war with Iran, the ongoing Department of Homeland Security (DHS) shutdown, and the affordability crisis facing Americans. Below are excerpts of his remarks during the episode:\nImage\nClick here to watch the full episode. ON THE WAR WITH IRAN“The Constitution says it is the Congress who declares war, that has us go to war, and legislation we have passed to make sure that occurs has been ignored. In fact, the President thinks it's unconstitutional itself. As Mark said, he didn't come to any of us. He didn't come to anybody, apparently. He didn't come to any of our allies. He didn't come to any of the countries in the Middle East, other than perhaps Israel. He decided that this was a go.”“…and now we are in a war, the war that's costing the American people a lot of money, not only on gasoline, but every other price, and the tariffs he imposed did the same.  …I think, had he talked to our allies, talked to Congress, had we reflected on it, we wouldn't be in this position.”ON THE DEPARTMENT OF HOMELAND SECURITY (DHS) SHUTDOWN“There's been a shutdown for way too long…it's not about appropriations. It's about how ICE and CBP conduct themselves and particularly how they conducted themselves in Minnesota and some of the other areas in which they have 'surged,' as they call it, and in our opinion, undermine the constitutional rights of many people and killed some people in the process, tragically, and need to be held accountable.”“We are prepared and, in fact, voted for a bill that funded everything else, including the Coast Guard and FEMA and other agencies which are critical to our homeland security and critical to America. But because we would not vote to fund those two agencies until we have some agreement on how they are going to correctly and constitutionally perform their duties, the Republican party would not take the bill up that the Senate sent us, which was exactly that…all the rest of DHS should be open as of today and should have been opened months ago.”ON AFFORDABILITY AND TRUMP’S ECONOMIC POLICIES“The President made a lot of claims of what he was going to do on the first day, or at least the first weeks. He said he was going to bring prices down – gasoline prices are up over a dollar everywhere. Utility costs are up almost everywhere. The tariffs have increased the prices on almost every good you buy that has been imported, maybe every one… people were upset about inflation and prices, and inflation went up, as I said, a point from February to March of this year. People are thinking, ‘What you told us you were going to do hasn't been done.’”“ …We got to stop focusing on war, stop focusing on tearing down the White House, or building super monuments, and focus on what people thought they were voting for that is reducing the costs of their everyday life.”","content_cn":"区域领导委员会\nSTENY能如何提供帮助？\n首页\n媒体\n新闻稿\n霍耶在C-SPAN《Ceasefire》节目中谈论伊朗战争、国土安全部持续停摆及美国人面临的生活成本危机\n2026年4月25日 新闻稿\n\n华盛顿特区——众议员Steny H. Hoyer（马里兰州第05选区）与Dasha Burns及众议员Mark Amodei（内华达州第02选区）共同参加C-SPAN的《Ceasefire》节目，进行两党对话，讨论伊朗战争、国土安全部（DHS）持续停摆，以及美国人面临的生活成本危机。以下是他在节目中发言的摘录：\n\n图片\n点击此处观看完整节目。\n\n关于伊朗战争\n\n“宪法规定，宣布战争、使我们进入战争的是国会；而我们为确保这一程序而通过的立法遭到了无视。事实上，总统认为这本身违宪。正如Mark所说，他没有找过我们任何人。他显然没有找过任何人。他没有找过我们的任何盟友。他没有找过中东任何国家，或许以色列除外。他决定这件事要推进。”\n\n“……如今我们已经身处一场战争，这场战争让美国人民付出大量金钱，不仅是汽油，其他每一种价格也是如此；他施加的关税也造成同样后果。……我认为，如果他与我们的盟友沟通、与国会沟通，如果我们对此进行了审议，我们就不会处于这个境地。”\n\n关于国土安全部（DHS）停摆\n\n“停摆已经持续太久了……这并非关于拨款，而是关于移民与海关执法局和海关与边境保护局如何行事，尤其是它们在明尼苏达州及其他一些它们所谓‘增派力量’的地区如何行事；在我们看来，它们损害了许多人的宪法权利，并在过程中悲剧性地导致一些人死亡，必须被追究责任。”\n\n“我们已经准备好，而且事实上已经投票支持一项法案，该法案为其他一切项目提供资金，包括对我们的国土安全和美国至关重要的海岸警卫队、联邦紧急事务管理局及其他机构。但由于在我们就这两个机构将如何正确且合宪地履行职责达成某些协议之前，我们不会投票为它们拨款，共和党就不愿审议参议院送交给我们的那项法案；该法案正是如此……国土安全部其余部门截至今天本应开放，而且本应在数月前就已开放。”\n\n关于生活成本与特朗普的经济政策\n\n“总统对他将在第一天、或至少最初几周做什么提出了许多说法。他说他会降低价格——各地汽油价格都上涨了超过一美元。几乎各地的公用事业费用都上涨了。关税提高了你购买的几乎每一种进口商品的价格，也许是每一种……人们曾因通胀和价格而不满，而正如我所说，今年通胀从2月到3月上升了一个点。人们在想，‘你告诉我们你会做的事情没有做到。’”\n\n“……我们必须停止把重点放在战争上，停止把重点放在拆除白宫或建造超级纪念碑上，而应关注人们以为自己投票支持的事情，那就是降低他们日常生活的成本。”","publish_source":"hoyer.house.gov","publish_time":"2026-04-25T14:15:57-04:00"}},{"id":"news-2142","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"霍耶在支持起诉特朗普政府破坏马里兰州新FBI总部项目的记者会上讲话","title_en":"Hoyer Remarks at Press Conference in Support of Suit Against Trump Administration's Attempt to Sabotage the New FBI headquarters Project in Maryland","summary_cn":"马里兰州民主党众议员斯泰尼·霍耶在记者会上支持州总检察长安东尼·布朗和乔治王子县提起诉讼，挑战特朗普政府2025年7月放弃已依法选定的马里兰州格林贝尔特FBI新总部选址、改选华盛顿特区里根大厦的决定。霍耶回顾自2009年以来FBI总部选址过程，称格林贝尔特是基于适用性和两党共识的最佳选择，指责该决定出于政治偏见，并表示相信诉讼将获胜。","summary_en":"Rep. Steny Hoyer (MD-05) spoke at a press conference supporting Maryland Attorney General Anthony Brown and Prince George’s County in filing a lawsuit challenging the Trump administration’s July 2025 decision to abandon the lawfully selected Greenbelt, Maryland site for the new FBI headquarters in favor of the Ronald Reagan Building in Washington, D.C. Hoyer recounted the site-selection process since 2009, said Greenbelt was chosen for suitability and bipartisan consensus, called the reversal politically motivated, and expressed confidence the suit will prevail.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-18T15:51:31.083034+00:00","url":"http://hoyer.house.gov/media/press-releases/hoyer-remarks-press-conference-support-suit-against-trump-administrations","content":"REGIONAL LEADERSHIP COUNCIL\nHOW CAN STENY HELP?\nHome\nMedia\nPress Releases\nHoyer Remarks at Press Conference in Support of Suit Against Trump Administration's Attempt to Sabotage the New FBI headquarters Project in Maryland\nNovember 7, 2025 Press Release\nWASHINGTON, DC – Congressman Steny H. Hoyer (MD-05) delivered the following remarks at a press conference in support of Attorney General Anthony Brown and Prince George's County filing a lawsuit that challenges the Trump Administration's July 2025 decision to abandon the lawfully selected Greenbelt, Maryland site for the new headquarters of the Federal Bureau of Investigation (FBI) in favor of the Ronald Reagan Building in Washington, D.C. Below is a video and full transcript of his remarks:\nImage\nClick here to watch a full video of his remarks. \"Before I talk about when I got into this issue, I want to talk about the fact that we need to open up the federal government for the people of the United States. The problem is, Democrats are negotiating with a group that does not want the government open. Just as Elon Musk – with his chainsaw – wanted to fire everybody. Russell Vought, who is essentially the CFO of our country – he’s called the OMB Director, but he’s the Chief Financial Officer. He has said he wants the federal employees perceived as the villains. He wants the federal employees to be perceived so badly that when they wake up in the morning, they don't want to come to work. You know, it is illegal in America to create a hostile workplace. Anthony, I’m pursuing with some folks the possibility of suing Russell Vought – probably can’t sue the president, but Russell Vought for creating consciously, intently, and with vengeful objectives the creation of a hostile workforce in the federal government. \"Now, what we are going to create here in Greenbelt, in Prince George’s County, in the state of Maryland, is a safe workforce. A strategically housed workforce. A workforce that is consistent with the request that was made of me. In 2009, I was the Majority Leader of the House of Representatives, and the director of the FBI came to my office, and he sat down and said, ‘Steny, this building in which we are housed is unsafe.’ 2009, this is 15 years later – 16 to be exact. The building was unsafe. There is not a Democrat or Republican who has visited that building, including Kash Patel, who doesn't say, ‘It is an unsafe environment for our employees.’ Or one could say a hostile environment. And Mr. Mueller said to me in 2009, ‘We need a space, somewhat like the CIA or NSA, that is a large enough space so that we can insulate ourselves and from terrorists, from people who would blow us up.’ And so they wanted a campus setting with at least a 150 foot setback. I don't know how many of you have gone by the Reagan building, 15 feet or so? A little short. And so I said, 'Mr. Director, I agree with you,' and we started this saga of transparency, honesty, of consideration, of all the factors that would make our FBI the place where people can work in security and be the most effective for the American people in keeping the peace and keeping law and order. And we worked hard on that from 2009 to 2016. And we were getting close. (makes pinching hand gesture) That close. We were almost there to get it done, and Donald Trump intervened. Donald Trump intervened – and by the way, we're going to have to clear that site where it's located now on Pennsylvania Avenue. And by the way, right across the street was a hotel. Who was the proprietor of that hotel? Donald Trump.\"And so he canceled it. He didn't decide, ‘We're going to put it somewhere else.’ He didn't decide [that] we need to tear down this building, because it is unsafe, Governor, for the people who work there. He simply canceled it, and so nothing was done for the next four years of a building that all Republicans and all Democrats who have been through it, say is unsafe and unworthy, and the directors will say [it] is unsuited to the way they do law enforcement today. So, we had another fight we started in ‘21, in ‘22 and ‘23. And because of the transparency they talked about, but mostly because of the suitability of the site to meet the needs and requests of the Federal Bureau of Investigation. That is why ultimately Greenbelt was [selected]. Not for political reasons, but for suitability to the task that we have assigned to the Federal Bureau of Investigation. And now we're in a fight because the president, not related to any specific criteria or strategic or decision making, but related more to his political bias. Hear me. His political bias. Now he's decided to move it to a building totally unsuited, unplanned for, undesigned for the purposes of a major law enforcement agency.“So, we're going to win this suit, and we’re going to win this battle. That is why – and a lot of people were really invested in this decision – that is why ultimately the GSA decided [that] this is the place, the best place from a cost standpoint, from a strategic standpoint, from a community standpoint where the Prince George’s community was a welcoming community – Mr. Mayor, I thank you and Greenbelt for their efforts. I want to mention [former] County Executive Alsobrooks, and I want to mention Larry Hogan, the governor. The governor said to all of his Republican colleagues, some of which he’s friendly with, some not, ‘This is the best site for the FBI.’ This was a bipartisan decision going forward, that has been turned into a petty, inappropriate small board decision for punitive purposes, not just against Prince George's County, but against the FBI, against the FBI.“So, I am hopeful that this suit will prevail. I believe it will prevail. The Congress has decided, but you remember I mentioned this guy, Russell Vought. Russell Vought believes that the passing of laws by the Congress is a suggestion to the Executive Department, and if they want to follow that, they can and if they don't, they won’t because he believes that Article II of the Constitution of the United States gives the president plenary power. That is, of course, untrue, and the Supreme Court has held it to be untrue. So, I want to thank the Attorney General. I want to thank Ben Cardin. I want to thank Ben Cardin, who was our senior United States Senator. I want to thank Angela [Alsobrooks], who fought so hard and worked with Hogan in getting the state to make a commitment on this.\"We have stepped up to the plate. We are ready. We are the place it ought to be and for every valid reason, ultimately, I believe the Congress and even the Executive Department will decide [that] Greenbelt is the site where the Federal Bureau of Investigation ought to be placed, and we ought to do it sooner rather than later. Now, let me also lastly, thank the person whose district the FBI is in. And that is Glenn Ivey. (applause) It was my district, it was Anthony's district, it’s been all over. So, we have an interest in this because we have studied this issue from 2009 to date, and it is absolutely the right decision the Congress has made: put it in Greenbelt and do it now.”\nIssues:\nNational Security & Veterans","content_cn":"地区领导委员会\n斯泰尼能如何帮忙？\n首页\n媒体\n新闻稿\n霍耶在支持起诉特朗普政府试图破坏马里兰州新 FBI 总部项目的新闻发布会上的发言\n2025年11月7日 新闻稿\n华盛顿特区——国会议员斯泰尼·H·霍耶（马里兰州第五选区）在新闻发布会上发表以下讲话，支持司法部长安东尼·布朗和乔治王子县提起诉讼，挑战特朗普政府2025年7月放弃依法选定的马里兰州格林贝尔特新联邦调查局（FBI）总部选址、转而选择华盛顿特区罗纳德·里根大楼的决定。以下是他讲话的视频和完整文字记录：\n图片\n点击此处观看他讲话的完整视频。“在我谈自己何时介入这个问题之前，我想谈谈这样一个事实：我们需要为美国人民重新开放联邦政府。问题是，民主党正在与一个不希望政府开门的人群谈判。就像埃隆·马斯克——拿着他的电锯——想解雇所有人一样。拉塞尔·沃特，他实际上是我们国家的首席财务官——他的头衔是 OMB 主任，但他是首席财务官。他说过，他希望联邦雇员被视为恶人。他希望联邦雇员被看得如此不堪，以至于他们早上醒来时不想来上班。你知道，在美国，制造敌意工作环境是违法的。安东尼，我正在和一些人与探讨起诉拉塞尔·沃特的可能性——大概不能起诉总统，但可以起诉拉塞尔·沃特，因为他有意识地、蓄意地、带着报复目标地在联邦政府中制造敌意劳动力。\n“现在，我们将在格林贝尔特、在乔治王子县、在马里兰州创造的，是一支安全的工作队伍。一支经过战略布局的工作队伍。一支符合对我所提要求的工作队伍。2009年，我担任美国众议院多数党领袖，FBI 局长来到我的办公室，他坐下来对我说：‘斯泰尼，我们所在的这栋楼不安全。’2009年，这是15年后——确切说是16年后。那栋楼不安全。没有一位参观过那栋楼的民主党人或共和党人，包括卡什·帕特尔，不说：‘这对我们的雇员来说是不安全的环境。’或者可以说，是敌意环境。2009年，穆勒先生对我说：‘我们需要一个类似 CIA 或 NSA 的空间，足够大，以便我们能够与恐怖分子、与那些想炸毁我们的人隔离开来。’所以他们想要一个园区式环境，至少有150英尺的退距。我不知道你们中有多少人经过里根大楼，大约15英尺？有点短。所以我说：‘局长先生，我同意你的看法。’然后我们开始了这段追求透明、诚实、考虑所有因素的漫长过程，这些因素将使我们的 FBI 成为人们能够安全工作的场所，并最有效地为美国人民维护和平、维护法律与秩序。从2009年到2016年，我们为此努力工作。我们越来越接近了。（做出捏手手势）就差那么一点。我们几乎就要完成了，结果唐纳德·特朗普插手了。唐纳德·特朗普插手了——顺便说一句，我们将不得不清理现在位于宾夕法尼亚大道的那个地点。顺便说一句，街对面就是一家酒店。那家酒店的老板是谁？唐纳德·特朗普。”\n“于是他取消了它。他不是决定‘我们要把它放到别处’。他不是决定我们需要拆掉这栋楼，因为州长，它对在那里工作的人来说不安全。他只是取消了它，于是在接下来的四年里，对于一栋所有经过它的共和党人和民主党人都说它不安全、不配使用，而且历任局长都会说它不适合他们今天执法方式的建筑，什么也没做。所以，我们在21年、22年和23年又开始了另一场斗争。由于他们所说的透明度，但主要是由于该地点适合满足联邦调查局的需求和要求。这就是为什么最终格林贝尔特被[选中]。不是出于政治原因，而是因为它适合我们赋予联邦调查局的任务。而现在我们陷入一场斗争，因为总统并非基于任何具体标准、战略或决策，而更多是基于他的政治偏见。听我说。他的政治偏见。现在他决定把它搬到一个完全不适合、未规划、未设计用于一个主要执法机构用途的建筑。”\n“所以，我们将赢得这场诉讼，我们将赢得这场战斗。这就是为什么——很多人确实在这项决定中投入了很多——这就是为什么最终 GSA 决定[这里]是这个地方，从成本角度、从战略角度、从社区角度都是最好的地方，乔治王子县社区是一个欢迎人的社区——市长先生，我感谢你和格林贝尔特的努力。我想提到[前]县长阿尔索布鲁克斯，我还想提到州长拉里·霍根。州长对他所有的共和党同僚，有些与他关系友好，有些不友好，说：‘这是 FBI 的最佳选址。’这是一个两党共同推进的决定，却被变成一个小气、不当的小董事会式决定，出于惩罚目的，不仅针对乔治王子县，也针对 FBI，针对 FBI。”\n“所以，我希望这场诉讼能够胜诉。我相信它会胜诉。国会已经决定，但你们记得我提到的这个人，拉塞尔·沃特。拉塞尔·沃特认为，国会通过法律是对行政部门的一种建议，如果他们想遵循，就可以遵循；如果他们不想遵循，就不会遵循，因为他认为\n[正文过长，翻译截断；对象库保留全文]","publish_source":"hoyer.house.gov","publish_time":"2025-11-07T10:36:13-05:00"}},{"id":"news-1309","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"排名成员霍耶：将FBI迁入里根大楼的欠考虑之举表明GSA存在失能","title_en":"Ranking Member Hoyer: This Ill-Conceived Effort to move the FBI into the Reagan Building is Indicative of the Dysfunction that Exists at GSA","summary_cn":"2026年3月26日，众议院拨款委员会金融服务与一般政府小组委员会排名成员霍耶在GAO监督听证会上发表讲话，批评特朗普政府将FBI总部从破旧的胡佛大楼迁至里根大楼的计划。他指出里根大楼设计强调开放性和通透性，不适合作为执法和情报机构，且改造至少需15亿美元，反映GSA管理失能。","summary_en":"On March 26, 2026, Ranking Member Hoyer of the FSGG Appropriations Subcommittee spoke at a GAO oversight hearing, criticizing the Trump administration's plan to move FBI headquarters from the dilapidated Hoover Building to the Reagan Building. He noted the Reagan Building was designed for openness and accessibility, unsuitable for a law enforcement and intelligence agency, and retrofitting would cost at least $1.5 billion, reflecting GSA dysfunction.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-18T14:37:31.076506+00:00","url":"http://hoyer.house.gov/media/press-releases/ranking-member-hoyer-ill-conceived-effort-move-fbi-reagan-building-indicative","content":"REGIONAL LEADERSHIP COUNCIL\nHOW CAN STENY HELP?\nHome\nMedia\nPress Releases\nRanking Member Hoyer: This Ill-Conceived Effort to move the FBI into the Reagan Building is Indicative of the Dysfunction that Exists at GSA\nMarch 26, 2026 Press Release\nWASHINGTON, DC – Today, Congressman Steny H. Hoyer (MD-05), Ranking Member of the Financial Services and General Government (FSGG) Appropriations Subcommittee, delivered opening remarks at the during the House Committee on Appropriations Oversight Hearing on the U.S. Government Accountability Office (GAO) with Director David Marroni. Below are a video and transcript of his remarks:\nImage\nClick here to watch a video of his remarks“Thank you very much, Mr. Chairman. I want to thank Mr. Marroni for being here and joining us today. We've heard much discussion of improving government efficiency and reducing waste this past year. All of us should share that objective. Although I have serious doubts about the Administration's commitment to those goals, we all ought to agree that those objectives ought to govern how we administer our federal real estate portfolio. We want to make sure we have the right amount of space and the right type of space for our federal employees to do their jobs on behalf of the American people as effectively and as safely as possible. I always say we need to rightsize the government, not increase – decrease, but rightsize for the job that we give them. I recognize that’s no easy task, as I'm sure Director Marroni would agree, but it is also clear that the General Services Administration management of our federal real estate is wanted in some cases. I'd like to quote from [the] Inspector General's report that was released just this week, and I have that report here and I imagine you brought it with you. I'd like to quote from that: ‘GSA is not consistently addressing deficient security fixtures at the GSA control facility, and as a result, is leaving the public, employees and property at risk from security threats.’ That finding ought to concern every Member of this committee and this House. Much of that report was redacted, but it indicated that – I presume, for security reasons itself – but it is indicated the GSA failure to meet this crucial responsibility was due in part to the immense cost of installing and maintaining security measures. To see the perils of this issue, just look down Pennsylvania Avenue.\"The Trump Administration is trying to move the FBI headquarters from the dilapidated and falling down J. Edgar Hoover building to the Reagan Building just a little way away. Moving the FBI out of one old, exposed, and inadequate building into another old, exposed, and inadequate building is not a solution. When former FBI Director Robert Mueller, who just died, approached me in 2009 about finding a new home for the FBI, he emphasized that the Bureau needed a new, secure, and consolidated facility on a large campus. The Reagan Building fails to meet the FBI security and operational issues. It was not designed as a secure law enforcement facility, rather, emphatically, as an open, accessible office for both public and private tenants. As a matter of fact, I have an article here that reflects that objective. To use the words of Paycom Fred and Partners, the architectural firm that designed the facility, quote, ‘The Reagan Building emphasizes access and permeability. Access and probability are great features of an international trade center, which the Reagan Building was designed to fulfill, but not a law enforcement and intelligence agency.’ An article in Chicago Tribune, published about the building in 1997, noted the very fact. It said, ‘The Reagan Building, quote, will open the standoffish domain of the federal bureaucracy to the city and teach an important lesson to the post Oklahoma City bombing era, when the temptation is to turn all government buildings into impressive fortresses.’ But the FBI headquarters needs to be impregnable.\"Even if the Reagan Building were not located between two major thoroughfares, 14th Street and Pennsylvania, it still would not meet Inter-Agency Security Committee facilities security level standards. The GSA says it will take at least $1.5 billion to retrofit the building. But anyone familiar with the GSA knows that project. These always cost much more, and the Architect of the Capitol said it would be cheaper to build a fourth building for the House than to locate Members while repairs are being made to Rayburn into the Madison Building. This ill-conceived effort to move the FBI into the Reagan Building is indicative of the dysfunction that exists at GSA. Director Marroni, I'm going to be asking you some questions as I told you I would. And I imagine you share some of these concerns which are reflected in this report as issues contributed to the mismanagement of our federal real estate. Thank you, Mr. Chairman. I have 13 seconds and I'll yield back.\"\nIssues:\nNational Security & Veterans","content_cn":"地区领导力委员会\n斯泰尼能帮什么忙？\n首页\n媒体\n新闻稿\n排名成员霍耶：这个将联邦调查局迁入里根大楼的考虑不周之举，恰恰体现了总务管理局内部存在的失能\n2026年3月26日新闻稿\n华盛顿特区——今天，国会议员斯泰尼·H·霍耶（马里兰州第五选区），金融服务和一般政府（FSGG）拨款小组委员会的排名成员，在众议院拨款委员会监督听证会上就美国政府问责局（GAO）与局长大卫·马罗尼作开场发言。以下是他发言的视频和文字记录：\n图片\n点击此处观看他发言的视频。“非常感谢您，主席先生。我要感谢马罗尼先生今天到场并加入我们。过去一年里，我们听到了许多关于提高政府效率和减少浪费的讨论。我们所有人都应当认同这一目标。尽管我对本届政府对这些目标的承诺深表怀疑，但我们所有人都应当同意，这些目标应当指导我们如何管理联邦房地产组合。我们希望确保我们拥有适量的空间和适当类型的空间，让我们的联邦雇员能够尽可能有效、尽可能安全地代表美国人民履行职责。我总是说，我们需要对政府进行规模调整，不是增加——而是减少，而是根据我们赋予他们的工作进行调整。我认识到这并非易事，我相信马罗尼局长也会同意，但同样清楚的是，总务管理局对我们联邦房地产的管理在某些情况下是有所欠缺的。我想引用本周刚刚发布的监察长报告中的内容，我这里有这份报告，我想您也带来了。我想引用其中的话：‘总务管理局未能持续解决其控制设施中存在的安全设施缺陷，因此使公众、雇员和财产面临安全威胁的风险。’这一发现应当引起本委员会和本众议院每一位成员的关注。该报告大部分内容被涂黑，但它表明——我推测是出于自身安全原因——但它表明，总务管理局未能履行这一关键职责，部分原因是安装和维护安全措施的巨大成本。要看到这一问题的危险，只需沿着宾夕法尼亚大道往下看。\n“特朗普政府正试图将联邦调查局总部从破败不堪、摇摇欲坠的J·埃德加·胡佛大楼迁至不远处的里根大楼。将联邦调查局从一个老旧、暴露且不达标的大楼迁入另一个老旧、暴露且不达标的大楼，并不是解决办法。已故的前联邦调查局局长罗伯特·穆勒在2009年就为联邦调查局寻找新址一事与我接触时，他强调该局需要一座位于大型园区内的新式、安全且集中的设施。里根大楼无法满足联邦调查局的安全和运营要求。它并非作为安全的执法设施而设计，恰恰相反，它是作为面向公共和私人租户的开放、便利的办公楼而设计的。事实上，我这里有一篇文章反映了这一目标。用设计该设施的建筑事务所Paycom Fred and Partners的话说，‘里根大楼强调可达性和通透性。可达性和通透性是国际贸易中心的绝佳特征，而里根大楼正是为满足这一功能而设计的，但不适合执法和情报机构。’1997年《芝加哥论坛报》一篇关于该建筑的文章指出了这一事实。文章说，‘里根大楼将向城市开放联邦官僚机构那冷漠疏远的领域，并为俄克拉荷马城爆炸案后的时代上了一堂重要的课，在那个时代，人们倾向于将所有政府建筑变成令人望而生畏的堡垒。’但联邦调查局总部需要坚不可摧。”\n“即使里根大楼不是位于两条主要干道——第十四街和宾夕法尼亚大道——之间，它仍然无法达到跨机构安全委员会设施安全等级标准。总务管理局表示，改造该建筑至少需要15亿美元。但任何熟悉总务管理局的人都知道，这类项目总是花费远超预算，而且国会大厦建筑师曾表示，为众议院建造第四座大楼，比在雷伯恩大楼维修期间将议员安置到麦迪逊大楼更便宜。这个将联邦调查局迁入里根大楼的考虑不周之举，恰恰体现了总务管理局内部存在的失能。马罗尼局长，正如我告诉过您的，我将向您提出一些问题。我想您也认同其中一些担忧，这些担忧在这份报告中有所反映，是导致我们联邦房地产管理不善的问题。谢谢您，主席先生。我还有13秒，我交回时间。”\n议题：\n国家安全与退伍军人事务","publish_source":"hoyer.house.gov","publish_time":"2026-03-26T11:28:49-04:00"}},{"id":"news-3173","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS (deep pilot)","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"FBI寻求有关伊朗情报官员的信息","title_en":"FBI Seeking Information on Iranian Intelligence Officers","summary_cn":"2025年2月4日，美国联邦调查局公布了涉嫌参与2007年绑架退休FBI特工罗伯特·A·“鲍勃”·莱文森的两名伊朗高级情报官员穆罕默德·巴塞里和艾哈迈德·哈扎伊的姓名，并发布通缉海报。莱文森据报在执行中情局任务时于伊朗基什岛失踪，是美国历史上被扣押时间最长的人质，据其家人称已在新冠疫情前去世。FBI悬赏最高500万美元征集线索，国务院“正义奖励”项目另悬赏最高2000万美元。","summary_en":"On February 4, 2025, the FBI released the names of two senior Iranian intelligence officers, Mohammad Baseri and Ahmad Khazai, allegedly involved in the 2007 abduction of retired FBI Special Agent Robert A. \"Bob\" Levinson, and issued seeking information posters. Levinson reportedly disappeared on Kish Island, Iran, while on a rogue CIA mission, and was the longest-held hostage in U.S. history; according to his family, he died before the COVID-19 pandemic. The FBI offers a reward of up to $5 million, while the State Department's Rewards for Justice program offers up to $20 million.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-25T11:26:58.515096+00:00","url":"http://iranprimer.usip.org/blog/2025/feb/05/fbi-seeking-information-iranian-intelligence-officers","content":"February 5, 2025\nOn Feb. 4, 2025, the Federal Bureau of Investigation (FBI) announced the names of two senior Iranian intelligence officers who were involved in the abduction of Robert. A “Bob” Levinson in 2007. The retired FBI agent was reportedly on a rogue Central Intelligence Agency mission when he disappeared on Kish Island in Iran. He was the longest held hostage in U.S. history and died at some point before the COVID-19 pandemic, according to the Levinson family. The FBI held Mohammad Baseri and Ahmad Khazai from Iran’s Ministry of Intelligence and Security (MOIS) accountable. The following are FBI posters and a press release.  FBI Washington Field Office Releases Seeking Information Posters for Two Senior Iranian Intelligence Officers Involved in the Abduction of Robert A. LevinsonThe FBI Washington Field Office today released seeking information posters featuring two senior Iranian intelligence officers who were involved in the abduction of retired FBI Special Agent Robert A. \"Bob\" Levinson from Kish Island, Iran, on March 9, 2007. The release of the posters is part of the FBI’s ongoing investigation into Bob’s abduction and our commitment to resolving the case for his long-suffering family.The two intelligence officers—Mohammad Baseri and Ahmad Khazai—allegedly acted in their capacity as officials of Iran’s Ministry of Intelligence and Security (MOIS) during Bob’s abduction, detention, and probable death.\"The FBI remains steadfast in our commitment to return Bob to his family,\" said Sanjay Virmani, special agent in charge of the FBI Washington Field Office’s Counterterrorism Division. “Our extensive investigation continues to develop new leads and intelligence, and we will pursue all options to hold every Iranian official involved in his abduction accountable.”For nearly 18 years, the Iranian government has denied knowledge of Bob's whereabouts despite senior intelligence officials authorizing Bob's abduction and detention and launching a disinformation campaign to deflect blame from the Iranian regime.Both Baseri and Khazai are high-ranking MOIS officers. In December 2020, the U.S. Treasury Department’s Office of Foreign Assets Control designated Baseri and Khazai for their role in Bob’s abduction.According to the designation, Baseri has been involved in counterespionage activities inside and outside Iran, as well as sensitive investigations related to Iranian national security issues. He has worked directly with intelligence officials from other countries to harm U.S. interests.Khazai has led MOIS delegations to other countries to assess security situations.The FBI continues to offer a reward of up to $5 million for information that leads to Bob's location, recovery, and return. If you have information about Bob or if you have information about Baseri, Khazai, or others who may have played a role in Bob's abduction, please email levinsonfbireward@fbi.gov. You can also contact your local FBI office or the nearest American Embassy or Consulate or submit a tip via tips.fbi.gov.Additionally, the U.S. State Department’s Rewards for Justice program is offering a reward of up to $20 million for information that leads to Bob’s location, recovery, and return. You can visit RFJ’s website for more information about this reward.","content_cn":"2025年2月5日\n2025年2月4日，联邦调查局（FBI）公布了两名伊朗高级情报官员的姓名，他们参与了2007年对罗伯特·A·“鲍勃”·莱文森的绑架。据报道，这名已退休的FBI特工在伊朗基什岛失踪时，正执行一项未经中央情报局授权的任务。根据莱文森家属的说法，他是美国历史上被扣押时间最长的人质，并在新冠疫情暴发前的某个时候死亡。FBI追究了伊朗情报与安全部（MOIS）的穆罕默德·巴塞里和艾哈迈德·哈扎伊的责任。以下为FBI海报和新闻稿。\n\nFBI华盛顿外地办事处发布寻求两名参与绑架罗伯特·A·莱文森的伊朗高级情报官员信息的海报\n\nFBI华盛顿外地办事处今日发布寻求信息海报，海报展示了两名参与于2007年3月9日在伊朗基什岛绑架已退休FBI特别探员罗伯特·A·“鲍勃”·莱文森的伊朗高级情报官员。发布这些海报是FBI持续调查鲍勃被绑架案，以及致力于为其长期受苦的家人解决此案的一部分。\n\n两名情报官员——穆罕默德·巴塞里和艾哈迈德·哈扎伊——据称在鲍勃遭绑架、拘押以及可能死亡期间，以伊朗情报与安全部（MOIS）官员的身份行事。\n\nFBI华盛顿外地办事处反恐部门负责人、特别探员桑贾伊·维尔马尼表示：“FBI始终坚定致力于让鲍勃回到家人身边。我们广泛的调查持续发现新的线索和情报，我们将寻求一切选择，追究每一名参与绑架他的伊朗官员的责任。”\n\n近18年来，尽管伊朗高级情报官员批准了对鲍勃的绑架和拘押，并发起虚假信息活动以将责任从伊朗政权身上转移，伊朗政府始终否认知晓鲍勃的下落。\n\n巴塞里和哈扎伊均为MOIS高级官员。2020年12月，美国财政部外国资产控制办公室因二人在绑架鲍勃一事中所起的作用，对巴塞里和哈扎伊实施制裁。\n\n根据制裁公告，巴塞里曾参与伊朗境内外的反间谍活动，以及与伊朗国家安全问题有关的敏感调查。他曾直接与其他国家的情报官员合作，损害美国利益。\n\n哈扎伊曾率领MOIS代表团前往其他国家评估安全形势。\n\nFBI继续悬赏最高500万美元，奖励能够促成确定鲍勃下落、找到并将其带回的信息。如果您掌握有关鲍勃的信息，或者掌握有关巴塞里、哈扎伊或其他可能在绑架鲍勃一案中发挥作用者的信息，请发送电子邮件至levinsonfbireward@fbi.gov。您也可以联系当地FBI办事处、最近的美国大使馆或领事馆，或通过tips.fbi.gov提交线索。\n\n此外，美国国务院“正义悬赏”计划正提供最高2,000万美元悬赏，奖励能够促成确定鲍勃下落、找到并将其带回的信息。您可以访问RFJ网站了解有关此项悬赏的更多信息。","publish_source":"iranprimer.usip.org","publish_time":"2025-02-05T16:25:37-04:00"}},{"id":"news-1517","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"对国土安全部的监督","title_en":"Oversight of the Department of Homeland Security","summary_cn":"2026年3月4日上午10点，众议院司法委员会将在雷伯恩众议院办公大楼2141室举行题为“对国土安全部的监督”的听证会，审查国土安全部的使命与项目。证人为主管美国国土安全部的部长克里斯蒂·诺姆。媒体需在2026年3月3日下午5点前向各自国会记者席回复确认。","summary_en":"On March 4, 2026, at 10:00 a.m. ET, the House Judiciary Committee will hold a hearing titled 'Oversight of the Department of Homeland Security' in Room 2141 of the Rayburn House Office Building to examine the mission and programs of DHS. The witness is the Honorable Kristi Noem, Secretary of the U.S. Department of Homeland Security. Press must RSVP to their respective Congressional galleries by 5:00 p.m. ET on March 3, 2026.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-24T20:34:14.522021+00:00","url":"http://judiciary.house.gov/committee-activity/hearings/oversight-department-homeland-security-0","content":"Home\nUpcoming Hearings\nOversight of the Department of Homeland SecurityHearing\nDate:Wed, 03/04/2026 - 10:00 AM\nLocation: 2141 Rayburn House Office Building&amp;nbsp;WASHINGTON, D.C. – The House Judiciary Committee will hold a hearing on Wednesday, March 4, 2026, at 10:00 a.m. ET. The hearing, \"Oversight of the Department of Homeland Security,\" will examine the mission and programs of the Department of Homeland Security. WITNESS: The Honorable Kristi Noem, Secretary, U.S. Department of Homeland SecurityPRESS: RSVP to your respective Congressional galleries by 5:00 p.m. ET on Tuesday, March 3, 2026.\nSubcommittees Committee on the Judiciary (119th Congress)","content_cn":"主页\n即将举行的听证会\n对国土安全部的监督\n听证会\n日期：2026年3月4日（星期三）- 上午10:00\n地点：2141 Rayburn House Office Building，华盛顿特区——众议院司法委员会将于2026年3月4日星期三美国东部时间上午10:00举行听证会。听证会“对国土安全部的监督”将审查国土安全部的使命和项目。\n证人：尊敬的Kristi Noem，美国国土安全部部长\n媒体：请于2026年3月3日星期二美国东部时间下午5:00前向各自的国会记者席位回复确认。\n\n各小组委员会\n众议院司法委员会（第119届国会）","publish_source":"judiciary.house.gov","publish_time":"2026-02-26T13:51:34-05:00"}},{"id":"news-2417","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"对联邦调查局的监督","title_en":"Oversight of the Federal Bureau of Investigation","summary_cn":"美国众议院司法委员会将于2025年9月17日上午10点举行题为“对联邦调查局的监督”的听证会，审查在局长卡什·帕特尔领导下的这一美国首要执法机构。听证会地点为华盛顿特区雷伯恩众议院办公大楼2141室，证人即为联邦调查局局长卡什·帕特尔。","summary_en":"The House Judiciary Committee will hold a hearing titled \"Oversight of the Federal Bureau of Investigation\" on Wednesday, September 17, 2025, at 10:00 a.m. ET, examining the nation's preeminent law enforcement agency under the direction of Director Kash Patel. The hearing will take place in Room 2141 of the Rayburn House Office Building in Washington, D.C., with Director Kash Patel as the witness.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-24T21:43:34.717569+00:00","url":"http://judiciary.house.gov/committee-activity/hearings/oversight-federal-bureau-investigation-10","content":"Home\nUpcoming Hearings\nOversight of the Federal Bureau of InvestigationHearing\nDate:Wed, 09/17/2025 - 10:00 AM\nLocation: 2141 Rayburn House Office Building&amp;nbsp;WASHINGTON, D.C. – The House Judiciary Committee will hold a hearing on Wednesday, September 17, 2025, at 10:00 a.m. ET. The hearing, \"Oversight of the Federal Bureau of Investigation,\" will examine the nation's preeminent law enforcement agency under the direction of Director Kash Patel.WITNESS: The Honorable Kash Patel, Director, Federal Bureau of Investigation - testimony\nSubcommittees Committee on the Judiciary (119th Congress)","content_cn":"主页\n即将举行的听证会\n对联邦调查局的监督\n听证会\n日期：2025年9月17日（星期三）上午10:00\n地点：华盛顿特区雷伯恩众议院办公楼2141室\n华盛顿特区——众议院司法委员会将于2025年9月17日星期三美国东部时间上午10:00举行听证会。听证会主题为“对联邦调查局的监督”，将审查在局长Kash Patel领导下的国家首要执法机构。\n证人：尊敬的Kash Patel，联邦调查局局长——证词\n下属委员会\n司法委员会（第119届国会）","publish_source":"judiciary.house.gov","publish_time":"2025-09-11T09:11:44-04:00"}},{"id":"news-2881","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"约翰逊要求国土安全部长克里斯蒂·诺姆遵守宪法","title_en":"Johnson Demands Homeland Security Secretary Kristi Noem Follow the Constitution","summary_cn":"在众议院国土安全委员会听证会上，得克萨斯州众议员朱莉·约翰逊要求国土安全部长克里斯蒂·诺姆遵守宪法，保护正当程序权利。约翰逊对国土安全部在驱逐出境过程中缺乏正当程序表示担忧，并援引最高法院裁定相关做法违宪的案例，还就移民与海关执法局便衣蒙面人员自称执法人员的做法提出质疑。","summary_en":"During a House Homeland Security Committee hearing, Congresswoman Julie Johnson (TX-32) demanded that Department of Homeland Security Secretary Kristi Noem follow the Constitution by protecting due process rights amid ongoing deportations. Johnson raised concerns about the lack of due process, citing a Supreme Court opinion that found the agency's actions unconstitutional, and questioned the Department's role in arrests, including plainclothes and masked ICE agents identifying themselves as law enforcement officers.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-24T21:46:02.733317+00:00","url":"http://juliejohnson.house.gov/media/press-releases/johnson-demands-homeland-security-secretary-kristi-noem-follow-constitution","content":"Home\nMedia\nPress Releases\nJohnson Demands Homeland Security Secretary Kristi Noem Follow the Constitution\nImage\nMay 14, 2025 Press Release\nWASHINGTON, DC—Today, during a House Homeland Security Committee Hearing with the Secretary of the Department of Homeland Security (DHS) Kristi Noem, Congresswoman Julie Johnson (TX-32) demanded that Noem follow the Constitution by protecting due process rights as DHS continues deportations.“I have a lot of concerns about the lack of due process that your agency has been affording people in this country,” Johnson said to Noem. “In Texas, for example, you had rounded up 171 individuals, were preparing to deport them, and it wasn’t until the Supreme Court issued an opinion that that was unconstitutional and that their due process rights were being violated, did your agency actually stop and adhere to the Supreme Court’s opinion.”Johnson also questioned Noem about the Department’s role in arresting people, raising the concern about U.S. Immigration and Customs Enforcement (ICE) agents identifying themselves as law enforcement officers when they are in plain clothes and masked.    To watch Johnson’s full remarks and questions, click here. Congresswoman Julie Johnson represents Texas’ 32nd Congressional District in the United States House of Representatives, serving on the Homeland Security Committee, Foreign Affairs Committee, and the House Administration Committee. Her district includes parts of Collin, Dallas, and Denton Counties.###\nIssues:\nCongress\nHomeland Security\nMedia\nPress Releases\nIn the News\nVideos","content_cn":"主页\n媒体\n新闻稿\n约翰逊要求国土安全部长克里斯蒂·诺姆遵守宪法\n图片\n2025年5月14日 新闻稿\n华盛顿特区——今天，在众议院国土安全委员会举行的国土安全部（DHS）部长克里斯蒂·诺姆出席的听证会上，众议员朱莉·约翰逊（德州第32选区）要求诺姆在国土安全部继续驱逐行动之际遵守宪法，保护正当程序权利。\n\n约翰逊对诺姆说：“我非常担心贵机构没有为这个国家的人提供正当程序。例如，在得克萨斯州，你们逮捕了171人，准备将他们驱逐出境；直到最高法院发表意见，认定这是违宪行为、他们的正当程序权利受到侵犯之后，贵机构才真正停止行动并遵守最高法院的意见。”\n\n约翰逊还就该部门在逮捕人员方面所起的作用向诺姆提问，并对美国移民与海关执法局（ICE）特工在便衣、戴口罩时将自己表明为执法人员表示担忧。\n\n要观看约翰逊完整的发言和提问，请点击此处。\n\n众议员朱莉·约翰逊代表得克萨斯州第32国会选区，在美国众议院任职，并担任国土安全委员会、外交委员会和众议院行政委员会委员。她的选区包括科林县、达拉斯县和丹顿县的部分地区。\n###\n议题：\n国会\n国土安全\n媒体\n新闻稿\n新闻报道\n视频","publish_source":"juliejohnson.house.gov","publish_time":"2025-05-14T18:10:43-04:00"}},{"id":"news-3232","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"约翰逊被任命为众议院国土安全委员会领导层成员","title_en":"Johnson Named to House Homeland Security Committee Leadership","summary_cn":"得克萨斯州众议员朱莉·约翰逊被任命为众议院国土安全委员会副主席（Vice Ranking Member），协助首席民主党人本尼·汤普森领导民主党在南部边境安全、联邦应急管理运作和国土保护方面的工作。该委员会对国土安全部拥有直接监督权，负责审议涉及美国安全的相关立法。","summary_en":"Congresswoman Julie Johnson (TX-32) was named Vice Ranking Member on the House Homeland Security Committee, assisting Ranking Member Bennie Thompson in leading Democratic efforts on southern border security, federal emergency management oversight, and homeland protection. The Committee has direct oversight of the Department of Homeland Security and reviews legislation related to U.S. security, including border, transportation, maritime security, and emergency management.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-24T22:12:40.214868+00:00","url":"http://juliejohnson.house.gov/media/press-releases/johnson-named-house-homeland-security-committee-leadership","content":"Home\nMedia\nPress Releases\nJohnson Named to House Homeland Security Committee Leadership\nJanuary 23, 2025 Press Release\nWASHINGTON, DC – Congresswoman Julie Johnson (TX-32) was named Vice Ranking Member on the House Homeland Security Committee. In this position, Johnson will assist Ranking Member Bennie Thompson (MS-02), the top Democrat on the Committee, in leading Democratic efforts to secure the southern border, oversee federal emergency management operations, and protect the homeland of the United States.  “Keeping our nation safe and strengthening the security of our southern border is a top priority of mine,” said Johnson. “As Vice Ranking Member on the House Homeland Security Committee, I am thrilled to be in a position that can help bring Democrats and Republicans together to develop bipartisan solutions on issues that matter to Texas families. It is critical that while we work to secure our border, we must create safe, legal, and efficient pathways for immigrants to come to our country and contribute to our economy. Texans have a responsibility to lead on these important issues, and I look forward to working with members of both parties to end the partisan bickering and deliver results for my neighbors.”“Rep. Julie Johnson will be an excellent Vice Ranking Member of the esteemed House Homeland Security Committee in the 119th Congress, and her well-deserved appointment is a reflection of her exceptional talents and strong leadership in Texas and beyond,” said Assistant Democratic Leader Joe Neguse. “Collaborating closely with Ranking Member Bennie Thompson, this committee will address critical challenges and advance meaningful initiatives for the American people. I look forward to witnessing all that Rep. Johnson will achieve in this vital role.”The Homeland Security Committee reviews legislation related to the security of the United States, including border security, transportation and maritime security, and emergency management. The Committee has direct oversight of the Department of Homeland Security. Congresswoman Julie Johnson represents Texas’ 32nd Congressional District in the United States House of Representatives, serving on the Homeland Security Committee, Foreign Affairs Committee, and the House Administration Committee. Her district includes parts of Collin, Dallas, and Denton Counties.###\nIssues:\nCongress\nMedia\nPress Releases\nIn the News\nVideos","content_cn":"主页\n媒体\n新闻稿\nJohnson被任命为众议院国土安全委员会领导层成员\n2025年1月23日 新闻稿\n\n华盛顿特区——众议员Julie Johnson（得克萨斯州第32选区）被任命为众议院国土安全委员会副首席少数党成员。在这一职位上，Johnson将协助委员会首席少数党成员、委员会最高级别民主党成员Bennie Thompson（密西西比州第2选区），领导民主党开展确保南部边境安全、监督联邦应急管理行动以及保护美国国土的工作。\n\nJohnson表示：“维护国家安全、加强南部边境安全是我的首要任务之一。作为众议院国土安全委员会副首席少数党成员，我非常荣幸能够担任这一职务，帮助民主党和共和党就关系到得克萨斯州家庭的问题制定两党解决方案。在努力确保边境安全的同时，我们必须为移民进入我国并为经济作出贡献创造安全、合法且高效的途径，这一点至关重要。得克萨斯人有责任在这些重要问题上发挥领导作用，我期待与两党成员合作，结束党派争吵，为我的选民取得成果。”\n\n助理民主党领袖Joe Neguse表示：“Julie Johnson众议员将成为第119届国会杰出的众议院国土安全委员会副首席少数党成员，她当之无愧的任命体现了她在得克萨斯州及其他地区展现出的非凡才能和强大领导力。在Bennie Thompson首席少数党成员的领导下，该委员会将应对关键挑战，推动对美国人民有意义的倡议。我期待见证Johnson众议员在这一重要职位上取得的一切成就。”\n\n国土安全委员会审议与美国安全有关的立法，包括边境安全、运输和海事安全以及应急管理。该委员会直接监督国土安全部。\n\n众议员Julie Johnson代表美国众议院得克萨斯州第32国会选区，并任职于国土安全委员会、外交事务委员会和众议院行政委员会。她的选区包括科林县、达拉斯县和丹顿县的部分地区。\n\n###\n议题：\n国会\n媒体\n新闻稿\n新闻报道\n视频","publish_source":"juliejohnson.house.gov","publish_time":"2025-01-23T13:18:04-05:00"}},{"id":"news-1663","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"约翰逊投票反对为ICE和国土安全部提供资金的法案","title_en":"Johnson Votes Against Bill to Fund ICE and the Department of Homeland Security","summary_cn":"2026年2月3日，得克萨斯州第32选区众议员、众议院国土安全委员会副主席朱莉·约翰逊投票反对为移民和海关执法局（ICE）及国土安全部提供资金的法案。她批评ICE在特朗普和部长诺姆领导下日益激进、缺乏问责，要求ICE立即撤出明尼阿波利斯、停止无司法令逮捕、对每起枪击独立调查、联邦探员佩戴执法记录仪并停止拘留美国公民。法案已获众议院通过，将为相关机构提供资金至2026年2月13日。","summary_en":"On February 3, 2026, Congresswoman Julie Johnson (TX-32), Vice Ranking Member of the House Homeland Security Committee, voted against a bill to fund ICE and the Department of Homeland Security. She criticized ICE under Trump and Secretary Noem as increasingly aggressive and unaccountable, demanding ICE leave Minneapolis, end warrantless arrests, independently investigate every DHS shooting, require body cameras, and stop detaining U.S. citizens. The bill passed the House and funds the agencies through February 13, 2026.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-18T15:35:20.845053+00:00","url":"http://juliejohnson.house.gov/media/press-releases/johnson-votes-against-bill-fund-ice-and-department-homeland-security","content":"Home\nMedia\nPress Releases\nJohnson Votes Against Bill to Fund ICE and the Department of Homeland Security\nFebruary 3, 2026 Press Release\nWASHINGTON, DC — Today, Congresswoman Julie Johnson (TX-32), Vice Ranking Member on the House Homeland Security Committee, voted against a bill to fund ICE and the Department of Homeland Security.“Congress cannot continue writing blank checks to an agency that is actively harming and killing American citizens. Under Trump and Secretary Kristi Noem, ICE has become increasingly aggressive, unaccountable, and violent—spreading fear in our cities and making our communities less safe,” said Johnson. “That is why I voted against funding the Department of Homeland Security and ICE, and why I will continue to oppose this funding until there are real, enforceable reforms. No more money without accountability. Secretary Noem must be held responsible for the violence she enabled—and Congress must finally do its job and uphold the Constitution.”To support continued funding for ICE and the Department of Homeland Security, Johnson is demanding that: ICE must immediately leave Minneapolis and stop terrorizing American cities. Arrests without judicial warrants must end, and arrests at churches, schools, shelters, and courthouses must stop.Every DHS shooting must be fully and independently investigated.Federal agents must be identifiable, accountable, and properly trained, including wearing body cameras.The detention and deportation of U.S. citizens must end.Detention facilities must meet basic standards of care and be subject to real oversight.The bill passed the House and will now go to the president for his signature. The bill funds ICE and the Department of Homeland Security through Friday, February 13, 2026.Congresswoman Julie Johnson represents Texas’s 32nd Congressional District in the United States House of Representatives, serving on the Homeland Security Committee, Foreign Affairs Committee, and the House Administration Committee. Her district includes parts of Collin, Dallas, and Denton Counties.###\nIssues:\nCongress\nHomeland Security\nMedia\nPress Releases\nIn the News\nVideos","content_cn":"首页\n媒体\n新闻稿\n约翰逊投票反对为移民和海关执法局及国土安全部提供资金的法案\n2026年2月3日新闻稿\n华盛顿特区——今天，国会议员朱莉·约翰逊（德克萨斯州第32选区），众议院国土安全委员会副主席排名成员，投票反对一项为移民和海关执法局及国土安全部提供资金的法案。“国会不能继续向一个正在积极伤害和杀害美国公民的机构开出空白支票。在特朗普和部长克里斯蒂·诺姆的领导下，移民和海关执法局变得越来越咄咄逼人、不负责任且充满暴力——在我们的城市中散播恐惧，使我们的社区变得更不安全，”约翰逊说。“这就是为什么我投票反对为国土安全部和移民和海关执法局提供资金，也是为什么我将继续反对这项拨款，直到有真正可执行的改革。没有问责就没有更多资金。诺姆部长必须为她所纵容的暴力行为负责——国会必须最终履行职责，维护宪法。”为了支持继续为移民和海关执法局和国土安全部提供资金，约翰逊要求：移民和海关执法局必须立即离开明尼阿波利斯，停止恐吓美国城市。没有司法逮捕令的逮捕必须结束，在教堂、学校、庇护所和法院的逮捕必须停止。国土安全部的每一起枪击事件都必须得到全面、独立的调查。联邦探员必须可识别、可问责并接受适当培训，包括佩戴随身摄像头。对美国公民的拘留和驱逐必须结束。拘留设施必须达到基本护理标准，并接受真正的监督。该法案在众议院获得通过，现将送交总统签署。该法案为移民和海关执法局和国土安全部提供资金至2026年2月13日星期五。国会议员朱莉·约翰逊代表德克萨斯州第32国会选区，任职于国土安全委员会、外交事务委员会和众议院行政委员会。她的选区包括科林县、达拉斯县和丹顿县的部分地区。###\n议题：\n国会\n国土安全\n媒体\n新闻稿\n新闻报道\n视频","publish_source":"juliejohnson.house.gov","publish_time":"2026-02-03T17:21:53-05:00"}},{"id":"news-1761","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"约翰逊投票反对国土安全部拨款法案，抨击ICE恐吓社区","title_en":"Johnson Votes Against Department of Homeland Security Funding, Blasts ICE for Terrorizing Communities","summary_cn":"2026年1月22日，得克萨斯州第32选区众议员朱莉·约翰逊投票反对为美国国土安全部提供至2026年9月的拨款法案，批评该部门无视宪法、法治和民众安全，指责ICE特工无正当理由拘留和逮捕美国公民、无搜查令进入住宅、过度使用武力。她此前提出四项限制ICE和国土安全部权力的修正案，均被共和党人阻止。法案以220票对207票在众议院通过，现已提交参议院审议。","summary_en":"On January 22, 2026, Congresswoman Julie Johnson (TX-32) voted against a bill to fund the Department of Homeland Security through September 2026, blasting the Department for disregarding the Constitution, the rule of law, and public safety. She accused ICE agents and DHS of detaining and arresting American citizens without justification, entering homes without warrants, using excessive force, and ignoring constitutional rights. Four amendments she offered to impose guardrails on ICE and DHS were blocked by Republicans. The House passed the funding bill 220-207, sending it to the Senate.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-24T20:42:15.181368+00:00","url":"http://juliejohnson.house.gov/media/press-releases/johnson-votes-against-department-homeland-security-funding-blasts-ice","content":"Home\nMedia\nPress Releases\nJohnson Votes Against Department of Homeland Security Funding, Blasts ICE for Terrorizing Communities\nImage\nJanuary 22, 2026 Press Release\nWASHINGTON, DC — Today, Congresswoman Julie Johnson (TX-32) voted against a bill to fund the Department of Homeland Security (DHS) through September 2026, blasting the Department’s disregard for the Constitution, the rule of law, and the safety of the people it is supposed to protect. “We have seen ICE agents and the Department of Homeland Security detain and arrest American citizens without justification, enter homes without warrants, use excessive force when it wasn’t required, and ignore constitutional rights. This is a department that is out of control, going rogue, and needs to be reined in,” said Johnson. “The American people deserve safety without fear, enforcement without lawlessness, and a government that follows the Constitution. Until the Department of Homeland Security is willing to operate within the rule of law, I cannot support continued funding without meaningful reform.”Last night, during a House Rules Committee hearing, Johnson offered four commonsense amendments to impose basic constitutional guardrails on ICE agents and DHS—limiting qualified immunity, requiring accountability for abuse, ensuring due process protections, and providing civil recourse when rights are violated. Republicans unanimously blocked the House from considering these amendments.The House passed the DHS funding bill by a vote of 220 to 207. The bill now moves to the Senate for consideration.Johnson has been a relentless advocate for accountability from ICE and the DHS, directly challenging Secretary Noem and her department for denying due process and violating constitutional rights. Last September, Johnson visited Texas’s Bluebonnet Detention Center, where she witnessed firsthand the treatment of detainees and spoke with individuals being held despite not having committed any crimes.Congresswoman Julie Johnson represents Texas’s 32nd Congressional District in the United States House of Representatives, serving on the Homeland Security Committee, Foreign Affairs Committee, and the House Administration Committee. Her district includes parts of Collin, Dallas, and Denton Counties.###\nIssues:\nCongress\nHomeland Security\nMedia\nPress Releases\nIn the News\nVideos","content_cn":"主页\n媒体\n新闻稿\n约翰逊投票反对国土安全部拨款，痛斥移民与海关执法局恐吓社区\n图片\n2026年1月22日 新闻稿\n华盛顿特区——今天，众议员朱莉·约翰逊（得克萨斯州第32选区）投票反对一项为国土安全部（DHS）提供资金至2026年9月的法案，并抨击该部门无视宪法、法治以及其本应保护的民众安全。“我们已经看到移民与海关执法局（ICE）特工和国土安全部在没有正当理由的情况下拘留和逮捕美国公民、无搜查令进入住宅、在不需要使用武力时使用过度武力，并无视宪法权利。这是一个已经失控、擅自妄为、需要被约束的部门，”约翰逊说。“美国人民应当享有不带恐惧的安全、遵守法律的执法，以及遵循宪法的政府。在国土安全部愿意在法治框架内运作并进行有意义的改革之前，我不能支持继续拨款。”昨晚，在众议院规则委员会听证会上，约翰逊提出了四项常识性修正案，旨在为ICE特工和DHS设置基本的宪法防护措施——限制合格豁免权、要求对滥用行为问责、确保正当程序保护，并在权利受到侵犯时提供民事救济。共和党人一致阻止众议院审议这些修正案。众议院以220票对207票通过了DHS拨款法案。该法案现提交参议院审议。约翰逊一直不懈地倡导追究ICE和DHS的责任，直接质疑诺姆部长及其部门拒绝提供正当程序并侵犯宪法权利的行为。去年9月，约翰逊访问了得克萨斯州的蓝帽拘留中心，亲眼目睹被拘留者所受待遇，并与一些尽管没有犯罪却仍被关押的人交谈。众议员朱莉·约翰逊代表美国众议院得克萨斯州第32国会选区，并在国土安全委员会、外交事务委员会和众议院行政委员会任职。她的选区包括科林县、达拉斯县和登顿县的部分地区。###\n议题：\n国会\n国土安全\n媒体\n新闻稿\n新闻报道\n视频","publish_source":"juliejohnson.house.gov","publish_time":"2026-01-22T17:05:58-05:00"}},{"id":"news-1214","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"基恩敦促新任国土安全部长马林“深入审视”拟建的罗克斯伯里设施","title_en":"Kean Urges New DHS Secretary Mullin to Take \"Deeper Look\" at Proposed Roxbury Facility","summary_cn":"美国众议员汤姆·基恩致信国土安全部长马林，要求深入审视该部拟在新泽西州罗克斯伯里镇建设的移民及海关执法局处理设施。基恩指出，当地官员担忧该设施将导致市政税收流失、加重警察与志愿消防等公共安全服务负担，并质疑公用设施、环境及分区条件是否适宜。他呼吁联邦与地方加强协调，并提及自己已提出《2026年地方纳税人保护法案》。","summary_en":"U.S. Rep. Tom Kean Jr. sent a letter to Homeland Security Secretary Markwayne Mullin urging a deeper review of the department's proposed ICE processing facility in Roxbury Township, New Jersey. Kean cited local officials' concerns about lost municipal tax revenue, added strain on police and volunteer fire services, and questions over utility infrastructure, environmental constraints and zoning. He called for stronger federal-local coordination and noted his Local Taxpayer Protection Act of 2026.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-18T14:34:48.760967+00:00","url":"http://kean.house.gov/media/press-releases/kean-urges-new-dhs-secretary-mullin-take-deeper-look-proposed-roxbury-facility","content":"X\nHow Can I Help?\nHome\nMedia\nPress Releases\nKean Urges New DHS Secretary Mullin to Take \"Deeper Look\" at Proposed Roxbury Facility\nImage April 7, 2026 Press Release(April 7, 2026) WASHINGTON, D.C. – Today, Congressman Tom Kean, Jr. (NJ-07) sent a letter to U.S. Department of Homeland Security (DHS) Secretary Markwayne Mullin urging a thorough review of the Department’s proposed processing facility in Roxbury Township, New Jersey.In his letter to the newly confirmed Secretary, Congressman Kean called for meaningful engagement with local officials who have raised concerns about the facility’s impact on their community.Congressman Kean wrote, “I respectfully request that the Department take a deeper look at the proposal and give careful consideration to the concerns raised by local officials, while working collaboratively with multiple levels of government to identify the most appropriate path forward.”Local elected officials have identified several concerns about the proposed site, including a loss of municipal tax revenue, operational strain on local public safety services, and the adequacy of utility infrastructure. In light of their concerns, Congressman Kean is pressing for greater communication between DHS and Township leadership as the Department moves through its decision-making process.Kean continued, “A high level of coordination between federal officials and local leadership would be hugely beneficial in addressing outstanding questions and ensuring that decisions are informed by on-the-ground realities.” In February, Congressman Kean introduced the Local Taxpayer Protection Act of 2026, federal legislation to ensure that local taxpayers and municipalities like Roxbury, New Jersey, are not left shouldering the costs associated with hosting federal law enforcement processing or detention facilities. Information on the bill can be found HERE.Read the full letter below and HERE. Dear Secretary Mullin:  Congratulations on your recent nomination and bipartisan confirmation. It was a pleasure working with you during your service in the United States Senate, where you consistently sought to build bipartisan consensus and advance meaningful policy solutions designed to stand the test of time. I look forward to continuing that work as you lead the Department in addressing complex security threats and challenges facing our country.  I write regarding the proposed U.S. Immigration and Customs Enforcement (ICE) processing facility in Roxbury Township, New Jersey, within my district. I respectfully request that the Department take a deeper look at the proposal and give careful consideration to the concerns raised by local officials, while working collaboratively with multiple levels of government to identify the most appropriate path forward.  Roxbury’s elected leaders have expressed several concerns related to the proposed facility. These include the projected fiscal impact associated with the federal acquisition of the property, which local officials indicate could result in a loss of municipal tax revenue, placing additional burden on local taxpayers. Township officials have also cited increased operational strain on local public safety services, including the Township’s police department, volunteer fire and rescue personnel. In addition, local leaders have raised questions regarding site suitability, including the adequacy of utility infrastructure, environmental constraints and zoning considerations. It is important that these local considerations are comprehensively evaluated as part of the Department’s decision-making process.   Since December 2025, I have been actively engaged on this issue on a daily basis and in consistent communication with senior officials at the Department of Homeland Security to ensure that Roxbury’s concerns are clearly conveyed and carefully reviewed. I will continue to serve as a conduit for constructive dialogue so that all perspectives are understood. A high level of coordination between federal officials and local leadership would be hugely beneficial in addressing outstanding questions and ensuring that decisions are informed by on-the-ground realities.  My priority is to ensure that any decision is the result of a thoughtful and balanced approach that considers law enforcement’s operational necessities alongside the interests of the local community. I remain fully committed to working with you and the residents of Roxbury to identify a workable solution. Thank you for your attention to this matter and for your continued commitment to thoughtful, collaborative engagement.Sincerely, Thomas H. Kean, Jr. Member of Congress###","content_cn":"X\n我能帮什么忙？\n首页\n媒体\n新闻稿\n基恩敦促新任国土安全部部长马林对拟建的罗克斯伯里设施进行“更深入审视”\n图片 2026年4月7日 新闻稿（2026年4月7日）华盛顿特区——今天，国会议员小汤姆·基恩（新泽西州第七选区）致信美国国土安全部（DHS）部长马克韦恩·马林，敦促对该部拟在新泽西州罗克斯伯里镇设立的处理设施进行全面审查。\n在致这位新确认部长的信中，基恩议员呼吁与已对该设施影响其社区提出担忧的地方官员进行有意义的接触。\n基恩议员写道：“我谨请求该部对这一提案进行更深入的审视，认真考虑地方官员提出的关切，同时与各级政府协同合作，确定最合适的前进道路。”\n当地民选官员已就拟建选址提出多项关切，包括市政税收损失、对地方公共安全服务的运营压力以及公用事业基础设施是否充足。鉴于他们的担忧，基恩议员正敦促国土安全部在该部推进决策过程中与镇政府领导层加强沟通。\n基恩继续写道：“联邦官员与地方领导层之间的高度协调将极大地有助于解决悬而未决的问题，并确保决策以实际情况为依据。”今年2月，基恩议员提出了《2026年地方纳税人保护法案》，这是一项联邦立法，旨在确保地方纳税人和像新泽西州罗克斯伯里这样的市政当局不会被迫承担因设立联邦执法处理或拘留设施而产生的相关成本。该法案的信息可在此处查阅。\n请在下方及此处阅读完整信函。\n尊敬的马林部长：\n祝贺您近期获得提名并获两党确认。在您担任美国参议员期间与您共事是我的荣幸，您始终寻求建立两党共识并推进旨在经得起时间考验的有意义的政策解决方案。我期待在您领导该部应对我国面临的复杂安全威胁和挑战时继续这一合作。\n我致信是关于拟设在我选区内新泽西州罗克斯伯里镇的美国移民和海关执法局（ICE）处理设施。我谨请求该部对这一提案进行更深入的审视，认真考虑地方官员提出的关切，同时与各级政府协同合作，确定最合适的前进道路。\n罗克斯伯里的民选领导人已就该拟建设施表达了多项关切。其中包括联邦收购该地产所带来的预计财政影响，地方官员表示这可能导致市政税收损失，给当地纳税人带来额外负担。镇政府官员还指出，这将对地方公共安全服务造成更大的运营压力，包括镇警察局、志愿消防和救援人员。此外，地方领导人还就选址适宜性提出疑问，包括公用事业基础设施是否充足、环境限制和分区规划方面的考量。在该部的决策过程中，对这些地方性考量进行全面评估十分重要。\n自2025年12月以来，我每天都积极参与这一问题，并与国土安全部高级官员保持持续沟通，以确保罗克斯伯里的关切得到明确传达和认真审查。我将继续充当建设性对话的渠道，使各方观点都能得到理解。联邦官员与地方领导层之间的高度协调将极大地有助于解决悬而未决的问题，并确保决策以实际情况为依据。\n我的首要任务是确保任何决定都是深思熟虑、平衡兼顾的结果，既考虑执法部门的运营需要，也兼顾当地社区的利益。我完全致力于与您和罗克斯伯里居民合作，找到可行的解决方案。感谢您对此事的关注，以及您对深思熟虑、协作接触的持续承诺。\n此致，\n小托马斯·H·基恩\n国会议员###","publish_source":"kean.house.gov","publish_time":"2026-04-07T15:08:24-04:00"}},{"id":"news-2026","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"国会议员克里希纳穆尔蒂要求国土安全部立即采取行动，因ICE阻止被拘留者获取联邦规定的隐私表格","title_en":"Congressman Krishnamoorthi Demands Immediate DHS Action After ICE Blocks Detainees from Accessing Federally Required Privacy Forms","summary_cn":"2025年12月2日，伊利诺伊州众议员拉贾·克里希纳穆尔蒂致信国土安全部长诺姆，指出ICE人员系统性未能向被拘留者提供联邦规定的隐私释放表格60-001，导致被拘留者无法授权国会查询，国会无法履行基本监督职能。他称这构成人为的“第22条军规”，违反《隐私法》等联邦法律，要求所有ICE拘留设施应要求提供该表格、及时处理并公开统一指引，并请求12月11日前获得简报和整改计划。","summary_en":"On December 2, 2025, Congressman Raja Krishnamoorthi (D-IL) sent a letter to Homeland Security Secretary Noem raising alarms that ICE personnel systematically fail to provide detainees with federally required Privacy Release Form 60-001, preventing detainees from authorizing congressional inquiries and blocking basic oversight. He described a manufactured catch-22 violating the Privacy Act and other laws, and demanded all ICE facilities provide the form on request, process it promptly, and issue public uniform guidance, requesting a briefing by December 11 and a remediation plan.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-18T15:56:34.134665+00:00","url":"http://krishnamoorthi.house.gov/media/press-releases/congressman-krishnamoorthi-demands-immediate-dhs-action-after-ice-blocks","content":"Image\nHome\nMedia\nPress Releases\nCongressman Krishnamoorthi Demands Immediate DHS Action After ICE Blocks Detainees from Accessing Federally Required Privacy FormsDecember 3, 2025 Press ReleaseWASHINGTON – Yesterday, Congressman Raja Krishnamoorthi (D-IL) sent a letter to Homeland Security Secretary Kristi Noem raising alarms over what he describes as persistent, systemic failures by U.S. Immigration and Customs Enforcement (ICE) personnel to provide detainees with access to Privacy Release Form 60-001, the federally required document that allows Members of Congress to lawfully obtain information about individual detainee cases and intervene when rights violations or urgent safety issues arise. Without this form, detainees cannot authorize congressional inquiries, and Congress cannot perform even the most basic oversight functions mandated under federal law.In the letter, Congressman Krishnamoorthi details repeated reports from attorneys, families, and advocates that detainees are either denied access to the form entirely or that completed forms “are never transmitted to the proper channels.” He cites ICE’s own Congressional Relations Office, which advised that detainees should be able to obtain the form by phone or written request, avenues that, in practice, “do not function,” according to the congressman.Congressman Krishnamoorthi wrote that this breakdown has produced what he described as a manufactured catch-22: ICE refuses to share information with Congress without a signed privacy waiver, while simultaneously refusing to provide detainees the very form required to authorize the release. This, he notes, unlawfully obstructs detainees’ rights and “prevents Congress from conducting even basic oversight.”The letter underscores that federal law, including the Privacy Act of 1974 and the Judicial Redress Act of 2015, presumes detainees have meaningful access to the required privacy form. The congressman argues denying that access effectively blocks lawful oversight and undermines the department’s own stated procedures.Congressman Krishnamoorthi calls on DHS to take immediate corrective action, including:Ensuring all ICE detention facilities provide Privacy Release Form 60-001 to any detainee upon request, without delay or obstruction.Directing all field offices, contractors, and personnel to promptly process completed forms and transmit them to congressional offices without exception.Issuing and publicly posting clear, uniform guidance affirming ICE’s legal obligations regarding privacy waivers and cooperation with congressional inquiries.He requests a DHS briefing by December 11 and a detailed plan to remedy and prevent future failures.The full letter can be found here.","content_cn":"图片\n首页\n媒体\n新闻稿\n国会议员克里希纳穆尔蒂要求国土安全部立即采取行动，此前ICE阻止被拘留者获取联邦规定的隐私表格\n2025年12月3日 新闻稿\n华盛顿——昨天，国会议员拉贾·克里希纳穆尔蒂（伊利诺伊州民主党人）致信国土安全部部长克里斯蒂·诺姆，对他所称的美国移民和海关执法局（ICE）人员长期、系统性未能向被拘留者提供隐私披露表格60-001一事发出警告。该表格是联邦规定的文件，允许国会议员合法获取有关个别被拘留者案件的信息，并在发生权利侵犯或紧急安全问题时代入干预。没有这份表格，被拘留者无法授权国会进行调查，国会也无法履行联邦法律所规定的最基本监督职能。\n在信中，克里希纳穆尔蒂议员详细列举了来自律师、家属和倡导者的反复报告，称被拘留者要么完全无法获得该表格，要么填好的表格“从未被传送到适当的渠道”。他援引ICE自己的国会关系办公室的建议，即被拘留者应能通过电话或书面请求获得该表格，而据这位议员称，这些途径在实践中“根本不起作用”。\n克里希纳穆尔蒂议员写道，这种失灵造成了他所称的人为的第22条军规：ICE在没有签署隐私豁免书的情况下拒绝与国会分享信息，同时又拒绝向被拘留者提供授权披露所需的那份表格。他指出，这非法妨碍了被拘留者的权利，并“使国会连最基本的监督都无法进行”。\n该信强调，联邦法律，包括1974年《隐私法》和2015年《司法救济法》，都推定被拘留者能够切实获得所需的隐私表格。这位议员认为，剥夺这一获取途径实际上阻碍了合法监督，并破坏了该部自己宣称的程序。\n克里希纳穆尔蒂议员呼吁国土安全部立即采取纠正措施，包括：\n确保所有ICE拘留设施在被拘留者提出请求时，无延迟、无阻碍地向其提供隐私披露表格60-001。\n指示所有外地办事处、承包商和人员迅速处理填好的表格，并将其无一例外地传送给国会办公室。\n发布并公开张贴明确、统一的指导意见，确认ICE在隐私豁免和配合国会调查方面的法律义务。\n他要求国土安全部在12月11日前进行简报，并提交一份详细的计划，以纠正和防止未来的失误。\n完整信函可在此处查阅。","publish_source":"krishnamoorthi.house.gov","publish_time":"2025-12-03T11:39:53-05:00"}},{"id":"news-1473","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"国会议员克里希纳穆尔蒂动议传唤国土安全部长诺姆，指控特朗普政府DHS、ICE和CBP滥用职权","title_en":"Congressman Krishnamoorthi Moves to Subpoena DHS Secretary Noem Over Trump Administration DHS, ICE, and CBP Abuses","summary_cn":"2026年3月4日，伊利诺伊州众议员拉贾·克里希纳穆尔蒂在众议院监督与政府改革委员会听证会上动议传唤国土安全部长克里斯蒂·诺姆，指控特朗普政府下DHS、ICE和CBP存在滥用行为且未配合国会监督。他提及联邦移民探员致命枪击事件、美国公民被拘留及对其伊利诺伊州ICE设施的进入被拒，并称诺姆未实质回应其十余封监督信函。该动议将留待听证会结束时表决。","summary_en":"On March 4, 2026, Congressman Raja Krishnamoorthi (D-IL) moved during a House Oversight and Government Reform Committee hearing to subpoena Homeland Security Secretary Kristi Noem, citing abuses by DHS, ICE, and CBP under the Trump administration and the Department's failure to comply with congressional oversight. He cited deadly shootings by federal immigration agents, detentions of U.S. citizens, and being denied entry to Illinois ICE facilities, noting Noem failed to substantively answer over a dozen oversight letters. The motion is held in abeyance until a vote at the hearing's end.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-18T15:26:33.133418+00:00","url":"http://krishnamoorthi.house.gov/media/press-releases/congressman-krishnamoorthi-moves-subpoena-dhs-secretary-noem-over-trump","content":"Image\nHome\nMedia\nPress Releases\nCongressman Krishnamoorthi Moves to Subpoena DHS Secretary Noem Over Trump Administration DHS, ICE, and CBP AbusesMarch 4, 2026 Press ReleaseWASHINGTON — During a hearing of the House Committee on Oversight and Government Reform today, Congressman Raja Krishnamoorthi (D-IL) moved to subpoena Department of Homeland Security Secretary Kristi Noem, citing abuses by DHS, Immigration and Customs Enforcement (ICE), and Customs and Border Protection (CBP) under the Trump administration and the Department’s failure to comply with congressional oversight. The motion came as Congressman Krishnamoorthi questioned Governor Tim Walz of Minnesota and Minnesota Attorney General Keith Ellison about the impact of recent immigration enforcement operations.During the hearing, Congressman Krishnamoorthi pointed to deadly shootings involving federal immigration agents, including the killings of Renée Nicole Good, Alex Pretti, and Silverio Villegas González, as well as detentions of U.S. citizens and the use of force against civilians during enforcement operations. He also noted that he has been denied entry to ICE facilities in Illinois and that Secretary Noem has failed to respond substantively to more than a dozen oversight letters from his office.Congressman Krishnamoorthi highlighted the individuals and families affected by DHS enforcement actions before formally moving to subpoena the Secretary:“Secretary Noem must answer for her wrongdoing. For Jaime, my State of the Union guest, who raises his little sister after his father was coerced into self-deportation. For Chicagoan Marimar Martinez, who was shot five times. For my constituent Evelyn, an 18-year-old U.S. citizen who was wrongfully detained by ICE. For Renée Nicole Good, Alex Pretti, and Silverio Villegas González, and all the other victims of ICE and CBP. For the American people. It's for all those reasons that, Mr. Chairman, pursuant to clause 2(k)(6) of House Rule XI, I move to subpoena Secretary Kristi Noem to testify before the House Committee on Oversight and Government Reform.”The motion is being held in abeyance until the end of the hearing when it will receive a vote.Footage of Congressman Krishnamoorthi’s remarks is available here.","content_cn":"图片\n首页\n媒体\n新闻稿\n国会议员克里希纳穆尔蒂动议传唤国土安全部部长诺姆，追究特朗普政府时期国土安全部、移民及海关执法局和海关与边境保护局的滥权行为\n2026年3月4日 新闻稿\n华盛顿——在今日举行的众议院监督与政府改革委员会听证会上，国会议员拉贾·克里希纳穆尔蒂（伊利诺伊州民主党人）动议传唤国土安全部部长克里斯蒂·诺姆，理由是在特朗普政府时期国土安全部、移民及海关执法局（ICE）和海关与边境保护局（CBP）存在滥权行为，且该部未能配合国会监督。此项动议提出之际，克里希纳穆尔蒂议员正就近期移民执法行动的影响，向明尼苏达州州长蒂姆·沃尔兹和明尼苏达州总检察长基思·埃里森进行质询。\n听证会期间，克里希纳穆尔蒂议员指出，涉及联邦移民执法人员的致命枪击事件，包括勒妮·妮科尔·古德、亚历克斯·普雷蒂和西尔韦里奥·比列加斯·冈萨雷斯被杀，以及美国公民遭拘留和执法行动中对平民使用武力的情况。他还指出，他本人被拒绝进入伊利诺伊州的ICE设施，而诺姆部长未能对其办公室发出的十余封监督信函作出实质性回应。\n克里希纳穆尔蒂议员在正式动议传唤部长之前，特别提到了受国土安全部执法行动影响的个人和家庭：\n“诺姆部长必须为其不当行为作出交代。为了海梅——我的国情咨文嘉宾，他在父亲被胁迫自行离境后抚养年幼的妹妹。为了芝加哥人玛丽玛尔·马丁内斯，她身中五枪。为了我的选民伊芙琳，一位18岁的美国公民，被ICE错误拘留。为了勒妮·妮科尔·古德、亚历克斯·普雷蒂和西尔韦里奥·比列加斯·冈萨雷斯，以及所有ICE和CBP的其他受害者。为了美国人民。基于以上所有理由，主席先生，依据众议院规则第十一条第2(k)(6)款，我动议传唤克里斯蒂·诺姆部长到众议院监督与政府改革委员会作证。”\n该动议将暂缓至听证会结束时进行表决。\n克里希纳穆尔蒂议员发言的视频可在此处获取。","publish_source":"krishnamoorthi.house.gov","publish_time":"2026-03-04T12:02:38-05:00"}},{"id":"news-1926","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"国会议员克里希纳穆尔蒂就司法部将FBI反恐和反间谍资源转用于大规模移民突袭发出警告","title_en":"Congressman Krishnamoorthi Sounds Alarm Over DOJ Diverting FBI Counterterrorism and Counterintelligence Resources to Mass Immigration Raids","summary_cn":"2025年12月23日，伊利诺伊州众议员拉贾·克里希纳穆尔蒂致信FBI局长卡什·帕特尔，警告司法部将FBI反恐和反间谍人员从核心国家安全任务转调至大规模移民执法，危及美国安全。信中援引报道称，约1.3万名FBI探员中近四分之一、最大外勤办公室多达40%被分配至移民执法，导致涉及伊朗石油黑市、外国影响力行动等关键调查延迟或停止，中国、俄罗斯、伊朗方向的反间谍专家被调离。他要求FBI就资源转调范围、影响及补救措施作出详细答复。","summary_en":"On December 23, 2025, Congressman Raja Krishnamoorthi (D-IL) sent a letter to FBI Director Kash Patel warning that the DOJ diverted FBI counterterrorism and counterintelligence personnel from core national security missions to mass immigration enforcement, putting the U.S. at risk. Citing reporting, nearly a quarter of the FBI's roughly 13,000 agents and up to 40 percent in the largest field offices remain assigned to immigration duties, delaying or halting investigations including the Iranian oil black market and foreign influence operations, with China, Russia, and Iran specialists reassigned. He demanded detailed answers on the scope, impact, and remedies.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-18T15:40:23.592673+00:00","url":"http://krishnamoorthi.house.gov/media/press-releases/congressman-krishnamoorthi-sounds-alarm-over-doj-diverting-fbi","content":"Image\nHome\nMedia\nPress Releases\nCongressman Krishnamoorthi Sounds Alarm Over DOJ Diverting FBI Counterterrorism and Counterintelligence Resources to Mass Immigration RaidsDecember 23, 2025 Press ReleaseWASHINGTON — Congressman Raja Krishnamoorthi (D-IL) today sent a letter to FBI Director Kash Patel raising serious concerns that the Department of Justice has diverted FBI counterterrorism and counterintelligence personnel away from their core national security missions and reassigned them to support mass immigration enforcement operations, putting the United States at risk. In the letter, Congressman Krishnamoorthi warned that senior DOJ officials have redirected personnel and assets from the FBI’s core mission despite the Bureau’s own assessment that terrorists and nation-state adversaries pose the most immediate threats to the homeland:“Over the last year, senior officials have reassigned personnel and assets from the Federal Bureau of Investigation’s (FBI) core national security mission to immigration enforcement, leaving counterterrorism and counterintelligence work compromised and putting our national security at risk.”The letter cites reporting that early in 2025, DOJ leadership directed FBI Joint Terrorism Task Forces to assist with immigration initiatives, requiring agents responsible for terrorism investigations, espionage detection, and cyber threat monitoring to prioritize immigration enforcement over national security work:“Agents responsible for espionage detection cyber threat monitoring, and terrorism investigation, therefore, were required to prioritize immigration enforcement, giving less attention to crucial national security threats.”Despite a rise in alleged terrorist incidents across the United States, the letter notes that a significant share of the Bureau remains diverted:“Nearly a quarter of the FBI’s roughly 13,000 agents nationwide, and up to 40 percent in the largest field offices, remain assigned to immigration enforcement duties.”Congressman Krishnamoorthi further highlighted reporting that analysts tracking terrorist financing, money laundering, and the illicit trade in looted antiquities, as well as investigations into the Iranian oil black market used to finance terrorism, have been delayed by months:“Internal sources further indicate that these core national security investigations, including into the black market for Iranian oil sold to finance terrorism, have been delayed by months.”According to additional reporting cited in the letter, the diversion of counterterrorism and counterintelligence personnel has halted critical investigations:“The shift of resources from counterterrorism and counterintelligence teams, including many FBI personnel working years-long complex investigations involving classified techniques and sources, have caused several critical investigations to stop.”The letter also raises alarm that counterintelligence specialists with deep expertise on China, Russia, and Iran have been reassigned to immigration cases, limiting enforcement of the Foreign Agents Registration Act and allowing foreign intelligence operatives greater freedom to operate inside the United States:“These shifts have limited investigations into violations of the Foreign Agents Registration Act and have allowed foreign intelligence operatives greater room to maneuver within the United States.”Emphasizing the FBI’s statutory mandate, the letter warns:“Its counterintelligence and counterterrorism components exist to detect and disrupt the activities of hostile foreign actors, not to conduct civil immigration enforcement or unrelated administrative duties.”In light of these concerns, Congressman Krishnamoorthi asked the FBI to promptly provide detailed answers to the following questions:To what extent have FBI personnel assigned to counterintelligence, counterterrorism, or related national security missions been redirected to assist with immigration enforcement or other non–national security duties?How have these reassignments affected FBI’s ability to investigate and disrupt espionage, terrorism, cyber intrusions, and other national security threats?Have any ongoing national security or counterterrorism investigations—such as the probe into the Iranian oil black market or cases involving foreign influence operations—been delayed, suspended, or deprioritized because of these diversions?Were formal operational risk assessments or impact analyses conducted prior to redirecting these agents, and if so, what did they conclude?What steps, if any, has the Bureau taken to return these personnel to their original counterintelligence and counterterrorism assignments and to restore full operational readiness in these mission areas?What mechanisms or internal controls will be implemented to prevent future diversions of national security resources for purposes unrelated to the FBI’s statutory counterintelligence and counterterrorism missions?Congressman Krishnamoorthi's letter is available here.","content_cn":"图片\n首页\n媒体\n新闻稿\n国会议员克里希纳穆尔蒂就司法部将联邦调查局反恐和反间谍资源转用于大规模移民突袭发出警报\n2025年12月23日 新闻稿\n华盛顿——国会议员拉贾·克里希纳穆尔蒂（伊利诺伊州民主党人）今日致函联邦调查局局长卡什·帕特尔，提出严重关切：司法部已将联邦调查局的反恐和反间谍人员从核心国家安全使命中调离，重新分配以支持大规模移民执法行动，使美国面临风险。在信中，克里希纳穆尔蒂议员警告称，司法部高级官员已将人员和资产从联邦调查局的核心使命中转移，尽管该局自身评估认为恐怖分子和民族国家对手对美国本土构成最直接的威胁：\n“在过去一年中，高级官员已将人员和资产从联邦调查局（FBI）的核心国家安全使命中重新分配至移民执法，使反恐和反间谍工作受到损害，将我们的国家安全置于风险之中。”\n信中援引报道称，2025年初，司法部领导层指示联邦调查局联合反恐工作组协助移民行动，要求负责恐怖主义调查、间谍侦查和网络威胁监控的特工将移民执法置于国家安全工作之上：\n“因此，负责间谍侦查、网络威胁监控和恐怖主义调查的特工被要求优先处理移民执法，对关键国家安全威胁的关注因此减少。”\n信中指出，尽管全美涉嫌恐怖事件有所增加，该局仍有相当大比例的人员被调离：\n“联邦调查局全国约13,000名特工中，近四分之一，以及最大外地办事处中高达40%的人员，仍被分配执行移民执法任务。”\n克里希纳穆尔蒂议员还着重提到有报道称，追踪恐怖融资、洗钱和被掠夺文物非法交易的分析人员，以及对用于资助恐怖主义的伊朗石油黑市的调查，已被延误数月：\n“内部消息人士进一步指出，这些核心国家安全调查，包括对用于资助恐怖主义的伊朗石油黑市的调查，已被延误数月。”\n根据信中援引的更多报道，反恐和反间谍人员的调离已使关键调查陷入停滞：\n“从反恐和反间谍团队调走资源——其中包括许多联邦调查局人员正在进行的、涉及机密手段和线人的多年复杂调查——已导致多项关键调查停止。”\n信中还对以下情况发出警报：在中国、俄罗斯和伊朗问题上具有深厚专业知识的反间谍专家已被重新分配至移民案件，限制了《外国代理人登记法》的执法，使外国情报人员在美国境内获得更大的活动空间：\n“这些调动限制了对违反《外国代理人登记法》行为的调查，并使外国情报人员在美国境内获得更大的回旋余地。”\n信中强调联邦调查局的法定职责，警告称：\n“其反间谍和反恐部门的存在是为了侦查和瓦解敌对外国行为者的活动，而非执行民事移民执法或无关的行政职责。”\n鉴于这些关切，克里希纳穆尔蒂议员要求联邦调查局就以下问题迅速提供详细答复：\n被分配至反间谍、反恐或相关国家安全任务的联邦调查局人员，在多大程度上被重新调配以协助移民执法或其他非国家安全职责？\n这些重新分配如何影响了联邦调查局调查和瓦解间谍活动、恐怖主义、网络入侵及其他国家安全威胁的能力？\n是否有任何正在进行的国家安全或反恐调查——例如对伊朗石油黑市的调查或涉及外国影响力行动的案例——因这些调离而被延误、中止或降低优先级？\n在重新调配这些特工之前，是否进行了正式的行动风险评估或影响分析？如有，结论如何？\n该局采取了哪些措施（如有）使这些人员回归其原有的反间谍和反恐岗位，并恢复这些任务领域的全面行动准备状态？\n将实施哪些机制或内部控制，以防止未来将国家安全资源转用于与联邦调查局法定反间谍和反恐使命无关的目的？\n克里希纳穆尔蒂议员的信函可在此处获取。","publish_source":"krishnamoorthi.house.gov","publish_time":"2025-12-23T12:04:24-05:00"}},{"id":"news-2132","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"国会议员克里希纳穆尔蒂警告国土安全部“赏金猎人”计划定位和追踪移民","title_en":"Congressman Krishnamoorthi Warns Against DHS ‘Bounty Hunter’ Plan to Locate and Track Immigrants","summary_cn":"2025年11月10日，伊利诺伊州众议员、众议院监督与政府改革委员会资深成员拉贾·克里希纳穆尔蒂致信国土安全部长诺姆，对DHS可能雇佣私人承包商“为营利定位、监视和举报移民社区个人”的报道表示严重关切。他警告此举将政府最具强制性的权力外包给缺乏监督的私人行为者，形成按抓捕人数付费的“赏金猎人”模式，必然导致错误和歧视性执法，并援引伊利诺伊州一名美国公民因外貌被DHS拘留的案例。他要求DHS就法律授权、数据访问、监督机制等问题作出答复。","summary_en":"On November 10, 2025, Congressman Raja Krishnamoorthi (D-IL), a senior member of the House Oversight and Government Reform Committee, sent a letter to Homeland Security Secretary Noem expressing grave concern over reports that DHS may hire private contractors to locate, surveil, and report on immigrant community individuals for profit. He warned this outsources coercive government power to poorly overseen actors, creating a quota-based bounty hunter model certain to produce mistakes and discriminatory enforcement, citing an Illinois U.S. citizen detained by DHS over her appearance. He demanded answers on legal authority, data access, and oversight mechanisms.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-18T16:15:47.338980+00:00","url":"http://krishnamoorthi.house.gov/media/press-releases/congressman-krishnamoorthi-warns-against-dhs-bounty-hunter-plan-locate-and","content":"Image\nHome\nMedia\nPress Releases\nCongressman Krishnamoorthi Warns Against DHS ‘Bounty Hunter’ Plan to Locate and Track ImmigrantsNovember 10, 2025 Press ReleaseWASHINGTON – Today, Congressman Raja Krishnamoorthi (D-IL), a senior member of the House Committee on Oversight and Government Reform, sent a letter to Homeland Security (DHS) Secretary Kristi Noem expressing “grave concern” over reports that DHS may hire private contractors to “locate, surveil, and report on individuals within immigrant communities for profit.”In his letter, Congressman Krishnamoorthi warned that the proposal would “outsource one of the government’s most coercive powers to actors who operate with little oversight and limited public accountability.” He wrote that such an arrangement “risks creating an enforcement apparatus that functions beyond the reach of ordinary checks and balances.”Congressman Krishnamoorthi cautioned that “once the state begins contracting out its power to police, it invites the very abuses, secrecy, and corruption our founders sought to prevent.” He added, “When citizens can no longer discern who acts in the name of government, trust gives way to fear. A government that rules through confusion and coercion rather than law and consent erodes its own legitimacy and the freedoms it exists to protect.”The Congressman also outlined the dangers of performance-based enforcement contracts that would effectively establish a “bounty hunter” model: “When the government pays private contractors based on how many people they can find, detain, or deliver, it turns them into bounty hunters. In such a system built on quotas and cash rewards with minimal oversight, mistakes are not just possible—they are certain.”Congressman Krishnamoorthi cited recent incidents of discriminatory enforcement, including a case in Illinois where a U.S. citizen was detained by DHS officers who “refused to believe her U.S. passport was real—because her appearance did not fit their assumptions about what someone with her last name ought to look like.” He warned that allowing private individuals to perform similar functions “will inevitably chill civic participation and deepen fear among law-abiding residents who already feel watched and vulnerable.”Drawing historical parallels, Congressman Krishnamoorthi wrote that “when governments blur the line between official authority and private surveillance, societies inevitably pay a steep price in lost trust and personal freedom.” He added, “While today’s circumstances are different, any system that rewards private actors for reporting on one another risks repeating those same mistakes—undermining community cohesion, eroding the rule of law, and betraying American values.”Congressman Krishnamoorthi’s letter calls on DHS to answer key questions about the scope and legality of the proposed program, including:What statutory or regulatory authority allows DHS to delegate investigatory or surveillance functions to private contractors?What personal or location data would these contractors have access to?What oversight mechanisms and identification requirements would be in place to prevent harassment, trespass, or unlawful surveillance?Would contractors be authorized or incentivized to physically confront, detain, or pursue individuals?Why is DHS outsourcing address verification and document delivery rather than relying on trained federal agents?Congressman Krishnamoorthi concluded by emphasizing that “outsourcing immigration enforcement to profit-driven contractors undermines the very trust between government and the people it serves, and risks normalizing a system incompatible with American values and due process.”A copy of the letter is available here.","content_cn":"图片\n首页\n媒体\n新闻稿\n国会议员克里希纳穆尔蒂警告反对国土安全部“赏金猎人”式定位和追踪移民的计划\n2025年11月10日 新闻稿\n华盛顿——今天，众议院监督与政府改革委员会资深成员、伊利诺伊州民主党国会议员拉贾·克里希纳穆尔蒂致信国土安全部部长克里斯蒂·诺姆，对有关国土安全部可能雇用私人承包商“为牟利而定位、监视和举报移民社区中的个人”的报道表示“严重关切”。\n克里希纳穆尔蒂议员在信中警告说，该提案将“把政府最具强制性的权力之一外包给那些在极少监督和有限公共问责下运作的行为主体”。他写道，这样的安排“有可能制造出一个超出常规制衡机制约束范围的执法机器”。\n克里希纳穆尔蒂议员告诫说：“一旦国家开始将其警务权力外包，就会招致我们建国先贤力图防止的那些滥用、秘密和腐败。”他还说：“当公民再也无法分辨谁是以政府名义行事时，信任就会让位于恐惧。一个靠混乱和强制而非法律与同意来统治的政府，会侵蚀自身的合法性以及它本应保护的自由。”\n这位议员还概述了基于绩效的执法合同所带来的危险，这种合同实际上将建立一种“赏金猎人”模式：“当政府根据私人承包商能找到、拘留或移交多少人向他们付钱时，就把他们变成了赏金猎人。在这样一个建立在配额和现金奖励、监督又极少的基础上，错误不仅可能发生——而是必然发生。”\n克里希纳穆尔蒂议员援引了近期歧视性执法的事件，包括伊利诺伊州的一起案件，一名美国公民被国土安全部官员拘留，这些官员“拒绝相信她的美国护照是真的——因为她的外貌不符合他们对拥有她那个姓氏的人应该长什么样的假设”。他警告说，允许私人个人执行类似职能“将不可避免地抑制公民参与，并加深那些已经感到被监视和脆弱的守法居民中的恐惧”。\n克里希纳穆尔蒂议员援引历史进行类比，写道：“当政府模糊官方权力与私人监视之间的界限时，社会必然在失去信任和个人自由方面付出沉重代价。”他还说：“尽管今天的情况有所不同，但任何奖励私人行为者相互举报的制度都有可能重蹈覆辙——破坏社区凝聚力，侵蚀法治，背叛美国价值观。”\n克里希纳穆尔蒂议员的信呼吁国土安全部就该拟议项目的范围和合法性回答关键问题，包括：\n哪些法定或监管授权允许国土安全部将调查或监视职能委托给私人承包商？\n这些承包商将能访问哪些个人或位置数据？\n将设立哪些监督机制和身份识别要求，以防止骚扰、非法侵入或非法监视？\n承包商是否会被授权或被激励去与个人进行身体对抗、拘留或追捕？\n为什么国土安全部要将地址核实和文件送达外包，而不是依靠训练有素的联邦探员？\n克里希纳穆尔蒂议员最后强调，“将移民执法外包给以营利为驱动的承包商，会破坏政府与其所服务人民之间的信任，并有可能使一种与美国价值观和正当程序不相容的制度常态化。”\n该信副本可在此处查阅。","publish_source":"krishnamoorthi.house.gov","publish_time":"2025-11-10T17:45:20-05:00"}},{"id":"news-1736","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS (deep pilot)","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"国会议员克里希纳穆尔蒂、兰兹曼牵头要求国土安全部与联邦应急管理局终止对紧急食品和住所资金的非法冻结","title_en":"Congressmen Krishnamoorthi, Landsman Lead Lawmakers Demanding DHS, FEMA End Unlawful Freeze of Emergency Food and Shelter Funds","summary_cn":"国会议员克里希纳穆尔蒂与兰兹曼等46名议员致信美国国土安全部及联邦应急管理局，要求立即发放国会已拨付的紧急食品和住所计划资金。信中警告，约1.17亿美元资金自2025年1月起被冻结，尽管法院已下令释放，仍被扣留，导致地方政府和非营利组织无法为饥饿和无家可归家庭提供援助。议员要求两机构在2026年2月26日前就法律依据、合规措施及机构调整后的保障作出答复。","summary_en":"Congressmen Krishnamoorthi and Landsman, joined by 44 colleagues, sent a letter to the Department of Homeland Security and FEMA demanding the immediate release of already-appropriated Emergency Food and Shelter Program funds. The letter warns that nearly $117 million has been frozen since January 2025 and remains withheld despite a federal court order, depriving local governments and nonprofits of resources to assist families facing hunger and homelessness. The members request answers by February 26, 2026, on legal authority, compliance steps, and assurances amid FEMA restructuring.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-25T11:22:08.155073+00:00","url":"http://krishnamoorthi.house.gov/media/press-releases/congressmen-krishnamoorthi-landsman-lead-lawmakers-demanding-dhs-fema-end","content":"Image\nHome\nMedia\nPress Releases\nCongressmen Krishnamoorthi, Landsman Lead Lawmakers Demanding DHS, FEMA End Unlawful Freeze of Emergency Food and Shelter FundsJanuary 26, 2026 Press ReleaseWASHINGTON — Today, Congressman Raja Krishnamoorthi (D-IL), Congressman Greg Landsman (D-OH) and 44 of their colleagues sent a letter to the Department of Homeland Security (DHS) and the Federal Emergency Management Agency (FEMA) demanding the immediate release of Emergency Food and Shelter Program (EFSP) funds that Congress has already appropriated and directed to be disbursed. The new letter follows previous letters on the issues led by Congressman Krishnamoorthi in August and Congressman Landsman in April.In the letter, the Members warn that DHS and FEMA’s continued failure to release EFSP reimbursements is unlawful and is depriving local governments and nonprofit organizations of critical resources needed to keep families fed, housed, and alive. The Members note that nearly $117 million in EFSP funding was frozen in January 2025 and remains withheld a year later, despite a federal court order requiring the funds to be released.EFSP is a long-standing, life-saving program that enables local governments and nonprofit organizations to provide shelter, food, and emergency assistance to individuals and families experiencing hunger or homelessness. By continuing to withhold these funds, local governments and organizations cannot aid families in crisis.In the letter, Congressmen Krishnamoorthi and Landsman lay out the real-world consequences of these delays for communities nationwide, including in Illinois. In 2024, the EFSP provided over $5 million in funding to more than 70 counties. However, none of the promised funds have been disbursed, and organizations approved months ago are still waiting.The letter also raises concern that these delays are occurring amid broader uncertainty about the future of FEMA, heightening anxiety among service providers already waiting for overdue EFSP dollars. Given the seriousness of DHS and FEMA’s actions, the Members are requesting answers to the following questions no later than February 26, 2026:Under what statutory authority is FEMA withholding EFSP funds that Congress has already appropriated, obligated, and directed the agency to disburse? Please cite the exact legal provisions you believe permitted this continued delay.GAO has concluded that FEMA’s refusal to release EFSP grants is unlawful and constitutes a violation of the Impoundment Control Act. What specific actions are FEMA taking to come into immediate compliance with this finding, and on what date will all overdue EFSP funds be fully disbursed?If FEMA’s structure or responsibilities are modified, reduced, or dissolved, what binding assurances can you provide that EFSP recipients will receive timely notice and uninterrupted access to the federal support they have been promised? How will the Administration ensure continued assistance for individuals and families experiencing homelessness or food insecurity during any such transition?The full letter is available here.","content_cn":"图片\n首页\n媒体\n新闻稿\n国会议员Krishnamoorthi、Landsman带领立法者要求DHS、FEMA结束对紧急食品和住所资金的非法冻结\n2026年1月26日 新闻稿\n华盛顿——今天，国会议员Raja Krishnamoorthi（伊利诺伊州民主党籍）、国会议员Greg Landsman（俄亥俄州民主党籍）及其44名同事致函国土安全部（DHS）和联邦紧急事务管理局（FEMA），要求立即发放国会已经拨款并指示支付的紧急食品和住所计划（EFSP）资金。这封新信函是在此前分别由国会议员Krishnamoorthi于8月和国会议员Landsman于4月牵头就这些问题发出的信函之后发出的。\n在信中，议员们警告称，DHS和FEMA持续未能发放EFSP报销款项属违法行为，并使地方政府和非营利组织失去维持家庭获得食物、住所和生存所需的关键资源。议员们指出，近1.17亿美元的EFSP资金于2025年1月被冻结，一年后仍被扣留，尽管联邦法院已下令必须发放这些资金。\nEFSP是一项历史悠久、挽救生命的计划，使地方政府和非营利组织能够向遭受饥饿或无家可归困境的个人及家庭提供住所、食物和紧急援助。由于持续扣留这些资金，地方政府和组织无法帮助处于危机中的家庭。\n在信中，国会议员Krishnamoorthi和Landsman列举了这些延误给全国各地社区——包括伊利诺伊州——带来的现实后果。2024年，EFSP向70多个县提供了超过500万美元资金。然而，承诺的资金一分未发，数月前获批的组织仍在等待。\n信中还对以下情况表示担忧：这些延误正发生在有关FEMA未来的更广泛不确定性之中，加剧了已在等待逾期EFSP款项的服务提供者的焦虑。鉴于DHS和FEMA行动的严重性，议员们要求不晚于2026年2月26日回答以下问题：\nFEMA依据何种法定授权扣留国会已经拨款、承付并指示该机构发放的EFSP资金？请引用您认为允许持续延误的确切法律条款。\nGAO已认定，FEMA拒绝发放EFSP补助金属违法行为，并构成违反《扣留资金控制法》。FEMA正采取哪些具体行动以立即遵守这一认定，以及所有逾期EFSP资金将于何日全部发放？\n如果FEMA的组织结构或职责被修改、缩减或解散，您能提供哪些具有约束力的保证，以确保EFSP受助者及时得到通知，并能不间断地获得已承诺的联邦支持？政府将如何确保在任何此类过渡期间，持续援助遭受无家可归或食品不安全困境的个人和家庭？\n完整信函可在此处查阅。","publish_source":"krishnamoorthi.house.gov","publish_time":"2026-01-26T13:48:39-05:00"}},{"id":"news-1643","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS (deep pilot)","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"克里希纳穆尔蒂宣布《自由选举法案》，回应特朗普选举接管言论，强化现有宪法和法律保护","title_en":"Krishnamoorthi Announces Free Elections Act in Response to Trump’s Election Takeover Remarks to Reinforce Existing Constitutional and Legal Protections Legislation Reaffirms That DHS, ICE, and CBP Agents Cannot Be Deployed at Election Sites","summary_cn":"国会议员克里希纳穆尔蒂宣布将提出《自由选举法案》，回应特朗普呼吁共和党“接管”和“国有化”美国选举的言论。该法案重申并澄清现有宪法和法定保护，明确禁止利用联邦权力干预选举，强调国土安全部、移民和海关执法局及海关与边境保护局人员不得部署在投票站。克里希纳穆尔蒂指出，特朗普已滥用联邦执法机构作为政治武器，法案将消除任何模糊空间。","summary_en":"Congressman Krishnamoorthi announced he will introduce the Free Elections Act in response to President Trump's remarks calling for Republicans to 'take over' and 'nationalize' American elections. The legislation reaffirms and clarifies existing constitutional and statutory protections prohibiting federal interference in elections, making clear that DHS, ICE, and CBP agents cannot be deployed at election sites. Krishnamoorthi said Trump has already misused federal law enforcement agencies as political weapons, and the bill removes any ambiguity.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-25T11:16:21.554500+00:00","url":"http://krishnamoorthi.house.gov/media/press-releases/krishnamoorthi-announces-free-elections-act-response-trumps-election-takeover","content":"Image\nHome\nMedia\nPress Releases\nKrishnamoorthi Announces Free Elections Act in Response to Trump’s Election Takeover Remarks to Reinforce Existing Constitutional and Legal Protections Legislation Reaffirms That DHS, ICE, and CBP Agents Cannot Be Deployed at Election SitesFebruary 6, 2026 Press ReleaseLegislation Reaffirms That DHS, ICE, and CBP Agents Cannot Be Deployed at Election SitesWASHINGTON — Congressman Raja Krishnamoorthi today announced that he will soon be introducing the Free Elections Act in direct response to President Donald Trump’s recent comments calling for Republicans to “take over” and “nationalize” American elections. The legislation will reinforce and clarify longstanding constitutional and statutory protections that already prohibit the use of federal power to interfere with U.S. elections—making unmistakably clear that elections belong to the people, not to any political party or president.“President Trump’s call for Republicans to ‘take over’ and ‘nationalize’ our elections is already unconstitutional and illegal,” said Congressman Krishnamoorthi. “This is not a hypothetical threat. President Trump has already brutally misused federal law enforcement agencies like ICE and CBP as political weapons—inflicting real harm, destroying lives, and leaving Americans dead. As Congress negotiates DHS reforms and funding right now, the Free Elections Act removes any ambiguity and makes unmistakably clear that no president—Donald Trump or anyone else—can invoke emergency powers or deploy federal forces, including DHS, ICE, or CBP agents to interfere with elections or override the will of the voters.”The Free Elections Act will reaffirm and strengthen existing prohibitions against invoking emergency powers to interfere with elections, including through misuse of authorities under the Insurrection Act, the National Emergencies Act, and related federal statutes. It reinforces long-established bans on deploying federal forces or law enforcement, including DHS agents, at election sites and clarifies that emergency authorities may not be used to control, monitor, or influence the electoral process.","content_cn":"图片\n首页\n媒体\n新闻稿\nKrishnamoorthi针对特朗普关于接管选举的言论宣布《自由选举法》，以强化现有宪法和法律保护\n该法案重申国土安全部、移民及海关执法局和海关与边境保护局人员不得部署在选举地点\n2026年2月6日 新闻稿\n该法案重申国土安全部、移民及海关执法局和海关与边境保护局人员不得部署在选举地点\n华盛顿——国会议员Raja Krishnamoorthi今天宣布，他将很快提出《自由选举法》，直接回应总统Donald Trump近期呼吁共和党“接管”并“国家化”美国选举的言论。该法案将强化并澄清长期存在的宪法和成文法保护，这些保护已经禁止利用联邦权力干预美国选举——明确表明选举属于人民，而非任何政党或总统。\n“特朗普总统呼吁共和党‘接管’并‘国家化’我们的选举，这已经违宪且违法，”国会议员Krishnamoorthi说。“这不是假设性的威胁。特朗普总统已经残酷地滥用ICE和CBP等联邦执法机构，将其作为政治武器——造成实际伤害、摧毁生命，并导致美国人死亡。当前国会正在就DHS改革和拨款进行谈判之际，《自由选举法》消除任何歧义，并明确表明，无论是Donald Trump还是其他任何人担任总统，都不能援引紧急权力或部署包括DHS、ICE或CBP人员在内的联邦力量来干预选举或推翻选民意愿。”\n《自由选举法》将重申并加强现有的禁令，禁止援引紧急权力干预选举，包括滥用《叛乱法》《国家紧急状态法》及相关联邦法规授予的权力。该法案强化长期存在的禁令，禁止在选举地点部署联邦力量或执法人员，包括DHS人员，并澄清不得利用紧急权力控制、监控或影响选举进程。","publish_source":"krishnamoorthi.house.gov","publish_time":"2026-02-06T11:46:24-05:00"}},{"id":"news-130","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"克里希纳穆尔蒂谴责锡克教卡车司机遭刺伤事件，抨击特朗普政府国土安全部帖文","title_en":"Krishnamoorthi Condemns Brutal Stabbing of Sikh Truck Driver, Denounces Trump DHS Post Demonizing Sikh Driver Amid Rising Anti-Sikh and Anti-South Asian Hate","summary_cn":"美国众议员拉贾·克里希纳穆尔蒂发表声明，谴责一名锡克教卡车司机在怀俄明州休息站被刺17刀的事件。他将此与针对锡克教及南亚裔美国人仇恨上升相联系，并批评特朗普政府国土安全部此前发布针对锡克教卡车司机的种族主义漫画帖文。他呼吁停止散播仇恨、追究暴力责任，并称此前已联合多位议员要求总统就相关帖文采取行动。","summary_en":"U.S. Rep. Raja Krishnamoorthi issued a statement condemning the stabbing of a Sikh truck driver 17 times at a Wyoming rest stop. He linked the attack to rising hatred against Sikh and South Asian Americans and denounced a Trump Department of Homeland Security post featuring a racist caricature of a Sikh truck driver. He called for an end to hateful rhetoric and accountability for violence, noting he had earlier led lawmakers in demanding action from the President.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-18T13:23:54.982837+00:00","url":"http://krishnamoorthi.house.gov/media/press-releases/krishnamoorthi-condemns-brutal-stabbing-sikh-truck-driver-denounces-trump-dhs","content":"Image\nHome\nMedia\nPress Releases\nKrishnamoorthi Condemns Brutal Stabbing of Sikh Truck Driver, Denounces Trump DHS Post Demonizing Sikh Driver Amid Rising Anti-Sikh and Anti-South Asian HateSeptember 17, 2026 Press ReleaseSCHAUMBURG, IL — Congressman Raja Krishnamoorthi (D-IL) today issued the following statement after reports that a Sikh truck driver was stabbed 17 times at a Wyoming rest stop:“I’m horrified by the brutal attack on a Sikh truck driver who was stabbed 17 times at a Wyoming rest stop. This comes amid rising hatred targeting Sikh and South Asian Americans, with even the Trump Department of Homeland Security recently posting a racist caricature of a Sikh truck driver telling him to ‘get off our roads’ and ‘self-deport or find out.’“Those spreading this hate, including officials in our own federal government, need to stop. Those who turn it into violence must be held accountable. And all of us need to stand together against both. America must be better than this. I’m praying for Mr. Singh’s full recovery and grateful to the family whose quick action helped save his life.”Earlier this month, Krishnamoorthi condemned the Trump DHS post, warning that it fueled xenophobia against Sikh and South Asian Americans. He later led Representatives Shri Thanedar, Suhas Subramanyam, Pramila Jayapal, and Ami Bera in demanding action from President Trump over the post and the broader use of racial, ethnic, and religious stereotypes in federal communications.","content_cn":"图片\n首页\n媒体\n新闻稿\n克里希纳穆尔蒂谴责锡克教卡车司机遭残忍刺伤，抨击特朗普政府国土安全部发布妖魔化锡克教司机的帖子，此时反锡克教和反南亚裔仇恨正在上升\n2026年9月17日 新闻稿\n伊利诺伊州绍姆堡——在有报道称一名锡克教卡车司机在怀俄明州一处休息站被刺17刀后，国会议员拉贾·克里希纳穆尔蒂（伊利诺伊州民主党人）今天发表以下声明：\n“我对一名锡克教卡车司机在怀俄明州一处休息站被刺17刀的残忍袭击感到震惊。此事发生之际，针对锡克教和南亚裔美国人的仇恨正在上升，甚至特朗普政府的国土安全部最近还发布了一幅种族主义漫画，描绘一名锡克教卡车司机，并告诉他‘滚出我们的道路’以及‘自行遣返，否则后果自负’。\n“那些散布这种仇恨的人，包括我们自己联邦政府中的官员，必须停止。那些将其转化为暴力的人必须被追究责任。而我们所有人都必须团结起来反对这两者。美国必须比这更好。我为辛格先生的完全康复祈祷，并感谢那个迅速行动帮助挽救他生命的家庭。”\n本月早些时候，克里希纳穆尔蒂谴责了特朗普政府国土安全部的帖子，警告称该帖子助长了对锡克教和南亚裔美国人的仇外情绪。他随后与国会议员什里·塔内达尔、苏哈斯·苏布拉马尼亚姆、普拉米拉·贾亚帕尔和阿米·贝拉一道，要求特朗普总统就该帖子以及联邦通讯中更广泛使用种族、族裔和宗教刻板印象的问题采取行动。","publish_source":"krishnamoorthi.house.gov","publish_time":"2026-09-17T19:21:10-04:00"}},{"id":"news-1180","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"克里希纳穆尔蒂就国土安全部与联邦应急管理局“影子行动”及管理不当报道要求答复","title_en":"Krishnamoorthi Demands Answers on Reported Shadow Operations and Improper Management of DHS and FEMA","summary_cn":"美国众议员拉贾·克里希纳穆尔蒂致信国土安全部长马林，就有关特别政府雇员、承包商等非职业人员对国土安全部和联邦应急管理局核心职能施加不当影响的报道要求答复。信中援引报道称，前助理科里·莱万多夫斯基超越特别政府雇员法定权限，承包商卡拉·沃里斯对联邦应急管理局运作施加过度影响。他要求该部在4月29日前书面回应多项问题。","summary_en":"U.S. Rep. Raja Krishnamoorthi sent a letter to Homeland Security Secretary Markwayne Mullin demanding answers over reports that Special Government Employees, contractors and other non-career personnel improperly influenced core functions at DHS and FEMA. The letter cited reports that former aide Corey Lewandowski exceeded statutory limits as an SGE and that contractor Kara Voorhies wielded outsized influence over FEMA operations. He requested written responses by April 29, 2026.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-18T14:34:07.085636+00:00","url":"http://krishnamoorthi.house.gov/media/press-releases/krishnamoorthi-demands-answers-reported-shadow-operations-and-improper","content":"Image\nHome\nMedia\nPress Releases\nKrishnamoorthi Demands Answers on Reported Shadow Operations and Improper Management of DHS and FEMAApril 15, 2026 Press ReleaseWASHINGTON — Congressman Raja Krishnamoorthi today demanded answers in a letter to Department of Homeland Security Secretary Markwayne Mullin following deeply troubling reports that Special Government Employees, contractors, and other non-career personnel exercised improper influence over core agency functions at DHS and FEMA, raising serious concerns about shadow operations, ethics compliance, and a broader breakdown in oversight across the Department.In the letter, Krishnamoorthi warned that “what may have initially appeared to be isolated misconduct instead reflected a broader breakdown in internal controls, ethics compliance, and oversight across the Department,” and raised alarm that safeguards governing Special Government Employees and contractors “appear to have been systematically disregarded.”The letter cites public reporting that former aide and Special Government Employee Corey Lewandowski “exceeded the statutory limits of his role as a Special Government Employee” and “exercised influence far beyond what is legally permitted,” raising grave concerns about conflicts of interest and misuse of public office.Krishnamoorthi also pointed to reports that contractor Kara Voorhies exercised “outsized and deeply inappropriate influence” over FEMA operations and spending decisions, allegedly functioning as a “shadow administrator” whose awareness or approval was required for routine agency functions, including engagement with Congress, coordination with governors, and communication with the White House.“Taken together, these reports raise profound concerns about a systemic failure of oversight and accountability within DHS, in which a Special Government Employee operating beyond the lawful bounds of his authority appears to have enabled a contractor to exercise similarly improper influence over core governmental functions,” Krishnamoorthi wrote.Given the gravity of the allegations, Krishnamoorthi requested written responses to the following questions no later than April 29, 2026:What actions has DHS taken, or will it take, to ensure that Special Government Employees, contractors, and other non-career personnel do not exceed the lawful scope of their authority or perform inherently governmental functions?What steps is DHS taking to determine whether additional contractors, consultants, SGEs, or other non-career personnel were granted similar authority or influence over operational, budgetary, grantmaking, procurement, or personnel decisions across DHS and its component agencies, including FEMA?Has DHS initiated any internal review, ethics inquiry, or referral to the Office of Inspector General regarding the conduct described above? If so, what is the scope, status, and timeline of that review, and does DHS intend to make any findings public?What corrective actions has DHS implemented, or does it plan to implement, to restore proper oversight, chain-of-command integrity, accountability, and compliance within FEMA and across the Department?Krishnamoorthi concluded by warning that “these failures are not isolated incidents but instead reflect deeper and more systemic breakdowns in oversight, accountability, and internal controls within the Department,” and called on Secretary Mullin to “restore integrity and lawful governance to the Department.”The full letter is available here.","content_cn":"图片\n首页\n媒体\n新闻稿\n克里希纳穆尔蒂就所报道的影子行动及国土安全部和联邦应急管理局的不当管理要求作出答复\n2026年4月15日 新闻稿\n华盛顿——国会议员拉贾·克里希纳穆尔蒂今日致函国土安全部部长马克韦恩·穆林，要求其作出答复。此前有令人深感不安的报道称，特别政府雇员、承包商及其他非职业人员对国土安全部和联邦应急管理局的核心机构职能施加了不当影响，引发了对影子行动、道德合规以及该部门整体监督失灵的严重关切。\n克里希纳穆尔蒂在信中警告称，“最初看似孤立的不当行为，实际上反映了该部门内部管控、道德合规和监督的更大范围失灵”，并对规范特别政府雇员和承包商的保障措施“似乎遭到系统性无视”表示警觉。\n信中援引公开报道称，前助手、特别政府雇员科里·莱万多夫斯基“超越了他作为特别政府雇员的法定权限”，“施加了远超法律允许范围的影响”，引发了对利益冲突和滥用公职的严重关切。\n克里希纳穆尔蒂还指出，有报道称承包商卡拉·沃里斯对联邦应急管理局的运营和支出决策施加了“过度且极不适当的影响”，据称其充当“影子局长”，机构日常职能——包括与国会接触、与州长协调以及与白宫沟通——均需其知情或批准。\n克里希纳穆尔蒂写道：“综合来看，这些报道引发了人们对国土安全部内部监督和问责系统性失灵的深切担忧，其中一名超越其法定权限运作的特别政府雇员似乎使一名承包商得以对核心政府职能施加同样不当的影响。”\n鉴于指控的严重性，克里希纳穆尔蒂要求最迟于2026年4月29日前就以下问题作出书面答复：\n国土安全部已采取或将要采取哪些行动，以确保特别政府雇员、承包商及其他非职业人员不超越其法定权限范围，或不履行本应属于政府的职能？\n国土安全部正在采取哪些措施，以确定是否有其他承包商、顾问、特别政府雇员或其他非职业人员被授予了类似的权限或影响力，从而影响国土安全部及其下属机构（包括联邦应急管理局）在运营、预算、拨款、采购或人事方面的决策？\n国土安全部是否已就上述行为启动任何内部审查、道德调查或提交监察长办公室？如是，该审查的范围、状态和时间表如何，国土安全部是否打算公开任何调查结果？\n国土安全部已实施或计划实施哪些纠正措施，以恢复联邦应急管理局及整个部门适当的监督、指挥链完整性、问责和合规？\n克里希纳穆尔蒂最后警告称，“这些失误并非孤立事件，而是反映了该部门在监督、问责和内部管控方面更深层、更系统性的失灵”，并呼吁穆林部长“恢复该部门的诚信与合法治理”。\n完整信函可在此处查阅。","publish_source":"krishnamoorthi.house.gov","publish_time":"2026-04-15T13:56:04-04:00"}},{"id":"news-724","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"克里希纳穆尔蒂就国土安全部可能在投票站附近部署移民及海关执法局人员要求答复","title_en":"Krishnamoorthi Demands Answers on Reports DHS May Deploy ICE Near Polling Places","summary_cn":"美国众议员拉贾·克里希纳穆尔蒂致信国土安全部长马林，就有报道称该部可能在2026年中期选举期间在投票站内或附近部署移民及海关执法局或其他人员一事要求答复。他警告此类部署可能引发法律问题、恐吓选民并削弱选举公正信心，并要求该部在6月30日前就部署计划、法律依据、培训及与司法部协调等问题作出书面回应。","summary_en":"U.S. Rep. Raja Krishnamoorthi sent a letter to Homeland Security Secretary Markwayne Mullin demanding answers over reports that DHS may deploy ICE or other personnel in connection with the 2026 midterm elections, including at or near polling places. He warned such actions could raise legal concerns, intimidate voters and undermine confidence in elections, and requested written responses by June 30, 2026 on deployment plans, legal basis, training and DOJ coordination.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-18T14:16:06.680130+00:00","url":"http://krishnamoorthi.house.gov/media/press-releases/krishnamoorthi-demands-answers-reports-dhs-may-deploy-ice-near-polling-places","content":"Image\nHome\nMedia\nPress Releases\nKrishnamoorthi Demands Answers on Reports DHS May Deploy ICE Near Polling Places June 17, 2026 Press ReleaseWASHINGTON — Congressman Raja Krishnamoorthi (IL-08) demanded answers from Department of Homeland Security Secretary Markwayne Mullin regarding reports that DHS may consider deploying Immigration and Customs Enforcement (ICE) or other DHS personnel in connection with the 2026 midterm elections, including at or near polling places.In the letter, Krishnamoorthi warned:\"The deployment of ICE or other DHS personnel in or around polling locations could raise serious legal concerns, particularly if such actions deter lawful participation or create the perception of intimidation. Even the perceived presence of immigration enforcement personnel near polling places, especially in communities with large immigrant or mixed-status populations, could chill lawful voter participation and undermine confidence in the fair and impartial administration of elections.\"Krishnamoorthi's letter follows recent reports and conflicting public statements from DHS officials regarding whether ICE personnel could be deployed near polling places during the upcoming midterm elections.\"These reports raise serious concerns about potential voter intimidation, federal interference in election administration, and the chilling effect such actions could have on lawful participation in our democracy.\"Krishnamoorthi requested that DHS provide responses no later than June 30, 2026. In the letter, he requested answers to the following questions:Confirm whether DHS intends to station ICE agents or other DHS law-enforcement personnel inside polling places, within statutorily defined buffer zones around polling locations, or at ballot drop boxes during the 2026 midterm elections. If not, confirm that DHS will not do so. If so, explain the circumstances under which such deployments would occur and the legal basis for them.Identify any plans, contingencies, operational guidance, or concepts of operations developed since January 20, 2025, concerning the deployment of ICE or other DHS personnel during the 2026 midterm elections, including any circumstances under which such personnel could be deployed to polling places or surrounding areas. Also identify any such deployments since January 20, 2025, and provide the date, location, component involved, number of personnel, purpose, and any after-action reports.Produce all communications between DHS, including ICE, and state, local, tribal, or territorial election officials concerning the potential presence of DHS personnel at or near polling places during the 2026 election cycle, including emails, memoranda, and meeting notes. Also produce any internal guidance, directives, or memoranda related to DHS or ICE involvement in election-related matters since January 20, 2025.Explain what training, if any, DHS and ICE personnel have received regarding voting rights protections, voter intimidation laws, and limits on the presence of federal officers at polling locations. Identify the oversight and compliance measures DHS has established to ensure adherence to these requirements.Explain any coordination between DHS and the Department of Justice, including the Civil Rights Division and Criminal Division, concerning the possible deployment of DHS or ICE personnel during elections, including any role DHS has been asked to play in “election integrity” efforts.Explain how DHS will ensure that any election-related security activities it undertakes, such as cyber support or threat monitoring, remain nonpartisan, respect state and local control of elections, and avoid actions that could reasonably be perceived as voter intimidation or partisan interference.Read the full letter here.","content_cn":"图片\n首页\n媒体\n新闻稿\n克里希纳穆尔蒂就国土安全部可能在投票站附近部署移民及海关执法局的报道要求作出答复\n2026年6月17日 新闻稿\n华盛顿——国会议员拉贾·克里希纳穆尔蒂（伊利诺伊州第八选区）就有关国土安全部可能考虑在2026年中期选举期间部署移民及海关执法局（ICE）或其他国土安全部人员（包括在投票站内或附近）的报道，要求国土安全部部长马克韦恩·穆林作出答复。\n克里希纳穆尔蒂在信中警告称：\n“在投票站内或周围部署移民及海关执法局或其他国土安全部人员可能引发严重的法律关切，尤其是如果此类行动阻碍合法参与或造成恐吓印象。即便只是移民执法人员在投票站附近的存在感，尤其是在移民人口或混合身份人口众多的社区，也可能抑制合法的选民参与，并削弱对选举公平公正进行的信心。”\n克里希纳穆尔蒂致函之前，近期有报道以及国土安全部官员就移民及海关执法局人员是否可能在即将到来的中期选举期间部署到投票站附近发表了相互矛盾的公开声明。\n“这些报道引发了严重关切，涉及潜在的选民恐吓、联邦对选举管理的干预，以及此类行动可能对我国民主合法参与产生的寒蝉效应。”\n克里希纳穆尔蒂要求国土安全部最迟于2026年6月30日前作出答复。他在信中要求回答以下问题：\n确认国土安全部是否打算在2026年中期选举期间，在投票站内、投票站周围法定缓冲区内或选票投递箱处派驻移民及海关执法局特工或其他国土安全部执法人员。如果不打算，请确认国土安全部不会这样做。如果打算，请解释此类部署将在何种情况下发生及其法律依据。\n说明自2025年1月20日以来制定的任何有关在2026年中期选举期间部署移民及海关执法局或其他国土安全部人员的计划、应急方案、行动指南或行动构想，包括此类人员可能被部署到投票站或周边地区的任何情形。同时说明自2025年1月20日以来的任何此类部署，并提供日期、地点、所涉部门、人员数量、目的及任何事后报告。\n提供国土安全部（包括移民及海关执法局）与州、地方、部落或领地选举官员之间就2026年选举周期内国土安全部人员可能在投票站内或附近出现一事的所有通信，包括电子邮件、备忘录和会议记录。同时提供自2025年1月20日以来与国土安全部或移民及海关执法局参与选举相关事务有关的任何内部指南、指令或备忘录。\n解释国土安全部和移民及海关执法局人员就投票权保护、选民恐吓法以及联邦官员在投票站存在的限制接受了哪些培训（如有）。说明国土安全部为确保遵守这些要求而建立的监督和合规措施。\n解释国土安全部与司法部（包括民权司和刑事司）之间就选举期间可能部署国土安全部或移民及海关执法局人员进行的任何协调，包括国土安全部被要求在“选举诚信”工作中发挥的任何作用。\n解释国土安全部将如何确保其开展的任何与选举相关的安全活动（如网络支持或威胁监测）保持无党派性，尊重州和地方对选举的控制，并避免采取任何可能被合理视为选民恐吓或党派干预的行动。\n在此处阅读完整信函。","publish_source":"krishnamoorthi.house.gov","publish_time":"2026-06-17T12:57:17-04:00"}},{"id":"news-1649","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"克里希纳穆尔蒂要求国土安全部解释ICE审查失败、极端主义招募信号及在反犹担忧中提拔格雷格·博维诺","title_en":"Krishnamoorthi Demands DHS Explain ICE Vetting Failures, Extremist Recruitment Signals, and Promotion of Greg Bovino Amid Antisemitism Concerns","summary_cn":"2026年2月5日，众议员拉贾·克里希纳穆尔蒂致函国土安全部长克里斯蒂·诺姆，再次对ICE招聘、审查与监督流程的系统性失败表达严重关切，包括提拔格雷格·博维诺的决定。他批评DHS在明尼阿波利斯枪击案后发布的招募内容使用与白人至上主义及极端运动相关的措辞，并指出博维诺曾有反犹言论。他要求DHS在2月20日前就审查流程、是否筛查1月6日国会骚乱参与者等问题作出答复。","summary_en":"On February 5, 2026, Congressman Raja Krishnamoorthi sent a follow-up letter to DHS Secretary Kristi Noem raising serious concerns about systemic failures in ICE's hiring, vetting and oversight, including the elevation of Greg Bovino. He criticized DHS recruitment content posted after the Minneapolis shooting for using language associated with white nationalist and extremist movements, and noted Bovino's prior antisemitic remarks. He requested answers by February 20 on vetting processes and whether DHS screens for January 6 participants.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-18T15:33:56.355394+00:00","url":"http://krishnamoorthi.house.gov/media/press-releases/krishnamoorthi-demands-dhs-explain-ice-vetting-failures-extremist-recruitment","content":"Image\nHome\nMedia\nPress Releases\nKrishnamoorthi Demands DHS Explain ICE Vetting Failures, Extremist Recruitment Signals, and Promotion of Greg Bovino Amid Antisemitism ConcernsFebruary 5, 2026 Press ReleaseSCHAUMBURG, IL — Congressman Raja Krishnamoorthi (IL-08) sent a follow-up letter to Department of Homeland Security Secretary Kristi Noem today raising serious concerns about systemic failures in U.S. Immigration and Customs Enforcement’s hiring, vetting, and oversight processes, as well as troubling DHS recruitment messaging and leadership decisions. In the letter, Krishnamoorthi wrote that he is “once again raising serious concerns regarding the lapses in U.S. Immigration and Customs Enforcement’s (ICE) hiring and vetting processes,” including the decision to elevate officers such as Greg Bovino. He noted that DHS has failed to respond to his November 24, 2025 request for documentation regarding ICE’s vetting practices, including whether recruits are permitted to begin training before completing background checks and how ICE verifies applicant information and detects undisclosed misconduct.Krishnamoorthi also raised alarm about DHS recruitment content posted shortly after the fatal shooting of Renée Good in Minneapolis. He wrote that the decision to use language closely associated with white nationalist and extremist movements “raises serious questions about whether your department is tolerating, or even courting, the attention of individuals and movements rooted in extremist ideology,” adding that “in the context of official recruitment communications, the use of language so closely associated with these movements cannot reasonably be dismissed as accidental.”Addressing reporting that Greg Bovino had made antisemitic remarks prior to his elevation into a DHS leadership role, Krishnamoorthi wrote that “the decision to promote an individual associated with antisemitic rhetoric reflects a serious failure of judgment” and that, at a moment when antisemitism is surging nationwide, “this episode undermines DHS’s credibility as an institution entrusted with protecting all communities.”The letter further cites recent reporting describing how individuals can move through ICE’s recruitment process with minimal scrutiny, warning that these accounts, when viewed alongside DHS messaging choices and prior personnel decisions, “point to systemic vetting and oversight failures, not isolated lapses.” Krishnamoorthi emphasized that, as Secretary, Noem is responsible for ensuring DHS leadership reflects “the values of professionalism, integrity, and respect for the rule of law.”Krishnamoorthi requested that DHS provide responses no later than February 20, 2026, to the following questions:What vetting, review, and approval processes were used in the decision to elevate Greg Bovino, and when did DHS leadership become aware of his antisemitic statements?Has DHS conducted, or does it intend to conduct, a review of Mr. Bovino’s record in light of this reporting?What steps is DHS taking to ensure that individuals with histories of misconduct, credibility issues, or extremist rhetoric are not promoted into positions of authority?Is DHS screening to make sure that it is not hiring agents who participated in the storming of the U.S. Capitol on January 6, 2021?When will DHS provide a response to the outstanding questions raised in my November 24, 2025 letter regarding ICE’s hiring, vetting, and oversight procedures?Congressman Krishnamoorthi’s letter is available here.","content_cn":"图片\n首页\n媒体\n新闻稿\n克里希纳穆尔蒂要求国土安全部解释ICE审查失职、极端主义招募信号以及在反犹主义担忧下提拔格雷格·博维诺一事\n2026年2月5日 新闻稿\n伊利诺伊州绍姆堡——国会议员拉贾·克里希纳穆尔蒂（伊利诺伊州第八选区）今日致函国土安全部部长克里斯蒂·诺姆，就美国移民和海关执法局（ICE）在招聘、审查和监督程序中存在的系统性失职，以及国土安全部令人不安的招募信息和领导层决定，再次提出严重关切。\n在信中，克里希纳穆尔蒂写道，他“再次就美国移民和海关执法局（ICE）招聘和审查程序中的疏漏提出严重关切”，包括提拔格雷格·博维诺等官员的决定。他指出，国土安全部尚未回应他2025年11月24日提出的关于ICE审查做法的文件请求，包括是否允许新员工在完成背景调查前就开始培训，以及ICE如何核实申请人信息并发现未披露的不当行为。\n克里希纳穆尔蒂还对明尼阿波利斯蕾妮·古德遭致命枪击后不久国土安全部发布的招募内容表示警惕。他写道，使用与白人民族主义和极端主义运动密切相关的措辞，“令人严重质疑贵部门是否在容忍、甚至招揽根植于极端主义意识形态的个人和运动的关注”，并补充说，“在官方招募通讯的语境下，使用与这些运动如此密切相关的措辞，不能合理地被视为偶然。”\n针对有关格雷格·博维诺在被提拔进入国土安全部领导层之前曾发表反犹言论的报道，克里希纳穆尔蒂写道，“提拔一个与反犹言论有关联的人，反映出严重的判断失误”，而在全美反犹主义急剧上升之际，“这一事件损害了国土安全部作为一个受命保护所有社区的机构所应有的公信力。”\n信中进一步援引近期报道，描述个人如何能以极少的审查通过ICE的招聘程序，并警告说，这些报道与国土安全部的信息选择及此前的人事决定放在一起看，“指向的是系统性的审查和监督失职，而非孤立的疏漏。”克里希纳穆尔蒂强调，作为部长，诺姆有责任确保国土安全部领导层体现“专业精神、正直和对法治的尊重等价值观”。\n克里希纳穆尔蒂要求国土安全部不迟于2026年2月20日就以下问题作出答复：\n在决定提拔格雷格·博维诺时使用了哪些审查、复核和批准程序，国土安全部领导层是何时得知其反犹言论的？\n国土安全部是否已根据这些报道对博维诺先生的记录进行审查，或打算进行审查？\n国土安全部正在采取哪些措施，确保有不当行为记录、信誉问题或极端主义言论的人不会被提拔到权威职位？\n国土安全部是否在进行筛查，以确保不雇用参与2021年1月6日冲击美国国会大厦的人员？\n国土安全部何时将就我2025年11月24日信中提出的关于ICE招聘、审查和监督程序的未决问题作出答复？\n克里希纳穆尔蒂议员的信函可在此处查阅。","publish_source":"krishnamoorthi.house.gov","publish_time":"2026-02-05T12:30:29-05:00"}},{"id":"news-1660","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"克里希纳穆尔蒂揭露特朗普时期国土安全部的系统性暴力与谎言，要求解职并追责","title_en":"Krishnamoorthi Exposes Trump DHS' Systemic Violence and Lying, Demands Firings and Accountability","summary_cn":"2026年2月3日，众议员拉贾·克里希纳穆尔蒂在两院影子听证会上揭露特朗普政府时期国土安全部在移民执法中的系统性暴力，包括对一岁儿童喷胡椒喷雾、电击美国公民、在居民区使用催泪瓦斯，以及芝加哥父亲西尔维里奥·维列加斯-冈萨雷斯被枪杀等事件。他指出官方常以虚假叙述为暴力辩护，并呼吁解职部长诺姆和格雷格·博维诺，追究授权、执行和掩盖滥权者的责任。","summary_en":"On February 3, 2026, Congressman Raja Krishnamoorthi exposed systemic violence by Trump-era DHS in immigration enforcement at a bicameral shadow hearing, citing pepper-spraying a one-year-old, tasing a U.S. citizen, tear gas in residential areas, and the killing of Chicago father Silverio Villegas-González. He said officials routinely justified violence with false narratives, and called for firing Secretary Noem and Greg Bovino and holding accountable those who authorized, carried out and covered up abuses.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-18T15:35:18.091856+00:00","url":"http://krishnamoorthi.house.gov/media/press-releases/krishnamoorthi-exposes-trump-dhs-systemic-violence-and-lying-demands-firings","content":"Image\nHome\nMedia\nPress Releases\nKrishnamoorthi Exposes Trump DHS' Systemic Violence and Lying, Demands Firings and AccountabilityFebruary 3, 2026 Press ReleaseWASHINGTON — Congressman Raja Krishnamoorthi (D-IL) today exposed a pattern of systemic violence by Trump DHS at a bicameral shadow hearing titled “Our Values at Stake: Examining DHS’ Use of Violence in Immigration Enforcement,” detailing repeated uses of excessive force, false official narratives, and entrenched impunity under President Trump.During the hearing, Krishnamoorthi laid out how DHS and ICE operations carried out under President Trump — including Operation Midway Blitz — inflicted serious, systemic harm on Chicago-area communities. Incidents examined included the pepper-spraying of a one-year-old child, the tasing of a U.S. citizen who refused to allow agents into his vehicle, the deployment of tear gas and smoke bombs in residential neighborhoods, and multiple shootings — including the killing of Silverio Villegas-González, a Chicago father of two who was shot after dropping his children off at school.Krishnamoorthi underscored that Trump DHS repeatedly justified these actions by claiming they made communities safer — claims that collapsed under scrutiny. Pointing to body-camera footage, eyewitness testimony, and court findings, he emphasized that violent encounters were routinely followed by misleading or false official accounts from Trump administration officials.Despite Trump's DHS claiming Mr. Villegas-González had attacked federal agents, \"there was no evidence,” Krishnamoorthi said. “This is part of a pattern.”He also warned against allowing the human cost of DHS violence to fade from public memory. “The nation knows the names Renée Good and Alex Pretti — but let us not forget Mr. Silverio Villegas-González, a Chicagoan and a father of two,” Krishnamoorthi said.Krishnamoorthi further highlighted testimony showing how DHS officials under President Trump advanced false narratives after violent encounters, only for those stories to unravel when video evidence and independent investigations emerged. Citing a federal court ruling in which a judge accused a senior Customs and Border Protection commander of “outright lying” about the use of force against peaceful protesters in the Chicago area, Krishnamoorthi stated bluntly: “He lied. He lied again.”The Congressman reiterated his call for accountability at the highest levels of the department. “I have already called for Secretary Noem to be fired or impeached,” Krishnamoorthi said. “Today, I am calling for Greg Bovino to be fired.” He emphasized that officials who authorize, carry out, and attempt to cover up abuses of power must be investigated and held accountable.Krishnamoorthi closed by warning that Trump DHS actions have placed lives at risk, eroded public trust, and undermined the rule of law — and that restoring accountability is essential to ensuring federal power is never again wielded with such impunity.Footage of Congressman Krishnamoorthi’s question line is available here.","content_cn":"图片\n首页\n媒体\n新闻稿\n克里希纳穆尔蒂揭露特朗普国土安全部的系统性暴力和谎言，要求解雇相关人员并追究责任\n2026年2月3日 新闻稿\n华盛顿——国会议员拉贾·克里希纳穆尔蒂（伊利诺伊州民主党人）今日在两院影子听证会“我们的价值观岌岌可危：审视国土安全部在移民执法中使用暴力的问题”上，揭露了特朗普国土安全部系统性暴力的模式，详细列举了在特朗普总统任内一再使用过度武力、发布虚假官方说法以及根深蒂固的有罪不罚现象。\n在听证会上，克里希纳穆尔蒂阐述了在特朗普总统任内开展的国土安全部和ICE行动——包括“中途闪电战”行动——如何对芝加哥地区社区造成严重、系统性的伤害。所审视的事件包括：对一名一岁儿童喷射胡椒喷雾、对一名拒绝让探员进入其车辆的美国公民使用电击枪、在居民区部署催泪瓦斯和烟雾弹，以及多起枪击事件——包括西尔韦里奥·比列加斯-冈萨雷斯被杀案，这位芝加哥两个孩子的父亲在送孩子上学后遭枪击身亡。\n克里希纳穆尔蒂强调，特朗普国土安全部一再声称这些行动让社区更安全，以此为其辩护——而这些说法在审视之下不攻自破。他援引随身摄像头录像、目击者证词和法院裁决，强调暴力冲突发生后，特朗普政府官员往往随之发布误导性或虚假的官方说法。\n尽管特朗普的国土安全部声称比列加斯-冈萨雷斯先生袭击了联邦探员，克里希纳穆尔蒂说：“没有任何证据。这是一贯模式的一部分。”\n他还警告不要让国土安全部暴力造成的人员代价从公众记忆中淡去。“全国都知道蕾妮·古德和亚历克斯·普雷蒂的名字——但让我们不要忘记西尔韦里奥·比列加斯-冈萨雷斯先生，一位芝加哥人，两个孩子的父亲，”克里希纳穆尔蒂说。\n克里希纳穆尔蒂进一步强调，证词显示特朗普总统任内的国土安全部官员在暴力冲突后散布虚假说法，而这些说法在视频证据和独立调查出现后便不攻自破。他援引一项联邦法院裁决，其中一名法官指责一名海关和边境保护局高级指挥官就芝加哥地区对和平抗议者使用武力一事“公然撒谎”，克里希纳穆尔蒂直言：“他撒了谎。他又撒了谎。”\n这位国会议员重申了他要求该部门最高层追究责任的呼吁。“我已经呼吁解雇或弹劾诺姆部长，”克里希纳穆尔蒂说。“今天，我呼吁解雇格雷格·博维诺。”他强调，授权、实施并试图掩盖滥用权力的官员必须受到调查并被追究责任。\n克里希纳穆尔蒂最后警告说，特朗普国土安全部的行动已将生命置于危险之中，侵蚀了公众信任，破坏了法治——而恢复问责制对于确保联邦权力永远不会再如此不受惩罚地行使至关重要。\n克里希纳穆尔蒂议员提问环节的视频可在此处查阅。","publish_source":"krishnamoorthi.house.gov","publish_time":"2026-02-03T20:12:14-05:00"}},{"id":"news-1073","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"克里希纳穆尔蒂就特朗普政府扩大索取敏感选民数据报道要求国土安全部作出答复","title_en":"Krishnamoorthi Presses DHS for Answers After New Reports of Trump Administration Expanding Demands for Sensitive Voter Data","summary_cn":"2026年4月29日，众议院监督委员会资深成员拉贾·克里希纳穆尔蒂致信美国国土安全部部长马克韦恩·马林，要求就特朗普政府扩大获取敏感选民信息并与州和地方选举官员直接接触的新报道作出答复。信中援引调查称，国土安全部人员在至少八个州索取选民登记记录、投票历史等选举数据，部分材料未脱敏，含签名和部分社会安全号码。他要求国土安全部在5月8日前提供法律授权、请求清单、事实依据、数据保护政策等多项信息。","summary_en":"On April 29, 2026, Congressman Raja Krishnamoorthi, a senior member of the House Oversight Committee, sent a letter to DHS Secretary Markwayne Mullin demanding answers after reports that the Trump administration expanded efforts to obtain sensitive voter information and engage state and local election officials. The letter cites an investigation finding DHS personnel requested voter registration records, voting histories, and other election data in at least eight states, sometimes including unredacted materials with signatures and partial Social Security numbers. Krishnamoorthi requested detailed information by May 8, 2026.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-24T20:23:14.338311+00:00","url":"http://krishnamoorthi.house.gov/media/press-releases/krishnamoorthi-presses-dhs-answers-after-new-reports-trump-administration","content":"Image\nHome\nMedia\nPress Releases\nKrishnamoorthi Presses DHS for Answers After New Reports of Trump Administration Expanding Demands for Sensitive Voter DataApril 29, 2026 Press ReleaseWASHINGTON — Congressman Raja Krishnamoorthi, a senior member of the House Oversight Committee, sent a letter to Department of Homeland Security Secretary Markwayne Mullin demanding answers following new reports that the Trump Administration has expanded efforts to obtain sensitive voter information and engage directly with state and local election officials. The letter cites new reports indicating that DHS personnel requested voter registration records, voting histories, and other election-related data in multiple states, in some cases including unredacted materials containing signatures and partial Social Security numbers.In the letter, Krishnamoorthi wrote:“A recent investigation found that DHS personnel requested voter registration records, voting histories, and other election-related data in at least eight states, including, in some cases, unredacted materials containing signatures and partial Social Security numbers. The reporting indicates that these requests were made without a clearly articulated investigative basis and in areas that do not traditionally fall within DHS’s core mission.” He continued:“These reported actions raise serious legal and constitutional concerns. Election administration is primarily the responsibility of state and local governments, and any federal involvement, particularly where it touches sensitive voter data, must be clearly authorized, narrowly scoped, and handled with care. They also risk eroding public confidence in the integrity and impartial administration of our elections.” Krishnamoorthi emphasized that these developments come amid broader efforts to expand federal involvement in election administration and growing concern among election officials about political pressure ahead of the 2026 election cycle.Krishnamoorthi requested that DHS provide the following information no later than May 8, 2026:Identify all statutory, regulatory, or other legal authorities DHS relies upon to request or obtain voter registration records, voting histories, or other election-related data from state or local officials. Provide a list of all jurisdictions in which DHS personnel have requested or obtained election-related records since January 20, 2025, including the type of information requested and whether such requests were fulfilled. For each request, describe the factual basis or predicate for the inquiry, including whether the request was tied to a specific allegation, referral, or ongoing investigation. Describe any coordination with the U.S. Department of Justice or other federal entities regarding election-related investigations, including whether such entities reviewed, approved, or directed any such requests. Detail the policies and procedures governing the handling, storage, retention, and protection of sensitive voter information obtained by DHS, including any limitations on dissemination, third-party access, breach notification protocols, and timelines for deletion or destruction of such data. Provide all internal guidance, memoranda, or directives governing DHS involvement in election-related matters, including any changes to DHS’s role in election security, investigations, or data collection since January 20, 2025. Explain how any voter data obtained by DHS has been used, including whether it has been shared with other federal agencies, used to initiate enforcement actions, or incorporated into broader federal databases. Describe the training provided to DHS personnel engaging with election officials and the oversight mechanisms in place to ensure compliance with applicable laws, privacy protections, and constitutional limits.The letter is available here.","content_cn":"图片\n主页\n媒体\n新闻稿\n新报告显示特朗普政府扩大获取敏感选民数据的要求后，克里希那莫提要求国土安全部作出答复\n2026年4月29日 新闻稿\n华盛顿——众议院监督委员会高级成员拉贾·克里希那莫提议员致信国土安全部长马克韦恩·穆林，要求其作出答复。此前有新报告称，特朗普政府扩大了获取敏感选民信息并直接与州和地方选举官员接触的努力。信中援引的新报告显示，国土安全部人员在多个州要求提供选民登记记录、投票历史及其他选举相关数据；在某些情况下，还包括含有签名和部分社会安全号码的未删节材料。\n克里希那莫提在信中写道：\n“最近的一项调查发现，国土安全部人员在至少八个州要求提供选民登记记录、投票历史和其他选举相关数据；在某些情况下，还要求提供含有签名和部分社会安全号码的未删节材料。报道显示，这些要求并没有明确说明调查依据，而且涉及的领域通常不属于国土安全部的核心使命。”\n他继续写道：\n“这些被报道的行动引发了严重的法律和宪法问题。选举管理主要由州和地方政府负责，任何联邦介入，尤其是涉及敏感选民数据时，都必须有明确授权、严格限定范围并谨慎处理。这些行动还可能削弱公众对选举完整性以及选举得到公正管理的信心。”\n克里希那莫提强调，这些事态发展发生之际，联邦政府正开展扩大其在选举管理中介入程度的更广泛努力，而选举官员也越来越担心2026年选举周期前的政治压力。\n克里希那莫提要求国土安全部不迟于2026年5月8日提供以下信息：\n说明国土安全部依据哪些成文法、法规或其他法律授权，向州或地方官员要求或获取选民登记记录、投票历史或其他选举相关数据。\n列出自2025年1月20日以来国土安全部人员要求或获取选举相关记录的所有辖区，包括所要求的信息类型以及这些要求是否得到满足。\n针对每项要求，说明调查的事实依据或启动条件，包括该要求是否与具体指控、转交事项或正在进行的调查有关。\n说明与美国司法部或其他联邦实体就选举相关调查进行的任何协调，包括这些实体是否审查、批准或指示了任何此类要求。\n详细说明国土安全部处理、存储、保留和保护所获取敏感选民信息的政策和程序，包括对传播、第三方访问、数据泄露通知规程以及删除或销毁此类数据时间表的任何限制。\n提供所有关于国土安全部参与选举相关事务的内部指导、备忘录或指令，包括自2025年1月20日以来国土安全部在选举安全、调查或数据收集方面职责的任何变化。\n解释国土安全部获取的任何选民数据如何被使用，包括是否与其他联邦机构共享、是否用于启动执法行动，或是否纳入更广泛的联邦数据库。\n说明向参与与选举官员接触的国土安全部人员提供了哪些培训，以及为确保遵守适用法律、隐私保护和宪法限制而设立的监督机制。\n信件全文可在此处查看。","publish_source":"krishnamoorthi.house.gov","publish_time":"2026-04-29T17:37:59-04:00"}},{"id":"news-2249","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"克里希纳穆尔蒂就暂停拘留监督及伊利诺伊ICE设施记者遭不当对待向国土安全部长诺姆施压","title_en":"Krishnamoorthi Presses DHS Secretary Noem Over Suspension of Detention Oversight and Reports of Mistreatment of Journalists at Illinois ICE Facility","summary_cn":"2025年10月17日，众议员拉贾·克里希纳穆尔蒂致函国土安全部长克里斯蒂·诺姆，要求为政府停摆期间DHS的行为负责，包括让拘留监督办公室全员休假，使逾6万名被拘留者失去独立检查。另一封信关注芝加哥地区及布罗德维尤ICE处理中心记者遭胡椒弹射击、催泪瓦斯及逮捕等事件，要求DHS提供与记者互动的政策、行动指令及涉记者武力使用数据，并敦促采取避免逮捕记者的政策。","summary_en":"On October 17, 2025, Congressman Raja Krishnamoorthi sent letters to DHS Secretary Kristi Noem demanding accountability for DHS actions during the government shutdown, including furloughing the entire Office of Detention Oversight, leaving over 60,000 detainees without independent inspection. A second letter addressed mistreatment of journalists in Chicago and at the Broadview ICE facility, including pepper balls, tear gas and arrests, and requested policies, operational directives and use-of-force data involving journalists.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-18T16:17:43.866667+00:00","url":"http://krishnamoorthi.house.gov/media/press-releases/krishnamoorthi-presses-dhs-secretary-noem-over-suspension-detention-oversight","content":"Image\nHome\nMedia\nPress Releases\nKrishnamoorthi Presses DHS Secretary Noem Over Suspension of Detention Oversight and Reports of Mistreatment of Journalists at Illinois ICE FacilityOctober 17, 2025 Press ReleaseSCHAUMBURG, IL – Congressman Raja Krishnamoorthi sent two letters to Homeland Security Secretary Kristi Noem last night demanding accountability for the Department of Homeland Security’s actions during the ongoing government shutdown — including the furlough of its detention oversight personnel and reports of mistreatment of journalists covering immigration enforcement operations at the ICE processing center in Broadview, Illinois.In one letter, Congressman Krishnamoorthi condemned DHS’s decision to furlough the Office of Detention Oversight (ODO) — the department’s primary safeguard against abuse and neglect in federal immigration detention centers. Although DHS has continued nearly all enforcement operations and retained roughly 92 percent of its workforce, the Office of Detention Oversight has been “entirely furloughed,” leaving more than 60,000 individuals in custody nationwide without independent inspection or accountability.“ODO’s inspectors are responsible for ensuring that facilities meet federal health, safety, and humane treatment standards,” Krishnamoorthi wrote. “With detention levels now among the highest in more than a decade, suspending this critical oversight function while enforcement operations proceed uninterrupted is indefensible and represents a profound failure of priorities.”Krishnamoorthi further noted that the furlough of ODO occurred even as DHS’s press and communications staff remain fully operational, raising “serious questions about the Department’s priorities during this shutdown.” He called on Secretary Noem to provide a breakdown of furloughed personnel across DHS, explain why the oversight office was shuttered while the press office was deemed essential, and clarify who, if anyone, is currently conducting detention-facility inspections during the shutdown.In a separate letter, Krishnamoorthi raised grave concerns over the treatment of journalists during recent immigration enforcement actions in the Chicago area, including at the Broadview ICE processing center. He emphasized that a “free and independent press is essential to public accountability and the rule of law,” warning that federal actions that chill newsgathering—through force, intimidation, or secrecy—have no place in a democracy.Citing multiple, well-documented incidents, Krishnamoorthi described how clearly identified journalists in Broadview reported being shot with pepper balls, exposed to tear gas, and, in at least one case, arrested while reporting. In a separate case now under local investigation, a CBS Chicago reporter’s vehicle was allegedly struck by a pepper-ball round outside the Broadview facility, dispersing chemical agents into the cabin. The Congressman also referenced allegations in Chicago Headline Club v. Noem that federal agents—“often masked and operating in combat gear”—used tear gas, flash grenades, and rubber bullets against journalists who were complying with police instructions, noting that “such conduct raises serious constitutional concerns and demands accountability from DHS leadership.”Krishnamoorthi further cited reports that hundreds of federalized National Guard troops are now operating in and around the Chicago area under presidential authority that is being challenged in federal court. “These developments underscore the urgent need for DHS to reaffirm its obligation to uphold—not suppress—the First Amendment rights of journalists and peaceful assembly,” he wrote.To uphold the First Amendment and restore public confidence, the Congressman requested that DHS provide:All policies and training materials governing interactions with journalists;Any operational plans, directives, or field guidance for Operation Midway Blitz concerning press access, media safety zones, and use-of-force thresholds;Incident-level data on uses of force or detentions involving journalists since September 1, 2025; andDetails of any coordination with federalized National Guard units or local authorities related to media access and crowd control.Krishnamoorthi also urged DHS to adopt an explicit arrest-avoidance policy for journalists, ensure visible identification for all responding agents, and meet with press-freedom organizations and Illinois news outlets to establish lawful and transparent press-police protocols.“Oversight and transparency are not optional; they are essential for maintaining public trust in the U.S. government,” Krishnamoorthi wrote. “At a time when that trust is historically low, DHS must recommit to accountability — both for how it treats those in its custody and those who report on it.Congressman Krishnamoorthi’s letter on the furlough of the Department of Homeland Security’s detention oversight person is available here.Congressman Krishnamoorthi’s letter on his concerns with the Department of Homeland Security’s treatment of the press is available here.","content_cn":"图片\n首页\n媒体\n新闻稿\n克里希纳穆尔蒂就拘留监督暂停及伊利诺伊州ICE设施记者遭不当对待的报道向国土安全部长诺姆施压\n2025年10月17日 新闻稿\n伊利诺伊州绍姆堡——国会议员拉贾·克里希纳穆尔蒂昨晚致函国土安全部长克里斯蒂·诺姆，要求其对国土安全部在持续政府停摆期间的行为负责——包括让其拘留监督人员停职休假，以及有关在伊利诺伊州布罗德维尤ICE处理中心报道移民执法行动的记者遭到不当对待的报道。\n在一封信中，克里希纳穆尔蒂议员谴责国土安全部决定让拘留监督办公室（ODO）——该部门防止联邦移民拘留中心内虐待和忽视的主要保障机构——停职休假。尽管国土安全部几乎继续了所有执法行动，并保留了约92%的员工，但拘留监督办公室已被“完全停职休假”，使全国超过6万名在押人员失去独立检查和问责。\n“ODO的检查员负责确保各设施符合联邦健康、安全和人道待遇标准，”克里希纳穆尔蒂写道。“在拘留人数现已达到十多年来最高水平之际，在执法行动不间断进行的同时暂停这一关键监督职能是站不住脚的，代表着优先事项的严重失败。”\n克里希纳穆尔蒂进一步指出，ODO被停职休假之际，国土安全部的新闻和通讯人员却仍全面运作，这引发了“对该部门在此次停摆期间优先事项的严重质疑”。他呼吁诺姆部长提供国土安全部各部门停职休假人员的明细，解释为何监督办公室被关闭而新闻办公室却被视为必要，并说明在停摆期间目前由谁（如果有的话）进行拘留设施检查。\n在另一封信中，克里希纳穆尔蒂对记者在芝加哥地区近期移民执法行动中（包括在布罗德维尤ICE处理中心）受到的对待提出严重关切。他强调，“自由和独立的新闻界对公共问责和法治至关重要”，并警告说，通过武力、恐吓或保密来压制新闻采集的联邦行为在民主国家没有立足之地。\n克里希纳穆尔蒂援引多起有充分记录的事件，描述了布罗德维尤身份明确可辨的记者报告称遭到胡椒球射击、接触催泪瓦斯，并至少有一人在报道时被捕。在另一起目前正由地方调查的案件中，一名CBS芝加哥记者的车辆据称在布罗德维尤设施外被胡椒球击中，化学剂散入车厢。这位国会议员还提到“芝加哥头条俱乐部诉诺姆案”中的指控，称联邦探员——“往往蒙面并身着作战装备”——对遵守警方指示的记者使用催泪瓦斯、闪光弹和橡皮子弹，并指出“此类行为引发严重的宪法关切，要求国土安全部领导层承担责任”。\n克里希纳穆尔蒂还援引报道称，数百名被联邦化的国民警卫队士兵目前正在芝加哥地区及其周边根据总统授权行动，而该授权正受到联邦法院的质疑。“这些事态发展凸显了国土安全部迫切需要重申其维护——而非压制——记者第一修正案权利及和平集会权利的义务，”他写道。\n为维护第一修正案并恢复公众信心，这位国会议员要求国土安全部提供：\n所有规范与记者互动的政策和培训材料；\n“中途闪电战”行动中有关媒体准入、媒体安全区和武力使用门槛的任何行动计划、指令或现场指导；\n自2025年9月1日以来涉及记者的武力使用或拘留的事件级数据；以及\n与联邦化国民警卫队单位或地方当局就媒体准入和人群控制进行任何协调的细节。\n克里希纳穆尔蒂还敦促国土安全部对记者采取明确的避免逮捕政策，确保所有响应探员有可见的身份标识，并与新闻自由组织和伊利诺伊州新闻媒体会面，建立合法透明的新闻-警方协议。\n“监督和透明不是可选项；它们对维持公众对美国政府的信任至关重要，”克里希纳穆尔蒂写道。“在该信任处于历史低点之际，国土安全部必须重新致力于问责——无论是对其如何对待在押人员，还是对报道它的人。\n克里希纳穆尔蒂议员关于国土安全部拘留监督人员停职休假的信可在此处查阅。\n克里希纳穆尔蒂议员关于其对国土安全部对待新闻界关切的信可在此处查阅。","publish_source":"krishnamoorthi.house.gov","publish_time":"2025-10-17T11:49:36-04:00"}},{"id":"news-1853","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"排名成员克里希纳穆尔蒂与加西亚要求部长克里斯蒂·诺姆就DHS杀人、非法拘留、系统性虐待及失控行动作证","title_en":"Ranking Members Krishnamoorthi and Garcia Demand Secretary Kristi Noem Testify on DHS Killings, Unlawful Detentions, Systemic Abuse, and Out of Control Operations Like 'Midway Blitz'","summary_cn":"2026年1月12日，众议院监督与政府改革委员会排名成员罗伯特·加西亚与小组委员会排名成员拉贾·克里希纳穆尔蒂致函主席詹姆斯·科默，要求立即安排公开听证会，让国土安全部长克里斯蒂·诺姆就致命执法行动、非法拘留和驱逐美国公民及系统性虐待宣誓作证。信中提及2026年1月7日美国公民蕾妮·古德在明尼阿波利斯被ICE官员枪杀，并批评诺姆事后发表不实声明。","summary_en":"On January 12, 2026, Ranking Members Robert Garcia and Raja Krishnamoorthi called on Oversight Chairman James Comer to immediately schedule a public hearing requiring DHS Secretary Kristi Noem to testify under oath on deadly enforcement actions, unlawful detentions and deportations of U.S. citizens, and systemic abuse. The letter cited the January 7, 2026 killing of U.S. citizen Renee Good by an ICE officer in Minneapolis and criticized Noem's false statements afterward.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-18T15:45:31.607313+00:00","url":"http://krishnamoorthi.house.gov/media/press-releases/ranking-members-krishnamoorthi-and-garcia-demand-secretary-kristi-noem-testify","content":"Image\nHome\nMedia\nPress Releases\nRanking Members Krishnamoorthi and Garcia Demand Secretary Kristi Noem Testify on DHS Killings, Unlawful Detentions, Systemic Abuse, and Out of Control Operations Like 'Midway Blitz'January 12, 2026 Press ReleaseWASHINGTON — Today, House Committee on Oversight and Government Reform Ranking Member Robert Garcia (D-CA) and Subcommittee on Health Care and Financial Services Ranking Member Raja Krishnamoorthi (D-IL) called on Oversight Chairman James Comer (R-KY) to immediately schedule a public hearing requiring Department of Homeland Security Secretary Kristi Noem to provide sworn testimony on deadly enforcement actions, unlawful detentions and deportations of U.S. citizens, and a documented pattern of abuse under her leadership.“To Democrats and Republicans, it is readily apparent that her gross mismanagement of one of the federal government’s most powerful agencies has left communities shattered, Americans dead or injured, citizens unlawfully detained and even deported, and federal agents encouraged to engage in aggressive tactics,” the Ranking Members wrote in their letter. “Over the past year, DHS has carried out raids across the country that have detained U.S. citizens, violated court orders, and even deported Americans. These actions have brought violence to communities around our country.”The letter highlighted the January 7, 2026, killing of Renee Good, a U.S. citizen and mother shot by an ICE officer in Minneapolis, and condemned DHS leadership’s response in the immediate aftermath.“In the wake of these shocking abuses, Secretary Noem and the Department have responded to public outrage with blatant lies. For example, hours after the tragic shooting death of Ms. Good, Secretary Noem declared that Ms. Good had attacked ICE officers and attempted to run them over—a conclusory statement that is devoid of the truth and has been debunked by eyewitness accounts and video analysis.”Beyond the Minneapolis shooting, the Ranking Members cited a broader record of systemic misconduct, writing, “Under her leadership, the Department has deployed tear gas against our constituents, undermined the legal immigration system by detaining asylum seekers at their own court appointments, and recorded the highest number of immigration detainee deaths in nearly 20 years.”The letter notes that Oversight Democrats have repeatedly sought Secretary Noem’s testimony, including a unanimous Democratic vote on January 7, 2026, to subpoena DHS regarding Ms. Good’s killing. As the Members state. The Ranking Members concluded the letter by making clear that continued refusal will trigger compulsory action and called upon Chairman Comer to schedule voluntary testimony.The letter is available here.","content_cn":"图片\n首页\n媒体\n新闻稿\n资深成员克里希纳穆尔蒂和加西亚要求部长克里斯蒂·诺姆就国土安全部杀人事件、非法拘留、系统性虐待以及像“中途闪电战”这样失控的行动作证\n2026年1月12日 新闻稿\n华盛顿——今天，众议院监督与政府改革委员会资深成员罗伯特·加西亚（加州民主党）和医疗保健与金融服务小组委员会资深成员拉贾·克里希纳穆尔蒂（伊利诺伊州民主党）呼吁监督委员会主席詹姆斯·科默（肯塔基州共和党）立即安排公开听证会，要求国土安全部部长克里斯蒂·诺姆就其领导下的致命执法行动、对美国公民的非法拘留和驱逐，以及有记录的虐待模式提供宣誓证词。\n“对民主党人和共和党人来说，显而易见的是，她对联邦政府最强大机构之一的严重管理不善已使社区支离破碎，美国人死亡或受伤，公民被非法拘留甚至驱逐，联邦探员被鼓励采取激进策略，”资深成员们在信中写道。“在过去一年里，国土安全部在全国各地开展突袭行动，拘留了美国公民，违反了法院命令，甚至驱逐了美国人。这些行动给我国各地社区带来了暴力。”\n信中强调了2026年1月7日美国公民、母亲蕾妮·古德在明尼阿波利斯被一名ICE官员枪杀的事件，并谴责国土安全部领导层在事发后的回应。\n“在这些令人震惊的虐待行为发生后，诺姆部长和该部门以赤裸裸的谎言回应公众愤怒。例如，在古德女士不幸遭枪杀数小时后，诺姆部长宣称古德女士袭击了ICE官员并试图驾车撞倒他们——这一结论性声明毫无事实依据，已被目击者陈述和视频分析驳斥。”\n除明尼阿波利斯枪击事件外，资深成员们还列举了更广泛的系统性不当行为记录，写道：“在她的领导下，该部门对我们的选民使用催泪瓦斯，通过在寻求庇护者自己的法庭预约时拘留他们来破坏合法移民制度，并录得近20年来最高的移民被拘留者死亡人数。”\n信中指出，监督委员会民主党人已多次寻求诺姆部长作证，包括2026年1月7日民主党一致投票决定就古德女士被杀事件向国土安全部发出传票。正如成员们所述。资深成员们在信末明确表示，继续拒绝将触发强制行动，并呼吁科默主席安排自愿作证。\n该信可在此处查阅。","publish_source":"krishnamoorthi.house.gov","publish_time":"2026-01-12T15:15:40-05:00"}},{"id":"news-2381","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"国土安全部因ICE批评针对康涅狄格州议员，他称不会退缩","title_en":"Homeland Security targets CT congressman for ICE criticism. He says he won’t back down.","summary_cn":"2025年9月19日《哈特福德新闻报》报道，国土安全部在查理·柯克遇刺及两起ICE探员遇袭后，发布声明指责“媒体、左翼团体和庇护政客”煽动暴力，并点名包括康涅狄格州众议员约翰·B·拉森在内的国会议员。拉森曾将ICE比作盖世太保和党卫军，并推动《禁止秘密警察法》。他和康州总检察长威廉·童称DHS此举是在针对批评者，重申捍卫宪法权利。","summary_en":"On September 19, 2025, the Hartford Courant reported that DHS, after Charlie Kirk's assassination and two assaults on ICE agents, issued a statement blaming the media, leftist groups and sanctuary politicians for political violence, naming congresspeople including Connecticut Rep. John B. Larson. Larson had likened ICE to the Gestapo and SS and pushed the No Secret Police Act. He and Connecticut AG William Tong said DHS was targeting critics and reaffirmed defending constitutional rights.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-18T16:20:55.323129+00:00","url":"http://larson.house.gov/media-center/in-the-news/homeland-security-targets-ct-congressman-ice-criticism-he-says-he-wont","content":"Home\nMedia\nIn the News\nHomeland Security targets CT congressman for ICE criticism. He says he won’t back down.\nImage September 19, 2025 In The NewsHartford Courant: Homeland Security targets CT congressman for ICE criticism. H…The Department of Homeland Security, following President Donald Trump, blamed “the media, leftist groups, and sanctuary politicians” for political violence and assaults on ICE agents, specifically naming U.S. congresspeople including Connecticut Rep. John B. Larson.The statement, posted to the official Homeland Security website, refers to the assassination last week of conservative activist Charlie Kirk and two recent assaults on ICE agents. The statement includes a quote from Assistant Secretary Tricia McLaughlin but text outside the quote also uses partisan language. It is entitled “DHS Calls for Media and Far Left to Stop the Demonization of President Trump, His Supporters, and DHS Law Enforcement.”“Following the evil act of political violence in the country this week and two brutal assaults on our brave ICE law enforcement last week, we are once again calling on the media and the far left to stop the hateful rhetoric directed at President Trump, those who support him, and our brave DHS law enforcement,” McLaughlin is quoted as saying in the statement.“This demonization is inspiring violence across the country. Our ICE officers are facing a more than 1000% increase in assaults against them. We have to turn down the temperature before someone else is killed. This violence must end.”A long list naming members of Congress, Democratic politicians, TikTokers and the ACLU follows with screenshots of conservative social media accounts quoting their criticisms of Immigration and Customs Enforcement. Many are from Rapid Response 47, which is attributed to the Trump and the White House. DHS describes the list as “violent rhetoric against DHS law enforcement.” Most of the criticism, including from Larson, likens ICE to the Gestapo, secret police, the SS, a neo-Nazi and a Nazi group.Larson, who recently called on Congress to pass the No Secret Police Act, which would require ICE agents to identify themselves and prohibit them from wearing masks, and the Protecting Sensitive Locations Act, to prevent ICE raids at schools, hospitals, courthouses, and places of worship, is shown in a video shouting, “This is not Germany. That’s the SS and the Gestapo. This is the United States of America – unmask yourselves.”Larson and Connecticut Attorney General William Tong described the DHS statement as “targeting Rep. Larson and immigrant advocates for speaking out against ICE’s abusive tactics and reaffirmed their commitment to defending constitutional rights and holding the Trump Administration accountable for its attacks on free speech and civil liberties.”The statement comes as Trump has blamed left-leaning groups for Kirk’s murder and threatened to crack down on “dangerous” political speech. Following Kirk’s murder thousands of Democrats were targeted with calls for their firing, expulsion or investigation for social media posts deemed celebratory or critical of Kirk. In Connecticut, at least one local official has stepped down after backlash for a social media post.It also coincides with the indefinite suspension of late-night ABC host Jimmy Kimmel over comments about conservative response to Kirk’s death. Trump had previously called for Kimmel’s firing and Democrats, including former President Barack Obama and FCC Commissioner Anna Gomez, have called it censorship and government coercion.While Republicans have decried Democrats as inciting political violence, Larson and Tong alleged the DHS post itself is dangerous.“This report is reckless, and this kind of irresponsible tagging of political enemies needs to stop…. ,” Tong said. “We have to do better.  But if I know one thing about John Larson, he will not be silenced. He’s going to keep speaking up—loudly—to call out wrongs when they occur, to defend our rights and our democracy, and to protect Connecticut families. And he’s going to do that with his voice and his votes, and it is incumbent upon all of us to see and know the difference between forceful and necessary democratic protest and bloodshed.”Gary Rose, professor of politics and scholar in residence at Sacred Heart University, said the DHS statement is a departure from normal workings of a government agency.“It’s very atypical for an executive agency to be calling out members of Congress and what is particularly interesting about that is that these agencies depend on congressional support for their survival,” Rose said by phone Thursday. “It’s very unusual to see the hostility against Congress.”The politicization is, he said, a symptom of the partisan division that is endemic in American society today.“It’s a reflection of the atmosphere we’re living in. Each side believes the other is hostile – that’s what’s going on here. And for Kristi Noem and others to be accusing members of Congress, it is a reflection of what has emerged in American politics these days,” Rose said.At Sacred Heart in Fairfield and across the country, he said, meetings and discussions are taking place about toning down rhetoric and working to restore civility. Several leaders have called this moment an inflection point in American politics and culture in which leaders should seek unity amid increasingly divisive views often perpetuated on social media in order to stem a wave of political violence.Rose said he didn’t hold much hope that would occur.“It’s getting worse and it’s going to get worse in the days and months and years ahead. I can’t say it’s just associated with the Trump presidency but I will say it has accelerated greatly under him,” Rose said. “Trump has the largest megaphone on that and he certainly can keep that going for as long as he wants but on the other side we have (U.S. Sen.) Chris Murphy and some people from Congress who also have megaphones.“They really see it as important to placate their unique constituencies and it does sustain them. If it didn’t they probably would tone it down but they find it benefits them.”Murphy, who has been one of Democrats’ most vocal critics of Trump, has claimed the president is rushing the country into fascism and illegally profiting off the presidency. Thursday he introduced the “No Political Enemies Act,” to put in place legal protections for prosecution or harassment for political speech.“The shooting of Charlie Kirk was a national tragedy. It should have been a line in the sand, an opportunity for President Trump to bring this country together, to do whatever is necessary to stamp out political violence … but Trump and his lieutenants are choosing a different path. They are choosing to exploit this tragedy, to weaponize the federal government to destroy Donald Trump’s political opposition,” Murphy said in a press conference announcing the Act.He referred to Kimmel’s firing: “Trump’s FCC forced a major network to pull a loud Trump critic, Jimmy Kimmel, off the air essentially saying that any media actor who doesn’t say what Trump wants them to say about Charlie Kirk or Trump’s policies is going to be silenced. That’s censorship. That’s state speech control. That’s not America. Trump is making it 100% clear that he is going to ramp up his efforts to use the power of the federal government to harass and punish his critics – not because they’re supporters of political violence – they are not – but because they have the audacity to openly oppose his policies.”\nIssues:ImmigrationStanding Up to Trump and ‘DOGE’","content_cn":"首页\n媒体\n新闻报道\n国土安全部因康涅狄格州议员批评ICE而将其列为目标。他表示不会退缩。\n图片 2025年9月19日 新闻报道 《哈特福德新闻报》：国土安全部因康涅狄格州议员批评ICE而将其列为目标。他……\n国土安全部追随总统唐纳德·特朗普，将政治暴力和针对ICE特工的袭击归咎于“媒体、左翼团体和庇护政客”，并特别点名了包括康涅狄格州众议员约翰·B·拉森在内的美国国会议员。\n这份发布在国土安全部官方网站上的声明，提到了上周保守派活动人士查理·柯克遭暗杀事件以及近期两起针对ICE特工的袭击。声明中引用了助理部长特里西娅·麦克劳克林的一段话，但引文之外的文字同样使用了党派性语言。声明标题为“国土安全部呼吁媒体和极左翼停止对特朗普总统、其支持者及国土安全部执法人员的妖魔化”。\n声明中援引麦克劳克林的话说：“在本周国内发生邪恶的政治暴力行为、上周我们勇敢的ICE执法人员遭到两起残暴袭击之后，我们再次呼吁媒体和极左翼停止针对特朗普总统、其支持者以及我们勇敢的国土安全部执法人员的仇恨言论。”\n“这种妖魔化正在全国范围内煽动暴力。我们的ICE官员遭受的袭击增加了1000%以上。我们必须在还有人被杀之前降温。这种暴力必须停止。”\n声明随后列出了一长串国会议员、民主党政治人物、TikTok博主和美国公民自由联盟的名字，并附上保守派社交媒体账号引用他们批评移民和海关执法局的截图。其中许多来自“快速反应47”，该账号被归于特朗普和白宫。国土安全部将这份名单描述为“针对国土安全部执法人员的暴力言论”。大多数批评，包括拉森的言论，都将ICE比作盖世太保、秘密警察、党卫军、新纳粹和纳粹组织。\n拉森最近呼吁国会通过《禁止秘密警察法案》，该法案将要求ICE特工表明身份并禁止他们戴口罩，以及《保护敏感地点法案》，以防止ICE在学校、医院、法院和礼拜场所进行突袭。在一段视频中，他高喊：“这不是德国。那是党卫军和盖世太保。这里是美利坚合众国——摘下你们的面具。”\n拉森和康涅狄格州总检察长威廉·童将国土安全部的声明描述为“针对拉森议员和移民倡导者，因为他们发声反对ICE的虐待性手段，并重申他们致力于捍卫宪法权利，追究特朗普政府攻击言论自由和公民自由的責任”。\n这份声明发布之际，特朗普正将柯克之死归咎于左倾团体，并威胁要打击“危险的”政治言论。柯克被杀后，数千名民主党人因在社交媒体上发布被视为庆祝柯克之死或批评柯克的帖子而成为被要求解雇、开除或调查的目标。在康涅狄格州，至少有一名地方官员因一条社交媒体帖子引发反弹后辞职。\n此事还恰逢美国广播公司深夜节目主持人吉米·坎摩尔因评论保守派对柯克之死的反应而被无限期停播。特朗普此前曾呼吁解雇坎摩尔，包括前总统巴拉克·奥巴马和联邦通信委员会委员安娜·戈麦斯在内的民主党人称这是审查和政府胁迫。\n尽管共和党人谴责民主党人煽动政治暴力，拉森和童却指称国土安全部的帖子本身就很危险。\n“这份报告是鲁莽的，这种不负责任地将政治对手标记出来的做法必须停止……”童说。“我们必须做得更好。但如果说我对约翰·拉森有一点了解，那就是他不会沉默。他会继续大声发声——在错误发生时指出错误，捍卫我们的权利和民主，保护康涅狄格州的家庭。他将用他的声音和选票来做到这一点，而我们所有人都有责任看到并分清强有力的、必要的民主抗议与流血事件之间的区别。”\n圣心大学政治学教授兼驻校学者加里·罗斯表示，国土安全部的声明偏离了政府机构的正常运作方式。\n“一个行政机构点名国会议员是非常不寻常的，特别有趣的是，这些机构的生存依赖于国会的支持，”罗斯周四在电话中说。“看到对国会如此敌意是非常不寻常的。”\n他说，这种政治化是当今美国社会普遍存在的党派分裂的一个症状。\n“这反映了我们生活的氛围。每一方都认为对方充满敌意——这就是正在发生的事情。克里斯蒂·诺姆和其他人指责国会议员，反映了美国政治中近来出现的现象，”罗斯说。\n他说，在费尔菲尔德的圣心大学以及全国各地，正在举行会议和讨论，主题是缓和言论并努力恢复文明。多位领导人称这一时刻是美国政治和文化的转折点，领导人应在日益分裂的观点（往往在社交媒体上被放大）中寻求团结，以遏制政治暴力浪潮。\n罗斯说，他对这种情况会发生不抱太大希望。\n“情况正在恶化，而且在未来数日、数月和数年里还会更糟。我不能说这仅仅与特朗普的总统任期有关，但我要说，在他任内这大大加速了，”罗斯说。“特朗普拥有最大的扩音器，他当然可以想持续多久就持续多久，但另一方面我们还有（美国参议员）克里斯·墨菲和一些国会议员，他们也有扩音器。\n“他们确实认为重要的是要发\n[正文过长，翻译截断；对象库保留全文]","publish_source":"larson.house.gov","publish_time":"2025-09-19T11:10:38-04:00"}},{"id":"news-2054","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"拉森抨击FBI因民主党议员行使第一修正案权利而展开调查","title_en":"Larson Blasts Disgraceful FBI Inquiry into Democratic Lawmakers for Exercising First Amendment Rights","summary_cn":"2025年11月25日，康涅狄格州第一选区众议员约翰·B·拉森发表声明，抨击联邦调查局反恐部门通知六名民主党议员将对其展开调查，包括参议员马克·凯利和埃莉萨·斯洛特金，以及众议员贾森·克劳、玛吉·古德兰德、克里斯·德卢齐奥和克丽西·胡拉汉。此前特朗普总统曾呼吁逮捕和起诉这些议员，因其出现在一段行使言论自由的视频中。拉森称此举是威权主义的新浪潮，表示不会被吓倒。","summary_en":"On November 25, 2025, Rep. John B. Larson (CT-01) released a statement blasting the FBI's Counterterrorism Division for notifying six Democratic lawmakers of an inquiry into them, including Senators Mark Kelly and Elissa Slotkin and Reps. Jason Crow, Maggie Goodlander, Chris Deluzio, and Chrissy Houlahan. The investigations followed President Trump's calls for their arrest and prosecution over a video in which they exercised free speech. Larson called it a new surge of authoritarianism and said he and his colleagues will not be intimidated.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-24T21:28:52.849979+00:00","url":"http://larson.house.gov/media-center/press-releases/larson-blasts-disgraceful-fbi-inquiry-democratic-lawmakers-exercising","content":"Home\nMedia\nPress Releases\nLarson Blasts Disgraceful FBI Inquiry into Democratic Lawmakers for Exercising First Amendment RightsNovember 25, 2025 Press ReleaseEast Hartford, CT – Today, Rep. John B. Larson (CT-01) released the following statement after the FBI’s Counterterrorism Division notified six Democratic lawmakers that they were launching an inquiry into them – Senators Mark Kelly (D-AZ) and Elissa Slotkin (D-MI), and Reps. Jason Crow (CO-06), Maggie Goodlander (NH-02), Chris Deluzio (PA-17), and Chrissy Houlahan (PA-06). These investigations come after President Trump called for their arrest and prosecution for appearing in a video exercising their freedom of speech. The President has suggested that their actions should be “punishable by death.”    “If the United States Congress speaking its will as a co-equal branch of government is now considered sedition and terrorism by President Trump and his henchmen, then we are entering a new surge of authoritarianism,” said Larson. “I stand firmly with my four colleagues in the House, and the two United States Senators, who as former members of the military and Intelligence communities, spoke vociferously about servicemembers’ constitutional rights and responsibilities. As they pointed out, we take an oath of allegiance, not to any President of the United States, but to the Constitution. Donald Trump might think he can use the FBI to scare my colleagues into silence, but it will not work. We the people will not be intimidated.”\nIssues:DefenseJudicialStanding Up to Trump and ‘DOGE’","content_cn":"首页\n媒体\n新闻稿\n拉尔森抨击联邦调查局对民主党议员行使第一修正案权利的可耻调查\n2025年11月25日 新闻稿\n康涅狄格州东哈特福德——今天，约翰·B·拉尔森众议员（CT-01）发表以下声明。此前，联邦调查局反恐部门通知六名民主党议员，将对他们展开调查——参议员马克·凯利（D-AZ）和埃莉萨·斯洛特金（D-MI），以及众议员杰森·克罗（CO-06）、玛吉·古德兰德（NH-02）、克里斯·德卢齐奥（PA-17）和克丽丝·霍拉汉（PA-06）。这些调查发生在特朗普总统呼吁逮捕并起诉他们之后，因为他们出现在一段行使言论自由的视频中。总统还暗示，他们的行为应当“处以死刑”。\n“如果美国国会作为政府中平等的一支表达自己的意志，如今被特朗普总统及其爪牙视为煽动叛乱和恐怖主义，那么我们正在进入新一轮威权主义浪潮，”拉尔森说。“我坚定地支持我在众议院的四位同事，以及两位美国参议员。他们曾是军方和情报部门成员，就军人受宪法保障的权利和责任直言不讳。正如他们所指出的，我们宣誓效忠的不是任何一位美国总统，而是宪法。唐纳德·特朗普可能以为他可以利用联邦调查局吓唬我的同事，让他们保持沉默，但这不会奏效。我们人民不会受到恐吓。”\n议题：国防 司法 挺身反对特朗普和“DOGE”","publish_source":"larson.house.gov","publish_time":"2025-11-25T17:58:52-05:00"}},{"id":"news-1868","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"拉森呼吁国土安全部长诺姆辞职，将提出法案阻止ICE未经州协调开展行动","title_en":"Larson Calls for Homeland Security Secretary Noem to Resign, Will Introduce Bill Blocking ICE Activities Without State Coordination","summary_cn":"美国众议员约翰·B·拉森就明尼阿波利斯暴力事件发表声明，呼吁国土安全部长克里斯蒂·诺姆辞职，指责其谎称死者为国内恐怖分子且无证据。拉森称武装ICE特工在缺乏监督和与地方执法协调的情况下行动导致流血事件，要求进行独立调查，并表示将提出立法，允许各州在未与州及地方执法机构充分协调时阻止ICE在其境内行动。","summary_en":"U.S. Rep. John B. Larson released a statement calling for Homeland Security Secretary Kristi Noem to resign following violence in Minneapolis. Larson accused Noem of falsely labeling Renee Nicole Good a domestic terrorist without evidence, blamed armed ICE agents operating without oversight or coordination with local law enforcement for bloodshed, demanded a full independent investigation, and said he will introduce legislation allowing states to block ICE operations within their borders absent full coordination with state and local law enforcement.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-24T20:43:12.219581+00:00","url":"http://larson.house.gov/media-center/press-releases/larson-calls-homeland-security-secretary-noem-resign-will-introduce","content":"Home\nMedia\nPress Releases\nLarson Calls for Homeland Security Secretary Noem to Resign, Will Introduce Bill Blocking ICE Activities Without State Coordination January 8, 2026 Press ReleaseWashington, D.C. - Today, Rep. John B. Larson (CT-01) released the following statement calling for Homeland Security Secretary Kristi Noem to resign following the violence in Minneapolis yesterday.  “This was a direct result of authoritarianism,” said Larson. “This was not an accident. There is blood on the hands of this Administration, the ICE agents involved in the execution of an American citizen, and every senior official in the Trump regime who has knowingly allowed these dangerous practices to continue.  “For months, I and others have warned that flooding our communities with armed ICE agents, masked, carrying military-grade weapons, operating without oversight and without coordination with local law enforcement, would end in bloodshed. This was never a question of if. It was always a question of when. That moment has arrived,” Larson continued. “Renee Nicole Good is dead. Three children have lost their mother. And responsibility does not end at the scene. It runs directly up the chain of command,” Larson continued. “This failure must be addressed. Kristi Noem must resign immediately after lying to the American people and claiming Renee was a domestic terrorist with no evidence or investigation. As Secretary of Homeland Security, she is responsible for overseeing ICE. Her continued leadership is incompatible with public safety, constitutional governance, and basic human decency,” Larson continued. “There must also be a full, independent investigation into this killing, including the actions of the agents who were involved, the command decisions that authorized these operations, and the policymakers who enabled this culture of lawlessness,” Larson continued.  “Until these tactics are stopped, more lives will be lost,” Larson concluded. “I will introduce legislation allowing states to prevent ICE from operating in their borders without full coordination with state and local law enforcement agencies. Enough is enough.”\nIssues:ImmigrationJudicialStanding Up to Trump and ‘DOGE’","content_cn":"主页\n媒体\n新闻稿\n拉尔森呼吁国土安全部长诺姆辞职，并将提出法案，阻止ICE未经州协调开展活动 2026年1月8日 新闻稿 华盛顿特区——今天，众议员约翰·B·拉尔森（康涅狄格州第01选区）发表以下声明，呼吁国土安全部长克里斯蒂·诺姆在昨日明尼阿波利斯发生暴力事件后辞职。\n“这是威权主义的直接结果，”拉尔森说。“这不是意外。这届政府、参与执行一名美国公民行动的ICE特工，以及特朗普政权中每一位明知却允许这些危险做法继续下去的高级官员，都手上沾有鲜血。\n“数月来，我和其他人一直警告，把全副武装的ICE特工大量派入我们的社区，他们戴着面具、携带军用级武器，在没有监督、也没有与地方执法部门协调的情况下行动，最终将导致流血。这从来不是‘是否会发生’的问题，而一直是‘何时发生’的问题。那个时刻已经到来，”拉尔森继续说。\n“蕾妮·妮科尔·古德死了。三个孩子失去了母亲。而责任不会止于现场，它会一直沿着指挥链向上追究，”拉尔森继续说。\n“必须处理这一失败。克里斯蒂·诺姆在没有任何证据或调查的情况下，向美国人民撒谎并声称蕾妮是国内恐怖分子，因此必须立即辞职。作为国土安全部长，她负责监督ICE。她继续领导与公共安全、宪政治理和基本的人道良知不相容，”拉尔森继续说。\n“还必须对这起杀戮展开全面、独立的调查，包括涉事特工的行为、授权这些行动的指挥决定，以及助长这种无法无天文化的政策制定者，”拉尔森继续说。\n“如果不停止这些策略，还会有更多生命失去，”拉尔森总结道。“我将提出立法，允许各州在ICE未与州和地方执法机构进行全面协调的情况下，阻止其在本州境内开展行动。够了。”\n议题：移民；司法；反对特朗普和‘DOGE’","publish_source":"larson.house.gov","publish_time":"2026-01-08T11:01:22-05:00"}},{"id":"news-1795","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"拉森反对未能约束ICE的国土安全部拨款法案","title_en":"Larson to Oppose Homeland Security Funding Bill that Fails to Rein in ICE","summary_cn":"众议员约翰·B·拉森宣布反对国土安全部拨款法案，该法案为ICE提供新资金却未包含问责改革。拉森批评特朗普和诺姆将ICE变成秘密警察，称其武装蒙面探员在康涅狄格州拆散家庭、在芝加哥对儿童使用催泪瓦斯，并捍卫在明尼阿波利斯枪杀美国公民的行为。他列举了要求探员表明身份、禁止蒙面、限制使用武力等改革诉求，表示将投反对票。","summary_en":"Rep. John B. Larson announced his opposition to the Department of Homeland Security funding bill, which provides new funding for ICE without accountability reforms. Larson criticized Trump and Noem for turning ICE into a secret police force, citing armed masked agents separating families in Connecticut, tear gassing children in Chicago, and defending the killing of an American citizen in Minneapolis. He listed reforms including unmasking agents, requiring warrants, and use of force requirements, and said he will vote no.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-18T15:42:07.239913+00:00","url":"http://larson.house.gov/media-center/press-releases/larson-oppose-homeland-security-funding-bill-fails-rein-ice","content":"Home\nMedia\nPress Releases\nLarson to Oppose Homeland Security Funding Bill that Fails to Rein in ICEJanuary 20, 2026 Press ReleaseWashington, D.C. - Ahead of a House vote later this week, Rep. John B. Larson (CT-01) announced his opposition to the Department of Homeland Security funding bill that provides new funding for ICE but does not include reforms to hold the agency accountable for their abuses of power. “Donald Trump and Kristi Noem have transformed ICE into their own secret police force, accountable to no one,” said Larson. “They have sent armed, masked agents to snatch mothers from their children here in Connecticut, overseen the tear gassing of kids in Chicago, and even defended the execution of an American citizen in Minneapolis – baselessly castigating Renee Nicole Good as a ‘domestic terrorist.’  While Democrats fought for reforms in funding negotiations, the bill House leadership released today does not even come close to the accountability this moment demands, including unmasking agents, requiring warrants, and use of force requirements. Congress cannot in good conscience vote to authorize more funding for the culture of lawlessness that has taken hold at ICE. I will vote NO on funding for the Department of Homeland Security when it comes up for a vote this week.” Earlier this month, after an ICE agent executed an American citizen, Renee Nicole Good, earlier this month, and a federal vehicle struck a protester in Hartford, Larson and Rep. Robin Kelly (IL-02) filed articles of impeachment against U.S. Secretary of Homeland Security Kristi Noem. He has also vowed to introduce legislation to stop ICE from operating in communities without notifying state and local law enforcement, and is a cosponsor of the following reforms: No Secret Police Act to require ICE agents to identify themselves, and bar them from wearing masks, Protecting Sensitive Locations Act to prohibit ICE raids in schools, hospitals, courthouses, places of worship, and social service agencies, DHS Use of Force Oversight Act to require agents to use only the force required during an arrest, and ban abusive tactics including chokeholds, Healthcare Reinvestment Act and Make Housing Affordable and Defend Democracy Act to redirect ICE funding from the Republican budget to lower health care premiums and expand affordable housing, and the Home Together Act to prohibit housing agencies from sharing data with ICE, including home addresses, race, and ethnicity.\nIssues:Human RightsImmigrationStanding Up to Trump and ‘DOGE’","content_cn":"首页\n媒体\n新闻稿\n拉森将反对未能约束ICE的国土安全部拨款法案\n2026年1月20日 新闻稿\n华盛顿特区——在众议院本周晚些时候进行投票之前，众议员约翰·B·拉森（康涅狄格州第一选区）宣布反对国土安全部拨款法案，该法案为ICE提供新资金，但未包含追究该机构滥用权力责任的改革措施。\n“唐纳德·特朗普和克里斯蒂·诺姆已将ICE变成他们自己的秘密警察部队，不对任何人负责，”拉森说。“他们派出武装、蒙面的特工在康涅狄格州从孩子身边夺走母亲，监督在芝加哥对儿童使用催泪瓦斯，甚至为在明尼阿波利斯处决一名美国公民辩护——毫无根据地诋毁蕾妮·妮可·古德为‘国内恐怖分子’。虽然民主党人在拨款谈判中争取改革，但众议院领导层今天公布的这项法案甚至远远达不到当前所需的问责要求，包括要求特工摘下面具、要求搜查令以及使用武力的规定。国会不能昧着良心投票授权为ICE已经形成的无法无天文化提供更多资金。本周国土安全部拨款法案付诸表决时，我将投反对票。”\n本月早些时候，在一名ICE特工处决美国公民蕾妮·妮可·古德、以及一辆联邦车辆在哈特福德撞击一名抗议者之后，拉森和众议员罗宾·凯利（伊利诺伊州第二选区）对国土安全部部长克里斯蒂·诺姆提出了弹劾条款。他还誓言提出立法，阻止ICE在未通知州和地方执法部门的情况下在社区开展行动，并且是以下改革法案的共同提案人：\n《禁止秘密警察法案》，要求ICE特工表明身份，并禁止他们戴口罩；\n《保护敏感地点法案》，禁止ICE在学校、医院、法院、礼拜场所和社会服务机构进行突袭；\n《国土安全部使用武力监督法案》，要求特工在逮捕期间仅使用必要的武力，并禁止包括锁喉在内的虐待性手段；\n《医疗再投资法案》和《让住房可负担并捍卫民主法案》，将ICE资金从共和党预算中转用于降低医疗保险费和扩大可负担住房；\n以及《居家团聚法案》，禁止住房机构与ICE共享数据，包括家庭住址、种族和族裔。\n议题：人权 移民 挺身对抗特朗普和“DOGE”","publish_source":"larson.house.gov","publish_time":"2026-01-20T19:32:50-05:00"}},{"id":"news-3197","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS (deep pilot)","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"拉森抨击周五晚间解雇调查国会山骚乱和特朗普的检察官及联邦调查局特工","title_en":"Larson Slams Friday Night Firing of Prosecutors and FBI Agents Who Investigated January 6th Insurrection and Donald Trump","summary_cn":"众议员约翰·B·拉森发表声明，抨击司法部解雇参与1月6日案件处理的联邦检察官以及联邦调查局解雇参与调查特朗普的高级特工。拉森称这是“独裁者”行径，指责总统针对职业执法官员，并警告对联邦调查局和司法部的清洗将导致罪犯逍遥法外、非法命令不受阻碍地执行。","summary_en":"Rep. John B. Larson released a statement slamming the Department of Justice's dismissal of federal prosecutors who worked on January 6th cases and the FBI's firing of senior agents involved in investigating Donald Trump. Larson called it the action of a 'Dictator-in-Chief,' accusing the President of targeting career law enforcement officials and warning that the purge of the FBI and DOJ will make it more likely criminals go free and illegal orders will be carried out unimpeded.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-25T11:28:38.185117+00:00","url":"http://larson.house.gov/media-center/press-releases/larson-slams-friday-night-firing-prosecutors-and-fbi-agents-who","content":"Home\nMedia\nPress Releases\nLarson Slams Friday Night Firing of Prosecutors and FBI Agents Who Investigated January 6th Insurrection and Donald Trump\nImage January 31, 2025 Press ReleaseEast Hartford, CT - Today, Rep. John B. Larson (CT-01) released the following statement slamming the Department of Justice’s (DOJ) dismissal of federal prosecutors who worked on January 6th cases and the FBI’s firing of senior agents involved in investigating Donald Trump. “What Americans are watching and witnessing is the Dictator-in-Chief in action,” said Larson. “The American Public will not be fooled – the President, by targeting career law enforcement officials simply because they were doing their job, has made his intentions clear. No one can claim the mantle of law and order when they pardon rioters who assault police officers and fire the men and women who investigated and prosecuted them. The ongoing purge of the FBI and DOJ will only make it more likely criminals go free and illegal orders by Trump will be carried out unimpeded. This is but another example of the Dictator-in-Chief putting himself and his desire for retribution above the public interest.\"\nIssues:JudicialStanding Up to Trump and ‘DOGE’","content_cn":"首页\n媒体\n新闻稿\n拉森谴责周五夜间解雇调查1月6日国会骚乱和唐纳德·特朗普的检察官及FBI探员\n图片 2025年1月31日 新闻稿\n康涅狄格州东哈特福德——今天，众议员约翰·B·拉森（康涅狄格州第01选区）发表以下声明，谴责司法部（DOJ）解雇曾参与1月6日案件的联邦检察官，以及联邦调查局解雇参与调查唐纳德·特朗普的高级探员。\n拉森表示：“美国人正在观看和见证的是‘独裁者总司令’在行动。美国公众不会被愚弄——总统仅仅因为职业执法官员在履行职责就将其作为目标，这已清楚表明他的意图。赦免袭击警察的暴徒、并解雇调查和起诉他们的男女执法人员的人，不能自称代表法治与秩序。对FBI和DOJ持续进行的清洗，只会使犯罪分子更有可能逍遥法外，并使特朗普的非法命令得以毫无阻碍地执行。这又是‘独裁者总司令’将自己及其报复欲望置于公共利益之上的一个例子。”\n议题：\n司法\n反对特朗普和‘DOGE’","publish_source":"larson.house.gov","publish_time":"2025-01-31T19:40:27-05:00"}},{"id":"news-1459","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"拉森就美国国土安全部长克里斯蒂·诺姆被解职发表声明","title_en":"Larson Statement on the Firing of U.S. Secretary of Homeland Security Kristi Noem","summary_cn":"美国众议员约翰·B·拉森就特朗普总统解职国土安全部长克里斯蒂·诺姆发表声明。拉森称，在其与众议员罗宾·凯利提出弹劾条款两个月后诺姆离任，并批评在其任内ICE被变成特朗普的私人军队。拉森强调诺姆仍须被追责，并提到他共同提案将750亿美元ICE资金转用于恢复医疗补助削减、阻止联邦执法在投票站部署，但修正案被规则委员会阻止。","summary_en":"U.S. Rep. John B. Larson issued a statement on President Trump's firing of Homeland Security Secretary Kristi Noem, two months after Larson and Rep. Robin Kelly filed articles of impeachment. Larson said ICE had been turned into Trump's personal army under Noem and insisted she must still be held accountable. He also cosponsored amendments to redirect a $75 billion ICE fund to restore Medicaid cuts and block federal law enforcement at polling places; Republicans blocked both in the Rules Committee.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-24T20:33:42.208023+00:00","url":"http://larson.house.gov/media-center/press-releases/larson-statement-firing-us-secretary-homeland-security-kristi-noem","content":"Home\nMedia\nPress Releases\nLarson Statement on the Firing of U.S. Secretary of Homeland Security Kristi NoemMarch 5, 2026 Press ReleaseWashington, D.C. - Today, Rep. John B. Larson (CT-01) released the following statement on President Trump’s firing of U.S. Secretary of Homeland Security Kristi Noem. The President’s replacement of Secretary Noem comes two months after Larson and Rep. Robin Kelly (IL-02) first filed articles of impeachment against her. “Two months after we filed articles of impeachment against Secretary Noem, I am glad to see her days finally come to an end at the Department of Homeland Security,” said Larson. “On her watch, ICE was transformed into Donald Trump’s personal army, as federal agents executed citizens in our streets, snatched mothers from their children in our communities, and threatened peaceful protesters across the country. Make no mistake – replacing Kristi Noem is only the beginning. While she has been dismissed, she must still be held accountable. She is not above the law, nor is any future Secretary of Homeland Security.” Ahead of tonight’s expected vote in the House to approve more funding for the Department of Homeland Security, Larson cosponsored amendments to redirect their $75 billion ICE slush fund to restoring the Republican Budget’s cut to Medicaid and block federal law enforcement from being deployed at polling places. Both amendments were blocked from advancing to a full House vote by Republicans on the Rules Committee last night. Larson has called for disbanding ICE and is championing legislation in Congress to require federal agents to identify themselves; bar ICE raids in schools, hospitals, courthouses, and places of worship; ban abusive tactics including chokeholds; and redirect ICE funding from the Republican budget to lower health care premiums and expand affordable housing.\nIssues:Human RightsImmigrationStanding Up to Trump and ‘DOGE’","content_cn":"首页\n媒体\n新闻稿\nLarson 关于解雇美国国土安全部长 Kristi Noem 的声明\n2026 年 3 月 5 日 新闻稿\n华盛顿特区——今天，众议员 John B. Larson（康涅狄格州第 01 选区）就特朗普总统解雇美国国土安全部长 Kristi Noem 发表以下声明。总统更换 Noem 部长，距离 Larson 和众议员 Robin Kelly（伊利诺伊州第 02 选区）首次对她提出弹劾条款已过去两个月。\nLarson 表示：“在我们对 Noem 部长提出弹劾条款两个月后，我很高兴看到她在国土安全部的日子终于结束了。在她任内，ICE 被转变为 Donald Trump 的私人军队，联邦特工在我们的街道上处决公民，在我们的社区中从孩子身边夺走母亲，并威胁全国各地的和平抗议者。请勿误解——替换 Kristi Noem 仅仅是开始。尽管她已被免职，她仍必须被追究责任。她并不凌驾于法律之上，任何未来的国土安全部长也不例外。”\n在预计众议院今晚就批准为国土安全部提供更多资金进行投票之前，Larson 联署提出修正案，拟将其 750 亿美元 ICE 自由支配资金重新用于恢复共和党预算对 Medicaid 的削减，并禁止在投票地点部署联邦执法人员。两项修正案昨晚均被规则委员会中的共和党人阻止进入众议院全体表决。\nLarson 一直呼吁解散 ICE，并在国会推动立法，要求联邦特工表明身份；禁止 ICE 在学校、医院、法院和宗教场所进行突袭；禁止包括锁喉在内的虐待性手段；并将 ICE 资金从共和党预算中重新用于降低医疗保险费和扩大可负担住房。\n议题：人权；移民；反对特朗普和“DOGE”","publish_source":"larson.house.gov","publish_time":"2026-03-05T15:18:52-05:00"}},{"id":"news-2347","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"拉森就前FBI局长詹姆斯·科米被起诉发表声明","title_en":"Larson Statement on the Indictment of Former FBI Director James Comey","summary_cn":"众议员约翰·B·拉森就司法部在特朗普敦促下起诉前FBI局长詹姆斯·科米发表声明。拉森称，在总统抱怨政治对手未受起诉后，弗吉尼亚东区联邦检察官被解职，由特朗普前私人律师林赛·哈利根接替，后者从未起诉过案件却签署了起诉书。拉森批评这是威权手段，并提到特朗普施压媒体、国土安全部攻击民主党人，表示相信科米能击败这些指控。","summary_en":"Rep. John B. Larson released a statement after the Justice Department indicted former FBI Director James Comey at President Trump's urging. Larson said the U.S. Attorney for the Eastern District of Virginia was fired and replaced by Lindsey Halligan, Trump's former personal attorney who has never prosecuted a case, and she signed the indictment. Larson called it authoritarian lawfare, cited pressure on media and a DHS report attacking Democrats, and expressed confidence Comey can beat the charges.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-18T16:15:25.572377+00:00","url":"http://larson.house.gov/media-center/press-releases/larson-statement-indictment-former-fbi-director-james-comey","content":"Home\nMedia\nPress Releases\nLarson Statement on the Indictment of Former FBI Director James Comey\nImage September 26, 2025 Press ReleaseEast Hartford, CT – Today, Rep. John B. Larson (CT-01) released the following statement after the U.S. Department of Justice indicted former FBI Director James Comey at the urging of President Trump.  Following complaints from the President that his political adversaries were not facing prosecution, the U.S. Attorney for the Eastern District of Virginia was fired and replaced with Lindsey Halligan, President Trump’s former personal attorney, who has never prosecuted a case. She signed Director Comey’s indictment. “Prosecuting political enemies with little to no evidence is straight out of the authoritarian playbook,” said Larson. “In the last couple weeks, President Trump put his thumb on the scales of justice to deliver this phony indictment, led a campaign to try to take Jimmy Kimmel off the air – threatening to pull broadcast licenses from media outlets he did not agree with, and had his Department of Homeland Security issue a ‘report’ attacking top Democrats, including myself, for speaking out forcefully against his policies. This lawfare is what we have come to expect from regimes like Russia and North Korea, not the United States of America. I applaud Director Comey for not backing down and have full confidence he can beat these trumped-up charges. We will continue, as will all Americans, to speak out. America will not be silenced.”\nIssues:JudicialStanding Up to Trump and ‘DOGE’","content_cn":"首页\n媒体\n新闻稿\n拉森就前联邦调查局局长詹姆斯·科米被起诉发表声明\n图片 2025年9月26日 新闻稿 康涅狄格州东哈特福德——今日，众议员约翰·B·拉森（康涅狄格州第一选区）在特朗普总统敦促下美国司法部起诉前联邦调查局局长詹姆斯·科米后，发表以下声明。在总统抱怨其政治对手未遭起诉后，弗吉尼亚东区联邦检察官被解职，由特朗普总统的前私人律师林赛·哈利根接替，此人从未起诉过任何案件。她签署了对科米局长的起诉书。“在几乎没有证据的情况下起诉政治敌人，正是威权主义剧本中的做法，”拉森说。“在过去几周里，特朗普总统将手伸向正义的天平，促成了这份虚假的起诉书，领导了一场试图让吉米·坎摩尔停播的运动——威胁要吊销他不同意的媒体的广播执照，并让其国土安全部发布一份‘报告’，攻击包括我在内的顶级民主党人，因为我们强烈发声反对他的政策。这种法律战是我们预期会从俄罗斯和朝鲜这样的政权那里看到的手段，而不是美利坚合众国。我赞扬科米局长没有退缩，并完全相信他能击败这些捏造的指控。我们将继续发声，所有美国人也将如此。美国不会被噤声。”\n议题：司法 挺身对抗特朗普和‘DOGE’","publish_source":"larson.house.gov","publish_time":"2025-09-26T11:42:54-04:00"}},{"id":"news-1288","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"众议员南希·梅斯解释众议院在国土安全部停摆问题上的处境","title_en":"Congresswoman Nancy Mace Explains Where The House Is At On The DHS Shutdown","summary_cn":"美国众议员南希·梅斯发布声明，说明参议院以口头表决通过一项为国土安全部拨款但不含移民及海关执法局和海关与边境保护局经费的法案后，众议院面临的三种选择：原样通过、修正后送回参议院或否决并继续停摆。她解释了众议院规则对暂停规则表决和同日审议规则的限制，并表示致力于让整个国土安全部重新开放。","summary_en":"U.S. Rep. Nancy Mace issued a statement explaining the House's position after the Senate passed by voice vote a bill funding DHS except ICE and CBP. She outlined three options: pass the bill as is, amend it to restore ICE and CBP funding and send it back, or reject it and continue the shutdown. She detailed House rules limiting suspension votes and same-day consideration of rules, and said she is committed to reopening all of DHS.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-18T14:38:58.149014+00:00","url":"http://mace.house.gov/media/press-releases/congresswoman-nancy-mace-explains-where-house-dhs-shutdown","content":"Home\nMedia\nPress Releases\nCongresswoman Nancy Mace Explains Where The House Is At On The DHS ShutdownMarch 27, 2026 Press Release\nImage  Where we are on TSA funding...The Senate unanimously decided to give in to Democrat demands to not fund ICE or CBP.They passed a bill by voice vote (which is why you saw them leaving town last night before the actual vote early this morning). The Senate sent it to the House to fund all of DHS except ICE and the Border Patrol (CBP), the agencies responsible for enforcing our immigration laws and removing criminal illegal aliens from the country.This surrender by Senate Republicans was passed in the middle of the night and then the entire Senate decided to go home for 2.5 weeks.This leaves the House with 3 undesirable options:(1) Pass the bill as is, cutting funding for U.S. immigration enforcement(2) Amend the bill to include funding for ICE and CBP and send it back to the Senate. Unfortunately given the Senate’s decision to take a 2.5-week vacation, the DHS shutdown would continue(3) Reject the bill, continuing the shutdown of DHS Given the Rules of the House, passing this bill as-is also has procedural barriers to overcomeIf there is bipartisan consensus behind a bill, typically the easiest way to pass the bill is under suspension of the rules. Under suspension of the rules, debate is limited to 40 minutes and it requires a 2/3 majority to pass.Unfortunately, clause 1(a) of Rule XV of the House provides “the Speaker may not entertain a motion that the House suspend the rules except on Mondays, Tuesdays, and Wednesdays”. Meaning we could not consider the bill under suspension of the rules until Monday.The other way in which to pass bills in the House is by passing a rule providing for consideration of the bill and then moving on to consider the bill under that rule. But, clause 6(a) of Rule XIII provides “a report by the Committee on Rules on a rule, joint rule, or the order of business may not be called up for consideration on the same day it is presented to the House”. This is what’s known as the “same day” rule.Under clause 6(a) of Rule XIII, there are limited exceptions in which a House may consider a rule the same day it is reported to the House by the Rules Committee. This includes when 2/3 of the House vote to do so. This is one way to pass the DHS appropriations bill (without ICE and CBP funding) today.There are also various ways in which the House can waive its own rules, including through unanimous consent, through a resolution, or other mechanism. The House can also adjourn midday and start a new legislative day after the rule is reported, bypassing the same-day rule because it is technically a new legislative day.There are still a lot of challenges ahead, but we are fully committed to getting ALL of DHS reopened for the American people.\nIssues:Congress","content_cn":"首页\n媒体\n新闻稿\n国会女议员南希·梅斯解释众议院在国土安全部停摆问题上的立场 2026年3月27日 新闻稿\n图片 我们在运输安全管理局（TSA）资金问题上的立场……参议院一致决定屈服于民主党人的要求，不为移民和海关执法局（ICE）或海关与边境保护局（CBP）提供资金。他们以口头表决方式通过了一项法案（这就是为什么你们看到他们昨晚在实际投票于今天凌晨进行之前就离开了城里）。参议院将该法案送交众议院，要求为整个国土安全部提供资金，但ICE和边境巡逻队（CBP）除外——这两个机构负责执行我们的移民法律并将犯罪的非法外国人驱逐出境。参议院共和党人的这一投降是在半夜通过的，随后整个参议院决定回家休假2.5周。这让众议院面临3个不受欢迎的选项：（1）按原样通过该法案，削减美国移民执法资金（2）修改法案以纳入ICE和CBP的资金，并将其送回参议院。不幸的是，鉴于参议院决定休2.5周的假，国土安全部的停摆将继续（3）拒绝该法案，继续国土安全部的停摆 鉴于众议院的规则，按原样通过该法案还存在需要克服的程序障碍。如果一项法案背后有两党共识，通常通过该法案最简单的方式是根据规则暂停适用程序。在暂停适用规则的情况下，辩论限于40分钟，并且需要三分之二多数才能通过。不幸的是，众议院规则第十五条第1(a)款规定“议长不得在星期一、星期二和星期三以外的时间受理要求众议院暂停适用规则的动议”。这意味着我们在星期一之前无法根据暂停适用规则审议该法案。在众议院通过法案的另一种方式是先通过一项规定该法案审议程序的规则，然后根据该规则继续审议该法案。但是，规则第十三条第6(a)款规定“规则委员会关于某项规则、联合规则或议事日程的报告，不得在其提交众议院的同一天提请审议”。这就是所谓的“同日”规则。根据规则第十三条第6(a)款，在有限例外情况下，众议院可以在规则委员会向众议院报告某项规则的当天审议该规则。这包括众议院三分之二投票同意这样做的情况。这是今天通过国土安全部拨款法案（不含ICE和CBP资金）的一种方式。众议院还可以通过各种方式放弃自身规则，包括通过一致同意、通过决议或其他机制。众议院还可以在中午休会，并在规则报告后开始新的立法日，从而绕过同日规则，因为这在技术上是一个新的立法日。前方仍有许多挑战，但我们完全致力于为美国人民重新开放整个国土安全部。\n议题：国会","publish_source":"mace.house.gov","publish_time":"2026-03-27T09:58:19-04:00"}},{"id":"news-1938","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"在马加齐纳推动下，国土安全部释放退伍军人妻子出ICE拘留","title_en":"Following Magaziner’s Advocacy, DHS Releases Wife of Combat Veteran from ICE Detention","summary_cn":"众议员塞思·马加齐纳对合法美国居民、海军退伍军人吉姆·布朗的妻子唐娜·休斯-布朗获释表示欢迎。她在赢得取消遣返听证后于2025年12月18日获释。马加齐纳曾邀请布朗出席国土安全委员会听证会，就拘留问题质询国土安全部长诺姆并获其审查承诺。马加齐纳批评特朗普政府所谓针对最恶劣者的承诺不实，将继续为被不公正拘留的家庭发声。","summary_en":"Rep. Seth Magaziner applauded the release of Donna Hughes-Brown, a legal U.S. resident and wife of Navy combat veteran Jim Brown, from ICE detention after winning her cancellation of removal hearing on December 18, 2025. Magaziner had invited Brown to a Homeland Security Committee hearing, questioned Secretary Noem about the detention, and secured a commitment to review the case. He criticized the Trump administration's claim of targeting the worst of the worst and vowed to keep fighting unjust detentions.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-18T15:51:39.088643+00:00","url":"http://magaziner.house.gov/media/press-releases/following-magaziners-advocacy-dhs-releases-wife-combat-veteran-ice-detention","content":"Home\nMedia\nPress Releases\nFollowing Magaziner’s Advocacy, DHS Releases Wife of Combat Veteran from ICE Detention\nImage\nDecember 19, 2025 Press Release\nWASHINGTON, DC — Today U.S. Representative Seth Magaziner (RI-02) applauded the news that Donna Hughes-Brown, a legal U.S. resident and the wife of U.S. Navy combat veteran Jim Brown of Missouri has been released from Immigration and Customs Enforcement (ICE) detention. Mrs. Hughes-Brown was immediately released after winning her cancellation of removal hearing on December 18, 2025, ending the deportation proceedings against her. Last week, Rep. Magaziner invited Jim Brown to attend a House Homeland Security Committee hearing with Department of Homeland Security (DHS) Secretary Kristi Noem. During the hearing, Magaziner questioned Secretary Noem directly about Mrs. Hughes-Brown’s detention and secured a commitment from her to review her case. You can watch the exchange between Jim Brown and Secretary Noem here. “The Trump Administration claimed it would target the ‘worst of the worst,’ but no one understands how false that promise was more than Jim and Donna Brown,” said Magaziner. “Jim Brown served our country in combat, and his family deserved better than months of unnecessary separation. This patriotic couple are now reunited just before Christmas. I will continue fighting this Administration over their unjust detentions and work to reunite more  innocent families targeted by Trump’s DHS.”Mr. Brown is a U.S. Navy and Gulf War combat veteran. His wife, Donna Hughes-Brown, is a grandmother and Blue Star military mother who has lived legally in the United States for 47 years. She was detained in Chicago, and imprisoned for months, after returning from a family visit to her native Ireland due to writing two bad checks totaling no more than $80 combined more than a decade ago.During the hearing, Magaziner asked Secretary Noem to use her broad discretion as Secretary to review Mrs. Hughes-Brown’s case, underscoring the injustice of detaining veteran families and longtime U.S. residents with deep family and community ties over minor, long-resolved offenses.","content_cn":"首页\n媒体\n新闻稿\n在马加齐纳的倡导下，国土安全部将一名战斗老兵的妻子从移民及海关执法局拘留中释放\n图片\n2025年12月19日新闻稿\n华盛顿特区——今日，美国众议员塞思·马加齐纳（罗德岛州第二选区）对以下消息表示赞赏：美国合法居民、密苏里州美国海军战斗老兵吉姆·布朗的妻子唐娜·休斯-布朗已从移民及海关执法局（ICE）拘留中获释。休斯-布朗女士于2025年12月18日赢得取消遣返听证后立即获释，针对她的遣返程序就此结束。上周，马加齐纳众议员邀请吉姆·布朗出席众议院国土安全委员会与国土安全部（DHS）部长克里斯蒂·诺姆举行的听证会。听证期间，马加齐纳直接就休斯-布朗女士被拘留一事质询诺姆部长，并获得她审查此案的承诺。您可以在此观看吉姆·布朗与诺姆部长的交流。“特朗普政府声称要针对‘最恶劣的罪犯’，但没有人比吉姆和唐娜·布朗更清楚这一承诺有多么虚假，”马加齐纳说。“吉姆·布朗曾在战斗中为国效力，他的家人本不应遭受数月不必要的分离。这对爱国夫妇如今在圣诞节前得以团聚。我将继续就本届政府的不公正拘留与之抗争，并努力让更多被特朗普的国土安全部针对的无辜家庭团聚。”布朗先生是美国海军及海湾战争战斗老兵。他的妻子唐娜·休斯-布朗是一位祖母，也是一位蓝星军属母亲，已在美国合法居住47年。她此前在探访祖国爱尔兰的家人后返回时在芝加哥被拘留，并被关押数月，原因是十多年前开具了两张总额不超过80美元的空头支票。听证期间，马加齐纳请求诺姆部长行使她作为部长的广泛自由裁量权审查休斯-布朗女士的案件，并强调因轻微且早已了结的违法行为而拘留老兵家属和拥有深厚家庭与社区纽带的长期美国居民是不公正的。","publish_source":"magaziner.house.gov","publish_time":"2025-12-19T14:57:27-05:00"}},{"id":"news-1397","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"马利奥塔基斯呼吁舒默和杰弗里斯为国土安全部拨款","title_en":"Malliotakis Calls On Schumer & Jeffries to Fund DHS Amid Rising Security Threats","summary_cn":"众议员妮可·马利奥塔基斯与地方官员、纽约警察工会及美国退伍军人协会成员共同呼吁舒默和杰弗里斯停止拿国家安全做游戏，提供重新开放并全额资助国土安全部所需的票数。她指出2026年1月众议院共和党人通过了全年拨款法案，但民主党人退出协议导致DHS停摆，TSA、FEMA仅执行基本职能，海岸警卫队人员无薪工作。她强调在纽约面临恐怖威胁之际应支持一线人员。","summary_en":"Rep. Nicole Malliotakis, joined by local officials, NYPD unions, and American Legion members, called on Chuck Schumer and Hakeem Jeffries to stop playing games with national security and provide votes to reopen and fully fund the Department of Homeland Security. She noted House Republicans passed a full-year funding bill in January 2026, but Democrats backed out, causing a DHS shutdown with TSA and FEMA performing only essential functions and Coast Guard personnel serving without pay. She stressed supporting frontline personnel amid threats in New York.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-18T15:22:58.135151+00:00","url":"http://malliotakis.house.gov/media/press-releases/malliotakis-calls-schumer-jeffries-fund-dhs-amid-rising-security-threats","content":"Home\nMedia\nPress Releases\nMalliotakis Calls On Schumer & Jeffries to Fund DHS Amid Rising Security Threats\nImage\nMarch 13, 2026 Press Release\n(STATEN ISLAND, NY) — Congresswoman Nicole Malliotakis (NY-11) was joined by local elected officials, NYPD police unions and members of the American Legion as she called on Chuck Schumer and Hakeem Jeffries to stop playing games with our national security and provide the votes necessary to reopen and fully fund the Department of Homeland Security. Fully funding DHS will ensure our Coast Guard, TSA, and law enforcement officers are paid and that critical security initiatives remain in place to keep our nation safe, particularly in light of the attempted attack by ISIS-inspired terrorists in New York City.In January 2026, House Republicans passed the full-year Department of Homeland Security (DHS) funding bill negotiated and agreed upon by both House and Senate Appropriators. However, House and Senate Democrats backed out of this deal forcing a shutdown of DHS operations critical to the safety and security of the American people. Agencies such as the Transportation Security Administration and the Federal Emergency Management Agency are only performing the most essential functions and Coast Guard personnel are currently serving without pay.Last week, the House passed H.R. 7744, Department of Homeland Security Appropriations Act of 2026, which provides: ﻿$64.4 billion in discretionary funding, including $3 billion for defense activities, to protect the homeland and keep American communities safe, secure, and resilient. $6.3 billion in discretionary appropriations that are offset by fee collections and $26.37 billion as an allocation adjustment for major disaster response and recovery activities.Ends programs that incentivize illegal immigration.Bolsters border protections by providing $513 million to sustain 22,000 Border Patrol agents and $3.8 billion for custody operations to strengthen the Administration’s efforts to detain and deport all criminal and removable aliens.$116 million to counter China by increasing the Coast Guard’s Indo-Pacific footprint while also funding a military pay raise for Coast Guard servicemembers.Enhances resources to detect and counter the spread of deadly drugs, like fentanyl, that poison our communities.“Just last week, House Republicans once again took action and passed legislation to fully fund the Department of Homeland Security and ensure the men and women protecting our country are paid. Despite four Democrats joining us in the House, Senate Democrats continue to block this critical funding, putting politics ahead of the safety and security of the American people. At a time when threats against our homeland remain real — especially here in New York — Congress should be focused on supporting the Coast Guard, TSA agents, and law enforcement officers who keep us safe,\" said Congresswoman Nicole Malliotakis.﻿\"This is not a time for partisan politics, we're all New Yorkers and we're all Americans. This has really got to stop. You need to pass these bills to get this funding to our men and women who are going without paychecks,\" said Assemblyman Sam Pirozzolo. \"These are families whose lives are being interrupted time and time again.\"\"This funding it really supports how we handle things not only here in New York but across the country. What's really impacted? Technology support from the federal government to our local law enforcement, to our fusion centers where vital information is shared. Without that support without that grant funding, our men and women in the field can't do their job.\" said Assemblyman Mike Reilly.“Today we join Congresswoman Malliotakis in requesting that Democratic leadership in Washington uphold our national security by ensuring that the necessary votes are cast to fully fund the Department of Homeland Security. The public safety of New Yorker’s cannot be used as a bartering chip within their political game. In the midst of recent terrorist attacks carried out by ISIS-inspired terrorists in NYC, this is no time to play politics. The United States Coast Guard, TSA, and law enforcement officers who put their lives on the line on a daily basis deserve to be paid for doing so. Securing the safety of our nation must never become a partisan issue,\" said Assemblyman Michael Tannousis.﻿\"The United States Coast Guard is an integral part of our nation's national security and homeland defense. At a time when the United States faces one of our highest levels of risk in decades due to ongoing global events, it is completely unacceptable for Coast Guard members and their families to face the possibility of missing a paycheck,\" said  Frank LaMarch, American Legion.View full press conference HERE.","content_cn":"首页\n媒体\n新闻稿\n马利奥塔基斯呼吁舒默和杰弗里斯在安全威胁上升之际为国土安全部提供资金\n图片\n2026年3月13日新闻稿\n（纽约州斯塔滕岛）——国会议员妮科尔·马利奥塔基斯（纽约州第11选区）与当地民选官员、纽约市警察局警察工会及美国退伍军人协会成员一道，呼吁查克·舒默和哈基姆·杰弗里斯停止拿我们的国家安全玩弄政治，并提供必要票数以重新开放并全额资助国土安全部。全额资助国土安全部将确保我们的海岸警卫队、运输安全管理局（TSA）和执法人员获得薪酬，并确保关键安全举措继续到位以保障国家安全，尤其是在纽约市发生受ISIS启发的恐怖分子未遂袭击之后。2026年1月，众议院共和党人通过了由参众两院拨款委员会协商并达成一致的国土安全部（DHS）全年拨款法案。然而，参众两院民主党人退出了这项协议，迫使对美国人安全与保障至关重要的国土安全部运作停摆。运输安全管理局和联邦紧急事务管理局等机构仅执行最基本职能，海岸警卫队人员目前无薪服役。上周，众议院通过了H.R. 7744号法案，即《2026年国土安全部拨款法案》，该法案提供：644亿美元可自由支配资金，其中包括30亿美元用于国防活动，以保护国土并保障美国社区安全、稳固和具有韧性。63亿美元可自由支配拨款，由收费收入抵消，以及263.7亿美元作为重大灾难响应和恢复活动的分配调整。终止激励非法移民的项目。加强边境保护，提供5.13亿美元以维持2.2万名边境巡逻人员，并提供38亿美元用于羁押行动，以加强政府拘留和驱逐所有犯罪及可驱逐外国人的努力。提供1.16亿美元以对抗中国，扩大海岸警卫队在印太地区的存在，同时为海岸警卫队军人提供军饷增长。增强资源以侦查和打击芬太尼等毒害我们社区的致命毒品扩散。“就在上周，众议院共和党人再次采取行动，通过了全额资助国土安全部的立法，确保保护我们国家的男女人员获得薪酬。尽管众议院有四位民主党人与我们一道支持，参议院民主党人仍继续阻挠这一关键资金，将政治置于美国人民的安全与保障之上。在我们国土面临的威胁依然真实之际——尤其是在纽约这里——国会应专注于支持保障我们安全的海岸警卫队、TSA人员和执法人员，”国会议员妮科尔·马利奥塔基斯说。“现在不是搞党派政治的时候，我们都是纽约人，我们都是美国人。这真的必须停止。你们需要通过这些法案，把资金送到那些拿不到薪水的男女人员手中，”州众议员萨姆·皮罗佐洛说。“这些家庭的生活一次又一次被打断。”“这笔资金确实支撑着我们不仅在纽约、而且在全国处理事务的方式。真正受到影响的是什么？是联邦政府向我们地方执法部门、向我们共享重要信息的情报融合中心提供的技术支持。没有那项支持，没有那笔拨款资金，我们在一线的人员就无法履行职责，”州众议员迈克·赖利说。“今天，我们与马利奥塔基斯国会议员一道，请求华盛顿的民主党领导层通过确保投出必要票数以全额资助国土安全部来维护我们的国家安全。纽约市民的公共安全不能成为他们政治游戏中的交易筹码。在纽约市近期发生受ISIS启发的恐怖分子实施的恐怖袭击之际，现在不是玩弄政治的时候。每天冒着生命危险执行任务的美国海岸警卫队、TSA和执法人员理应为此获得薪酬。保障我们国家的安全绝不能成为一个党派问题，”州众议员迈克尔·坦努西斯说。“美国海岸警卫队是我们国家国家安全和国土防御不可或缺的一部分。在美国因持续的全球事件而面临数十年来最高风险水平之一之际，海岸警卫队成员及其家人面临可能拿不到薪水的处境是完全不可接受的，”美国退伍军人协会的弗兰克·拉马奇说。在此观看完整新闻发布会。","publish_source":"malliotakis.house.gov","publish_time":"2026-03-13T14:02:27-04:00"}},{"id":"news-1791","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"麦考尔在国土安全听证会上强调网络安全能力的重要性","title_en":"McCaul Highlights Importance of Cybersecurity Capabilities at Homeland Security Hearing","summary_cn":"众议员迈克尔·麦考尔在国土安全委员会题为“国土安全部监督：CISA、TSA、S&T”的听证会上发言，强调网络安全能力的重要性。作为CISA法案作者，他询问代理局长戈图穆卡拉关于《网络信息共享法》即将于1月30日到期的问题，指出该法授权CISA与私营部门共享约80%的网络威胁信息，若失效将严重损害保护国家的能力，并批评参议院未采取行动。","summary_en":"Rep. Michael McCaul spoke at a Homeland Security Committee hearing titled Oversight of the Department of Homeland Security: CISA, TSA, S&T, highlighting cybersecurity capabilities. As author of the CISA Act, he asked Acting Director Gottumukkala about the Cyber Information Sharing Act expiring January 30, noting it authorizes CISA to share about 80% of cyber threat information with the private sector. He warned that a lapse would harm national protection efforts and criticized the Senate for inaction.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-18T15:42:05.436859+00:00","url":"http://mccaul.house.gov/media-center/press-releases/mccaul-highlights-importance-cybersecurity-capabilities-homeland","content":"Home\nMedia Center\nPress Releases\nMcCaul Highlights Importance of Cybersecurity Capabilities at Homeland Security HearingJanuary 21, 2026 Press ReleaseWASHINGTON – Today, U.S. Congressman Michael McCaul (R-Texas) — chairman emeritus and current vice chairman of the House Committee on Homeland Security — spoke at a full committee hearing titled, “Oversight of the Department of Homeland Security: CISA, TSA, S&T.”During his tenure as chairman, McCaul authored the Cybersecurity and Infrastructure Security Agency Act and championed the passage of the Cyber Information Sharing Act. During today's hearing, he underscored the importance of both initatives and asked Acting CISA Director Dr. Gottumukkala about their status.\nImage Click to watchTranscript of McCaul's Exchange:MCCAUL: Let me just say first, when I was chairman of this committee in 2015, we passed the Cyber Information Sharing Act, the ranking member and I did, together. It’s been a very bipartisan issue. In 2018, we passed the Cyber Security and Information Security Agency permanent authorization. And the reason why I’m going through this legislative history [is] it’s very important to know what is still authorized today and what is not. One of the most critical pieces of CISA as we imagined in Congress was to share information with the private sector — not only to the private sector but from the private sector, which holds about 80% of the cyber threat information. Would you agree with that, sir?GOTTUMUKKALA: Yes sir.MCCAUL: So that was vitally important as the authors of this agency, and we had quite a battle, I’d say, with [the House Intelligence Committee] over whether this should be warehoused under the National Security Agency, which is not a civilian agency. To interact with the private sector, we thought a civilian agency would be the better fit. I like to think that we were right about that. But then the goal was to expand the capabilities so that you can meet those requirements. Do you feel that you have those capabilities today?GOTTUMUKKALA: Sir, the CISA 2015, the Cybersecurity Information Sharing Act that you are referring to, it provides the legal foundation for cyber threat information sharing between the federal government and the private sector, and it remains one of the most important authorities for defending the U.S. critical infrastructure against increasingly sophisticated cyber threats.MCCAUL: Now let me go back to the authorizations, because this is really important for the committee members to know. Now, CISA the agency was permanently authorized, so there’s no expiration. However, there is one on the Cyber Information Sharing Act, which was brought about by a compromise with various members who would not vote for it unless we put that expiration term in there. So ... it will expire on January 30th of this year. ...It is not in the Homeland appropriations that we’re voting on this week. My question to you is: While you still have appropriations to the majority of your agency, if not all, to not be authorized — to have a lapse in authorization — at this point in time where the cyber threat is far greater today than when Mr. Thompson and I first created the agency and the [Cyber] Information Sharing Act, in addition coupled with the World Cup FIFA events coming up, the Olympics, and our 250th anniversary of the republic... How does that harm your efforts to protect the nation?GOTTUMUKKALA: Congressman, thank you again. Like I said, I personally support and DHS also supports the long-term reauthorization of CISA 2015, and I understand that the act expires January 30th. One of the strengths of CISA is the partnership and collaboration with the private sector, and the private sector understands that this will be extended through the continuing resolution. And we have worked with Chairman Garbarino and the committee and the widespread information-MCCAUL: This is not your fault; this is congress’s fault. I think the [committee] has done its job, but the Senate has not done their job on this. And so it’s vitally important — and this is a message to the Senate — that when we do pass this again, that the Senate reauthorize your mission. Otherwise, your ability to collect 80% of the threat information from the private sector is gone; you’re no longer authorized to do that by law. And so that is why that is so important, sir. And this has, as Mr. Thompson knows, always been a bipartisan issue. I really hope, I don’t have any doubt in my colleagues on the other side of the aisle or in the House that we’re going to get this done, but the Senate, for the sake of the nation and our security, needs to act on this. It is highly irresponsible and quite frankly, it’s just downright dangerous what they’re doing, and they’re playing games with something that’s very serious.###\nIssues:Homeland Security","content_cn":"首页\n媒体中心\n新闻稿\n麦考尔在国土安全委员会听证会上强调网络安全能力的重要性 2026年1月21日 新闻稿 华盛顿——今天，美国国会议员迈克尔·麦考尔（德克萨斯州共和党人）——众议院国土安全委员会荣休主席、现任副主席——在题为“对国土安全部的监督：CISA、TSA、S&T”的全委员会听证会上发言。在担任主席期间，麦考尔起草了《网络安全和基础设施安全局法》，并推动通过了《网络信息共享法》。在今天的听证会上，他强调了这两项举措的重要性，并向代理CISA局长戈图穆卡拉博士询问了它们的现状。\n图片 点击观看麦考尔发言记录：麦考尔：首先我要说，2015年我担任本委员会主席时，我们通过了《网络信息共享法》，是我和资深委员一起推动的。这一直是一个高度两党共识的议题。2018年，我们通过了网络安全和信息安全局的永久授权。我之所以回顾这段立法史，是因为非常重要的是要知道今天哪些授权仍然有效、哪些已经失效。正如我们在国会所设想的，CISA最关键的部分之一是与私营部门共享信息——不仅是向私营部门提供信息，还要从私营部门获取信息，因为私营部门掌握着约80%的网络威胁信息。先生，您同意这一点吗？戈图穆卡拉：是的，先生。麦考尔：作为这个机构的起草者，这一点至关重要，而且我要说，我们曾与[众议院情报委员会]就是否应将其置于国家安全局之下展开过相当激烈的争论，因为国家安全局不是文职机构。要与私营部门互动，我们认为文职机构更合适。我愿意认为我们当时是对的。但接下来的目标是扩展能力，以便能够满足这些要求。您觉得您今天具备这些能力吗？戈图穆卡拉：先生，您提到的2015年CISA，即《网络安全信息共享法》，为联邦政府与私营部门之间的网络威胁信息共享提供了法律基础，它仍然是保护美国关键基础设施免受日益复杂的网络威胁的最重要授权之一。麦考尔：现在让我回到授权问题，因为这对委员会成员来说确实非常重要。CISA这个机构已获得永久授权，所以没有到期问题。然而，《网络信息共享法》有一个到期日，这是与一些成员的妥协结果，他们除非我们加入这一到期条款，否则不会投票支持。所以……它将于今年1月30日到期。……它不在我们本周投票的国土安全拨款法案中。我的问题是：虽然你们机构的大部分——如果不是全部——拨款仍然存在，但在授权失效——在授权出现空档——之际，而此时网络威胁远比汤普森先生和我最初创建该机构和《[网络]信息共享法》时严重得多，再加上即将到来的世界杯国际足联赛事、奥运会，以及我们共和国250周年纪念……这如何损害您保护国家的努力？戈图穆卡拉：议员，再次感谢您。正如我所说，我个人支持，国土安全部也支持对2015年CISA进行长期重新授权，我理解该法将于1月30日到期。CISA的优势之一是与私营部门的伙伴关系和协作，私营部门也明白这将通过持续决议得到延长。我们一直在与加巴里诺主席、委员会以及广泛的信息——麦考尔：这不是您的错；这是国会的错。我认为[委员会]已经尽了自己的职责，但参议院在这方面没有尽到职责。所以至关重要的是——这也是给参议院的信息——当我们再次通过这项法案时，参议院必须重新授权你们的使命。否则，你们从私营部门收集80%威胁信息的能力就没了；你们在法律上不再被授权这样做。先生，这就是为什么这一点如此重要。正如汤普森先生所知，这一直是一个两党共识的议题。我真的希望——我对对面党派的同事或众议院同仁毫不怀疑——我们会完成这件事，但参议院为了国家和我们安全的利益，需要就此采取行动。他们的所作所为是极不负责任的，坦率地说，简直危险至极，他们在拿非常严肃的事情玩弄政治。###\n议题：国土安全","publish_source":"mccaul.house.gov","publish_time":"2026-01-21T15:04:03-05:00"}},{"id":"news-1622","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"麦考尔在国土安全委员会听证会上就DHS监督质询ICE代理局长莱昂斯","title_en":"McCaul Questions Acting ICE Director Lyons at Homeland Security Committee Hearing on DHS Oversight","summary_cn":"美国众议员迈克尔·麦考尔在众议院国土安全委员会听证会上质询ICE代理局长托德·莱昂斯，讨论国土安全部监督问题。麦考尔批评明尼阿波利斯等庇护城市不配合ICE拘留令，称左翼言论导致针对ICE人员的袭击激增，并提到博维诺被撤换、霍曼接手后转向有针对性的执法行动，莱昂斯回应称抗议有所缓和。","summary_en":"U.S. Rep. Michael McCaul questioned Acting ICE Director Todd Lyons at a House Homeland Security Committee hearing on DHS oversight. McCaul criticized sanctuary cities like Minneapolis for not honoring ICE detainers, said left-wing rhetoric led to a surge in assaults on ICE officers, and noted that after Bovino was replaced by Homan, operations shifted to targeted enforcement. Lyons said protests have subsided.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-18T15:32:24.005262+00:00","url":"http://mccaul.house.gov/media-center/press-releases/mccaul-questions-acting-ice-director-lyons-homeland-security-committee","content":"Home\nMedia Center\nPress Releases\nMcCaul Questions Acting ICE Director Lyons at Homeland Security Committee Hearing on DHS OversightFebruary 11, 2026 Press ReleaseWASHINGTON – Congressman Michael McCaul (R-Texas) — chairman emeritus and current vice chair of the House Committee on HomelandSecurity — questioned Acting ICE Director Todd Lyons at a committee hearing, entitled \"Oversight of the Department of Homeland Security: ICE, CBP, and USCIS.”\nImage Click to watchFull Exchange:McCaul: A decade ago, when I chaired this committee, Mr. Thompson and I passed a bill to authorize ICE into law. It was a bipartisan effort. It passed the House overwhelmingly — both Republican and Democrat.A decade later, here we are. The [Democrats] have called to abolish ICE; now they’re trying to shut it down. So what has happened in that ten years?Let’s go back to the last four to five years. What happened in this country and at the border? As someone who lives in a border state, Texas, we saw the most dangerous wide-open border that I’ve seen in my 22 years in Congress.Ten to twelve million people — and that’s what we know about, [but] I think it’s far greater — came into this country, many of them dangerous, violent criminals [and] some known or suspected terrorists, which I find extremely dangerous.That’s why I served as an impeachment manager for Mayorkas because he violated federal law. The federal statute says — as a former federal prosecutor I know this — “shall” detain aggravated felons. What did Mayorkas do? He told his agents, “that’s discretionary; you can release them.”As a result, we had tens of thousands of aggravated felons left on the streets of America to roam freely — not to mention the human sex trafficking of children, Mr. Lyons, as you pointed out.So what is the administration trying to do? They’re trying to remove a public safety threat from the United States of America.That is their job. Restoring public safety should be the number one priority.And one of the problems here, as I examined it, is that Minnesota — Minneapolis in particular is a sanctuary city. What does that mean? That means it’s a magnet. … They’re protected under the current situation because state and locals will not cooperate with federal law enforcement.In fact, Mr. Lyons, is it not true that they were not honoring ICE detainers that were put on dangerous felons in prison so that you could remove them from the United States?Lyons: That is correct sir. The detainers were not honored at the local level in Minneapolis.McCaul: This is the number one violation. In addition, the rhetoric on the Left led to [an] over 1,000% increase in assaults on ICE officers, an increase of over 8,000 [percent on] death threats to them. All this created a perfect storm for our officers being thrown into this situation. And then Agent Bovino came into the picture, and I would argue, in fairness, that he escalated the situation by the way that was handled.Your officers are not trained to effectuate crowd control; they are trained to move in surgically, [to] go in and remove these dangerous, violent criminals from the United States of America.I’ve called for de-escalation after the two deaths, the two shootings that took place. I believe these roving patrols should be done at the border, rather than in the major cities of the United States. So when the president decided to remove Agent Bovino and put in Tom Homan, whom I’ve known for years, a consummate law enforcement professional, I commended the president. And what has been done since Mr. Homan came into the job?We now have targeted law enforcement operations. He is returning to the original mission of ICE. He is working with state and locals to do the crowd control. He is getting them to honor the ICE detainers. He is also getting the body cameras put on them. And the roving patrols, in his words to me, should be done at the border, not in major cities.My question to you, Mr. Lyons: [Are Mr. Homan’s] operations in Minneapolis now bringing the situation under control?Lyons: We’ve seen de-escalation in the fact that the protests — while they still go on — have subsided, and ICE has been allowed to do their targeted, intelligence-driven enforcement operation.Just the other night, local authorities arrested 54 protestors at the local level, where ICE officers did not have to be engaged in that.###\nIssues:Homeland Security","content_cn":"首页\n媒体中心\n新闻稿\n麦考尔在国土安全委员会关于国土安全部监督的听证会上质询代理ICE局长莱昂斯 2026年2月11日 新闻稿 华盛顿——国会议员迈克尔·麦考尔（德克萨斯州共和党人）——众议院国土安全委员会荣休主席、现任副主席——在题为“对国土安全部的监督：ICE、CBP和USCIS”的委员会听证会上质询了代理ICE局长托德·莱昂斯。\n图片 点击观看完整问答：麦考尔：十年前，当我担任本委员会主席时，我和汤普森先生通过了一项法案，将ICE授权写入法律。这是一项两党努力。它在众议院以压倒性多数通过——共和党和民主党都支持。十年后，我们却到了这一步。[民主党人]曾呼吁废除ICE；现在他们试图关掉它。那么这十年间发生了什么？让我们回到过去四五年。这个国家和边境发生了什么？作为一个生活在边境州德克萨斯的人，我们看到了我在国会22年来见过的最危险、最敞开的边境。有一千万到一千二百万人——这只是我们所知道的，[但]我认为实际数字要大得多——进入这个国家，其中许多是危险的暴力罪犯，[还有]一些已知或疑似恐怖分子，我认为这极其危险。这就是为什么我担任了对马约卡斯的弹劾管理人，因为他违反了联邦法律。联邦法规规定——作为前联邦检察官我知道这一点——“应当”拘留加重重罪犯。马约卡斯做了什么？他告诉他的探员，“那是自由裁量的；你们可以释放他们。”结果，我们有数万名加重重罪犯被留在美国街头自由游荡——更不用说对儿童的人口性贩运了，莱昂斯先生，正如您所指出的。那么这届政府在试图做什么？他们在试图从美国清除一个公共安全威胁。那是他们的职责。恢复公共安全应该是头等大事。而这里的问题之一，正如我所审视的，是明尼苏达州——尤其是明尼阿波利斯——是一个庇护城市。这意味着什么？这意味着它是一个磁石。……在当前情况下他们受到保护，因为州和地方执法部门不会与联邦执法部门合作。事实上，莱昂斯先生，难道不是这样吗——他们不遵守针对监狱中危险重罪犯的ICE拘留令，以便你们能将其驱逐出美国？莱昂斯：是的，先生。在明尼阿波利斯，地方层面不遵守拘留令。麦考尔：这是头号违规行为。此外，左翼的言论导致对ICE官员的袭击增加了1000%以上，对他们的死亡威胁增加了8000[%]以上。所有这些为我们的官员被抛入这种处境制造了一场完美风暴。然后博维诺探员进入了画面，公平地说，我认为他处理此事的方式使局势升级了。你们的官员没有接受过人群控制的训练；他们接受的训练是精准行动，进入并把这些危险、暴力的罪犯从美国清除出去。在两人死亡、两起枪击事件发生后，我呼吁缓和局势。我认为这些流动巡逻应该在边境进行，而不是在美国的大城市。所以当总统决定撤换博维诺探员，换上我认识多年的汤姆·霍曼——一位完美的执法专业人士——时，我赞扬了总统。霍曼先生上任以来做了什么？我们现在有了有针对性的执法行动。他正在回归ICE的原始使命。他正在与州和地方合作进行人群控制。他正在让他们遵守ICE拘留令。他还在让他们佩戴随身摄像头。而流动巡逻，用他对我说的话，应该在边境进行，而不是在大城市。莱昂斯先生，我的问题是：[霍曼先生的]行动现在是否使明尼阿波利斯的局势得到控制？莱昂斯：我们看到了缓和，事实上抗议活动——虽然仍在继续——已经减弱，ICE得以开展其有针对性的、情报驱动的执法行动。就在前几天晚上，地方当局在地方层面逮捕了54名抗议者，ICE官员不必介入其中。###\n议题：国土安全","publish_source":"mccaul.house.gov","publish_time":"2026-02-11T11:59:46-05:00"}},{"id":"news-1766","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"视频：众议员戴夫·闵对增加DHS拨款说“绝对不行”","title_en":"WATCH: Rep. Dave Min Says “Hell No” to More Funding for DHS","summary_cn":"加州众议员戴夫·闵在新闻稿中抨击即将表决的DHS拨款法案，称“ICE已经失控，必须被追究责任”。他提到自己赴明尼苏达参加监督ICE行为的现场听证会，并列举拘留五岁儿童、无搜查令突袭民宅等指控，表示将投票反对ICE与DHS拨款法案，呼吁加强问责与约束。","summary_en":"California Rep. Dave Min slammed the upcoming DHS funding bill, saying 'ICE is out of control, and they need to be held to account.' He cited a field hearing in Minnesota on ICE misconduct and listed allegations including detaining five-year-olds and warrantless home raids, saying he will vote no on the ICE-DHS funding bill and calling for accountability and guardrails.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-18T15:41:13.334137+00:00","url":"http://min.house.gov/media/press-releases/watch-rep-dave-min-says-hell-no-more-funding-dhs","content":"Home\nMedia\nPress Releases\nWATCH: Rep. Dave Min Says “Hell No” to More Funding for DHS\nJanuary 22, 2026 Press Release\nRep. Min: “ICE is out of control, and they need to be held to account.”\nWashington, D.C. — Representative Dave Min (CA-47), member of the House Oversight Committee, slammed the upcoming DHS funding bill, saying, “ICE is out of control, and they need to be held to account.”Last week, Rep. Min joined members of Congress in Minnesota for a field hearing to conduct oversight of ICE misconduct and Donald Trump’s law breaking. Rep. Min has been outspoken about the lawlessness of ICE, sending multiple letters demanding answers from Department of Homeland Secretary Kristi Noem and other top officials. WATCH HERE\nImage\nTRANSCRIPT:“It’s Congressman Dave Min, and what we have seen out of Minneapolis the last few weeks has just been horrific. Detaining five year-olds, pulling seniors out of their homes in their underwear in freezing cold weather, murdering people who are in ICE detention, a memo, apparently instructing ICE agents to raid and break into people’s homes without a warrant, ramming of cars intentionally, and then arresting US citizens claiming that they weaponized their vehicles.”“This is just outrageous. It’s systematically illegal, and it's terrifying our communities. It has to stop. That is why I’m voting hell no on the upcoming ICE DHS funding bill. Enough is enough. We need accountability. We need guardrails. ICE is out of control, and they need to be held to account.”\nMedia\nPress Releases\nIn the News\nBack to top button","content_cn":"首页\n媒体\n新闻稿\n观看：众议员戴夫·闵表示对国土安全部增加拨款“坚决说不”\n2026年1月22日 新闻稿\n闵众议员：“移民和海关执法局已经失控，他们必须被追究责任。”\n华盛顿特区——众议院监督委员会成员、代表加利福尼亚州第47选区的众议员戴夫·闵猛烈抨击即将出台的国土安全部拨款法案，称：“移民和海关执法局已经失控，他们必须被追究责任。”上周，闵众议员与国会议员同僚在明尼苏达州参加了一场实地听证会，对移民和海关执法局的不当行为以及唐纳德·特朗普的违法行为进行监督。闵众议员一直直言不讳地批评移民和海关执法局的无视法律行为，多次致函要求国土安全部部长克里斯蒂·诺姆及其他高级官员作出答复。点击此处观看\n图片\n文字记录：“我是国会议员戴夫·闵，过去几周我们从明尼阿波利斯看到的情况简直令人震惊。拘留五岁的儿童，在严寒天气中把老年人从家中拽出来，他们只穿着内衣，杀害被移民和海关执法局拘留的人，一份备忘录，显然指示移民和海关执法局探员在没有搜查令的情况下突袭并闯入民宅，故意撞车，然后逮捕美国公民，声称他们将车辆武器化。”“这简直令人发指。这是系统性的违法行为，正在恐吓我们的社区。这必须停止。这就是为什么我对即将出台的移民和海关执法局/国土安全部拨款法案投下坚决反对票。够了就是够了。我们需要问责。我们需要护栏。移民和海关执法局已经失控，他们必须被追究责任。”\n媒体\n新闻稿\n新闻报道\n返回顶部按钮","publish_source":"min.house.gov","publish_time":"2026-01-22T15:05:46-05:00"}},{"id":"news-1674","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"法院命令DHS恢复国会对ICE拘留设施的监督后，众议员内古斯发表声明","title_en":"Congressman Neguse Issues Statement After Court Orders DHS to Restore Congressional Oversight of ICE Detention Facilities","summary_cn":"联邦法院批准众议员乔·内古斯等13名议员申请的紧急救济，命令国土安全部和ICE恢复其对ICE拘留设施的不事先通知的国会监督。内古斯称这是美国人民的胜利。此前DHS要求议员提前通知探访，多名议员持有效法院命令仍被拒之门外，法院裁决恢复了议员实时进入设施、会见被拘留者并调查拥挤、戴镣、缺乏医疗等问题。","summary_en":"A federal court granted emergency relief to Rep. Joe Neguse and 12 other lawmakers, ordering DHS and ICE to restore unannounced congressional oversight of ICE detention facilities. Neguse called it a victory for the American people. After DHS imposed a prior-notice requirement and members with valid court orders were denied entry, the ruling restores their ability to enter facilities, meet detainees, and investigate overcrowding, shackling, and lack of medical care.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-18T15:35:27.717140+00:00","url":"http://neguse.house.gov/media/press-releases/congressman-neguse-issues-statement-after-court-orders-dhs-restore-0","content":"Image\nHome\nMedia\nPress Releases\nCongressman Neguse Issues Statement After Court Orders DHS to Restore Congressional Oversight of ICE Detention Facilities\nFebruary 2, 2026 Press Release\nEmergency Ruling Reaffirms the Right and Duty of Members of Congress to Conduct Unannounced Inspections Amid Alarming Reports of Abuse\nWashington, D.C. — Colorado Congressman and Assistant Democratic Leader Joe Neguse issued the following statement after a federal court granted emergency relief to him and 12 other Members of Congress, ordering the U.S. Department of Homeland Security (DHS) and Immigration and Customs Enforcement (ICE) to restore plaintiffs’ unannounced congressional oversight of ICE detention facilities. The ruling enforces federal law and reaffirms Congress’s constitutional authority to investigate detention conditions and ensure accountability.“The Court’s decision today to grant a temporary restraining order against ICE’s unlawful effort to obstruct congressional oversight is a victory for the American people. We will keep fighting to ensure the rule of law prevails,” said Assistant Democratic Leader Joe Neguse. After the court preliminarily stayed a DHS policy requiring members of Congress to provide prior notice of oversight visits to ICE facilities in December, and following the fatal shooting of a U.S. citizen by a federal agent in Minnesota, DHS Secretary Kristi Noem secretly reinstated the requirement through a previously undisclosed memorandum. The memo came to light only after multiple members of Congress were denied entry to an ICE facility in Minnesota despite presenting a valid court order. Today’s decision follows another emergency motion filed by Democracy Forward and American Oversight on behalf of the members, after those unlawful denials of entry pursuant to the new DHS memo. Those denials of entry directly interfere with Congress’s right and duty to investigate detention conditions, ensure compliance with the law, and respond to rising reports of abuse and violence inside detention centers. The court’s ruling restores the plaintiff members’ ability to enter detention facilities in real time, speak with detainees, and investigate conditions that include overcrowding, shackling, denial of medical care, and lack of access to counsel.In addition to Assistant Democratic Leader Joe Neguse, plaintiffs include Congressional Hispanic Caucus Chair Rep. Adriano Espaillat; Homeland Security Committee Ranking Member Rep. Bennie G. Thompson; Judiciary Committee Ranking Member Rep. Jamie Raskin; House Oversight and Government Reform Committee Ranking Member Rep. Robert Garcia; House Homeland Security Committee Subcommittee on Border Security and Enforcement Ranking Member Rep. J. Luis Correa; and Reps. Jason Crow, Veronica Escobar, Dan Goldman, Jimmy Gomez, Kelly Morrison, Raul Ruiz, and Norma Torres.The case is Joe Neguse et al. v. Immigration and Customs Enforcement, et al. The Members of Congress are represented in this suit by Democracy Forward Foundation and American Oversight.Read the order HERE.###","content_cn":"图片\n首页\n媒体\n新闻稿\n法院命令国土安全部恢复国会对移民和海关执法局拘留设施的监督后，国会议员内古斯发表声明\n2026年2月2日 新闻稿\n紧急裁决重申国会议员在令人震惊的虐待报道中进行突击检查的权利和义务\n华盛顿特区——在联邦法院向科罗拉多州国会议员、助理民主党领袖乔·内古斯及其他12名国会议员授予紧急救济，命令美国国土安全部和移民和海关执法局恢复原告对移民和海关执法局拘留设施的突击国会监督后，乔·内古斯发表了以下声明。该裁决执行了联邦法律，并重申了国会调查拘留条件和确保问责的宪法权力。“法院今天决定对移民和海关执法局非法阻挠国会监督的行为颁发临时限制令，这是美国人民的胜利。我们将继续奋斗，确保法治获胜，”助理民主党领袖乔·内古斯表示。在法院于12月初步中止了一项要求国会议员事先通知对移民和海关执法局设施进行监督访问的国土安全部政策之后，以及在明尼苏达州一名联邦探员致命枪击一名美国公民之后，国土安全部部长克里斯蒂·诺姆通过一份此前未披露的备忘录秘密恢复了该要求。该备忘录是在多名国会议员尽管出示了有效法院命令仍被拒绝进入明尼苏达州一处移民和海关执法局设施后才曝光的。今天的裁决是在“民主前进”组织和“美国监督”组织代表这些议员提交另一份紧急动议之后作出的，此前他们依据国土安全部的新备忘录被非法拒绝进入。这些拒绝进入的行为直接干涉了国会调查拘留条件、确保遵守法律以及回应拘留中心内日益增多的虐待和暴力报道的权利和义务。法院的裁决恢复了原告议员实时进入拘留设施、与被拘留者交谈以及调查包括过度拥挤、戴镣铐、拒绝提供医疗护理和缺乏律师接触在内的条件的权利。除助理民主党领袖乔·内古斯外，原告还包括国会拉美裔党团主席阿德里亚诺·埃斯帕伊拉特众议员；国土安全委员会资深成员本尼·G·汤普森众议员；司法委员会资深成员杰米·拉斯金众议员；众议院监督和政府改革委员会资深成员罗伯特·加西亚众议员；众议院国土安全委员会边境安全和执法小组委员会资深成员J·路易斯·科雷亚众议员；以及众议员杰森·克劳、维罗妮卡·埃斯科巴、丹·戈德曼、吉米·戈麦斯、凯利·莫里森、劳尔·鲁伊斯和诺玛·托雷斯。此案为乔·内古斯等人诉移民和海关执法局等人。国会议员在此诉讼中由“民主前进”基金会和“美国监督”组织代理。点击此处阅读命令。###","publish_source":"neguse.house.gov","publish_time":"2026-02-02T13:20:25-05:00"}},{"id":"news-1442","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"众议员内古斯揭露DHS“全面腐败”后，诺姆部长被解职","title_en":"Secretary Noem Fired After Congressman Neguse Exposes “Wholesale Corruption” at DHS","summary_cn":"新闻稿称，特朗普总统解除了国土安全部长克里斯蒂·诺姆的职务，原因与其参与一项耗资2.2亿美元、由纳税人出资、以诺姆骑马为背景的广告宣传活动有关。众议员内古斯在司法委员会听证会上就欺诈、腐败和利益冲突提出质询，称这是“欺诈”，并预测将有人被追责。文中还引用其在电视采访中批评DHS将纳税人资金当作私产。","summary_en":"The release says President Trump fired Homeland Security Secretary Kristi Noem over her involvement in a $220 million taxpayer-funded ad campaign featuring her on horseback. Rep. Neguse questioned Noem at a Judiciary Committee hearing about fraud, corruption, and conflicts of interest, calling it 'fraud' and predicting accountability. It also quotes his TV interview criticizing DHS for treating taxpayer money as its own.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-18T15:24:06.294694+00:00","url":"http://neguse.house.gov/media/press-releases/secretary-noem-fired-after-congressman-neguse-exposes-wholesale-corruption-dhs","content":"Image\nHome\nMedia\nPress Releases\nSecretary Noem Fired After Congressman Neguse Exposes “Wholesale Corruption” at DHS\nMarch 6, 2026 Press Release\nWashington, D.C. — Yesterday, President Donald Trump fired Homeland Security Secretary Kristi Noem over reported “frustrations” with her involvement in a $220 million, taxpayer-funded ad campaign featuring Noem on horseback in front of Mount Rushmore. Congressman Neguse was part of the tipping point that led to Noem’s ousting, raising questions during Wednesday’s Judiciary Committee hearing that were similar to those posed by Republican Senator John Kennedy about allegations of fraud, corruption, and conflicts of interest surrounding the ad campaign.“It is fraud, and ultimately, I think there's going to be ​accountability,” Neguse said on Wednesday.View Rep. Neguse’s questioning of Secretary Noem HERE.\nImage\nThe Colorado congressman also joined Morning Joe on MS NOW on Thursday to call for Secretary Noem’s termination and to further discuss his line of questioning.View Rep. Neguse’s interview on Morning Joe HERE.\nImage\nOn Secretary Noem’s $220 Million Taxpayer-Funded Ad Campaign: JOHNATHAN LEMIRE (HOST): Congressman, we want to turn now to the hearing with Homeland Security Secretary Noem. You had questions for her. Got a lot of attention. You focused on $143 million contract that DHS gave to a company with ties to her political allies back in South Dakota. For those who aren't following closely, give a quick summary as to what you were talking about and whether you found her answers sufficient. REP. NEGUSE: Yeah, well, first let me just say, Jonathan, I think, unfortunately, one of the political realities that we have to grapple with is that these hearings and oversight is kind of viewed through a very partisan lens, but the hearing yesterday, and the hearing in the Senate, and the very compelling questions that were posed by my colleagues, including, by the way, to their credit, Republican Senator Kennedy and Senator Tillis in the Senate, that perhaps this pierces through, because what we're talking about is bad and wholesale corruption. That's it. It's very simple. In this instance, you have the Secretary and senior officials at DHS treating taxpayer money as though it is their own. In this particular example, it's a $143 million ad campaign that Secretary Noem authorized. You may be familiar with these ads. These are ads of her at Mount Rushmore and other locations. And this contract was not put up for a competitive bid. The department skipped the typical procurement process and instead gave it to what looks to be a political ally, certainly someone who was involved in Republican politics. So, in my view, it is very clear that they are violating the law. It's the reason, of course, why the Secretary is trying to stop the Inspector General from investigating a host of different issues that have percolated over the Department of Homeland Security. I think the people of our country should be offended at the way in which they are grifting and ultimately committing fraud with taxpayer dollars. ###","content_cn":"图片\n首页\n媒体\n新闻稿\n在众议员内古斯揭露国土安全部“全面腐败”后，诺姆部长被解职\n2026年3月6日 新闻稿\n华盛顿特区——昨日，唐纳德·特朗普总统解除了国土安全部部长克里斯蒂·诺姆的职务，据报道原因是她对一项耗资2.2亿美元、由纳税人资助的广告宣传活动参与其中，该广告中诺姆骑马出现在拉什莫尔山前，令总统感到“不满”。众议员内古斯是导致诺姆下台的临界点之一，他在周三的司法委员会听证会上提出的问题，与共和党参议员约翰·肯尼迪就围绕该广告宣传活动的欺诈、腐败和利益冲突指控所提出的问题类似。“这是欺诈，最终，我认为将会有人承担责任，”内古斯在周三表示。在此观看内古斯众议员对诺姆部长的质询。\n图片\n这位科罗拉多州众议员周四还做客MS NOW的《早安乔》节目，呼吁解除诺姆部长的职务，并进一步讨论了他的质询思路。在此观看内古斯众议员在《早安乔》节目中的采访。\n图片\n关于诺姆部长耗资2.2亿美元、由纳税人资助的广告宣传活动：约翰纳森·勒米尔（主持人）：众议员，我们现在想谈谈与国土安全部部长诺姆的听证会。你向她提出了问题。引起了很大关注。你聚焦于国土安全部将一份1.43亿美元的合同授予了一家与她南达科他州政治盟友有关联的公司。对于那些没有密切关注的人，请简要概括一下你当时谈论的内容，以及你是否认为她的回答足够充分。内古斯众议员：是的，首先我要说，约翰纳森，我认为不幸的是，我们必须应对的政治现实之一是，这些听证和监督往往被以一种非常党派化的视角来看待，但昨天的听证会，以及参议院的听证会，还有我的同事们提出的非常有力的质询——顺便说一句，这要归功于参议院的共和党参议员肯尼迪和参议员蒂利斯——也许能够穿透这一切，因为我们谈论的是糟糕的、全面的腐败。就是这样。非常简单。在这种情况下，部长和国土安全部的高级官员把纳税人的钱当作自己的钱来对待。在这个具体例子中，是诺姆部长批准的一项1.43亿美元的广告宣传活动。你可能对这些广告很熟悉。这些是她在拉什莫尔山和其他地点的广告。而这份合同没有经过竞标。该部门跳过了典型的采购程序，而是把它交给了一个看起来是政治盟友的人，肯定是参与共和党政治的人。所以，在我看来，很明显他们在违法。当然，这就是为什么部长试图阻止监察长调查国土安全部积累的一系列不同问题。我认为我们国家的人民应该对他们这种骗取并最终用纳税人资金实施欺诈的方式感到愤怒。###","publish_source":"neguse.house.gov","publish_time":"2026-03-06T14:29:16-05:00"}},{"id":"news-2393","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS (deep pilot)","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"众议员内古斯就埃弗格林高中枪击案相关社交媒体账户调查质询FBI局长卡什·帕特尔","title_en":"WATCH: Rep. Neguse Questions FBI Director Kash Patel Following Reports the Agency Was Investigating “Violent” Social Media Account Linked to Evergreen High School Shooter","summary_cn":"2025年9月17日，科罗拉多州众议员乔·内古斯在众议院司法委员会听证会上，就联邦调查局调查可能与埃弗格林高中枪击案凶手有关的社交媒体账户一事，质询FBI局长卡什·帕特尔。内古斯援引公开报道称，FBI自7月起对该账户展开评估调查，直至9月10日案发当天仍在追查用户身份。帕特尔回应称，主动排查庞大社交媒体平台是最大障碍，需依赖服务提供商配合。","summary_en":"On September 17, 2025, during a House Judiciary Committee hearing, Colorado Rep. Joe Neguse questioned FBI Director Kash Patel about the bureau's investigation into a social media account possibly linked to the Evergreen High School shooter. Neguse cited public reporting that the FBI opened an assessment in July and worked to identify the user until September 10, the day of the shooting. Patel said proactively monitoring vast social media platforms is the biggest impediment and that the FBI relies on service providers.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-25T11:06:06.599481+00:00","url":"http://neguse.house.gov/media/press-releases/watch-rep-neguse-questions-fbi-director-kash-patel-following-reports-agency","content":"Image\nHome\nMedia\nPress Releases\nWATCH: Rep. Neguse Questions FBI Director Kash Patel Following Reports the Agency Was Investigating “Violent” Social Media Account Linked to Evergreen High School Shooter\nImage\nSeptember 17, 2025 Press Release\nWashington, D.C. — Today, during a House Judiciary Committee hearing, Colorado Congressman Joe Neguse questioned Kash Patel, the Director of the Federal Bureau of Investigation (FBI), on the agency’s investigation of a social media account that may have belonged to the teenager responsible for shooting two students at Evergreen High School last week. Neguse asked for further information regarding the FBI’s efforts to track down who was behind the account.Watch the full clip HERE. The clip is available for download HERE.A full transcript of the exchange is available below. NEGUSE: Thank you, Mr. Chairman, for holding this hearing. Thank you, Director Patel, for being here today. I have a couple of questions regarding a terrible shooting that occurred in Colorado. The state, that as you may know, that I represent. You’ve testified previously about, I think, what you would describe as your efforts to provide more information regarding the investigation with respect to the horrific assassination of Mr. [Charlie] Kirk. And so, in that same vein, I’m hoping you can provide this Committee and my constituents in Colorado with some clarity—PATEL: Absolutely. NEGUSE: I think, as my colleagues know, in Evergreen, Colorado—Jefferson County—a county that I proudly represent. In Evergreen High School, a shooter ultimately injured two students—we’re praying for their swift recovery. There's an article here from Colorado Public Radio, the title is, quote, “FBI was already investigating an account that may have been linked to the Evergreen shooter.” And you're familiar with the circumstances generally, Director, regarding this terrible tragedy? PATEL: Of course. Yes. NEGUSE: So, my understanding from the public reporting, is that an organization reported to the FBI in July of this year regarding, just reading here from the article, that “the FBI opened an assessment into a social media account user whose identity was unknown and who was discussing the planning of a mass shooting with threats non-specific in nature.” This is the FBI’s statement to the press, and that the FBI continued to work this assessment investigation to identify the name and location of the user up until September 10th, 2025, which was the day of the tragedy. Can you provide us some clarity on what were the impediments to finding, you know, the account user and maybe describe in greater detail the FBI’s work in that regard?PATEL: Generally speaking, yes, because I know even though the shooter's deceased, the investigation is…we're not done. And so, the impediments to finding these individuals, and you highlight a great point. We had two huge tragedies in the span of days in this country. The school shooting in Evergreen, Colorado, being one of them. And, proactively going out onto these social media platforms, which are so large, is our biggest impediment. And we need to rely on the service providers. There's actual legislation, I can't remember the name of it that’s up for renewal, which will, and I think at the end of the month, which gives service providers the ability to report that information from their end without liability. We need that to continue, because while the FBI has so many people and the police are great at doing it, there's just too many platforms to cover down on.NEGUSE: I appreciate that, Director Patel and I think we're certainly—I'm interested in continuing this conversation because I think the reporting suggests, that this, that there's a pattern and that ultimately, you know, we want to make sure that law enforcement is able to prevent this kind of tragedy from happening in the future. ###","content_cn":"图片\n主页\n媒体\n新闻稿\n观看：Neguse众议员在报道称联邦调查局正在调查一个与Evergreen高中枪手有关的“暴力”社交媒体账户后，向FBI局长Kash Patel提问\n图片\n2025年9月17日 新闻稿\n华盛顿特区——今天，在众议院司法委员会举行听证会期间，科罗拉多州众议员Joe Neguse向联邦调查局（FBI）局长Kash Patel提问，内容涉及该机构对一个社交媒体账户的调查；据称，该账户可能属于上周在Evergreen高中枪击两名学生的青少年。Neguse要求进一步了解FBI为追查该账户背后人员所作的努力。观看完整视频剪辑请点击这里。视频剪辑可在这里下载。以下提供了双方交流的完整文字记录。\n\nNEGUSE：感谢主席举行此次听证会。Patel局长，感谢您今天到场。我有几个问题要询问，涉及科罗拉多州发生的一起可怕枪击事件。正如您可能知道的，这是我所代表的州。您此前曾就——我想，您会将其描述为您努力提供更多信息、以了解有关[Charlie] Kirk先生那起可怕暗杀事件的调查——作过证词。因此，本着同样的精神，我希望您能向本委员会以及我在科罗拉多州的选民提供一些澄清——\n\nPATEL：当然可以。\n\nNEGUSE：我想，正如我的同事们所知，在科罗拉多州Evergreen——杰斐逊县——这是我自豪地代表的县。在Evergreen高中，一名枪手最终导致两名学生受伤——我们祈祷他们早日康复。这里有一篇来自科罗拉多州公共广播电台的文章，标题是，引用：“FBI此前已经在调查一个可能与Evergreen枪手有关的账户。”局长，您熟悉这场可怕悲剧的大致情况吗？\n\nPATEL：当然。是的。\n\nNEGUSE：根据公开报道，我的理解是，今年7月有一个组织向FBI报告了相关情况。这里直接引用文章内容：“FBI对一名身份不明的社交媒体账户用户展开评估，该用户正在讨论策划大规模枪击事件，并作出性质不具体的威胁。”这是FBI向媒体发表的声明；声明还称，FBI继续开展这项评估调查，以确定该用户的姓名和所在地，直到2025年9月10日，也就是悲剧发生当天。您能否向我们说明，查找该账户用户时遇到了哪些障碍，并更详细地描述FBI在这方面所做的工作？\n\nPATEL：总的来说，可以，因为我知道，即使枪手已经死亡，调查仍在进行……我们还没有结束。因此，寻找这些人的障碍——您指出了一个很重要的问题。几天之内，这个国家发生了两起重大悲剧。科罗拉多州Evergreen的校园枪击案就是其中之一。主动在这些规模如此庞大的社交媒体平台上开展工作，是我们面临的最大障碍。我们需要依靠服务提供商。实际上，有一项立法——我记不起它的名字——目前正在等待续期，我想是在本月底。该法允许服务提供商从自身一端报告相关信息而不承担责任。我们需要让它继续有效，因为尽管FBI拥有很多人员，警方也非常擅长开展这类工作，但平台实在太多，无法全部覆盖。\n\nNEGUSE：Patel局长，我感谢您，我认为我们当然——我有兴趣继续这一对话，因为我认为报道表明，这里存在一种模式，而归根结底，我们希望确保执法部门能够防止此类悲剧在未来发生。\n###","publish_source":"neguse.house.gov","publish_time":"2025-09-17T13:42:03-04:00"}},{"id":"news-1456","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"纽豪斯投票推动国土安全部拨款法案","title_en":"Newhouse Votes to Advance Homeland Security Funding","summary_cn":"2026年3月5日，美国众议员丹·纽豪斯就H.R. 7744《2026年国土安全部拨款法案》以221比209通过发表声明，称众议院共和党人再次推动为本财年剩余时间内的国土安全部提供资金，以结束政府停摆，并强调在中东军事行动导致国内威胁上升之际，需尽快为反恐、网络安全、边境安全、运输安全管理局和应急管理机构拨款。","summary_en":"On March 5, 2026, U.S. Rep. Dan Newhouse issued a statement after the House passed H.R. 7744, the Department of Homeland Security Appropriations Act, 2026, by a vote of 221-209. He said House Republicans are again advancing legislation to fund DHS for the remainder of the fiscal year and end the shutdown, stressing that with increased domestic threats due to military action in the Middle East, Congress must swiftly fund counterterrorism, cybersecurity, border security, TSA and emergency management agencies.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-24T20:33:31.991995+00:00","url":"http://newhouse.house.gov/media-center/press-releases/newhouse-votes-advance-homeland-security-funding","content":"Home\nNews\nPress Releases\nNewhouse Votes to Advance Homeland Security Funding\nMarch 5, 2026 Press Release\nWASHINGTON, D.C. – Today, Rep. Dan Newhouse released the following statement after passage of H.R. 7744, Department of Homeland Security Appropriations Act, 2026. The legislation passed by a vote of 221-209. “Once again, House Republicans are advancing legislation to fund the Department of Homeland Security for the remainder of the fiscal year and end the shutdown perpetrated by my colleagues on the other side of the aisle.\" said Rep. Newhouse. “With increased domestic threats due to military action in the Middle East, we must act swiftly to fund counterterrorism, cybersecurity, border security, TSA, and emergency management agencies. Partisan games that threaten the safety of American citizens are dangerous, and we must fund the Department of Homeland Security immediately.”\nIssues:\nImmigration and the Southern Border\nSpending and Economy\nService Center\nFlag\nRequests\nMobile Office\nHours\nVisiting DC\nand Tours\nMilitary Academy Nominations\nHelp with a\nFederal Agency","content_cn":"主页\n新闻\n新闻稿\n纽豪斯投票推进国土安全部拨款\n2026年3月5日 新闻稿\n华盛顿特区——今天，众议员丹·纽豪斯在H.R. 7744号《2026年国土安全部拨款法案》通过后发表了以下声明。该法案以221票对209票通过。\n“众议院共和党人再次推动立法，为国土安全部提供本财年剩余时间的资金，并结束由我在议会另一边的同事所造成的政府停摆。”纽豪斯众议员说。“鉴于中东军事行动导致国内威胁增加，我们必须迅速采取行动，为反恐、网络安全、边境安全、运输安全管理局（TSA）和应急管理机构提供资金。威胁美国公民安全的党派游戏十分危险，我们必须立即为国土安全部提供资金。”\n议题：\n移民与南部边境\n支出与经济\n服务中心\n旗帜\n请求\n流动办公室\n办公时间\n访问华盛顿特区\n及参观\n军事学院提名\n获取联邦机构帮助","publish_source":"newhouse.house.gov","publish_time":"2026-03-05T16:57:00-05:00"}},{"id":"news-1302","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"纽豪斯投票支持为国土安全部提供资金","title_en":"Newhouse Votes to Fund Department of Homeland Security","summary_cn":"2026年3月26日，美国众议员丹·纽豪斯就H.R. 8029《支付我们的国土捍卫者法案》以218比206通过发表声明，称众议院再次通过为国土安全部提供资金、支付运输安全管理局人员、海岸警卫队、联邦应急管理署和网络安全与基础设施安全局人员薪酬的法案，并批评民主党人危及关键国家安全项目，敦促参议院尽快行动结束国土安全部停摆。","summary_en":"On March 26, 2026, U.S. Rep. Dan Newhouse issued a statement after the House passed H.R. 8029, the Pay Our Homeland Defenders Act, by a vote of 218-206. He said the House again passed a bill to fund the Department of Homeland Security and pay TSA agents, Coast Guardsmen, FEMA employees and CISA agents, accused Democrats of jeopardizing critical national security programs, and urged the Senate to act swiftly to end the DHS shutdown.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-24T20:30:04.589371+00:00","url":"http://newhouse.house.gov/media-center/press-releases/newhouse-votes-fund-department-homeland-security","content":"Home\nNews\nPress Releases\nNewhouse Votes to Fund Department of Homeland Security\nMarch 26, 2026 Press Release\nFor Immediate Release: March 26, 2026Contact: Juan Ayala, (202) 713-7750WASHINGTON, D.C. – Today, Rep. Dan Newhouse released the following statement after passage of H.R. 8029, Pay Our Homeland Defenders Act. The legislation passed by a vote of 218-206.\"It’s Groundhog Day on Capitol Hill. Once again, the House of Representatives has passed a bill to fund the Department of Homeland Security and pay TSA agents, Coast Guardsmen, FEMA employees, and CISA agents,\" said Rep. Newhouse. \"This legislation makes our country safer and safeguards the American public from cyberthreats, terrorism, foreign adversaries, and illegal immigration. Unfortunately, Democrats are jeopardizing critical national security programs to try and advance nonsensical reforms to immigration enforcement. Congress has a Constitutional responsibility to fund the federal government and I urge the Senate to act swiftly to end the DHS shutdown.\"\nIssues:\nService Center\nFlag\nRequests\nMobile Office\nHours\nVisiting DC\nand Tours\nMilitary Academy Nominations\nHelp with a\nFederal Agency","content_cn":"首页\n新闻\n新闻稿\n纽豪斯投票支持为国土安全部提供资金\n2026年3月26日 新闻稿\n即时发布：2026年3月26日 联系人：胡安·阿亚拉，(202) 713-7750 华盛顿特区——今天，众议员丹·纽豪斯在H.R. 8029号法案《为我们的国土保卫者发薪法案》通过后发表如下声明。该法案以218票对206票获得通过。“国会山又到了‘土拨鼠日’。众议院再次通过了一项法案，为国土安全部提供资金，并向运输安全局特工、海岸警卫队成员、联邦紧急事务管理局雇员和网络安全与基础设施安全局特工发放薪酬，”纽豪斯众议员表示。“这项立法让我们的国家更安全，并保护美国公众免受网络威胁、恐怖主义、外国对手和非法移民的危害。遗憾的是，民主党人为推进毫无意义的移民执法改革，正危及关键的国家安全项目。国会负有为联邦政府提供资金的宪法责任，我敦促参议院迅速采取行动，结束国土安全部停摆。”\n议题：\n服务中心\n旗帜\n请求\n流动办公室\n办公时间\n访问华盛顿特区\n及参观\n军事学院提名\n获得联邦机构帮助","publish_source":"newhouse.house.gov","publish_time":"2026-03-26T17:03:15-04:00"}},{"id":"news-1825","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"帕内塔众议员呼吁国土安全顾问米勒及DHS领导层辞职、免职和弹劾","title_en":"Rep. Panetta Statement Calling for Resignation, Removal, and Impeachment of Homeland Security Advisor Stephen Miller and DHS leadership","summary_cn":"众议员帕内塔发表声明，称ICE和CBP人员近期在多地开枪致人死亡，反映DHS及政府领导失败。他批评特朗普驱逐政策由国土安全顾问斯蒂芬·米勒推动，DHS在1650亿美元拨款下快速扩充ICE和CBP，培训仅47天，人员被推向城市环境。他呼吁米勒和DHS部长辞职或被免职，并支持众议院国土安全委员会和司法委员会的问责调查及弹劾程序。","summary_en":"Rep. Panetta said recent fatal shootings by ICE and CBP officers reflect a leadership failure at DHS and the administration. He criticized Trump's deportation policy, driven by Homeland Security Advisor Stephen Miller, and DHS's rapid expansion of ICE and CBP under $165 billion with only 47 days of training, pushing officers into urban settings. He called for Miller and the DHS Secretary to resign or be removed, and backed accountability investigations and impeachment proceedings.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-18T15:43:59.743563+00:00","url":"http://panetta.house.gov/media/press-releases/rep-panetta-statement-calling-resignation-removal-and-impeachment-homeland","content":"Home\nMedia\nPress Releases\nRep. Panetta Statement Calling for Resignation, Removal, and Impeachment of Homeland Security Advisor Stephen Miller and DHS leadership\nImage\nJanuary 15, 2026 Press Release\nWashington, DC — Rep. Panetta released the following statement:\n\"The recent deadly shootings of people in communities across the country by Immigration and Customs Enforcement (ICE) and Customs and Border Protection (CBP) officers reveal a failure in leadership at the Department of Homeland Security (DHS) and in this Administration. The horrific shooting death of Renee Nicole Good in Minneapolis was unnecessary, but predictable based on the unprofessionalism and lack of training that appears to pervade the ranks of ICE and CBP.\n\"The recent shootings are reported to stem from the rushed implementation by DHS of President Trump's deportation policy, that is created and driven by Homeland Security Advisor Stephen Miller. That massive immigration crackdown, along with the current injection of $165 billion in funding for DHS from the purely partisan One Big Beautiful Bill Act is not only growing the ranks of ICE and CBP officers, but also pushing them through a reduced training program of 47 days and pushing them away from the border and into urban and suburban settings across the nation.\n\"The ICE and CBP officers appear to be untrained for that environment, and unprofessional when it comes to confrontations with people and protestors. DHS Secretary Noem is responsible for implementing the Administration's deportation policy and the standards and oversight that govern ICE and CBP operations. However, based on reporting and what we've seen, it appears that the ranks of ICE and CBP are filled with substandard officers that are poorly trained, sheltered from the consequences of their actions, and empowered to behave recklessly and with impunity. Moreover, and as we experienced after the shooting in Minneapolis, the Administration, including President Trump, provides irresponsible defenses and explanations for this ineptitude, which appear to normalize brutality, violence, and lawlessness, rather than accountability and transparency. That is why I continue to call for accountability through a full independent investigation into the shootings of people by ICE and CBP officers, including what transpired in Minnesota.\n\"Moreover, as the architect and implementor of this overreaching, failed, and dangerous deportation policy that makes our communities less safe, Stephen Miller, as well as the DHS Secretary, must resign or be removed from their positions. If President Trump refuses to remove these individuals from his Administration, the House and Senate must act accordingly. I support impeachment proceedings based on the accountability investigation that is currently being conducted by the House Committee on Homeland Security and being led by Democratic ranking member Bennie Thompson. I also support an investigation by the House Committee on Judiciary led by Democratic ranking member Jamie Raskin into the DHS Secretary’s management. Such investigations will help provide the foundation and facts upon which we could properly begin formal impeachment proceedings. Unfortunately, the Republican Majority and chairmen of those two committees will not act. Moreover, for an impeachment to succeed it must garner a majority of votes in the Republican-led House of Representatives to adopt articles of impeachment and then get sent to the Republican-led Senate for final adjudication.\n\"Despite the burdens that we face with this Republican led Congress and Senate, we must stand together and act to try to ensure that the Trump Administration is held accountable. That is why I call on Congress to act now to restrain Stephen Miller and DHS leadership and stop the recklessness and violence by ICE and CBP. Now more than ever, Democrats and Republicans in Congress must fulfill our Constitutional responsibilities with proper oversight to check this executive branch and to ensure transparency, accountability, and safety in our communities.\"\nIssues:\nImmigration","content_cn":"首页\n媒体\n新闻稿\n帕内塔众议员发表声明，呼吁国土安全顾问斯蒂芬·米勒和国土安全部领导层辞职、免职并予以弹劾\n图片\n2026年1月15日 新闻稿\n华盛顿特区——帕内塔众议员发表以下声明：\n“近期，移民和海关执法局（ICE）以及海关和边境保护局（CBP）官员在全国各地社区枪杀民众的事件，暴露出国土安全部（DHS）和本届政府领导层的失职。蕾妮·妮可·古德在明尼阿波利斯惨遭枪杀身亡，这起事件本可避免，但鉴于似乎弥漫于ICE和CBP队伍中的不专业和缺乏训练，这又是可以预见的。\n“据报道，近期的枪击事件源于国土安全部仓促实施特朗普总统的驱逐出境政策，而该政策由国土安全顾问斯蒂芬·米勒制定并推动。这场大规模的移民打击行动，加上目前根据纯粹党派性的《一项大而美的法案》向国土安全部注入的1650亿美元资金，不仅扩大了ICE和CBP官员的队伍，还让他们接受缩减至47天的培训项目，并将他们从边境推向全国各地的城市和郊区环境。\n“ICE和CBP官员似乎没有为那种环境接受过训练，在与民众和抗议者对峙时也表现得不专业。国土安全部部长诺姆负责实施本届政府的驱逐出境政策，以及管理ICE和CBP运作的标准和监督。然而，根据报道和我们所看到的情况，ICE和CBP的队伍中似乎充斥着不合格的官员，他们训练不足，免受自身行为后果的追究，并被赋予鲁莽行事且不受惩罚的权力。此外，正如我们在明尼阿波利斯枪击事件后所经历的那样，包括特朗普总统在内的本届政府为这种无能提供了不负责任的辩护和解释，似乎将残暴、暴力和无法无天正常化，而不是追求问责和透明。这就是为什么我继续呼吁通过全面的独立调查来追究责任，调查ICE和CBP官员枪杀民众的事件，包括明尼苏达州发生的一切。\n“此外，作为这项过度扩张、失败且危险的驱逐出境政策的设计者和实施者——该政策使我们的社区更不安全——斯蒂芬·米勒以及国土安全部部长必须辞职或被免职。如果特朗普总统拒绝将这些个人从政府中清除，众议院和参议院必须采取相应行动。我支持基于众议院国土安全委员会目前正在进行、由民主党资深成员本尼·汤普森领导的问责调查启动弹劾程序。我也支持由民主党资深成员杰米·拉斯金领导的众议院司法委员会对国土安全部部长的管理进行调查。此类调查将有助于提供基础和事实，使我们能够适当地启动正式弹劾程序。不幸的是，共和党多数派和这两个委员会的主席不会采取行动。此外，弹劾要想成功，必须在共和党领导的众议院获得多数票通过弹劾条款，然后送交共和党领导的参议院进行最终裁决。\n“尽管我们面临这个共和党领导的国会和参议院带来的重重困难，我们必须团结一致，采取行动，努力确保特朗普政府被追究责任。这就是为什么我呼吁国会现在就采取行动，约束斯蒂芬·米勒和国土安全部领导层，制止ICE和CBP的鲁莽和暴力行为。现在比以往任何时候都更需要国会中的民主党人和共和党人履行我们的宪法职责，通过适当的监督来制衡这一行政部门，并确保我们社区的透明、问责和安全。”\n议题：\n移民","publish_source":"panetta.house.gov","publish_time":"2026-01-15T13:45:38-05:00"}},{"id":"news-1555","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"新罕布什尔州国会代表团继续敦促国土安全部长诺姆就ICE设施提案与梅里马克地方官员接触","title_en":"NH Congressional Delegation Continues to Urge DHS Secretary Kristi Noem to Engage with Local Merrimack Officials on ICE Facility Proposal | Congressman Chris Pappas","summary_cn":"2026年2月23日，美国众议员克里斯·帕帕斯与新罕布什尔州参议员哈桑、沙欣及众议员古德兰德继续敦促国土安全部长克里斯蒂·诺姆回应梅里马克地方官员对移民和海关执法局拟在该镇新建拘留设施的关切。代表团致信诺姆并转交州众议员比尔·博伊德的反对信，指出地方官员仍未获国土安全部或ICE联系，并要求尽快与地方领导、执法和应急部门沟通。","summary_en":"On February 23, 2026, U.S. Rep. Chris Pappas joined Senators Hassan and Shaheen and Rep. Goodlander in continuing to urge Homeland Security Secretary Kristi Noem to address concerns raised by Merrimack, New Hampshire, officials about ICE's proposed new detention facility there. The delegation wrote to Noem transmitting a state representative's letter of opposition, noted that local officials still had not been contacted by DHS or ICE, and requested prompt engagement with local leadership, law enforcement and emergency services.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-24T20:35:52.151735+00:00","url":"http://pappas.house.gov/media/press-releases/nh-congressional-delegation-continues-to-urge-dhs-secretary-kristi-noem-to-engage-with-local-merrimack-officials-on-ice-facility-proposal","content":"Image\nHome\nMedia\nPress Releases\nNH Congressional Delegation Continues to Urge DHS Secretary Kristi Noem to Engage with Local Merrimack Officials on ICE Facility ProposalFebruary 23, 2026 Press ReleaseCongressman Chris Pappas (NH-01) joined Senator Maggie Hassan (NH), a senior member of the Homeland Security and Governmental Affairs Committee, Senator Jeanne Shaheen (NH), and Congresswoman Maggie Goodlander (NH-02) in continuing to push Secretary of Homeland Security Kristi Noem to address the serious concerns raised by local Merrimack officials regarding ICE’s effort to build a new detention facility in the town. The New Hampshire Congressional Delegation wrote to Secretary Noem transmitting a letter from New Hampshire State Representative Bill Boyd outlining his opposition and concerns regarding ICE’s proposed Merrimack facility. Despite widespread public concern in Merrimack about the project, local Merrimack officials say they have still not been contacted by DHS or ICE about the project. “The accompanying letter details the potential negative impact this facility may have on the community’s economic development, as well as the potential strain such a facility would place upon the local economy, infrastructure, and public safety,” wrote New Hampshire’s Congressional Delegation in their push on Kristi Noem to respond. “We share the local concerns expressed about the project, and these concerns must be addressed.”  “We...request that you expeditiously engage with local leadership, including law enforcement and emergency services, regarding the proposed plan. We look forward to your prompt outreach to local officials, law enforcement, and emergency services,” concluded the Congressional Delegation.  In January, Pappas led the New Hampshire Congressional delegation in demanding that Secretary Noem swiftly acknowledge and address concerns raised by the Merrimack Town Council about reports that ICE plans to establish a new processing center in the town. In a letter earlier this month, Pappas also urged Appropriations Committee leaders to include language in any DHS funding to protect states' and localities' ability to make decisions about what is best for their communities.","content_cn":"图片\n首页\n媒体\n新闻稿\n新罕布什尔州国会代表团继续敦促国土安全部部长克里斯蒂·诺姆与梅里马克当地官员就ICE设施提案进行接洽\n2026年2月23日 新闻稿\n众议员克里斯·帕帕斯（新罕布什尔州第01选区）与国土安全和政府事务委员会资深成员、参议员玛吉·哈桑（新罕布什尔州）、参议员珍妮·沙欣（新罕布什尔州）以及众议员玛吉·古德兰德（新罕布什尔州第02选区）一道，继续敦促国土安全部部长克里斯蒂·诺姆回应梅里马克当地官员就ICE拟在该镇建设一座新拘留设施所提出的严重关切。新罕布什尔州国会代表团致函诺姆部长，转交新罕布什尔州众议员比尔·博伊德的一封信；该信概述了他对ICE拟建梅里马克设施的反对意见及担忧。尽管梅里马克公众广泛关注该项目，当地梅里马克官员表示，国土安全部或ICE至今仍未就该项目与他们联系。\n新罕布什尔州国会代表团在敦促克里斯蒂·诺姆作出回应时写道：“随附信函详细说明了该设施可能对社区经济发展造成的负面影响，以及此类设施可能给当地经济、基础设施和公共安全带来的压力。我们认同当地对该项目表达的担忧，这些担忧必须得到解决。”\n国会代表团总结道：“我们……要求您就拟议计划迅速与当地领导层，包括执法部门和紧急服务部门，开展接洽。我们期待您尽快联系当地官员、执法部门和紧急服务部门。”\n今年1月，帕帕斯带领新罕布什尔州国会代表团要求诺姆部长迅速确认并回应梅里马克镇议会提出的关切；此前有报道称，ICE计划在该镇设立一个新的处理中心。本月早些时候，帕帕斯还致函拨款委员会领导人，敦促他们在任何国土安全部资金安排中纳入相关措辞，以保护各州和地方政府就何为最符合其社区利益作出决定的能力。","publish_source":"pappas.house.gov","publish_time":"2026-02-23T13:34:13-05:00"}},{"id":"news-1709","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"新罕布什尔州国会代表团呼吁诺姆与国土安全部回应梅里马克居民及镇议会关于拟建ICE处理中心的关切","title_en":"NH Delegation Calls on Noem, DHS to Respond to Concerns of Merrimack Residents, Town Council Over Proposed ICE Processing Center | Congressman Chris Pappas","summary_cn":"新罕布什尔州国会代表团（众议员帕帕斯、参议员沙欣与哈桑、众议员古德兰德）致信美国国土安全部，要求部长诺姆尽快确认收到梅里马克镇议会反对在该镇设立移民与海关执法局（ICE）处理中心的信函，并认真考虑其预算与运营方面的关切。新闻稿指出，尽管代表团和镇政府多次联系，国土安全部仍未证实或否认相关报道，也未回应各方提问。","summary_en":"The New Hampshire congressional delegation (Rep. Pappas, Sens. Shaheen and Hassan, Rep. Goodlander) sent a letter to the Department of Homeland Security urging Secretary Noem to promptly acknowledge and respond to the Merrimack Town Council's concerns about reports that ICE plans to establish a processing center in the town. The release notes that despite repeated outreach from the delegation and the town, DHS has neither confirmed nor denied the reports nor answered questions from the town, delegation, and residents.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-24T20:40:46.233872+00:00","url":"http://pappas.house.gov/media/press-releases/nh-delegation-calls-on-noem-dhs-to-respond-to-concerns-of-merrimack-residents-town-council-over-proposed-ice-processing-center","content":"Image\nHome\nMedia\nPress Releases\nNH Delegation Calls on Noem, DHS to Respond to Concerns of Merrimack Residents, Town Council Over Proposed ICE Processing CenterJanuary 28, 2026 Press ReleaseDespite repeated outreach, DHS has failed to establish clear lines of communication with the Town of Merrimack following reports ICE plans to establish a processing center in the townToday Congressman Chris Pappas (NH-01), joined by U.S. Senators Jeanne Shaheen and Maggie Hassan, and Congresswoman Maggie Goodlander (NH-02), sent a letter to the Department of Homeland Security (DHS) demanding that Secretary Noem swiftly acknowledge and respond to concerns expressed by the Merrimack Town Council regarding reports Immigration and Customs Enforcement (ICE) plans to establish a new processing center in the town. “As the state’s congressional delegation, we urge the Department to confirm its receipt of the Town Council’s letter as soon as possible and to give full and fair consideration to the Council’s budgetary and operational concerns,” the delegation wrote.The delegation also pushed the Department to communicate clearly with the town regarding the proposed Merrimack processing center, writing, “We request that the Department acknowledge the Council’s letter and establish clear lines of communication with local officials as soon as possible to ensure the Council’s perspective is considered.”Despite repeated outreach from the New Hampshire Congressional Delegation and the Town of Merrimack, DHS has yet to confirm or deny whether reports of ICE plans to establish a processing center in the town are true, or answer questions posed by the town, delegation, and residents of Merrimack.The full letter is available here and below:Dear Secretary Noem:We write to transmit a letter from the Merrimack Town Council expressing concerns and its formal opposition to the Department of Homeland Security proposal to establish an Immigration and Customs Enforcement Processing Center in Merrimack, New Hampshire.As the state’s congressional delegation, we urge the Department to confirm its receipt of the Town Council’s letter as soon as possible and to give full and fair consideration to the Council’s budgetary and operational concerns. We request that the Department acknowledge the Council’s letter and establish clear lines of communication with local officials as soon as possible to ensure the Council’s perspective is considered.We appreciate your attention to this matter and look forward to your response and to meaningful engagement between the Department and the Merrimack Town Council.","content_cn":"图片\n主页\n媒体\n新闻稿\n新罕布什尔州代表团致函诺姆，敦促国土安全部回应梅里马克居民和镇议会对拟议ICE处理中心的关切\n2026年1月28日 新闻稿\n在收到多次联系后，国土安全部仍未与梅里马克镇建立明确的沟通渠道。此前有报道称，移民及海关执法局（ICE）计划在该镇设立一座处理中心。\n今天，国会议员克里斯·帕帕斯（新罕布什尔州第一区）与美国参议员珍妮·沙欣、玛吉·哈桑以及国会议员玛吉·古德兰德（新罕布什尔州第二区）共同致函国土安全部（DHS），要求部长诺姆迅速确认并回应梅里马克镇议会就有关移民及海关执法局（ICE）计划在该镇设立新处理中心的报道所表达的关切。\n代表团写道：“作为本州的国会代表团，我们敦促该部尽快确认已收到镇议会的信函，并全面、公正地考虑议会在预算和运营方面的关切。”\n代表团还敦促该部就拟议的梅里马克处理中心与该镇进行清晰沟通，并写道：“我们请求该部确认收到议会的信函，并尽快与地方官员建立明确的沟通渠道，以确保议会的观点得到考虑。”\n尽管新罕布什尔州国会代表团和梅里马克镇多次联系，国土安全部至今仍未确认或否认有关ICE计划在该镇设立处理中心的报道是否属实，也未回答该镇、代表团及梅里马克居民提出的问题。\n完整信函可在此处及下方查阅：\n尊敬的诺姆部长：\n我们谨转交梅里马克镇议会的一封信函。该信函表达了对国土安全部拟在新罕布什尔州梅里马克设立移民及海关执法局处理中心的提案的关切，并正式表示反对。\n作为本州的国会代表团，我们敦促该部尽快确认已收到镇议会的信函，并全面、公正地考虑议会在预算和运营方面的关切。我们请求该部确认收到议会的信函，并尽快与地方官员建立明确的沟通渠道，以确保议会的观点得到考虑。\n感谢您关注此事，我们期待您的回复，也期待该部与梅里马克镇议会开展有意义的沟通。","publish_source":"pappas.house.gov","publish_time":"2026-01-28T15:56:34-05:00"}}];
